for a preliminary run-through. Will the final version of the lighting be ready by then?\n\nAll other aspects of the game are on schedule. Please send me an update about the lighting at your earliest convenience.\n\nRegards,"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Cliff Merson Project Manager, Rimerko Games\n\nReview of Titan Adventure: Neptune''s Voyage\n\nBy Leo Weber, April 1\n\nThis new installment of Titan Adventure will surprise and delight both new players and old aficionados long familiar with the series. Though open-world formats have been widespread in recent years, Neptune''s Voyage brings something new to the format, By strippingdown instructional guides, the game gives users the opportunity to discover new areas and devices. In Neptune''s Voyage, you wake up as Thetis, a dolphin that is tasked with rescuing Neptune from an underwater cave, Users then climb, run, ride, sail, and fly through the world of the game, encountering new towns, ruins, and other creatures along the way. Some of these creatures will be familiar to long time fans, but there is plenty of novelty as well. This newest version also corrects the green and blue image rendering that was sometimes a problem in earlier installments of Titan Adventure. Neptune''s Voyage launches May 5 on Rimerko Clutch and FS5.It is available in English, Korean, Japanese, French, and Spanish."}],"question":"What can be concluded about Ms.Hanshu?","bilingual":"Có thể kết luận gì về cô Hanshu?","options":["She wrote the script for Neptune''s Voyage.","She successfully addressed Mr.Merson''s concern.","She won an award for game design.","She is a project manager."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"She successfully addressed Mr.Merson''s concern.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"discussed","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈskəst/","meaning":"đã thảo luận"},{"word":"challenge","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈʧælənʤ/","meaning":"hoàn cảnh khó khăn; một cái gì đó kiểm tra khả năng của một người"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy đã viết kịch bản cho Neptune''sVoyage.","Cô ấy đã giải quyết thành công mối quan ngại của ông Merson.","Cô đã giành được giải thưởng về thiết kế trò chơi.","Cô ấy là người quản lý dự án."]},{"questionNum":"184","passageTitle":"*E-mail*","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\n*E-mail*\n\n:01 | Linda Hanshu\n\nFrom: | Cliff Merson\n\nSubject: | Lighting Issue\n\nDate: | September 4,10:12A.M.\n\nHi, Ms. Hanshu:\n\nI want to check on the issue we discussed about lighting in the latest chapter of Titan Adventure. In past versions of the game, getting the reflections and lighting in green and blue areas correct has been a particular challenge, and it was a problem.that kept arising. As the new release, Neptune''s Voyage, is primarily an underwater adventure, addressing this problem is crucial. You said you would take charge of this, and I hope to hear that you have found a solution to the problem. The team was hoping to have one last rendering of the lighting for the game by October 10 for a preliminary run-through. Will the final version of the lighting be ready by then?\n\nAll other aspects of the game are on schedule. Please send me an update about the lighting at your earliest convenience.\n\nRegards,\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nCliff Merson Project Manager, Rimerko Games\n\nReview of Titan Adventure: Neptune''s Voyage\n\nBy Leo Weber, April 1\n\nThis new installment of Titan Adventure will surprise and delight both new players and old aficionados long familiar with the series. Though open-world formats have been widespread in recent years, Neptune''s Voyage brings something new to the format, By strippingdown instructional guides, the game gives users the opportunity to discover new areas and devices. In Neptune''s Voyage, you wake up as Thetis, a dolphin that is tasked with rescuing Neptune from an underwater cave, Users then climb, run, ride, sail, and fly through the world of the game, encountering new towns, ruins, and other creatures along the way. Some of these creatures will be familiar to long time fans, but there is plenty of novelty as well. This newest version also corrects the green and blue image rendering that was sometimes a problem in earlier installments of Titan Adventure. Neptune''s Voyage launches May 5 on Rimerko Clutch and FS5.It is available in English, Korean, Japanese, French, and Spanish.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"*E-mail*\n\n:01 | Linda Hanshu\n\nFrom: | Cliff Merson\n\nSubject: | Lighting Issue\n\nDate: | September 4,10:12A.M.\n\nHi, Ms. Hanshu:\n\nI want to check on the issue we discussed about lighting in the latest chapter of Titan Adventure. In past versions of the game, getting the reflections and lighting in green and blue areas correct has been a particular challenge, and it was a problem.that kept arising. As the new release, Neptune''s Voyage, is primarily an underwater adventure, addressing this problem is crucial. You said you would take charge of this, and I hope to hear that you have found a solution to the problem. The team was hoping to have one last rendering of the lighting for the game by October 10 for a preliminary run-through. Will the final version of the lighting be ready by then?\n\nAll other aspects of the game are on schedule. Please send me an update about the lighting at your earliest convenience.\n\nRegards,"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Cliff Merson Project Manager, Rimerko Games\n\nReview of Titan Adventure: Neptune''s Voyage\n\nBy Leo Weber, April 1\n\nThis new installment of Titan Adventure will surprise and delight both new players and old aficionados long familiar with the series. Though open-world formats have been widespread in recent years, Neptune''s Voyage brings something new to the format, By strippingdown instructional guides, the game gives users the opportunity to discover new areas and devices. In Neptune''s Voyage, you wake up as Thetis, a dolphin that is tasked with rescuing Neptune from an underwater cave, Users then climb, run, ride, sail, and fly through the world of the game, encountering new towns, ruins, and other creatures along the way. Some of these creatures will be familiar to long time fans, but there is plenty of novelty as well. This newest version also corrects the green and blue image rendering that was sometimes a problem in earlier installments of Titan Adventure. Neptune''s Voyage launches May 5 on Rimerko Clutch and FS5.It is available in English, Korean, Japanese, French, and Spanish."}],"question":"What does Mr.Weber find exciting about Neptune''s Voyage?","bilingual":"Ông Weber thấy điều gì thú vị về Hành trình 7 của Sao Hải Vương?","options":["It has players act in the role of Neptune.","It uses lighting to show players where to navigate.","It introduces a completely new set of characters.","It lets players explore new features without guidance."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"It lets players explore new features without guidance.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"completely","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/kəmˈplitli/","meaning":"hoàn toàn"},{"word":"introduce","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪntrəˈdus/","meaning":"trình bày lần đầu tiên; bắt đầu; thành lập; ĐẾN"},{"word":"discussed","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈskəst/","meaning":"đã thảo luận"}],"optionMeanings":["Nó yêu cầu người chơi đóng vai Neptune.","Nó sử dụng ánh sáng để chỉ cho người chơi nơi để điều hướng.","Nó giới thiệu một bộ ký tự hoàn toàn mới.","Nó cho phép người chơi khám phá các tính năng mới mà không cần hướng dẫn."]},{"questionNum":"185","passageTitle":"*E-mail*","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\n*E-mail*\n\n:01 | Linda Hanshu\n\nFrom: | Cliff Merson\n\nSubject: | Lighting Issue\n\nDate: | September 4,10:12A.M.\n\nHi, Ms. Hanshu:\n\nI want to check on the issue we discussed about lighting in the latest chapter of Titan Adventure. In past versions of the game, getting the reflections and lighting in green and blue areas correct has been a particular challenge, and it was a problem.that kept arising. As the new release, Neptune''s Voyage, is primarily an underwater adventure, addressing this problem is crucial. You said you would take charge of this, and I hope to hear that you have found a solution to the problem. The team was hoping to have one last rendering of the lighting for the game by October 10 for a preliminary run-through. Will the final version of the lighting be ready by then?\n\nAll other aspects of the game are on schedule. Please send me an update about the lighting at your earliest convenience.\n\nRegards,\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nCliff Merson Project Manager, Rimerko Games\n\nReview of Titan Adventure: Neptune''s Voyage\n\nBy Leo Weber, April 1\n\nThis new installment of Titan Adventure will surprise and delight both new players and old aficionados long familiar with the series. Though open-world formats have been widespread in recent years, Neptune''s Voyage brings something new to the format, By strippingdown instructional guides, the game gives users the opportunity to discover new areas and devices. In Neptune''s Voyage, you wake up as Thetis, a dolphin that is tasked with rescuing Neptune from an underwater cave, Users then climb, run, ride, sail, and fly through the world of the game, encountering new towns, ruins, and other creatures along the way. Some of these creatures will be familiar to long time fans, but there is plenty of novelty as well. This newest version also corrects the green and blue image rendering that was sometimes a problem in earlier installments of Titan Adventure. Neptune''s Voyage launches May 5 on Rimerko Clutch and FS5.It is available in English, Korean, Japanese, French, and Spanish.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"*E-mail*\n\n:01 | Linda Hanshu\n\nFrom: | Cliff Merson\n\nSubject: | Lighting Issue\n\nDate: | September 4,10:12A.M.\n\nHi, Ms. Hanshu:\n\nI want to check on the issue we discussed about lighting in the latest chapter of Titan Adventure. In past versions of the game, getting the reflections and lighting in green and blue areas correct has been a particular challenge, and it was a problem.that kept arising. As the new release, Neptune''s Voyage, is primarily an underwater adventure, addressing this problem is crucial. You said you would take charge of this, and I hope to hear that you have found a solution to the problem. The team was hoping to have one last rendering of the lighting for the game by October 10 for a preliminary run-through. Will the final version of the lighting be ready by then?\n\nAll other aspects of the game are on schedule. Please send me an update about the lighting at your earliest convenience.\n\nRegards,"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Cliff Merson Project Manager, Rimerko Games\n\nReview of Titan Adventure: Neptune''s Voyage\n\nBy Leo Weber, April 1\n\nThis new installment of Titan Adventure will surprise and delight both new players and old aficionados long familiar with the series. Though open-world formats have been widespread in recent years, Neptune''s Voyage brings something new to the format, By strippingdown instructional guides, the game gives users the opportunity to discover new areas and devices. In Neptune''s Voyage, you wake up as Thetis, a dolphin that is tasked with rescuing Neptune from an underwater cave, Users then climb, run, ride, sail, and fly through the world of the game, encountering new towns, ruins, and other creatures along the way. Some of these creatures will be familiar to long time fans, but there is plenty of novelty as well. This newest version also corrects the green and blue image rendering that was sometimes a problem in earlier installments of Titan Adventure. Neptune''s Voyage launches May 5 on Rimerko Clutch and FS5.It is available in English, Korean, Japanese, French, and Spanish."}],"question":"When will Neptune''s Voyage be available?","bilingual":"Khi nào Neptune''s Voyage sẽ ra mắt?","options":["OnSeptember4","OnOctober10","On April 1","On May 5"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"On May 5\".","vocabList":[{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"},{"word":"discussed","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈskəst/","meaning":"đã thảo luận"},{"word":"challenge","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈʧælənʤ/","meaning":"hoàn cảnh khó khăn; một cái gì đó kiểm tra khả năng của một người"}],"optionMeanings":["Vào ngày 4 tháng 9","Vào ngày 10 tháng 10","Vào ngày 1 tháng 4","Vào ngày 5 tháng 5"]},{"questionNum":"186","passageTitle":"Wonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nWonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday\n\n6A.M.-Noon | Noon-4 P.M. | 4 P.M.-7 P.M. | 7 P.M.10 P.M.\n\nCOFFEEBREAK | AFTERNOONJAZZ | FOLKFRENZY | JOSIE''SJOINT\n\nLocal news and | Music from | Folk music | Modern sounds\n\ninterviews with | traditional jazz | from around | selected by our\n\ncommunity | to jazzfusion | the world | station''s own\n\nmembers | music director\n\nHost: | Host: | Host: | Host:\n\nFelice Finney | Malachi Mzee | Penny Ariza | Josie Jones\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | feedback@wonderridgeradio.org From: | pfabre@sendmail.net Subject: | My new radio station!\n\nDate: | October 22\n\nTothefolksat Wonder Ridge Radio: As I was driving last week, I got tired of listening to sports talk and turned the dial. Suddenly, my car was filled with a song that I hadn''t heard in many years. It was traditional music from France, where my grandmother was born. She used to play that song when I was a child. I never expected to hear it on the radio here in Wonder Ridge. Thanks for this experience and for all your great programs. Your new fan, Pierre Fabre\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nWonder Ridge Radio Job Opening:Programming Assistant Posted November 2 Job Description The programming assistant reports to the director of programming and supports the radio station by performing a variety of research and communication functions. This role is an entry-level, part-time position. Responsibilities Conducting background research on interviewees Keeping up-to-date on news and news makers in order to suggest potential topics and guests for on-air interviews Updating the station''s Web site and program host biography pages Using scheduling software to update the broadcast schedule Communicating with listeners, especially via e-mail and social media To apply, e-mail a resume and cover letter to hiring@wonderridgeradio.org.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Wonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday\n\n6A.M.-Noon | Noon-4 P.M. | 4 P.M.-7 P.M. | 7 P.M.10 P.M.\n\nCOFFEEBREAK | AFTERNOONJAZZ | FOLKFRENZY | JOSIE''SJOINT\n\nLocal news and | Music from | Folk music | Modern sounds\n\ninterviews with | traditional jazz | from around | selected by our\n\ncommunity | to jazzfusion | the world | station''s own\n\nmembers | music director\n\nHost: | Host: | Host: | Host:\n\nFelice Finney | Malachi Mzee | Penny Ariza | Josie Jones"},{"label"