 functions. This role is an entry-level, part-time position. Responsibilities Conducting background research on interviewees Keeping up-to-date on news and news makers in order to suggest potential topics and guests for on-air interviews Updating the station''s Web site and program host biography pages Using scheduling software to update the broadcast schedule Communicating with listeners, especially via e-mail and social media To apply, e-mail a resume and cover letter to hiring@wonderridgeradio.org.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Wonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday\n\n6A.M.-Noon | Noon-4 P.M. | 4 P.M.-7 P.M. | 7 P.M.10 P.M.\n\nCOFFEEBREAK | AFTERNOONJAZZ | FOLKFRENZY | JOSIE''SJOINT\n\nLocal news and | Music from | Folk music | Modern sounds\n\ninterviews with | traditional jazz | from around | selected by our\n\ncommunity | to jazzfusion | the world | station''s own\n\nmembers | music director\n\nHost: | Host: | Host: | Host:\n\nFelice Finney | Malachi Mzee | Penny Ariza | Josie Jones"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | feedback@wonderridgeradio.org From: | pfabre@sendmail.net Subject: | My new radio station!\n\nDate: | October 22\n\nTothefolksat Wonder Ridge Radio: As I was driving last week, I got tired of listening to sports talk and turned the dial. Suddenly, my car was filled with a song that I hadn''t heard in many years. It was traditional music from France, where my grandmother was born. She used to play that song when I was a child. I never expected to hear it on the radio here in Wonder Ridge. Thanks for this experience and for all your great programs. Your new fan, Pierre Fabre"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"Wonder Ridge Radio Job Opening:Programming Assistant Posted November 2 Job Description The programming assistant reports to the director of programming and supports the radio station by performing a variety of research and communication functions. This role is an entry-level, part-time position. Responsibilities Conducting background research on interviewees Keeping up-to-date on news and news makers in order to suggest potential topics and guests for on-air interviews Updating the station''s Web site and program host biography pages Using scheduling software to update the broadcast schedule Communicating with listeners, especially via e-mail and social media To apply, e-mail a resume and cover letter to hiring@wonderridgeradio.org."}],"question":"What does the job advertisement suggest applicants must have?","bilingual":"Quảng cáo tuyển dụng yêu cầu ứng viên phải có những gì?","options":["A willingness to travel","Familiarity with computers","A degree in communications","Extensive experience in the radio industry"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Familiarity with computers\".","vocabList":[{"word":"advertisement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/æd.vɝːˈtaɪz.mənt/","meaning":"bản tin quảng cáo"},{"word":"communication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəmˌjunəˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"trao đổi thông tin hoặc ý tưởng; chuyển khoản; đi qua"},{"word":"description","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"bản mô tả, sự mô tả"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"}],"optionMeanings":["Sẵn sàng đi du lịch.","Làm quen với máy tính.","Bằng cấp về truyền thông.","Có nhiều kinh nghiệm trong lĩnh vực phát thanh."]},{"questionNum":"190","passageTitle":"Wonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nWonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday\n\n6A.M.-Noon | Noon-4 P.M. | 4 P.M.-7 P.M. | 7 P.M.10 P.M.\n\nCOFFEEBREAK | AFTERNOONJAZZ | FOLKFRENZY | JOSIE''SJOINT\n\nLocal news and | Music from | Folk music | Modern sounds\n\ninterviews with | traditional jazz | from around | selected by our\n\ncommunity | to jazzfusion | the world | station''s own\n\nmembers | music director\n\nHost: | Host: | Host: | Host:\n\nFelice Finney | Malachi Mzee | Penny Ariza | Josie Jones\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | feedback@wonderridgeradio.org From: | pfabre@sendmail.net Subject: | My new radio station!\n\nDate: | October 22\n\nTothefolksat Wonder Ridge Radio: As I was driving last week, I got tired of listening to sports talk and turned the dial. Suddenly, my car was filled with a song that I hadn''t heard in many years. It was traditional music from France, where my grandmother was born. She used to play that song when I was a child. I never expected to hear it on the radio here in Wonder Ridge. Thanks for this experience and for all your great programs. Your new fan, Pierre Fabre\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nWonder Ridge Radio Job Opening:Programming Assistant Posted November 2 Job Description The programming assistant reports to the director of programming and supports the radio station by performing a variety of research and communication functions. This role is an entry-level, part-time position. Responsibilities Conducting background research on interviewees Keeping up-to-date on news and news makers in order to suggest potential topics and guests for on-air interviews Updating the station''s Web site and program host biography pages Using scheduling software to update the broadcast schedule Communicating with listeners, especially via e-mail and social media To apply, e-mail a resume and cover letter to hiring@wonderridgeradio.org.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Wonder Ridge Radio Broadcast Schedule, Monday-Friday\n\n6A.M.-Noon | Noon-4 P.M. | 4 P.M.-7 P.M. | 7 P.M.10 P.M.\n\nCOFFEEBREAK | AFTERNOONJAZZ | FOLKFRENZY | JOSIE''SJOINT\n\nLocal news and | Music from | Folk music | Modern sounds\n\ninterviews with | traditional jazz | from around | selected by our\n\ncommunity | to jazzfusion | the world | station''s own\n\nmembers | music director\n\nHost: | Host: | Host: | Host:\n\nFelice Finney | Malachi Mzee | Penny Ariza | Josie Jones"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | feedback@wonderridgeradio.org From: | pfabre@sendmail.net Subject: | My new radio station!\n\nDate: | October 22\n\nTothefolksat Wonder Ridge Radio: As I was driving last week, I got tired of listening to sports talk and turned the dial. Suddenly, my car was filled with a song that I hadn''t heard in many years. It was traditional music from France, where my grandmother was born. She used to play that song when I was a child. I never expected to hear it on the radio here in Wonder Ridge. Thanks for this experience and for all your great programs. Your new fan, Pierre Fabre"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"Wonder Ridge Radio Job Opening:Programming Assistant Posted November 2 Job Description The programming assistant reports to the director of programming and supports the radio station by performing a variety of research and communication functions. This role is an entry-level, part-time position. Responsibilities Conducting background research on interviewees Keeping up-to-date on news and news makers in order to suggest potential topics and guests for on-air interviews Updating the station''s Web site and program host biography pages Using scheduling software to update the broadcast schedule Communicating with listeners, especially via e-mail and social media To apply, e-mail a resume and cover letter to hiring@wonderridgeradio.org."}],"question":"What radio program will probably receive the most support from the programming assistant?","bilingual":"Chương trình phát thanh nào có thể sẽ nhận được sự hỗ trợ nhiều nhất từ ​​trợ lý lập trình?","options":["Coffee Break","Afternoon Jazz","Folk Frenzy","Josie''s Joint"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Coffee Break\".","vocabList":[{"word":"communication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəmˌjunəˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"trao đổi thông tin hoặc ý tưởng; chuyển khoản; đi qua"},{"word":"description","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"bản mô tả, sự mô tả"},{"word":"interviews","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɪntərvˌjuz/","meaning":"phỏng vấn"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"}],"optionMeanings":["Nghỉ giải lao","Afternoon Jazz","Folk Frenzy","Josie''s Joint"]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nInstructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nCity of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"City of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103"}],"question":"What do the instructions indicate about records requests?","bilingual":"Hướng dẫn chỉ ra điều gì về yêu cầu bản ghi?","options":["They can be made only on certain days.","They can be made only online.","They can be filed only by authorized personnel.","They can be filed only after a fee is paid."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"They can be made only online.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"environmental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.t̬əl/","meaning":"(thuộc) môi trường"},{"word":"confirmation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌkɑːn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự xác nhận, chứng thực"},{"word":"instruction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"giảng dạy; phương hướng; hướng dẫn; đào tạo; giáo dục;"}],"optionMeanings":["Chúng chỉ có thể được thực hiện vào một số ngày nhất định.","Chúng chỉ có thể được thực hiện trực tuyến.","Chỉ những người có thẩm quyền mới có thể lưu trữ chúng.","Chúng chỉ có thể được nộp sau khi đã trả phí."]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nInstructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nCity of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"City of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103"}],"question":"According to the e-mail, how does Mr. Brandenberg plan to use some public information?","bilingual":"Theo e - qua thư, ông Brandenberg dự định sử dụng một số thông tin công khai như thế nào?","options":["To add information to a Web portal","To help his company advise the city","To identify an accounting error","To learn how an agency is structured"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To help his company advise the city\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"environmental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.t̬əl/","meaning":"(thuộc) môi trường"},{"word":"confirmation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌkɑːn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự xác nhận, chứng thực"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"}],"optionMeanings":["Để thêm thông tin vào cổng Web","Để giúp công ty của anh ấy tư vấn cho thành phố","Để xác định lỗi kế toán","Để tìm hiểu cách cấu trúc của một cơ quan"]},{"questionNum":"193","passageTitle":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nInstructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nCity of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"City of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103"}],"question":"What does the sign indicate visitors must do before entering a building?","bilingual":"Biển báo cho biết du khách phải làm gì trước khi vào tòa nhà?","options":["Go through a security screening","Get a parking permit","Present some identification","Sign a log book"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Sign a log book\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"environmental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.t̬əl/","meaning":"(thuộc) môi trường"},{"word":"confirmation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌkɑːn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự xác nhận, chứng thực"},{"word":"instruction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"giảng dạy; phương hướng; hướng dẫn; đào tạo; giáo dục;"}],"optionMeanings":["Trải qua quá trình kiểm tra bảo mật.","Nhận giấy phép đậu xe.","Trình bày một số thông tin nhận dạng.","Ký vào nhật ký."]},{"questionNum":"194","passageTitle":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nInstructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nCity of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"City of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103"}],"question":"What was Mr.Brandenberg expecting to receive?","bilingual":"Ông Brandenberg mong đợi nhận được gì?","options":["An itemized statement of fees","A letter from his company","A phone call from a city official","A password for the Webportal"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"An itemized statement of fees\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"environmental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.t̬əl/","meaning":"(thuộc) môi trường"},{"word":"confirmation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌkɑːn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự xác nhận, chứng thực"},{"word":"instruction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"giảng dạy; phương hướng; hướng dẫn; đào tạo; giáo dục;"}],"optionMeanings":["Bảng kê chi phí được chia thành từng khoản.","Một lá thư từ công ty của anh ấy.","Một cuộc điện thoại từ một quan chức thành phố.","Mật khẩu cho cổng Web."]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nInstructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nCity of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Instructions for Requesting Records Thank you for your interest in official records and documents maintained by the City of Abilene. To file a request for public information, please follow these steps. 1.Create an account in the Records Center Web portal. Currently, all requests must be made through the portal. 2. Use the drop-down menu to locate the department from which you are seeking information and submit your request. You will receive a confirmation e-mail with a reference number. 3. The department staff will locate the requested records and contact you when they are available. You can have the records delivered to you, or you can pick them up in person. If you prefer to pick them up in person, you must make an appointment with the department staff. 4. If there are any fees associated with your request, you will receive an itemized statement detailing the services provided and the charges for those specific services.\n\nE-Mail Message"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Joo-Hee Park <jhpark@coa.net> From: | Keith Brandenberg <kbrandenberg@mailcurrent.com> Date: | May 3\n\nSubject: | RE:ReferencenumberW2486\n\nDear Ms. Park, Thank you for confirming that my documents are available.I would like to pick them up in person as soon as possible. Do you have any appointments available this week? I have a question about the fee. Apparently, I am being charged $300 for my documents.I do not understand why the fee is so high, and there was no explanation included in your e-mail. I have requested records several times in the past in my role with RJ Environmental Engineering and have never paid such a high fee. In this case, I am only requesting two maps of the city''s underground pipelines, which will inform our firm''s current work advising the city on wastewatermanagcmcnt. Please clarify the fee for me, and let me know if I can pick up my documents this week. Thank you. Best regards, Keith Brandenberg"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"City of Abilene Administrative Building\n\nVisitors must sign in prior to entering this facility. Please enter your name and the room you will visit in the log book.\n\nFirst-Floor Directory: IT Services-R00m 100 Parks and Recreation-Room101 Transportation-Room102 Wastewater-R00m103"}],"question":"What room will Mr.Brandenberg most likely visit?","bilingual":"Ông Brandenberg sẽ ghé thăm phòng nào nhiều nhất?","options":["R00m 100","Room 101","R00m 102","R00m 103"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"R00m 103\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"environmental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.t̬əl/","meaning":"(thuộc) môi trường"},{"word":"confirmation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌkɑːn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự xác nhận, chứng thực"},{"word":"instruction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"giảng dạy; phương hướng; hướng dẫn; đào tạo; giáo dục;"}],"optionMeanings":["Phòng 100","Phòng 101","Phòng 102","Phòng 103 (C) Phòng 102(D) Phòng 103 Từ vựng: - thả - down (a): kéo thảnh thơi - Portal (n): cồng thông tin - nước thải (n): nước thải - logbook (n): nhật kýDiễn viên nổi tiếng, Cuốn sách đầu tiênLONDON (25 tháng 2) -- Những người hâm mộ Simon Eklund sẽrất vui mừng với cuốn tự truyện của anhấy, The Theater Lights Dimmed, cuốn sách đầutiên anhấy viết trong hiệp sĩ diễn viên lừng lẫy của mình. Nó cung cấp cáinhìn sắc đẹp sâu sắc tuyệt vời vềsự sáng tác của anhấy, bắt đầu với những vai diễn đầu tiên trongđiện ảnhởquê hương Thụy Điển, chuyển sang tác sản phẩm của anhấyởPháp và Ý, và kết thúc với sản phẩm sân khấu gần đây của anhấyởVương quốc Anh. Trong cuốn sách của mình, ông Eklund dành khá nhiều nội dung để thảo luận về người cốvấn của mình, Charles Gunnarsson, người đã giúp phát triển các kỹ năng của mình từrất sớmStockholm. Anh cũng mô tả về sự khó khăn khi hóa thân thành nhiều loại vai khác nhau, đặc biệt là từhài kịch sang chínhkịch. Anh thấy bao gồm một sốgiai trò chuyện hài hước về những điều khó khăn Năng lực đầu tiên của anh đạt được khi biểu diễn trên sân khấu ở London. Anh thấy mô tả họ là thảm họa, nhưng bất kỳ ai xem màn hình diễn đàn gần đây của anh thấy trong Life andGames sẽ nói ngược lại. Ông Eklund từlâu đã là một thành viên thu hút trên sân khấu và màn ảnh, và giờ đây là một tác giả hoàn toàn thú vị. --- Uma Joshi Đến: Edith HockingTừ: Uma JoshiNgày: 2 tháng 3 Chủ đề: Phản hồi: Cơ hộiEdith thân mến, Cảm ơn bạn đã đồng ý sắp xếp một cuộc phỏng vấn với Eklund cho tôi. Tôi nghĩ đây sẽ là phần tiếp theo tuyệt vời cho các sản phẩm gần đây của tôi. Trong một sự kiện hợp hữu hữu, tôi sẽ đến thăm quê hương của anh lấy vào tháng để phát biểu tại một cuộc bầu cử của các nhà báo. Tôi là diễn đàn đơn giảnbật và sẽ thảo luận vềlợi ích của đa dạng trong báo chí. Tôi chắc chắn rằng chúng tôi có thểsắp xếp điều gì đó với Eklund ngay trước hoặc sau bài phát biểu của tôi. Tốt nhất, Uma JoshiBiên viên Văn hóa Nghệthuật Tin tức hàng đầu Vương quốc Anh *Thư điện tử* ĐẾN: Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> Từ: Maria Cazalla <mcazalla@zephyrmail.se>Ngày: 20 tháng baChủ đề: Phản hồi: Thông tinCô Joshi thân mến, Tất cả chúng tôi đều rất vui mừng về cuộc trò chuyện của bạn vào tháng tới với Eklund. Anh thích tất cả các bài viết của bạn cho Top News U.K. -các câu chuyện thời sự, các cuộc phỏng vấn, và tất nhiên, bài viết gần đây của bạn vềThe Theater Lights Dimmed! Tôi chỉ muốn hoàn thiện một vài chi tiết với bạn. Chúng tôi đã sắp xếp phương tiện di chuyển cho bạn từ khách sạn của bạn đến nhà của ôngEklund và sau đó quay trở lạilại khách sạn. Vui lòng cho tôi biết sẽ có bao nhiêu người trong nhóm của bạn, vì Eklund muốn tất cả các bạn mở văn dài. Trân trọng, Maria Cazalla196. Bài đánh giá đề cập đến điều gì về ông Eklund?(A) Ông ấy thích công việc giám đốc của mình. (B) Anh ấy là người cố vấn cho nhiều người trẻ. (C) Anh ấy là một người giỏi - diễn viên nổi tiếng. (D) Anh ấy đã viết nhiều sách."]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Famous Actor, First Book","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFamous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Famous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla"}],"question":"What does the review mention about Mr.Eklund?","bilingual":"","options":["He enjoys his work as a director.","He has been a mentor to many young people.","He is a well-known actor.","He has written many books."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"He is a well-known actor.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"performance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pə''fɔ:məns/","meaning":"sự biểu diễn, việc đóng (phim, kịch...); cuộc"},{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"}]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"Famous Actor, First Book","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFamous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Famous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla"}],"question":"Where most likely will Ms, Joshi meet Mr.Eklund?","bilingual":"Có nhiều khả năng cô Joshi sẽ gặp ông Eklund ở đâu?","options":["In Sweden","In France","In Italy","In the United Kingdom"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"In Sweden\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"performance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pə''fɔ:məns/","meaning":"sự biểu diễn, việc đóng (phim, kịch...); cuộc"},{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"}],"optionMeanings":["Ở Thụy Điển","Ở Pháp","Tại Ý","Tại Vương quốc Anh"]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"Famous Actor, First Book","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFamous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Famous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla"}],"question":"According to the first e-mail, what is one reason Ms. Joshi will travel in April?","bilingual":"Theo e đầu tiên - thư, lý do cô Joshi sẽ đi du lịch vào tháng 4 là gì?","options":["To go on a vacation","To interview for a new job","To attend an international film festival","To speak ata conference Stop! This is the end of the test. If you finish before time is called, you may go back to Parts 5, 6, and7and check your work."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To speak ata conference Stop! This is the end of the test. If you finish before time is called, you may go back to Parts 5, 6, and7and check your work.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"international","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.t̬ɚˈnæʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"quốc tế, đa quốc gia"},{"word":"performance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pə''fɔ:məns/","meaning":"sự biểu diễn, việc đóng (phim, kịch...); cuộc"},{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"}],"optionMeanings":["Để đi nghỉ","Để phỏng vấn xin việc mới","Để tham dự một liên hoan phim quốc tế","Phát biểu tại một hội nghị"]},{"questionNum":"199","passageTitle":"Famous Actor, First Book","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFamous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Famous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla"}],"question":"What is the purpose of the second e-mail?","bilingual":"Mục đích của e thứ hai là gì - thư à?","options":["To reserve a hotel room","To confirm meeting arrangements","To discuss an idea for a movie","To ask for transportation"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To confirm meeting arrangements\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"arrangement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈreɪndʒ.mənt/","meaning":"sự sắp đặt"},{"word":"performance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pə''fɔ:məns/","meaning":"sự biểu diễn, việc đóng (phim, kịch...); cuộc"},{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"}],"optionMeanings":["Để đặt phòng khách sạn","Để xác nhận sắp xếp cuộc họp","Để thảo luận về ý tưởng cho một bộ phim","Để xin phương tiện đi lại"]},{"questionNum":"200","passageTitle":"Famous Actor, First Book","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFamous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Famous Actor, First Book\n\nLONDON (25 February)Fans of Simon Eklund will be delighted with his auto biography, The Theatre Lights Dimmed, the first book he has written in his storied career as an actor. It provides wonderful insight into his career, starting with his first roles in cinema in his native Sweden, moving into his work in France and Italy, and finishing with his recent theatre work in the U.K. In his book, Mr.Eklund dedicates a fair amount of text to discussing his mentor, Charles Gunnarsson, who helped him develop his skills early on in Stockholm. He also describes the difficulty of transitioning into different types of roles, especially from comedic to dramatic acting. He includes several funny anecdotes about his first attempts at acting on stage here in London. He describes them as disastrous, but anyone who saw his recent performance in Life and Games would say just the opposite. Mr. Eklund has long been a captivating actor on stage and screen, and now he is a thoroughly engaging author. Uma Joshi"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Edith Hocking\n\nFrom: | Uma Joshi\n\nDate: | 2 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Opportunity\n\nDear Edith,\n\nThank you for agreeing to arrange an interview with Mr. Eklund for me. I think this will be a great follow-up to my recent piece.\n\nIn a helpful coincidence, I will be visiting his home country next month to address a journalists'' convention.I am the featured speaker and will discuss the benefits of diversity in journalism.I''m sure we can set up something with Mr.Eklund just before or after my speech.\n\nBest,\n\nUma Joshi Arts and Culture Editor Top News U.K."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Uma Joshi <ujoshi@topnews.co.uk> From: | Maria Cazalla < mcazalla@zephyrmail.se Date: | 20 March\n\nSubject: | RE:Information\n\nDear Ms. Joshi,\n\nWe are all very excited about your interview next month with Mr.Eklund. He enjoys all your writing for Top News U.K.-the news stories, interviews, and, of course, your recent article about The Theatre Lights Dimmed!\n\nI just wanted to finalize a few details with you. We have arranged transportation for you from your hotel to Mr.Eklund''s house and then back to the hotel. Please let me know how many people there will be in your group, because Mr.Eklund would like you all to stay for lunch.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMaria Cazalla"}],"question":"200.What can be concluded about Mr.Eklund?","bilingual":"Có thể kết luận gì về ông Eklund?","options":["He hopes to write for a Britishnews site.","He just hired a new assistant.","He was pleased with Ms.Joshi''s review of his book.","He frequently cooks special meals."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"He was pleased with Ms.Joshi''s review of his book.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"performance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pə''fɔ:məns/","meaning":"sự biểu diễn, việc đóng (phim, kịch...); cuộc"},{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"}],"optionMeanings":["Anh ấy hy vọng sẽ viết cho một trang tin tức của Anh.","Anh ấy vừa thuê một trợ lý mới.","Anh ấy hài lòng với bài đánh giá của cô Joshi về cuốn sách của anh ấy.","Anh ấy thường xuyên nấu những bữa ăn đặc biệt."]}]'::jsonb,
