d it the next time I need it.\n\nJoanne Matos(12:04P.M.) No problem. Thanks!"}],"question":"At12:04p.M.,what does Ms.Matosmost likely mean when she writes,\"No problem\"?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 12:04 chiều, rất có thể cô Matos có ý gì khi viết, \"Không vấn đề gì”?","options":["She will probably be finished soon.","She will meet Mr.Thomas at the entrance.","She will return an item to its original location.","She understands Ms. Nguyen''s explanation."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She will return an item to its original location.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"understand","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈstænd/","meaning":"hiểu, nắm bắt được"},{"word":"advertise","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈæd.vɚ.taɪz/","meaning":"quảng cáo, thông báo"},{"word":"probably","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/´prɔbəbli/","meaning":"có khả năng, có lẽ, có thể"}],"optionMeanings":["Chắc cô ấy sẽ sớm xong thôi.","Cô ấy sẽ gặp ông Thomas ở lối vào.","Cô ấy sẽ trả một vật phẩm về vị trí ban đầu.","Cô hiểu lời giải thích của cô Nguyễn."]},{"questionNum":"176","passageTitle":"Central Art Museum","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nCentral Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nReview of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Central Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Review of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100"}],"question":"According to the schedule, what would a visitor most likely see at the first special exhibit?","bilingual":"Theo lịch trình, du khách có thể sẽ thấy gì ở buổi triển lãm đặc biệt đầu tiên?","options":["Shoes","Furniture","Radios","Paintings"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Shoes\".","vocabList":[{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"collection","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","meaning":"lựa chọn; sự lựa chọn; phân loại; sự tích lũy"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dướ