. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Central Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Review of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100"}],"question":"What is indicated about the special exhibit in February?","bilingual":"Triển lãm đặc biệt tháng 2 nói lên điều gì?","options":["It includes mostly paintings done by local artists.","It will end before the other exhibits listed on the Web site.","Visitors may see items similar to those that they have in their homes.","It has returned to the museum after a popular earlier appearance."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Visitors may see items similar to those that they have in their homes.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"appearance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈpɪrəns/","meaning":"ấn tượng; cách một người nhìn; hình ảnh; vẻ bề ngoài"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"collection","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","meaning":"lựa chọn; sự lựa chọn; phân loại; sự tích lũy"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"}],"optionMeanings":["Nó bao gồm hầu hết các bức tranh được thực hiện bởi các nghệ sĩ địa phương.","Nó sẽ kết thúc trước các phần trưng bày khác được liệt kê trên trang Web.","Khách tham quan có thể thấy những món đồ tương tự như những món đồ họ có trong nhà.","Nó đã quay trở lại bảo tàng sau lần xuất hiện phổ biến trước đó."]},{"questionNum":"178","passageTitle":"Central Art Museum","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nCentral Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nReview of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Central Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Review of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100"}],"question":"Why did Ms.Walsh go to the museum a second time?","bilingual":"Tại sao cô Walsh lại đến bảo tàng lần thứ hai?","options":["She wanted to take more photographs.","She wanted to see more of the museum.","She accidentally left an item at the museum.","She got a discount on a ticket."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"She wanted to see more of the museum.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"photographs","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfoʊtəˌgræfs/","meaning":"Ảnh"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"collection","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","meaning":"lựa chọn; sự lựa chọn; phân loại; sự tích lũy"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy muốn chụp nhiều ảnh hơn.","Cô ấy muốn xem thêm về bảo tàng.","Cô ấy vô tình để quên một món đồ ở bảo tàng.","Cô ấy đã được giảm giá vé."]},{"questionNum":"179","passageTitle":"Central Art Museum","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nCentral Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nReview of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Central Art Museum\n\nUpcoming Special Exhibits\n\nWorldwide Fashion November 1-28 Discover how clothing and accessories have changed throughout time in various parts of the world. See clothing samples, historical items, and sketches.\n\nJeffrey Lamb:Naturalist December 1-29 Scientist Jeffrey Lamb spent his life studying and taking pictures of wildlife on six continents. See photos of animals and landscapes from the researcher''s personal collection, taken during his forty-year career.\n\nHumans in Art January 1-29 This collection of paintings and sculptures from dozens of artists, past and present, shows us the many ways artists can depict a human subject. Works from both famous and relatively unknown artists are included here.\n\nEveryday Art February 1-26 A variety of handmade items are on display in this exhibit showing art in everyday life. From handmade quilts to furniture, see these household items in a whole new way."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Review of Central Art Museum Reviewer:Mary Walsh Stars:★★★★★ I recommend the Central Art Museum to anyone interested in not only art but history as well.I''ve made two trips to the museum recently. My first trip was with my school''s photography club. We only saw the special exhibit featuring photography, but I left wanting to see the rest of the museum. Ireturned a few days later and had the chance to walk through the entire museum. Each exhibit was different but full of interesting pieces, Be sure to stop at the interactive room near the gift shop for a hands-on experience. During my first trip, the room had cameras with fun backgrounds. Visitors took pictures of themselves, and for a small fee, Igot a printout of myself as if I were holding a flag on the moon! Like the special exhibits, the activities at the interactive room change every month, so you will always find something new and interesting to do.\n\n100"}],"question":"What does Ms.Walsh recommend that readers do?","bilingual":"Bà Walsh khuyên độc giả nên làm gì?","options":["Take a guided tour of the museum","Call the museum for more information","Buy something at the museum gift shop","Participate in an activity at the museum"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Participate in an activity at the museum\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"participate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pɑrˈtɪsəˌpeɪt/","meaning":"được tham gia; tham gia vào"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"collection","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","meaning":"lựa chọn; sự lựa chọn; phân loại; sự tích lũy"}],"optionMeanings":["Tham gia chuyến tham quan có hướng dẫn viên trong bảo tàng","Gọi cho bảo tàng để biết thêm thông tin","Mua thứ gì đó tại cửa hàng quà tặng bảo tàng","Tham 