ook a table should act fast. Some restaurants require reservations, and the most popular places book up quickly. To see the list of participating restaurants and make a reservation, visit www.alexandriarestaurants.com/showcase."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.alexandriarestaurants.com/showcase/reservations Showing search results for:Center City Neighborhood Claire''s Frenchfood Serving lunchand3-course dinner Open Tuesday-Sunday Call (703)555-0102tomakeareservation.\n\nFresh Fish Grill Seafood Serving lunchand3-course dinner Open Monday-Sunday Call (703)555-0195 to make a reservation.\n\nJin-Yi''s House Koreanfood Serving2-course dinner Open Wednesday-Saturday Call (703)555-0198tomakeareservation.\n\nRoberto''s Pizzeria"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"Italian food Serving lunch only Open Tuesday-Sunday No reservations necessary\n\n104 https://www.foodreviews.com/alexandria/freshfishgrill Nori Sato I highly recommend Fresh Fish Grill. It was my first time eating there, and not only was the food excellent, but the staff was welcoming and efficient. I had some clients in town and was lucky enough to get a reservation on the last day of the restaurant showcase. We all really enjoyed the experience.I would gladly take clients there again."}],"question":"190. What is suggested about Ms. Sato?","bilingual":"Những gì được đề xuất về Ms. Sato?","options":["ShewenttoFreshFishGrillonJuly25","She went to Fresh Fish Grill with her family.","She has dined at the Fresh Fish Grill many times.","She knows the owner of Fresh Fish Grill."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"ShewenttoFreshFishGrillonJuly25\".","vocabList":[{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"},{"word":"participate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pɑrˈtɪsəˌpeɪt/","meaning":"được tham gia; tham gia vào"},{"word":"restaurants","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrɛˌstrɑnts/","meaning":"Nhà hàng"},{"word":"reservation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌrez.ɚˈveɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"dự phòng"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy đã đến Fresh Fish Grill vào tháng 7","Côấy đã đến Fresh Fish Grill với gia đình 25.(B) Cô ấy đến quán Fresh Fish Grill cùng gia đình.","Cô đã ăn tối tại Fresh Fish Grill nhiều lần.","Cô ấy biết chủ quán Fresh FishGrill. đình. (C) Cô ấy đã ăn tối tốiCá tươi nướng nhiều lần. (D) Biết chủ sở hữu của Fresh Fish Grill. VOCAB: - người đam mê (n): người say mê, người có nhiệt tình - mở rộng (v) = mở rộng = mở rộng: mởmở rộng, kéo dài - booking (n): đặt chỗ trước Điều khiển viên Hoạt động sinh viên Đại học RollervyMaynard, MA 01754 nhiệm vụ: ● Thúc đẩy sự kiện tham gia vào các hoạt động ngoại khóa trong các trường dữ liệu như hội đồng sinh viên, nghệ thuật, sân khấu, các tổ chức văn hóa, các nhóm tình nguyện và các cấp độ câu lạc bộ thể thao ● Cập nhật trang web hoạt động của sinh viên Đại học Rollervy và quản lý tất cả các phương tiện truyền thông xã hộitôi ● Điều phối các chuyến đi của si nh viên tới các sự kiện văn hóa và thểthao tác địa phương trong khu vực đô thịBoston ● giải quyết các thắc mắc bằng cách trả lời điện thoại, trả lờilời e - mail vàchào đón khách đến thăm để đăng ký, hãy viết thư xin việc của bạn trong e -mail, đính kèm sơ yếu lý lịch của bạn và gửi cho Giám đốc Nhân sự, tại jobs@rollervy.edu. Vui lòng giải quyết như sau: ● Bạn có kinh nghiệm làm việc liên quan gì? ● Tại sao bạn tin rằng bạn phù hợp với vị trí này? ● Thếmạnh nghề nghiệp của bạn là gì? ● Bạn có thể cải thiện các lĩnh vực nào? Đến: Việc làm <jobs@rollervy.edu> Từ:Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com>Ngày: Ngày 10 tháng 9 Chủ đề: Điều phối hoạt động Sinh viênTập tin đính kèm: Bản tóm tắtGửi đến những người có thể quan tâm, Đại học Rollervy đang tìm người điều phối các hoạt động, hoàn đẩy sựtham gia của sinh viên và cung cấp dịch vụ khách hàng chuyên nghiệp. Tôi đã làm cả ba công việc này trong nhiệm kỳ của mình với tư cách là Giám đốc Giải trí trong trường học Cao đẳng Parvaton. Tại Parvaton, tôi đã tăngtỷ lệ tham gia vào các hoạt động của sinh viên lên 37 phần trăm. Tôi cũng thành lập một câu lạc bộ chạy bộ và lên kếhoạch cho những chuyến du lịch ngoài sân khách. Tôi rất chú ý đến hoạt động tình nguyện, bao gồm các dự án kết hợp các đại sư học với các học sinh trung học địa phương cần giúp đỡlàm bài tập trên lớp. Nhìn chung, tôi tin rằng mình rất phù hợp với vị trí hiện có. Tôi đúng giờ, định hướng chi tiết và cam kết tăng cường kết nối của sinh viên với tổ chức học thuật của họ. Tôi mong muốn được nghe lại về một cuộc phỏng vấn tiềm năng. Trân trọng, Samantha Bradbury *Thư điện tử* Đến: Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Từ: Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu>Ngày: ngày 2 tháng 10 Chủ đề: Thủ vấnSamantha thân mến, Tôi viết thư này để kiểm tra xem bạn có sẵn sàng phỏng vấn cho vị trí Điều phối hoạt động Sinh viên hay không. Cuộc phỏng vấn sơ bộ của bạn sẽ được thực hiện. Nếu được chọn vào vòng tiếp theo, cuộc phỏng vấn của bạn sẽ diễn ra trực tiếp tại địa chỉ người dùng chính của Đại học Rollervy. Nếu bạn vẫn quan tâm, vui lòng phản hồi và cho tôi biết nếu bạn rảnh vào lúc 9 giờ sáng ngày 8 hoặc 9 tháng 10. Trân trọng, Lisa Cooper"]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Respon","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nStudent Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper"}],"question":"According to the job advertisement, what is one responsibility of the Student Activities Coordinator?","bilingual":"Theo quảng cáo tuyển dụng, trách nhiệm của Điều phối viên Hoạt động Sinh viên là gì?","options":["Help students with difficult assignments","Inform students about local events","Train students to give presentations","Lead workshops about Web site development"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Inform students about local events\".","vocabList":[{"word":"responsibility","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/rɪˌspɑːn.səˈbɪl.ə.t̬i/","meaning":"trách nhiệm; sự chịu trách nhiệm; bổn phận;"},{"word":"advertisement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/æd.vɝːˈtaɪz.mənt/","meaning":"bản tin quảng cáo"},{"word":"presentations","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌprɛzənˈteɪʃənz/","meaning":"Bài thuyết trình"},{"word":"organization","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,ɔ:gənai''zeiʃn/","meaning":"sự tổ chức, sự cấu tạo"}],"optionMeanings":["Giúp học sinh làm những bài tập khó","Thông báo cho sinh viên về các sự kiện địa phương","Đào tạo học viên cách thuyết trình","Dẫn dắt các buổi hội thảo về phát triển trang Web"]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Respon","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nStudent Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper"}],"question":"According to the first e-mail, what is one way that Ms.Bradbury promoted student engagement?","bilingual":"Theo e đầu tiên - thư, Một cách mà cô Bradbury thúc đẩy sự tham gia của sinh viên là gì?","options":["She volunteered at a local recreation center.","She participated in several cultural excursions.","She recruited high school students to be tutors.","She started a sports group."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"She started a sports group.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"organization","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,ɔ:gənai''zeiʃn/","meaning":"sự tổ chức, sự cấu tạo"},{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"participate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pɑrˈtɪsəˌpeɪt/","meaning":"được tham gia; tham gia vào"},{"word":"government","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈgəvərnmənt/","meaning":"cai trị một quốc gia hoặc khu vực; kiểm soát chính trị; thẩm quyền"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy tình nguyện làm việc tại một trung tâm giải trí địa phương.","Cô ấy đã tham gia một số chuyến du ngoạn văn hóa.","Cô tuyển học sinh cấp 3 làm gia sư.","Cô ấy thành lập một nhóm thể thao."]},{"questionNum":"193","passageTitle":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Respon","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nStudent Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper"}],"question":"What information did Ms.Bradbury leave out of her cover letter?","bilingual":"Bà Bradbury đã bỏ sót thông tin gì trong thư xin việc?","options":["Her relevant job experience","Her interest in the position","Her professional strengths","Her areas for improvement"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Her areas for improvement\".","vocabList":[{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"organization","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,ɔ:gənai''zeiʃn/","meaning":"sự tổ chức, sự cấu tạo"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"improvement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪmˈpruːv.mənt/","meaning":"sự cải thiện, cải tiến"}],"optionMeanings":["Kinh nghiệm làm việc liên quan của cô ấy","Sự quan tâm của cô ấy đối với vị trí","Điểm mạnh chuyên môn của cô ấy","Những lĩnh vực mà cô ấy cần cải thiện (C) Điểm mạnh nghề nghiệp của cô (D) Các lĩnh vực cần được cải thiện"]},{"questionNum":"194","passageTitle":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Respon","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nStudent Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropo