ou are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper"}],"question":"What does these conde-mail indicate about the hiring process?","bilingual":"e thứ hai làm gì - gửi thư cho biết về quá trình tuyển dụng?","options":["Every applicant must fill in a form online.","Applicants should submit two reference letters.","Some applicants will have an in-person interview.","Applicants with four-year degrees are preferred."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Some applicants will have an in-person interview.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"organization","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,ɔ:gənai''zeiʃn/","meaning":"sự tổ chức, sự cấu tạo"},{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"government","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈgəvərnmənt/","meaning":"cai trị một quốc gia hoặc khu vực; kiểm soát chính trị; thẩm quyền"},{"word":"coordinate","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/koʊˈɔrdəˌneɪt/","meaning":"bình đẳng; tương đương; có cấp bậc hoặc quyền hạn ngang nhau"}],"optionMeanings":["Mỗi ứng viên đều phải điền vào một mẫu đơn.","Ứng viên nên nộp hai thư giới thiệu.","Một số ứng viên sẽ có địa chỉ -cuộc phỏng vấn người.","Ứng viên có bốn - bằng cấp năm được ưu tiên."]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Respon","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nStudent Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Student Activities Coordinator Rollervy University Maynard, MA 01754 Responsibilities: ·Promotes involvement in campus extracurricular activities such as student government, arts, theater, cultural organizations, volunteer groups, and athletic club teams. Updates the Rollervy University student activities Web site and manages all social media.Coordinates student outings to local sporting and cultural events in the Boston metropolitan area • Addresses inquiries by answering phones, responding to e-mails, and greeting walk-in visitors To apply, write your cover letter in an e-mail, attach your resume, and send it to the Human Resources Manager, at jobs@rollervy.edu. Please address the following:.What relevant job experience do you have?. Why do you believe you are a good fit for the position?.What are your professional strengths?.In which areas could you improve?"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Jobs <jobs@rollervy.edu> From: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Date: | September 10\n\nSubject: | Student Activities Coordinator\n\nAttachment: | Résume\n\nTo Whom It May Concern, Rollervy University is looking for someone to coordinate activities, promote student engagement, and provide professional customer service.I did all three during my tenure as the Campus Recreation Manager at Parvaton College. At Parvaton, I increased participation in student activities by 37 percent. I also created a running club and planned excursions off campus. Iplaced a great emphasis on volunteering, including a project to pair college tutors with local high school students who needed help with class work. Overall, I believe I''m an excellent fit for the available position. I am punctual, detail oriented, and committed to increasing students'' connection to their academic institution, I look forward to hearing back about a potential interview. Sincerely, Samantha Bradbury\n\n106"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Samantha Bradbury <sambradbury25@rapidonet.com> Lisa Cooper <jobs@rollervy.edu> Date: | October 2\n\nSubject: | Interview\n\nDear Samantha, I am writing to check on your availability to interview for the Student Activities Coordinator position. Your preliminary interview would be conducted virtually. If selected for the next round, your second interview would be in person at the Rollervy University main campus. If you are still interested, please respond and let me know if you are free at 9 A.M. on either October 8 or October 9. Kind regards, Lisa Cooper"}],"question":"Who most likely is Ms.Cooper?","bilingual":"Cô Cooper có nhiều khả năng là ai nhất?","options":["The Human Resources Manager","An office assistant","A university admissions counselor","The Student Activities Coordinator"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"The Human Resources Manager\".","vocabList":[{"word":"organization","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,ɔ:gənai''zeiʃn/","meaning":"sự tổ chức, sự cấu tạo"},{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"government","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈgəvərnmənt/","meaning":"cai trị một quốc gia hoặc khu vực; kiểm soát chính trị; thẩm quyền"},{"word":"coordinate","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/koʊˈɔrdəˌneɪt/","meaning":"bình đẳng; tương đương; có cấp bậc hoặc quyền hạn ngang nhau"}],"optionMeanings":["Giám đốc nhân sự","Một trợ lý văn phòng","Nhân viên tư vấn tuyển sinh đại học","Điều phối viên hoạt động sinh viên"]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"To: | Celeste O''Brien","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nLocation: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Location: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only."}],"question":"What is the purpose of the e-mail?","bilingual":"Mục đích của khóa học là gì -thư?","options":["To describe patterns of employee behavior","To suggest updates to certain technology","To consider replacing a vendor","To request a revision to a reimbursement policy"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To request a revision to a reimbursement policy\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"appropriate","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈproʊpriˌeɪt/","meaning":"thích hợp; lắp"},{"word":"technology","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/tɛkˈnɑləʤi/","meaning":"khoa học nghệ thuật công nghiệp; khoa học ứng dụng"},{"word":"accounting","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈkaʊn.t̬ɪŋ/","meaning":"sự tính toán, thanh toán"}],"optionMeanings":["Để mô tả các kiểu hành vi của nhân viên.","Để đề xuất cập nhật cho công nghệ nhất định.","Để xem xét việc thay thế một nhà cung cấp.","Để yêu cầu sửa đổi chính sách hoàn trả."]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"To: | Celeste O''Brien","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nLocation: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Location: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only."}],"question":"According to the e-mail, who is Ms. Cheung?","bilingual":"Theo e - thư, cô là ai? Trương?","options":["A telemarketer","A member of the accounting team","Ahuman resources specialist","An electronics engineer"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"A member of the accounting team\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"electronics","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪˌlɛkˈtrɑnɪks/","meaning":"Điện tử"},{"word":"appropriate","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈproʊpriˌeɪt/","meaning":"thích hợp; lắp"},{"word":"accounting","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈkaʊn.t̬ɪŋ/","meaning":"sự tính toán, thanh toán"}],"optionMeanings":["Một người tiếp thị qua điện thoại.","Là thành viên của nhóm kế toán.","Chuyên gia nhân sự.","Một kỹ sư điện tử."]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"To: | Celeste O''Brien","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nLocation: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Location: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only."}],"question":"What did Ms. O''Brien do after receiving Ms. Cheung''s e-mail?","bilingual":"Cô O’Brien đã làm gì sau khi nhận được email của cô Cheung - thư à?","options":["She invited Ms. Cheung to a meeting.","She rejected Ms. Cheung''s suggestion but proposed alternatives.","She collaborated with other company leaders to address an issue.","She transferred to a different department. Stop! This is the end of the test. If you finish before time is called, you may go back to Parts 5, 6,and7and check your work."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She collaborated with other company leaders to address an issue.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"alternative","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɑːlˈtɝː.nə.t̬ɪv/","meaning":"xen kẽ, luân phiên"},{"word":"appropriate","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈproʊpriˌeɪt/","meaning":"thích hợp; lắp"},{"word":"suggestion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈdʒes.tʃən/","meaning":"sự đề xuất"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy đã mời cô Cheung đi họp.","Cô ấy từ chối lời đề nghị của cô Cheung nhưng đề xuất các giải pháp thay thế.","Cô cộng tác với các lãnh đạo công ty khác để giải quyết một vấn đề.","Cô ấy đã chuyển sang bộ phận khác."]},{"questionNum":"199","passageTitle":"To: | Celeste O''Brien","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nLocation: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Location: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only."}],"question":"According to the policy, who qualifies to receive a company mobile phone?","bilingual":"Theo chính sách, ai đủ điều kiện nhận điện thoại di động của công ty?","options":["Ferd Data Services managers and executives only","All Ferd Data Services employees who work from home","Employees who travel for business purposes","Employees who submit a monthly form"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Ferd Data Services managers and executives only\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"appropriate","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈproʊpriˌeɪt/","meaning":"thích hợp; lắp"},{"word":"accounting","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈkaʊn.t̬ɪŋ/","meaning":"sự tính toán, thanh toán"},{"word":"department","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈpɑːrt.mənt/","meaning":"khoa, bộ"}],"optionMeanings":["Các nhà quản lý Dịch vụ Dữ liệu Ferd và","Tất cả nhân viên của Ferd Data Services làm việc tại nhà.","Nhân viên đi công tác.","Nhân viên gửi biểu mẫu hàng tháng. của Ferd. (B) Tất cả các cảnh viên Dịch vụ lưu trữ của Ferd làm việc tại nhà. (C) Nhân viên đi công tác. (D) Nhân viên trả mẫu hàng tháng."]},{"questionNum":"200","passageTitle":"To: | Celeste O''Brien","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nLocation: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Celeste O''Brien\n\nFrom: | Monica Cheung\n\nDate: | October 15\n\nSubject: | Mobile phone reimbursement policy\n\nDear Ms.O''Brien, As the Assistant Director of Accounting, I am writing about the policy regarding mobile phone expenses. Many Ferd Data Services employees use their personal mobile phones for business calls. To get reimbursed, they must submit a form every month. Ferd then pays up to 30 percent of the phone bill. My department confirms each employee''s calculations and then schedules payments that vary every month. Some companies have moved to a flat-rate model, where by all employees who qualify receive a fixed amount each month (e.g., $20). No staff time is required for monthly processing; the allowance is automatically included in each paycheck. Ihope that, as head of Human Resources, you will consider adopting a policy like this. Sincerely, Monica Cheung\n\nFerd Data Services MEETINGAGENDA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Location: Online\n\nDate: October 24\n\nTime: 3:00 P.M. Host:Celeste O''Brien, Vice President, Human Resources Attendees: Human Resources Managers; Finance Managers; Department Heads\n\nOBJECTIVES: 1. Consider issues with the current mobile phone reimbursement program 2.Review other options along with advantages and disadvantages 3. Select a new reimbursement model, if appropriate\n\nOPTIONS: 1.Continue to reimburse employees for up to 30 percent of their business mobile phone use 2. Provide a flat monthly amount to employees who qualify; employees with high costs can submit requests for additional compensation 3.Provide qualified employees with mobile phones for business use\n\n108\n\nFerd Data Services Employee Policies\n\nMobile Phone Reimbursement Policy RevisedOctober30\n\nEmployees who work remotely and/or travel for business purposes should be reimbursed for business use of mobile phones. Three options are available::Employees who qualify will receiveamobilephoneallowanceofs20permonth, regardless of actual expenses. To enroll in the program, employees must submit a Mobile Phone Allowance form with their supervisor''s signature. The $20\n\nallowance will be applied to each month''s paycheck. allowance will | paycneek\n\n.Employees with large charges may submit actual expenses to receive additional reimbursement. Managers and executives may opt for a company mobile phone, which is for business use only."}],"question":"What best describes the result of the meeting on October 24?","bilingual":"Điều gì mô tả đúng nhất về kết quả của cuộc họp vào ngày 24 tháng 10?","options":["Attendees agreed to continue following the original procedures.","Attendees decided to collect more information before making a decision.","Attendees decided to adopt some of the options discussed.","Attendees completed a survey about mobile phone use."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Attendees decided to adopt some of the options discussed.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"appropriate","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈproʊpriˌeɪt/","meaning":"thích hợp; lắp"},{"word":"accounting","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈkaʊn.t̬ɪŋ/","meaning":"sự tính toán, thanh toán"}],"optionMeanings":["Những người tham dự đồng ý tiếp tục làm theo các thủ tục ban đầu.","Những người tham dự quyết định thu thập thêm thông tin trước khi đưa ra quyết định.","Những người tham dự đã quyết định áp dụng một số phương án đã được thảo luận.","Những người tham dự đã hoàn thành bản khảo sát về việc sử dụng điện thoại di động."]}]'::jsonb,
