o\n\nI would welcome your help in this matter. Could we get together in the next few days for lunch or coffee? As you know, I have always valued your input, and I have missed our lunchtime conversations since you retired. Quentin","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Dialed-ln:The Web Site for Professional Connections\n\nQuentin Rines | Position wanted:\n\nDialed-In Code number:04404782 | Director of Commercial Lending\n\nExperience: Assistant Manager, Commercial Lending First Bank of Barbados Three years, three months (present position)\n\nLoan Officer First Bank of Barbados Three years, eight months\n\nTeller First Bank of Barbados 1 year, two months"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Quentin Rines <qrines@islandlink.bb> From: | Rozella Huy <rozella.huy@ventana.com> Date: | 14 November\n\nSubject: | Job offer\n\nDear Mr.Rines: On behalf of all staff here at Ventana Bank, I want to say how pleased we were to meet you last week. We appreciate that you were able to spend so much time with us discussing your background and plans for the future. We are pleased to offer you the position of director of commercial lending. The position will be based in our George Town location on the Cayman Islands. Should you accept the position, you will receive the pay and benefits described during the interview process, as well as a relocation reimbursement of USD $1,000. Please let us know whether you accept the offer by 29 November and inform us of your preferred start date, We hope to have the position filled by mid-December. Congratulations on being selected. We look forward to welcoming you to our team. Sincerely, Rozella Huy President, Ventana Bank"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Tom as Melville <tmelville@homenetwork.bb> From: | Quentin Rines <qrines@islandlink.bb> Date: | 14 November\n\nSubject: | New position\n\nMr. Melville, I just received the job offer from Ventana Bank that we discussed on Monday. They are meeting my salary request and offering me money for relocating too. This has been my goal ever since you hired me as a teller, right out of college. But now that I have been offered my dream job, I am having doubts. The new location seems so\n\nI would welcome your help in this matter. Could we get together in the next few days for lunch or coffee? As you know, I have always valued your input, and I have missed our lunchtime conversations since you retired. Quentin"}],"question":"According to the second e-mail, why does Mr.Rines want to meet with Mr.Melville?","bilingual":"Theo e thứ hai -mail, tại sao ông Rines lại muốn gặp ông John? Melville?","options":["To offer him a job","To request a loan","To ask for advice","To thank him for his help"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"To ask for advice\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"conversation","pos":"Noun (Danh từ)","level":"A2","ipa":"/ˌkɑːnvərˈseɪʃn/","meaning":"cuộc đối thoại"},{"word":"commercial","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmərʃəl/","meaning":"liên quan đến kinh doanh; liên quan đến việc mua và"}],"optionMeanings":["Để mời anh ấy một công việc","Để yêu cầu một khoản vay","Để xin lời khuyên","Để cảm ơn sự giúp đỡ của anh ấy190. Điều gì được gợi ý về ông Melville? (A) Ông ấy sống ở George Town. (B) Anh ấy đã liên lạc với ông Rines bằng cách sử dụng Dialed - Trang web. (C) Anh ấy là bạn của cô Huy. (D) Anh ấy từng làm việc tại First Bank of Barbados. BÃN DỊCH: Đã gọi -in: Website dành cho các kết nối chuyên nghiệpQuentin RinesMã sốDialed - Tại: 04404 782 Vị trí mong muốn: Giám đốc cho vay thương mạiKinh nghiệm: Trợlý giám đốc cho vay thương mạiFirst Bank of Barbados3 năm, 3 tháng (hiện tại) bộtín dụngFirst Bank of Barbados3 năm, 8 thángGiao dịch viênFirst Bank of Barbados1 năm m, 2 tháng Đoạn 2: Tới Quentin Rinesqrines@islandlink.bbTừRozella Huyrozella.huy@ventana.comNgày: 14 tháng 11 Chủ đề: Đềnghị công Đông Rines thân mến: T hay mặt cho tất cả cảnh báo tại Ngân hàng Ventana, tôi muốn nói rằng chúng tôi rất vui khi được gặp vào tuần trước. Chúng tôi rất trân trọng khi chúng tôi đã có thể sẵn sàng nhiều thời gian để chúng tôi cùng trao đổi vềcông việc nhỏ cũng được xác định cho tương lai. Chúng tôi rất vui được làm hỏng vị trívị trí giám đốc cho vay thương mạtôi. Vị trí này sẽ làm việc tại chi nhánh George Town của chúng tôi trên Quần đảo Cayman. Nếu anh chấp nhận điều này, anh sẽ nhận được tài khoản tiền lương và các khoản hỗ trợ được mô tả trong quá trình mô phỏng, cũng nhưkhoản tiền bồi thường cho việc tái cư trị giá 1.000 USD. Vui lòng cho chúng tôi biết tài liệu có chấp nhận đềnghị này hay không trước ngày 29 tháng 11 và thông báo cho chúng tôi biết về ngày bắt đầu có thể làm việc. Chúng tôi hy vọng điều này sẽ được hoàn thành trước giữa tháng 12. Chúc mừng lựa chọn đã được chọn. Chúng tôi mong đợi được chào đón ở mức độ của chúng tôi. Trân trọng, Rozella HuyChủtịch, Ngân hàng Ventana Đoạn 3: Tới: Tomas Melville <tmelville @homenetwork.bb> Từ: Quentin Rines <qrines @islandlink.bb>Ngày 14 tháng 11 Chủ đề: Công việc mới Tôi vừa nhận được công việc từ Ngân hàng Ventana mà chúng tôi đã thảo luận vào thứHai. Họsẽ đáp ứng yêu cầu về lương của tôi và cũng cung cấp cho tôi tiền để chuyển chỗ. Đây là mục tiêu của tôi từ khi tôi thuê người làm giao dịch viên, ngay sau khi tốt nghiệp cao đẳng. Nhưng dù bây giờ tôi đã được đềnghị công việc của mình vĩnh viễnmongước, tôi lại có chút chút yên dodự. Điểm mới này xuất hiệnrất xa. I willhiếm khi được gặp mẹ và anh chị em của mình. Tôi cần kích thước của anh ấy trong vấn đề này. Chúng ta có thể gặp nhau trong vài ngày tới để ăn hoặc mua cà phê không? Như ông đã biết, tôi luôn nhắc nhở giá cao những ý kiến ​​đó ng gó p của ông và tôi cũng rất nhớ những cuộc trò chuyện vào giờ ăn trưa của họ ta dạy từkhiông nghỉhưu. Quentin"]},{"questionNum":"190","passageTitle":"Dialed-ln:The Web Site for Professional Connections","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nDialed-ln:The Web Site for Professional Connections\n\nQuentin Rines | Position wanted:\n\nDialed-In Code number:04404782 | Director of Commercial Lending\n\nExperience: Assistant Manager, Commercial Lending First Bank of Barbados Three years, three months (present position)\n\nLoan Officer First Bank of Barbados Three years, eight months\n\nTeller First Bank of Barbados 1 year, two months\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Quentin Rines <qrines@islandlink.bb> From: | Rozella Huy <rozella.huy@ventana.com> Date: | 14 November\n\nSubject: | Job offer\n\nDear Mr.Rines: On behalf of all staff here at Ventana Bank, I want to say how pleased we were to meet you last week. We appreciate that you were able to spend so much time with us discussing your background and plans for the future. We are pleased to offer you the position of director of commercial lending. The position will be based in our George Town location on the Cayman Islands. Should you accept the position, you will receive the pay and benefits described during the interview process, as well as a relocation reimbursement of USD $1,000. Please let us know whether you accept the offer by 29 November and inform us of your preferred start date, We hope to have the position filled by mid-December. Congratulations on being selected. We look forward to welcoming you to our team. Sincerely, Rozella Huy President, Ventana Bank\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Tom as Melville <tmelville@homenetwork.bb> From: | Quentin Rines <qrines@islandlink.bb> Date: | 14 November\n\nSubject: | New position\n\nMr. Melville, I just received the job offer from Ventana Bank that we discussed on Monday. They are meeting my salary request and offering me money for relocating too. This has been my goal ever since you hired me as a teller, right out of college. But now that I have been offered my dream job, I am having doubts. The new location seems so\n\nI would welcome your help in this matter. Could we get together in the next few days for lunch or coffee? As you know, I have always valued your input, and I have missed our lunchtime conversations since you retired. Quentin","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Dialed-ln:The Web Site for Professional Connections\n\nQuentin Rines | Position wanted:\n\nDialed-In Code number:04404782 | Director of Commercial Lending\n\nExperience: Assistant Manager, Commercial Lending First Bank of Barbados Three years, three months (present position)\n\nLoan Officer First Bank of Barbados Three years, eight months\n\nTeller First Bank of Barbados 1 year, two months"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Quentin Rines <qrines@islandlink.bb> From: | Rozella Huy <rozella.huy@ventana.com> Date: | 14 November\n\nSubject: | Job offer\n\nDear Mr.Rines: On behalf of all staff here at Ventana Bank, I want to say how pleased we were to meet you last week. We appreciate that you were able to spend so much time with us discussing your background and plans for the future. We are pleased to offer you the position of director of commercial lending. The position will be based in our George Town location on the Cayman Islands. Should you accept the position, you will receive the pay and benefits described during the interview process, as well as a relocation reimbursement of USD $1,000. Please let us know whether you accept the offer by 29 November and inform us of your preferred start date, We hope to have the position filled by mid-December. Congratulations on being selected. We look forward to welcoming you to our team. Sincerely, Rozella Huy President, Ventana Bank"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | Tom as Melville <tmelville@homenetwork.bb> From: | Quentin Rines <qrines@islandlink.bb> Date: | 14 November\n\nSubject: | New position\n\nMr. Melville, I just received the job offer from Ventana Bank that we discussed on Monday. They are meeting my salary request and offering me money for relocating too. This has been my goal ever since you hired me as a teller, right out of college. But now that I have been offered my dream job, I am having doubts. The new location seems so\n\nI would welcome your help in this matter. Could we get together in the next few days for lunch or coffee? As you know, I have always valued your input, and I have missed our lunchtime conversations since you retired. Quentin"}],"question":"What is suggested about Mr. Melville?","bilingual":"","options":["He lives in George Town.","He contacted Mr.Rines using the Dialed-ln Web site.","Heis a friend of Ms.Huy''s.","He once worked at First Bank of Barbados."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"He once worked at First Bank of Barbados.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reimbursement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌriɪmˈbərsmənt/","meaning":"hành động trả lại; hoàn trả; bồi thường cho một"},{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"conversation","pos":"Noun (Danh từ)","level":"A2","ipa":"/ˌkɑːnvərˈseɪʃn/","meaning":"cuộc đối thoại"},{"word":"commercial","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmərʃəl/","meaning":"liên quan đến kinh doanh; liên quan đến việc mua và"}]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"The Mayan Joy Cocoa Process From our organic fields to your kitchen table!","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nThe Mayan Joy Cocoa Process From our organic fields to your kitchen table!\n\n1. We plant | 2. We dry, | 3.Wetoast | 4. We grind | 5. YOU enjoy\n\nand cultivate | clean, and | the cocoa | the shelled | our Mexican\n\nthe seeds | prepare the | beans and | beans to | cocoa, a rich,\n\nfollowing | seeds | remove the | produce | sensational,\n\nancient | naturally. | shells by | 100% pure | delicious\n\ntraditions. | hand. | cocoa | super food!\n\npowder.\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Av Tulum Plaza Galerias Cancun, QuintanaR0097655 Mexico March 24\n\nJames Grigio 39 Lansford Lane Valley Falls, Kansas 66088 United States\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Representative: When I was recently in Mexico, I purchased a block of your fine cocoa. It was the best I ever had! I did some research on your products, and I was very impressed with your process. I especially appreciate that your workers take care to remove the shells from the beans by hand.\n\nI would like to purchase some more to make my own chocolates at home. Please send me information and pricing.I would prefer to purchase a one-pound block of pure, unsweetened Yucatan cocoa. I will be sweetening the candy myself, so I am not looking for sweetened cocoa. Thank you. James Grigio James Grigio\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nMayan Joy Cocoa Products Chart\n\nHouse Blend | Artisan Block | Block Gift | Mountain Bag\n\nHalf-pound bag $25 1 pound $40 | 2 pounds $98 | 1 pound $65\n\nItem:D-23 | Item:C-100 | Item:C-200 | Item:M-42\n\nRich, bittersweet, | Pure cocoa | Pure cocoa | Mountain grown\n\nblendedpowder | from the | from the | in the highlands of\n\nYucatan | Yucatan | Guatemala\n\nReady for making Perfect for drinks, | Beautifully | Unsweetened\n\nsteamy, frothy, hot cooking, baking, | displayed in a | cocoa in bag\n\ndrinks | and confections | handcrafted | designed with\n\nwooden gift box artwork from Guatemala\n\nCocoa, white and | 100% pure cocoa | 100%purecocoa 100%purecocoa\n\nbrown sugar, | in block form | in block form | in block form\n\ncinnamon, an cho, all spice, anise, and cayenne","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"The Mayan Joy Cocoa Process From our organic fields to your kitchen table!\n\n1. We plant | 2. We dry, | 3.Wetoast | 4. We grind | 5. YOU enjoy\n\nand cultivate | clean, and | the cocoa | the shelled | our Mexican\n\nthe seeds | prepare the | beans and | beans to | cocoa, a rich,\n\nfollowing | seeds | remove the | produce | sensational,\n\nancient | naturally. | shells by | 100% pure | delicious\n\ntraditions. | hand. | cocoa | super food!\n\npowder.\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Av Tulum Plaza Galerias Cancun, QuintanaR0097655 Mexico March 24\n\nJames Grigio 39 Lansford Lane Valley Falls, Kansas 66088 United States\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Representative: When I was recently in Mexico, I purchased a block of your fine cocoa. It was the best I ever had! I did some research on your products, and I was very impressed with your process. I especially appreciate that your workers take care to remove the shells from the beans by hand.\n\nI would like to purchase some more to make my own chocolates at home. Please send me information and pricing.I would prefer to purchase a one-pound block of pure, unsweetened Yucatan cocoa. I will be sweetening the candy myself, so I am not looking for sweetened cocoa. Thank you. James Grigio James Grigio"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Mayan Joy Cocoa Products Chart\n\nHouse Blend | Artisan Block | Block Gift | Mountain Bag\n\nHalf-pound bag $25 1 pound $40 | 2 pounds $98 | 1 pound $65\n\nItem:D-23 | Item:C-100 | Item:C-200 | Item:M-42\n\nRich, bittersweet, | Pure cocoa | Pure cocoa | Mountain grown\n\nblendedpowder | from the | from the | in the highlands of\n\nYucatan | Yucatan | Guatemala\n\nReady for making Perfect for drinks, | Beautifully | Unsweetened\n\nsteamy, frothy, hot cooking, baking, | displayed in a | cocoa in bag\n\ndrinks | and confections | handcrafted | designed with\n\nwooden gift box artwork from Guatemala\n\nCocoa, white and | 100% pure cocoa | 100%purecocoa 100%purecocoa\n\nbrown sugar, | in block form | in block form | in block form\n\ncinnamon, an cho, all spice, anise, and cayenne"}],"question":"Based on the process chart, what is done to the seeds immediately after they are cultivated?","bilingual":"Dựa trên sơ đồ quy trình, hạt giống được làm gì ngay sau khi chúng được gieo trồng?","options":["They are made into a beverage.","They are ground into powder.","They are toasted.","They are dried."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"They are dried.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"representative","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,repri''zentətiv/","meaning":"miêu tả, biểu hiện"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"},{"word":"appreciate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈpriː.ʃi.eɪt/","meaning":"đánh giá cao, cảm kích"}],"optionMeanings":["Chúng được pha thành đồ uống.","Chúng được nghiền thành bột.","Chúng đã được nướng.","Chúng đã được sấy khô.192. Ông Grigio chỉ ra điều gì trong bức thư? (A) Ông sống ở Cancun, Quintana Roo. (B) Ông trồng ca cao tự nhiên. (C) Ông sở hữu một cửa hàng sô cô la. (D) Ông mua ca cao ở Mexico.193. Ông Grigio khen ngợi bước nào trong quy trình của Maya Joy Cocoa?(A) Bước 1(B) Bước 2(C) Bước 3(D) Bước 4194. Điều gì đúng về Quà tặng Maya Joy Block? (A) Đây là sản phẩm duy nhất được đựng trong hộp đựng có trang trí. (B) Đây là sản phẩm duy nhất đến từ Yucatan. (C) Nó lớn hơn các sản phẩm khác của Mayan Joy. (D) Nó chứa nhiều đường bổ sung hơn các sản phẩm khác của MayanJoy."]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"The Mayan Joy Cocoa Process From our organic fields to your kitchen table!","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nThe Mayan Joy Cocoa Process From our organic fields to your kitchen table!\n\n1. We plant | 2. We dry, | 3.Wetoast | 4. We grind | 5. YOU enjoy\n\nand cultivate | clean, and | the cocoa | the shelled | our Mexican\n\nthe seeds | prepare the | beans and | beans to | cocoa, a rich,\n\nfollowing | seeds | remove the | produce | sensational,\n\nancient | naturally. | shells by | 100% pure | delicious\n\ntraditions. | hand. | cocoa | super food!\n\npowder.\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Av Tulum Plaza Galerias Cancun, QuintanaR0097655 Mexico March 24\n\nJames Grigio 39 Lansford Lane Valley Falls, Kansas 66088 United States\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Representative: When I was recently in Mexico, I purchased a block of your fine cocoa. It was the best I ever had! I did some research on your products, and I was very impressed with your process. I especially appreciate that your workers take care to remove the shells from the beans by hand.\n\nI would like to purchase some more to make my own chocolates at home. Please send me information and pricing.I would prefer to purchase a one-pound block of pure, unsweetened Yucatan cocoa. I will be sweetening the candy myself, so I am not looking for sweetened cocoa. Thank you. James Grigio James Grigio\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nMayan Joy Cocoa Products Chart\n\nHouse Blend | Artisan Block | Block Gift | Mountain Bag\n\nHalf-pound bag $25 1 pound $40 | 2 pounds $98 | 1 pound $65\n\nItem:D-23 | Item:C-100 | Item:C-200 | Item:M-42\n\nRich, bittersweet, | Pure cocoa | Pure cocoa | Mountain grown\n\nblendedpowder | from the | from the | in the highlands of\n\nYucatan | Yucatan | Guatemala\n\nReady for making Perfect for drinks, | Beautifully | Unsweetened\n\nsteamy, frothy, hot cooking, baking, | displayed in a | cocoa in bag\n\ndrinks | and confections | handcrafted | designed with\n\nwooden gift box artwork from Guatemala\n\nCocoa, white and | 100% pure cocoa | 100%purecocoa 100%purecocoa\n\nbrown sugar, | in block form | in block form | in block form\n\ncinnamon, an cho, all spice, anise, and cayenne","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"The Mayan Joy Cocoa Process From our organic fields to your kitchen table!\n\n1. We plant | 2. We dry, | 3.Wetoast | 4. We grind | 5. YOU enjoy\n\nand cultivate | clean, and | the cocoa | the shelled | our Mexican\n\nthe seeds | prepare the | beans and | beans to | cocoa, a rich,\n\nfollowing | seeds | remove the | produce | sensational,\n\nancient | naturally. | shells by | 100% pure | delicious\n\ntraditions. | hand. | cocoa | super food!\n\npowder.\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Av Tulum Plaza Galerias Cancun, QuintanaR0097655 Mexico March 24\n\nJames Grigio 39 Lansford Lane Valley Falls, Kansas 66088 United States\n\nMayan Joy Cocoa Representative: When I was recently in Mexico, I purchased a block of your fine cocoa. It was the best I ever had! I did some research on your products, and I was very impressed with your process. I especially appreciate that your workers take care to remove the shells from the beans by hand.\n\nI would like to purchase some more to make my own chocolates at home. Please send me information and pricing.I would prefer to purchase a one-pound block of pure, unsweetened Yucatan cocoa. I will be sweetening the candy myself, so I am not looking for sweetened cocoa. Thank you. James Grigio James Grigio"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Mayan Joy Cocoa Products Chart\n\nHouse Blend | Artisan Block | Block Gift | Mountain Bag\n\nHalf-pound bag $25 1 pound $40 | 2 pounds $98 | 1 pound $65\n\nItem:D-23 | Item:C-100 | Item:C-200 | Item:M-42\n\nRich, bittersweet, | Pure cocoa | Pure cocoa | Mountain grown\n\nblendedpowder | from the | from the | in the highlands of\n\nYucatan | Yucatan | Guatemala\n\nReady for making Perfect for drinks, | Beautifully | Unsweetened\n\nsteamy, frothy, hot cooking, baking, | displayed in a | cocoa in bag\n\ndrinks | and confections | handcrafted | designed with\n\nwooden gift box artwork from Guatemala\n\nCocoa, white and | 100% pure cocoa | 100%purecocoa 100%purecocoa\n\nbrown sugar, | in block form | in block form | in block form\n\ncinnamon, an cho, all spice, anise, and cayenne"}],"question":"What does Mr.Grigio indicate in the letter?","bilingual":"","options":["He