we are having our special promotion, giving away samples of our new ice cream flavors. I need a third person to help with that. Emily Chin (10:40 A.M.) I''m attending a birthday party this afternoon, so I can''t do it. Cameron Stein (10:42A.M.) I could stay on after my day shift is over. Emily Chin (10:43 A.M.) Actually, I could work 6-9 P.M.if you don''t want to stay. My party is only a few hours. What do you think? Cameron Stein (10:44A.M.) Well, I could really use the overtime hours. Emily Chin (10:45 A.M.) OK. Jack Elling (10:46 A.M.) Thanks, Cameron!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Jack Elling (10:35A.M.) Hi, everyone. Would anyone be able to come into the shop to work tonight? Kelly is having car problems and can''t work her shift. Emily Chin (10:37A.M.) Ican''t, sorry. But aren''t Maria and Koji also working? Don''t we usually have two people in the evenings? Jack Elling (10:39A.M.) Yes, we usually have two people, and those two are working tonight. But we are having our special promotion, giving away samples of our new ice cream flavors. I need a third person to help with that. Emily Chin (10:40 A.M.) I''m attending a birthday party this afternoon, so I can''t do it. Cameron Stein (10:42A.M.) I could stay on after my day shift is over. Emily Chin (10:43 A.M.) Actually, I could work 6-9 P.M.if you don''t want to stay. My party is only a few hours. What do you think? Cameron Stein (10:44A.M.) Well, I could really use the overtime hours. Emily Chin (10:45 A.M.) OK. Jack Elling (10:46 A.M.) Thanks, Cameron!"}],"question":"Why does Mr.Elling start the text-message chain?","bilingual":"Tại sao ông Eiling lại bắt đầu văn bản - chuỗi tin nhắn?","options":["To tell Ms. Chin that she missed a work shift","To ask someone to cover a work shift","To extend an invitation to a special event","To ask for a ride to work"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To ask someone to cover a work shift\".","vocabList":[{"word":"invitation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnvɪˈteɪʃən/","meaning":"yêu cầu sự hiện diện của một người; triệu tập; gọi"},{"word":"promotion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''mou∫n/","meaning":"sự thăng chức, sự đề bạt"},{"word":"attending","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈtɛndɪŋ/","meaning":"tham dự"},{"word":"actually","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈæk.tʃu.ə.li/","meaning":"thực sự, trên thực tế"}],"optionMeanings":["Nhắn tin cho chị Chín lỡ ca làm việc","Để nhờ ai đó thay ca làm việc","Để gửi lời mời tham dự một sự kiện đặc biệt","Để xin xe đi làm169. Tối nay có chuyện gì ở cửa hàng vậy? (A) Nhân viên sẽ nghiên cứu các công thức nấu ăn mới. (B) Nhân viên sẽ cung cấp các buổi nếm thử kem miễn phí. (C) Nhân viên sẽ tham gia vào một buổi đào tạo. (D) Nhân viên sẽ tổ chức một buổi thử nghiệm -tiệc đi xa của đồng nghiệp."]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"Jack Elling (10:35A.M.) Hi, everyone. Would anyone be able to come into the","passageText":"Jack Elling (10:35A.M.) Hi, everyone. Would anyone be able to come into the shop to work tonight? Kelly is having car problems and can''t work her shift. Emily Chin (10:37A.M.) Ican''t, sorry. But aren''t Maria and Koji also working? Don''t we usually have two people in the evenings? Jack Elling (10:39A.M.) Yes, we usually have two people, and those two are working tonight. But we are having our special promotion, giving away samples of our new ice cream flavors. I need a third person to help with that. Emily Chin (10:40 A.M.) I''m attending a birthday party this afternoon, so I can''t do it. Cameron Stein (10:42A.M.) I could stay on after my day shift is over. Emily Chin (10:43 A.M.) Actually, I could work 6-9 P.M.if you don''t want to stay. My party is only a few hours. What do you think? Cameron Stein (10:44A.M.) Well, I could really use the overtime hours. Emily Chin (10:45 A.M.) OK. Jack Elling (10:46 A.M.) Thanks, Cameron!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Jack Elling (10:35A.M.) Hi, everyone. Would anyone be able to come into the shop to work tonight? Kelly is having car problems and can''t work her shift. Emily Chin (10:37A.M.) Ican''t, sorry. But aren''t Maria and Koji also working? Don''t we usually have two people in the evenings? Jack Elling (10:39A.M.) Yes, we usually have two people, and those two are working tonight. But we are having our special promotion, giving away samples of our new ice cream flavors. I need a third person to help with that. Emily Chin (10:40 A.M.) I''m attending a birthday party this afternoon, so I can''t do it. Cameron Stein (10:42A.M.) I could stay on after my day shift is over. Emily Chin (10:43 A.M.) Actually, I could work 6-9 P.M.if you don''t want to stay. My party is only a few hours. What do you think? Cameron Stein (10:44A.M.) Well, I could really use the overtime hours. Emily Chin (10:45 A.M.) OK. Jack Elling (10:46 A.M.) Thanks, Cameron!"}],"question":"What is happening at the shop tonight?","bilingual":"Tối nay quán có chuyện gì vậy?","options":["Staff will work on new recipes.","Staff will offer free ice cream tastings.","Staff will participate in a training session.","Staff will hold a going-away party for a colleague."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Staff will offer free ice cream tastings.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"participate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pɑrˈtɪsəˌpeɪt/","meaning":"được tham gia; tham gia vào"},{"word":"colleague","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑlig/","meaning":"đồng nghiệp; đồng nghiệp"},{"word":"promotion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''mou∫n/","meaning":"sự thăng chức, sự đề bạt"},{"word":"attending","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈtɛndɪŋ/","