stay on after my day shift is over. Emily Chin (10:43 A.M.) Actually, I could work 6-9 P.M.if you don''t want to stay. My party is only a few hours. What do you think? Cameron Stein (10:44A.M.) Well, I could really use the overtime hours. Emily Chin (10:45 A.M.) OK. Jack Elling (10:46 A.M.) Thanks, Cameron!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Jack Elling (10:35A.M.) Hi, everyone. Would anyone be able to come into the shop to work tonight? Kelly is having car problems and can''t work her shift. Emily Chin (10:37A.M.) Ican''t, sorry. But aren''t Maria and Koji also working? Don''t we usually have two people in the evenings? Jack Elling (10:39A.M.) Yes, we usually have two people, and those two are working tonight. But we are having our special promotion, giving away samples of our new ice cream flavors. I need a third person to help with that. Emily Chin (10:40 A.M.) I''m attending a birthday party this afternoon, so I can''t do it. Cameron Stein (10:42A.M.) I could stay on after my day shift is over. Emily Chin (10:43 A.M.) Actually, I could work 6-9 P.M.if you don''t want to stay. My party is only a few hours. What do you think? Cameron Stein (10:44A.M.) Well, I could really use the overtime hours. Emily Chin (10:45 A.M.) OK. Jack Elling (10:46 A.M.) Thanks, Cameron!"}],"question":"At 10:44 A.M., what does Mr. Stein most likely mean when he writes,\"Well, I could really use the overtime hours\"?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 10:44 sáng, rất có thể ông Stein có ý gì khi viết: “Chà, tôi thực sự có thể sử dụng số giờ làm thêm”?","options":["He is accepting Ms. Chin''s apology.","He is declining Ms.Chin''s offer.","He enjoys working at the shop.","He prefers to work in the evening."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"He is declining Ms.Chin''s offer.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"promotion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''mou∫n/","meaning":"sự thăng chức, sự đề bạt"},{"word":"attending","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈtɛndɪŋ/","meaning":"tham dự"},{"word":"actually","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈæk.tʃu.ə.li/","meaning":"thực sự, trên thực tế"},{"word":"usually","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈjuʒəwəli/","meaning":"thông thường; nói chung là; thường xuyên"}],"optionMeanings":["Anh ấy chấp nhận lời xin lỗi của cô Chin.","Anh ấy đang từ chối lời đề nghị của cô Chin.","Anh ấy thích làm việc ở cửa hàng.","Anh ấy thích làm việc vào buổi tối."]},{"questionNum":"172","passageTitle":"Kiame Tire Factory Productivity Report","passageText":"Kiame Tire Factory Productivity Report\n\nPreparer: Wilma Najar, Systems Engineer Date of review:April 10 Reason for review:Quarterly inspection\n\nSummary: I have completed my inspection of all equipment and machinery at the plant.[1]The main components of the production line are running as expected. These components include mixers, rollers, and the textile production system. - [2] -. The rotating drums for assembling the tires that were added last quarter have also been functioning as expected. Finally, the molds for the tire treads are beginning to show some signs of wear. Employees have flagged these molds, and the molds will be removed from the production line.\n\nRecommendations: Purchasing new replacement molds is the top priority. See the report in the section dedicated to tire molds for details. [3].Finally, as the Kiameplant increases its production, adding more mixers will be crucial to making more tires. The company must decide at that point whether to purchase newer mixer models or to\n\nthe older mixers will speed up production, which will likely outweigh any additional cost.\n\n158","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Kiame Tire Factory Productivity Report\n\nPreparer: Wilma Najar, Systems Engineer Date of review:April 10 Reason for review:Quarterly inspection\n\nSummary: I have completed my inspection of all equipment and machinery at the plant.[1]The main components of the production line are running as expected. These components include mixers, rollers, and the textile production system. - [2] -. The rotating drums for assembling the tires that were added last quarter have also been functioning as expected. Finally, the molds for the tire treads are beginning to show some signs of wear. Employees have flagged these molds, and the molds will be removed from the production line.\n\nRecommendations: Purchasing new replacement molds is the top priority. See the report in the section dedicated to tire molds for details. [3].Finally, as the Kiameplant increases its production, adding more mixers will be crucial to making more tires. The company must decide at that point whether to purchase newer mixer models or to\n\nthe older mixers will speed up production, which will likely outweigh any additional cost.\n\n158"}],"question":"Why did Ms.Najarmost likely prepare the report?","bilingual":"Tại sao cô Najjar có nhiều khả năng chuẩn bị báo cáo nhất?","options":["To explain why the mixing equipment is not working properly","To document findings of a factory inspection","To explain why productivity has recently decreased","To justify the purchase of new rotating drums"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To document findings of a factory inspection\".","vocabList":[{"word":"recommendation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/¸rekəmen´deiʃən/","meaning":"sự giới thiệu, sự tiến cử"},{"word":"productivity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌproʊdəkˈtɪvɪti/","meaning":"thước đo sản lượng trên mỗi giờ làm việc;"},{"word":"functioning","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfəŋkʃənɪŋ/","meaning":"hoạt động"},{"word":"inspection","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈspɛkʃən/","meaning":"hành động xem xét cẩn thận và phê phán; chính thức"}],"optionMeanings":["Để giải thích tại sao thiết bị trộn không hoạt động bình thường","Để ghi lại kết quả kiểm tra nhà máy","Để giải thích lý do tại sao năng suất gần đây giảm","Để biện minh cho việc mua trống quay mới173. Điều gì đúng về khuôn lốp xe? (A) Có một phần riêng về chúng trong báo cáo. (B) Tất cả chúng đều đã được thay thế gần đây. (C) Chúng không được sản xuất trong nhà máy. (D) Giờ đây, nhiều lốp xe hơn có thể được sản xuất với ít khuôn hơn."]},{"questionNum":"173","passageTitle":"Kiame Tire Factory Productivity Report","passageText":"Kiame Tire Factory Productivity Report\n\nPreparer: Wilma Najar, Systems Engineer Date of review:April 10 Reason for review:Quarterly inspection\n\nSummary: I have completed my inspection of all equipment and machinery at the plant.[1]The main components of the production line are running as expected. These components include mixers, rollers, and the textile production system. - [2] -. The rotating drums for assembling the tires that were added last quarter have also been functioning as expected. Finally, the molds for the tire treads are beginning to show some signs of wear. Employees have flagged these molds, and the molds will be removed from the production line.\n\nRecommendations: Purchasing new replacement molds is the top priority. See the report in the section dedicated to tire molds for details. [3].Finally, as the Kiameplant increases its production, adding more mixers will be crucial to making more tires. The company must decide at that point whether to purchase newer mixer models or to\n\nthe older mixers will speed up production, which will likely outweigh any additional cost.\n\n158","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Kiame Tire Factory Productivity Report\n\nPreparer: Wilma Najar, Systems Engineer Date of review:April 10 Reason for review:Quarterly inspection\n\nSummary: I have completed my inspection of all equipment and machinery 