 Zealand goes back many whose work on building designs | project were thought fully selected by\n\nyears, won the award for her design of | impact, Young added. “However, what is Ms. Rahotu to minimize environmental\n\nthe Row an Community Centre. The centre utilized renewable and recycled materials | exceptional about Ms.Rahotu''s design is\n\nthroughout its construction. In April, | how well it harvests solar energy.\" According to experts at LNZB, her solar\n\nMs. Rahotu will be formally presented | design generates a high surplus of\n\nthe centre; details will be announced with the award during the ceremony at | electricity beyond the building''s\n\nsoon.\"It was a tough decision this year,\" | requirements. This surplus is transmitted to the region''s power grid-in effect\n\nsaid LNZB''s director, Thomas Young. \"All applicants chose materials that | reducing strain on local energy\n\nminimize environmental impact. But we | production.\n\n160"}],"question":"According to the article, why is Ms.Rahotu''s design exceptional?","bilingual":"Theo bài báo, tại sao thiết kế của cô Rahotu lại đặc biệt?","options":["It uses a high percentage of recycled materials.","It produces a large amount of electricity.","Its roof and walls have curved shapes.","It has a garden that covers most of the roof."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"It produces a large amount of electricity.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"environmental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.t̬əl/","meaning":"(thuộc) môi trường"},{"word":"construction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"xây dựng; kết cấu; ngành xây dựng tòa nhà"},{"word":"professional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''feʃənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) nghề, (thuộc) nghề nghiệp; có tay nghề"},{"word":"celebration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌsel.əˈbreɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"lễ kỉ niệm"}],"optionMeanings":["Nó sử dụng tỷ lệ vật liệu tái chế cao.","Nó tạo ra một lượng điện lớn.","Mái và tường của nó có hình dạng cong.","Nó có một khu vườn bao phủ gần hết mái nhà."]},{"questionNum":"181","passageTitle":"LAZONCOLOR SWIRLCUTTINGBOARD Model#B875","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nLAZONCOLOR SWIRLCUTTINGBOARD Model#B875\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nAlways wash the product soon after each use, especially after cutting acidic fruits and vegetables like oranges and tomatoes. Refrain from using bleach or cleaners with chlorine, which the board can absorb. For tough food stains, soak the board in soapy water for five minutes, Be sure to remove the leather hanging strap before cleaning, since water will make the leather tough and brittle, To store your product, hang it upright from the leather strap on a wall or shelf. Do not store it in direct sunlight, since this will cause the vibrant colors of the board to fade, Periodically, polish the board with a light coat of olive oil to help the board''s colors stay bright. Like all Lazon products, our cutting boards are handmade. With minimal upkeep, you can keep your product looking like new. If you have any problems with your board, please e-mail us at support@lazonproducts.com. Our policy is to replace at no cost any defective parts or products within three months of purchase, At Lazon Products, quality is our top priority!\n\nFrom: | Jonas E.Iversen <jonaseiversen@daylightcommerce.com> To: | support@lazonproducts.com Date: | August 2, 4:58 P.M.\n\nSubject: | Model#B875\n\nHello, I''m writing in regard to a defect in my Lazon Model #B875 board. I was very careful to follow all the maintenance tips that came with the product, but when I was taking off the leather strap as instructed, I noticed a small tear had formed in the middle. It''s not very large now, but it will only get bigger after a couple more months of use. Even though i purchased the product four months ago, I only started using it one month ago. Is the ieather strap still covered under your defective parts policy? I''d like to get a new one. Thank you for your assistance. Jonas E. Iversen\n\n162","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"LAZONCOLOR SWIRLCUTTINGBOARD Model#B875"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Always wash the product soon after each use, especially after cutting acidic fruits and vegetables like oranges and tomatoes. Refrain from using bleach or cleaners with chlorine, which the board can absorb. For tough food stains, soak the board in soapy water for five minutes, Be sure to remove the leather hanging strap before cleaning, since water will make the leather tough and brittle, To store your product, hang it upright from the leather strap on a wall or shelf. Do not store it in direct sunlight, since this will cause the vibrant colors of the board to fade, Periodically, polish the board with a light coat of olive oil to help the board''s colors stay bright. Like all Lazon products, our cutting boards are handmade. With minimal upkeep, you can keep your product looking like new. If you have any problems with your board, please e-mail us at support@lazonproducts.com. Our policy is to replace at no cost any defective parts or products within three months of purchase, At Lazon Products, quality is our top priority!\n\nFrom: | Jonas E.Iversen <jonaseiversen@daylightcommerce.com> To: | support@lazonproducts.com Date: | August 2, 4:58 P.M.\n\nSubject: | Model#B875\n\nHello, I''m writing in regard to a defect in my Lazon Model #B875 board. I was very careful to follow all the maintenance tips that came with the product, but when I was taking off the leather strap as instructed, I noticed a small tear had formed in the middle. It''s not very large now, but it will only get bigger after a couple more months of use. Even though i purchased the product four months ago, I only started using it one month ago. Is the ieather strap still covered under your defective parts policy? I''d like to get a new one. Thank you for your assistance. Jonas E. Iversen\n\n162"}],"question":"What do the instructions describe?","bilingual":"Hướng dẫn mô tả những gì?","options":["How to display a piece of artwork","How to prepare a type of gourmet food","How to use a construction tool","How to take care of a piece of kitchen equipment"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"How to take care of a piece of kitchen equipment\".","vocabList":[{"word":"construction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"xây dựng; kết cấu; ngành xây dựng tòa nhà"},{"word":"instruction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"giảng dạy; phương hướng; hướng dẫn; đào tạo; giáo dục;"},{"word":"maintenance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/´meintənəns/","meaning":"sự giữ gìn, sự duy trì; sự bảo vệ"},{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"}],"optionMeanings":["Cách trưng bày một tác phẩm nghệ thuật (B ) Cách chế biến một loại thức ăn dành cho người sành ăn (C) Cách sử dụng một công cụ xây dựng (D) Cách chăm sóc một thiết bị nhà bếp","Để làm cho sản phẩm trông đẹp hơn","Để làm cho sản phẩm chạy nhanh hơn","Để làm cho sản phẩm mạnh mẽ hơn183. Ông Iversen có nhiều khả năng sẽ làm gì nhất khi nhận thấy có vấn đề? (A) Làm sạch sản phẩm (B) Bảo quản sản phẩm (C) Trưng bày sản phẩm (D) Lắp ráp sản phẩm184. Ông Iversen đã sở hữu sản phẩm được bao lâu rồi? (A) Trong một tháng(B) Trong hai tháng(C) Trong ba tháng(D) Trong bốn tháng185. Ông Iversen yêu cầu Lazon Products làm gì?(A) Cho anh ta lời khuyên bảo trì(B) Hoàn lại toàn bộ số tiền cho anh ta(C) Gửi một bộ phận thay thế(D) Đề nghị sửa chữa sản phẩmB ẢN DỊCH:"]},{"questionNum":"182","passageTitle":"LAZONCOLOR SWIRLCUTTINGBOARD Model#B875","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 