 60 hectares of hilly terrain featuring lush English gardens and an impressive manor house that was designed by noted architect Owen Barton. Ten years ago, the Clarrell Foundation decided to transform the estate into an arts centre. Initially, the foundation opened the manor house to the public, highlighting the Clarrell family art collection. In the last three years, a large, multiuse complex was built near the property entrance, complete with art studios and a theatre.\n\nThe Clarrell Estate''s museum and gardens are open to the public free of charge. In addition, the theatre hosts public lectures as well as musical performances, and the studios showcase individual artists'' curated works. For a complete schedule, a list of current artists, and information on admission fees for the theatre and studios, please visit the Events page.\n\nJoin the Clarrell Foundation to enjoy members-only special events and discounts on performances. Members also have the opportunity to reserve the gardens for private events. To become a member, contact Alicia Ji at aji@clarrellestate.com.au.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"https://www.clarrellestate.com.au/about About | Events | Photos | The Foundation\n\nWelcome to the Clarrell Estate-Ballarton''s premier centre for the arts! The exquisite grounds of the estate are situated on 60 hectares of hilly terrain featuring lush English gardens and an impressive manor house that was designed by noted architect Owen Barton. Ten years ago, the Clarrell Foundation decided to transform the estate into an arts centre. Initially, the foundation opened the manor house to the public, highlighting the Clarrell family art collection. In the last three years, a large, multiuse complex was built near the property entrance, complete with art studios and a theatre.\n\nThe Clarrell Estate''s museum and gardens are open to the public free of charge. In addition, the theatre hosts public lectures as well as musical performances, and the studios showcase individual artists'' curated works. For a complete schedule, a list of current artists, and information on admission fees for the theatre and studios, please visit the Events page.\n\nJoin the Clarrell Foundation to enjoy members-only special events and discounts on performances. Members also have the opportunity to reserve the gardens for private events. To become a member, contact Alicia Ji at aji@clarrellestate.com.au."}],"question":"What does the Web page focus on?","bilingual":"Trang Web tập trung vào điều gì?","options":["An overview of an attraction","A town''s cultural festival","A local gardening club","An opportunity to buy art"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"An overview of an attraction\".","vocabList":[{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"performance","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pə''fɔ:məns/","meaning":"sự biểu diễn, việc đóng (phim, kịch...); cuộc"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"foundation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃən/","meaning":"căn cứ; nền tảng; công trình phụ; thành lập; tổ chức"}],"optionMeanings":["Tổng quan về một điểm du lịch","Lễ hội văn hóa của một thị trấn","Một câu lạc bộ làm vườn địa phương","Cơ hội mua tác phẩm nghệ thuật"]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"https://www.clarrellestate.com.au/about About | Events | Photos | The Found","passageText":"https://www.clarrellestate.com.au/about About | Events | Photos | The Foundation\n\nWelcome to the Clarrell Estate-Ballarton''s premier centre for the arts! The exquisite grounds of the estate are situated on 60 hectares of hilly terrain featuring lush English gardens and an impressive manor house that was designed by noted a