n","chậm"]},{"questionNum":"179","passageTitle":"To: | Bridget Morandi","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Bridget Morandi\n\nFrom: | Marybeth Wright\n\nDate: | March 23\n\nSubject: | Refund request\n\nHi Bridget, I was wondering if you have heard from Sujata Reddy. She was enrolled in the painting class I teach on Tuesday and Thursday. She was only able to attend for the first week because another commitment came up. She said she asked someone in the Tucson Adult School office if she could drop thc class, and shc has rcqucstcd a rcfund of the course tuition. She said she hasn''t received her refund yet. Did she contact you? Best, Marybeth Wright\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Marybeth Wright\n\nFrom: | Bridget Morandi\n\nDate: | March 24\n\nSubject: | Re:Refund request\n\nHi Marybeth, The name is familiar, but Ms.Reddy hasn''t been in touch with me personally. Actually, I''m not the person she should contact. I just handle the scheduling as well as ordering supplies fort heart classes. I don''t know who Ms.Reddy spoke to. According to our refund policy on the Tucson Adult School Web site, refunds are only granted if they are requested before the class begins or if there is a documented health reason for dropping the class. In the case of a health reason, the amount of the refund will be based on the number of classes completed. Maybe Ms.Reddy can attend your second semester class instead of this semester''s.That would be my suggestion. Bridget Morandi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Bridget Morandi\n\nFrom: | Marybeth Wright\n\nDate: | March 23\n\nSubject: | Refund request\n\nHi Bridget, I was wondering if you have heard from Sujata Reddy. She was enrolled in the painting class I teach on Tuesday and Thursday. She was only able to attend for the first week because another commitment came up. She said she asked someone in the Tucson Adult School office if she could drop thc class, and shc has rcqucstcd a rcfund of the course tuition. She said she hasn''t received her refund yet. Did she contact you? Best, Marybeth Wright"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Marybeth Wright\n\nFrom: | Bridget Morandi\n\nDate: | March 24\n\nSubject: | Re:Refund request\n\nHi Marybeth, The name is familiar, but Ms.Reddy hasn''t been in touch with me personally. Actually, I''m not the person she should contact. I just handle the scheduling as well as ordering supplies fort heart classes. I don''t know who Ms.Reddy spoke to. According to our refund policy on the Tucson Adult School Web site, refunds are only granted if they are requested before the class begins or if there is a documented health reason for dropping the class. In the case of a health reason, the amount of the refund will be based on the number of classes completed. Maybe Ms.Reddy can attend your second semester class instead of this semester''s.That would be my suggestion. Bridget Morandi"}],"question":"Why most likely has Ms.Reddy not yet received a tuition refund?","bilingual":"Tại sao rất có thể cô Reddy vẫn chưa được hoàn lại học phí?","options":["The registration office has been closed.","The refund check is still in the mail.","She failed to submit her request in writing.","She already attended part of the class."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"The registration office has been closed.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"registration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,redʤis''treiʃn/","meaning":"sự đăng ký, sự ghi vào sổ"},{"word":"commitment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmɪtmənt/","meaning":"nghĩa vụ; hứa"},{"word":"scheduling","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈskɛʤʊlɪŋ/","meaning":"lên lịch"},{"word":"suggestion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈdʒes.tʃən/","meaning":"sự đề xuất"}],"optionMeanings":["Văn phòng đăng ký đã bị đóng.","Kiểm tra hoàn tiền vẫn còn trong thư.","Cô ấy đã không gửi được yêu cầu của mình bằng văn bản.","Cô ấy đã tham gia một phần của lớp học."]},{"questionNum":"180","passageTitle":"To: | Bridget Morandi","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Bridget Morandi\n\nFrom: | Marybeth Wright\n\nDate: | March 23\n\nSubject: | Refund request\n\nHi Bridget, I was wondering if you have heard from Sujata Reddy. She was enrolled in the painting class I teach on Tuesday and Thursday. She was only able to attend for the first week because another commitment came up. She said she asked someone in the Tucson Adult School office if she could drop thc class, and shc has rcqucstcd a rcfund of the course tuition. She said she hasn''t received her refund yet. Did she contact you? Best, Marybeth Wright\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Marybeth Wright\n\nFrom: | Bridget Morandi\n\nDate: | March 24\n\nSubject: | Re:Refund request\n\nHi Marybeth, The name is familiar, but Ms.Reddy hasn''t been in touch with me personally. Actually, I''m not the person she should contact. I just handle the scheduling as well as ordering supplies fort heart classes. I don''t know who Ms.Reddy spoke to. According to our refund policy on the Tucson Adult School Web site, refunds are only granted if they are requested before the class begins or if there is a documented health reason for dropping the class. In the case of a health reason, the amount of the refund will be based on the number of classes completed. Maybe Ms.Reddy can attend your second semester class instead of this semester''s.That would be my suggestion. Bridget Morandi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Bridget Morandi\n\nFrom: | Marybeth Wright\n\nDate: | March 23\n\nSubject: | Refund request\n\nHi Bridget, I was wondering if you have heard from Sujata Reddy. She was enrolled in the painting class I teach on Tuesday and Thursday. She was only able to attend for the first week because another commitment came up. She said she asked someone in the Tucson Adult School office if she could drop thc class, and shc has rcqucstcd a rcfund of the course tuition. She said she hasn''t received her refund yet. Did she contact you? Best, Marybeth Wright"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Marybeth Wright\n\nFrom: | Bridget Morandi\n\nDate: | March 24\n\nSubject: | Re:Refund request\n\nHi Marybeth, The name is familiar, but Ms.Reddy hasn''t been in touch with me personally. Actually, I''m not the person she should contact. I just handle the scheduling as well as ordering supplies fort heart classes. I don''t know who Ms.Reddy spoke to. According to our refund policy on the Tucson Adult School Web site, refunds are only granted if they are requested before the class begins or if there is a documented health reason for dropping the class. In the case of a health reason, the amount of the refund will be based on the number of classes completed. Maybe Ms.Reddy can attend your second semester class instead of this semester''s.That would be my suggestion. Bridget Morandi"}],"question":"What does Ms.Morandi suggest that Ms.Reddymay be able to do?","bilingual":"Cô Morandi gợi ý rằng cô Reddy có thể làm gì?","options":["Use her previously paid tuition to take a future class","Find the same class at another adult school","Attend half the class and still receive credit","Contact the teacher to arrange for private tutoring"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Use her previously paid tuition to take a future class\".","vocabList":[{"word":"previously","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpriviəsli/","meaning":"trước; vào thời điểm sớm hơn; trong quá khứ; trước đây"},{"word":"commitment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmɪtmənt/","meaning":"nghĩa vụ; hứa"},{"word":"scheduling","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈskɛʤʊlɪŋ/","meaning":"lên lịch"},{"word":"suggestion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈdʒes.tʃən/","meaning":"sự đề xuất"}],"optionMeanings":["Sử dụng học phí đã đóng trước đây của cô ấy để tham gia một lớp học trong tương lai","Tìm cùng lớp ở trường người lớn khác","Tham dự một nửa buổi học và vẫn nhận được tín chỉ","Liên hệ với giáo viên để sắp xếp dạy kèm riêng"]},{"questionNum":"181","passageTitle":"New Bakery Coming to Town","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nNew Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nDear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"New Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Dear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton"}],"question":"What is indicated about Orevale City?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về OrevaleCity?","options":["It has little open land for development.","It has two warehouse districts.","It is home to a university.","It has a growing population."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It has little open land for development.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"},{"word":"development","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈvel.əp.mənt/","meaning":"sự phát triển"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"surrounding","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈraʊn.dɪŋ/","meaning":"bao quanh"}],"optionMeanings":["Nó có một vùng đất mở nhỏ để phát triển.","Nó có hai khu kho.","Đây là nơi có trường đại học.","Nó có dân số ngày càng tăng."]},{"questionNum":"182","passageTitle":"New Bakery Coming to Town","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nNew Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nDear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"New Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Dear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton"}],"question":"What is different about new Cresson''s Bakery locations?","bilingual":"Các địa điểm của newCresson''s Bakery có gì khác biệt?","options":["Theyreplicatehistoric architectural features.","They offer a wider variety of baked goods.","They do not offer seating for customers.","They are located outside of city centers."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Theyreplicatehistoric architectural features.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"surrounding","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈraʊn.dɪŋ/","meaning":"bao quanh"},{"word":"convenient","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈvinjənt/","meaning":"thoải mái; hữu ích; có thể sử dụng được"}],"optionMeanings":["Chúng tái tạo các đặc điểm kiến ​​trúc lịch sử.","Họ cung cấp nhiều loại bánh nướng hơn","Họ không cung cấp chỗ ngồi cho khách hàng.","Chúng nằm bên ngoài trung tâm thành phố. hơn. (C) Họ không cung cấp chỗ ngồi cho khách hàng. (D) Chúng ở bên ngoài trung tâm thành phố."]},{"questionNum":"183","passageTitle":"New Bakery Coming to Town","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nNew Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nDear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"New Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Dear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton"}],"question":"What is indicated about Mr.Lu?","bilingual":"Điều gì nói lên điều gì về ông Lữ?","options":["He is Ms.Holton''s next-door neighbor.","He plans topatronize Cresson''s Bakery.","He recently moved to Orevale City.","Heis a member of a historic preservation group."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"He is Ms.Holton''s next-door neighbor.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"surrounding","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈraʊn.dɪŋ/","meaning":"bao quanh"},{"word":"convenient","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈvinjənt/","meaning":"thoải mái; hữu ích; có thể sử dụng được"}],"optionMeanings":["Anh ấy là hàng xóm của cô Holton.","Anh ấy dự định bảo trợ Cresson''sBakery.","Anh ấy mới chuyển đến Thành phố Orevale.","Anh ấy là thành viên của nhóm bảo tồn lịch sử."]},{"questionNum":"184","passageTitle":"New Bakery Coming to Town","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nNew Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nDear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"New Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Dear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton"}],"question":"Where did Ms.Holton take photos of vehicle traffic?","bilingual":"Cô Holton đã chụp ảnh phương tiện giao thông ở đâu?","options":["On Canton Avenue","On Wofford Drive","On Ridley Street","On Paxton Road"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"On Canton Avenue\".","vocabList":[{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"surrounding","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈraʊn.dɪŋ/","meaning":"bao quanh"},{"word":"convenient","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈvinjənt/","meaning":"thoải mái; hữu ích; có thể sử dụng được"}],"optionMeanings":["Trên Đại lộ Canton","Trên Wofford Drive","Trên phố Ridley","Trên đường Paxton"]},{"questionNum":"185","passageTitle":"New Bakery Coming to Town","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nNew Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nDear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"New Bakery Coming to Town\n\nOREVALECITY(October 14)-A | The bakery will occupy Canton Avenue''s\n\nCresson''s Bakery is opening soon at the | smallest vacant lot. Approval for the\n\ncorner of Canton Avenue and Ridley | project followed a public hearing where\n\nStreet. The location will be the national | area residents voiced mixed opinions.\n\nchain''s first within the city limits. Like all Gina Holton, who lives on Paxton Road,\n\nCresson''s Bakery stores, it will operate | said she liked the idea of having a new\n\nseven days a week. | bakery in her neighborhood but worries\n\nThe only similar business in the vicinity | about traffic congestion on Ridley Street.\n\nis the Donut Station on the Kupperman | As evidence, she presented pictures of\n\nUniversity campus. Cresson''s Bakery will heavy vehicle traffic there. Wofford Drive offer breakfast sandwiches andfruitjuices resident Steven Lu said he would enjoy\n\nin addition to its signature coffee and | having a convenient place to grab a quick\n\nbaked goods. The company is following | snack.\n\nits revised business model to open | Cresson''s Bakery is slated to welcome its\n\ncompact facilities rather than sit-down | first customers in early March.\n\neateries. This means the Orevale City location will offer takeout and drive- through service only."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Dear Editor, As a lifelong resident of Orevale City, I appreciate your coverage of Cresson''s Bakery. Unfortunately, the October 14 article contained some inaccurate information. The photos that I shared during the public hearing captured images of traffic congestion in front of my house. Also, as a member of the city''s Historic Preservation Committee, I was primarily concerned about thebakery''s architecture. The initial building design for Cresson''s Bakery was contemporary.I am pleased to report that the chain has agreed to modify the exterior so that it blends in better with the older structures surrounding it. Sincerely, Gina Holton"}],"question":"What does the letter suggest about Ms.Holton?","bilingual":"Bức thư gợi ý điều gì về cô Holton?","options":["She is happy that a building design was changed.","She is planning to start her own bakery business.","She did not attend a public hearing","She wants to submit an article to the newspaper."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"She is happy that a building design was changed.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"surrounding","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈraʊn.dɪŋ/","meaning":"bao quanh"},{"word":"convenient","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈvinjənt/","meaning":"thoải mái; hữu ích; có thể sử dụng được"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy rất vui vì thiết kế tòa nhà đã được thay đổi.","Cô ấy đang có ý định bắt đầu kinh doanh tiệm bánh của riêng mình.","Cô ấy đã không tham dự buổi điều trần công khai.","Cô ấy muốn gửi một bài báo cho tờ báo."]},{"questionNum":"186","passageTitle":"Brandy Mortimer Raxconnect, Inc. 620WeirRoad Glasgow G919HX","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nBrandy Mortimer Raxconnect, Inc. 620WeirRoad Glasgow G919HX\n\n11 March\n\nAlyssa Susilo 29 Lefroy Street GlasgowG37BQ\n\nDear Ms. Susilo,\n\nAs you may know, Raxconnect has been expanding its services in the Glasgow area over the past year. Our new fibre-optic cable lines offer faster and more reliable\n\nwork, we need to install Internet connection devices throughout the city. Phase 1 of our construction work involved City Centre. Phase2involvedWestEnd. Although Phase2tooklongerthan expected, we were able to expeditePhase3andgetback on schedule. Phase 4 is now ready to begin in your area.\n\nRaxconnect would like to place a small Internet connection hub on your property at 29LefroyStreet. Because of its central location on the street, your front yard would make an optimal connection point. Please call us at 0141 496 0001 by 10 April to let us know whether we may proceed. Thank you.\n\nSincerely, Brandy Mortimer Brandy Mortimer, Utilities Adviser\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nRaxconnect Expands Service\n\nGLASGOW (14 March)—After unexpected delays in West End, Raxconnect has finally completed the latest phase of its project to install fibre-optic cable throughout the city. Residents and businesses in Southside are now enjoying faster Internet service. For the next phase of the project, in Finnieston, Raxconnect has identified key locations for connection hubs and is currently reaching out to residents and homeowners so that work can begin as soon as possible. The moves follow an announcement made earlier this year that Raxconnect had invested f350 million to expand its network. Local officials hope that the project brings new business and spending to their neighbourhoods.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nNotice of Temporary Road Closure\n\nPlease be aware that construction at 29 Lefroy Street will result in the closure of the entire street. The closure will last from Monday,31 May, until Tuesday,8 June. During that period, automobile access will be limited to residents who live on Lefroy Street.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Brandy Mortimer Raxconnect, Inc. 620WeirRoad Glasgow G919HX\n\n11 March\n\nAlyssa Susilo 29 Lefroy Street GlasgowG37BQ\n\nDear Ms. Susilo,\n\nAs you may know, Raxconnect has been expanding its services in the Glasgow area over the past year. Our new fibre-optic cable lines offer faster and more reliable\n\nwork, we need to install Internet connection devices throughout the city. Phase 1 of our construction work involved City Centre. Phase2involvedWestEnd. Although Phase2tooklongerthan expected, we were able to expeditePhase3andgetback on schedule. Phase 4 is now ready to begin in your area.\n\nRaxconnect would like to place a small Internet connection hub on your property at 29LefroyStreet. Because of its central location on the street, your front yard would make an optimal connection point. Please call us at 0141 496 0001 by 10 April to let us know whether we may proceed. Thank you.\n\nSincerely, Brandy Mortimer Brandy Mortimer, Utilities Adviser"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Raxconnect Expands Service\n\nGLASGOW (14 March)—After unexpected delays in West End, Raxconnect has finally completed the latest phase of its project to install fibre-optic cable throughout the city. Residents and businesses in Southside are now enjoying faster Internet service. For the next phase of the project, in Finnieston, Raxconnect has identified key locations for connection hubs and is currently reaching out to residents and homeowners so that work can begin as soon as possible. The moves follow an announcement made earlier this year that Raxconnect had invested f350 million to expand its network. Local officials hope that the project brings new business and spending to their neighbourhoods."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"Notice of Temporary Road Closure\n\nPlease be aware that construction at 29 Lefroy Street will result in the closure of the entire street. The closure will last from Monday,31 May, until Tuesday,8 June. During that period, automobile access will be limited to residents who live on Lefroy Street."}],"question":"What is the main purpose of the letter?","bilingual":"Mục đích chính của lá thư là gì?","options":["To apologize for poor Internet service","To seek permission from a property owner","To provide an explanation for a delay","To persuade acustomer to switch Internet providers"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"To apologize for poor Internet service\".","vocabList":[{"word":"construction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"xây dựng; kết cấu; ngành xây dựng tòa nhà"},{"word":"announcement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈnaʊnsmɛnt/","meaning":"tuyên ngôn; để ý; hành động thông báo cho công chúng"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"apologize","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","i