ade earlier this year that Raxconnect had invested f350 million to expand its network. Local officials hope that the project brings new business and spending to their neighbourhoods.\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nNotice of Temporary Road Closure\n\nPlease be aware that construction at 29 Lefroy Street will result in the closure of the entire street. The closure will last from Monday,31 May, until Tuesday,8 June. During that period, automobile access will be limited to residents who live on Lefroy Street.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Brandy Mortimer Raxconnect, Inc. 620WeirRoad Glasgow G919HX\n\n11 March\n\nAlyssa Susilo 29 Lefroy Street GlasgowG37BQ\n\nDear Ms. Susilo,\n\nAs you may know, Raxconnect has been expanding its services in the Glasgow area over the past year. Our new fibre-optic cable lines offer faster and more reliable\n\nwork, we need to install Internet connection devices throughout the city. Phase 1 of our construction work involved City Centre. Phase2involvedWestEnd. Although Phase2tooklongerthan expected, we were able to expeditePhase3andgetback on schedule. Phase 4 is now ready to begin in your area.\n\nRaxconnect would like to place a small Internet connection hub on your property at 29LefroyStreet. Because of its central location on the street, your front yard would make an optimal connection point. Please call us at 0141 496 0001 by 10 April to let us know whether we may proceed. Thank you.\n\nSincerely, Brandy Mortimer Brandy Mortimer, Utilities Adviser"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"Raxconnect Expands Service\n\nGLASGOW (14 March)—After unexpected delays in West End, Raxconnect has finally completed the latest phase of its project to install fibre-optic cable throughout the city. Residents and businesses in Southside are now enjoying faster Internet service. For the next phase of the project, in Finnieston, Raxconnect has identified key locations for connection hubs and is currently reaching out to residents and homeowners so that work can begin as soon as possible. The moves follow an announcement made earlier this year that Raxconnect had invested f350 million to expand its network. Local officials hope that the project brings new business and spending to their neighbourhoods."},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"Notice of Temporary Road Closure\n\nPlease be aware that construction at 29 Lefroy Street will result in the closure of the entire street. The closure will last from Monday,31 May, until Tuesday,8 June. During that period, automobile access will be limited to residents who live on Lefroy Street."}],"question":"190.What does the notice suggest about people who live on Lefroy Street?","bilingual":"Thông báo gợi ý điều gì về những người sống trên Phố Lefroy?","options":["They will have access to a shuttle service to their homes.","They will receive free Internet service for one week.","They will be asked to fill out a form when Raxconnect''s work is done.","They will be able to use the street during construction."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"They will have access to a shuttle service to their homes.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"construction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"xây dựng; kết cấu; ngành xây dựng tòa nhà"},{"word":"announcement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈnaʊnsmɛnt/","meaning":"tuyên ngôn; để ý; hành động thông báo cho công chúng"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"completed","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/kəmˈplitɪd/","meaning":"đã hoàn thành"}],"optionMeanings":["Họ sẽ có quyền sử dụng dịch vụ đưa đón đến nhà của họ.","Họ sẽ nhận được dịch vụ Internet miễn phí trong một tuần.","Họ sẽ được yêu cầu điền vào biểu mẫu khi công việc của Raxconnect hoàn thành.","Họ sẽ có thể sử dụng công trình đường phố trong quá trình xây dựng."]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nhttps://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"https://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!"}],"question":"What is announced in the press release?","bilingual":"Thông cáo báo chí được công bố gì?","options":["The merger of two companies","The retirement of a company''s leaders","The expansion of a product line","The relocation of a production plant"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"The merger of two companies\".","vocabList":[{"word":"retirement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈtaɪərmənt/","meaning":"sự ẩn dật, sự về hưu"},{"word":"production","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pərˈdəkʃən/","meaning":"sản xuất; cuộc họp; đầu ra; năng suất"},{"word":"expansion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspæn.ʃən/","meaning":"sử mở rộng, giãn nở"},{"word":"president","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɛzɪdənt/","meaning":"cái đầu; lãnh đạo; chủ tịch; người đứng đầu"}],"optionMeanings":["Việc sáp nhập hai công ty","Lãnh đạo một công ty nghỉ hưu","Việc mở rộng dòng sản phẩm","Việc di dời nhà máy sản xuất (C) Việc mở rộng một dòng sản phẩm (D) Việc di chuyển một nhà sản xuất"]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nhttps://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"https://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!"}],"question":"What does the press release suggest about Albert and Annie''s South Africandivision?","bilingual":"Thông cáo báo chí gợi ý điều gì về khu vực Nam Phi của Albert và Annie?","options":["It will open in mid-November.","It will not be hiring until mid-December.","It will soon launch its own Web site.","It will not sell ice cream directly to consumers."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It will open in mid-November.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"president","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɛzɪdənt/","meaning":"cái đầu; lãnh đạo; chủ tịch; người đứng đầu"},{"word":"interview","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.t̬ɚ.vjuː/","meaning":"phỏng vấn"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"},{"word":"directly","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈrɛkli/","meaning":"ngay sau đây; khoảnh khắc đó; càng sớm càng"}],"optionMeanings":["Nó sẽ mở vào giữa tháng 11.","Nó sẽ không được tuyển dụng cho đến giữa Tháng mười hai.","Nó sẽ sớm ra mắt trang Web của riêng mình.","Nó sẽ không bán kem trực tiếp cho người tiêu dùng."]},{"questionNum":"193","passageTitle":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich