se would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"https://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!"}],"question":"What is indicated about Ms.Both a?","bilingual":"Những gì được chỉ ra về Ms. Botha?","options":["She plans to attend the Wooden Sailboat Festival.","She grew up in the Cape Town area.","She wants to talk to Mr.and Ms.Grundon.","She applied for a job in Albert and Annie''s South African division."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"She plans to attend the Wooden Sailboat Festival.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"president","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɛzɪdənt/","meaning":"cái đầu; lãnh đạo; chủ tịch; người đứng đầu"},{"word":"interview","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.t̬ɚ.vjuː/","meaning":"phỏng vấn"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"},{"word":"division","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈvɪʒən/","meaning":"phân vùng; phòng; giảng viên; xếp hạng; mức độ"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô dự định tham dự Lễ hội Thuyền buồm Gỗ.","Cô lớn lên ở khu vực Cape Town.","Cô muốn nói chuyện với ông bà Grundon.","Cô ấy đã nộp đơn xin việc ở bộ phận Nam Phi của Albert và Annie."]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nhttps://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"FORIMMEDIATERELEASE Contact:Kevin Oessenich, kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au GOOLWA(2 November)Yesterday, Albert and Annie''s, a leading maker of gourmet frozen desserts, unveiled several new treats:Triple Time Chocolate ice cream, a waltz of light and dark chocolate with a chocolate crumb swirl Toffee Spree, a vanilla and toffee ice cream with sweet biscuit infusions; and a raspberry sorbet, featuring bits of real fruit. The new products are expected to be in Australian stores by mid-November. The company was founded 25 years ago by Albert and Annie Grundon, president and CEO, respectively. Earlier this year, they announced the opening of a South African division. South African retailers will get access to a number of Albert and Annie''s products in mid-December."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | Kevin Oessenich <kevin.o@albertandannies.com.au> From: | Skye Both a <sbotha@westerncapeeats.co.za> Date: | 3 November\n\nSubject: | Interview request\n\nDear Mr.Oessenich,\n\nI am a reporter for Western Cape Eats, a news site for food lovers in the Cape Town area. I would very much like to interview one or both of your company''s founders about your products and to find out which products will be available here in South Africa. My readers are eager to know what to expect. Readers would also like to know if Albert and Annie''s will be promoting itself at this year''s Wooden Sailboat Festival. Most local businesses rent booths there as it is a major event. The interview can be conducted by phone or video chat. I look forward to your reply.\n\nSincerely, Skye Both a"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"https://www.westerncapeeats.co.za/reviews About | News | Events | Reviews\n\nJim Sato,31 December\n\nYour article informing me about Albert and Annie''s, an ice-cream company that just came to South Africa, gave me one more reason to attend the annual Wooden Sailboat Festival.I got to sample some sensational ice creams at Albert and Annie''s booth. The booth offered three amazing flavours:Coffee Truffle, Fudge Mint, and Chocolate Pretzel Delight. In your article, Mr.Oessenich stated that these would be the first flavours to be rolled out to grocery outlets in South Africa and that more will become available over time. Ican''t wait!"}],"question":"What can be concluded about Albert and Annie''s booth at the festival?","bilingual":"","options":["It was staffed by Mr.Oessenich.","It did not have coffee ice cream when Mr. Sato arrived.","It was one of three booths featuring frozen desserts.","It did not offer samples of the company''s newest flavors."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It was staffed by Mr.Oessenich.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"president","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɛzɪdənt/","meaning":"cái đầu; lãnh đạo; chủ tịch; người đứng đầu"},{"word":"interview","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.t̬ɚ.vjuː/","meaning":"phỏng vấn"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"},{"word":"conclude","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kənˈkluːd/","meaning":"kết thúc, chấm dứt, kết luận"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nBen''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nwww.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard."}],"question":"What is the purpose of the blog post?","bilingual":"Mục đích của bài đăng trên blog là gì?","options":["To provide grant-writing tips","To recommend a learning experience","To spotlight an employee","Top review changes to a Website"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To recommend a learning experience\".","vocabList":[{"word":"international","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.t̬ɚˈnæʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"quốc tế, đa quốc gia"},{"word":"registration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,redʤis''treiʃn/","meaning":"sự đăng ký, sự ghi vào sổ"},{"word":"application","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌæp.ləˈkeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"ứng dụng, sự áp dụng"},{"word":"description","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"bản mô tả, sự mô tả"}],"optionMeanings":["Để cung cấp các mẹo viết tài trợ","khuyến nghị kinh nghiệm học tập","Để làm nổi bật một nhân viên","Để xem trước các thay đổi đối với một trang Web"]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nBen''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nwww.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard."}],"question":"According to Mr.Fine man, when does the registration period end?","bilingual":"Theo ông Fineman, khi nào thời gian đăng ký kết thúc?","options":["OnSeptember30","On October 1","On November 1","OnDecember6"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"On November 1\".","vocabList":[{"word":"international","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.t̬ɚˈnæʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"quốc tế, đa quốc gia"},{"word":"registration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,redʤis''treiʃn/","meaning":"sự đăng ký, sự ghi vào sổ"},{"word":"application","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌæp.ləˈkeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"ứng dụng, sự áp dụng"},{"word":"description","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"bản mô tả, sự mô tả"}],"optionMeanings":["Vào ngày 30 tháng 9","Vào ngày 1 tháng 10","Vào ngày 1 tháng 11","Ngày 6 tháng 12"]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nBen''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nwww.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard."}],"question":"What is indicated about Ms.Ballard?","bilingual":"Những gì được chỉ ra về Ms. Ballard?","options":["She registered for the grant-writing coursebeforeOctober1.","She currently works as a grant writer.","She took a course from Ms.Gilliam on a previous occasion.","She edits Mr.Fine man''s blog posts. Stop! This is the end of the test. If you finish before time is called, you may go backtoParts5,6,and7andcheckyourwork."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"She registered for the grant-writing coursebeforeOctober1.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"international","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.t̬ɚˈnæʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"quốc tế, đa quốc gia"},{"word":"registration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/,redʤis''treiʃn/","meaning":"sự đăng ký, sự ghi vào sổ"},{"word":"application","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌæp.ləˈkeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"ứng dụng, sự áp dụng"},{"word":"description","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"bản mô tả, sự mô tả"}],"optionMeanings":["Cô ấy đã đăng ký khóa học viết văn trước ngày 1 tháng 10.","Cô ấy hiện đang làm người viết tài trợ.","Cô đã tham gia một khóa học từ cô Gilliamon vào dịp trước.","Cô ấy chỉnh sửa các bài đăng trên blog của ông Fineman."]},{"questionNum":"199","passageTitle":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nBen''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to December 6. For details and registration, visit www.kristinagilliam.ca/course,Use the promo code NPBURST at checkout to get 15 percent off the $350 tuition, This code expires on September 30. On October 1, only full-price registration will be available until the final registration day, Novemberl. www.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name:Natalie Ballard\n\nLocation: Winnipeg\n\nComment: Relatively short compared to other writing courses I''ve taken, Writing Great Grants provided a decent overview. I was impressed to learn that the instructor helped companies get millions of dollars in grants during her career, and\n\nFortunately, I used Ben''s Nonprofit Burst''s promo code when I registered. Otherwise, d have considered the tuition too high. The Web site gave me the impression that Ms. Gilliam would include more specifics about the actual writing process than she did.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nwww.kristinagilliam.ca/feedback Thank you for participating in my Writing Great Grants course. Please take a moment to tell me about your experience by filling out the form below. Name: Paul Voigt Location: Toronto\n\nComment: This was a great course overall. The instructor shared a wealth of valuable in sights, including her experiences as the founder of Orden International. I never realized that grant-writing firms even existed! I might start one of my own\n\nresearching grant opportunities and analyzing. samples of successful grant applications. When several of us asked for specific writing tips during the final session, Ms. Gilliam simply referred us to other resources. The course description on her Web site was a bit misleading in that regard.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Ben''s Nonprofit Burst-Resources for those who work in the nonprofit sector\n\nGetting Grants\n\nPosted on August 18 by Ben Fine man\n\nGrant writing is the art of completing applications for financial aid offered by government agencies, schools, corporations, or other entities, There is huge competition for grants and no room for mediocrity in grant writing. To improve your grant-writing skills, consider taking an online course taught by Kristina Gilliam of Meadow Park University. Her Writing Great Grants course is divided into four 90-minute interactive sessions. It is designed for people with some basic knowledge of grant writing. These Monday cvcning classcs run from Novcmbcr 15 to Decembe