ents don''t wait-if we don''t respond to their requests immediately, they move on to the next supplier. Nicolette Kone (11:02 A.M.) That''s true. I''l let you know if I get any updates."}],"question":"At11:02A.M., what does Ms.Konemost likely mean when she writes, \"That''s true\"?","bilingual":"","options":["She feels that the supplier makes unreasonable requests.","She understands that customers can be impatient.","She thinks her company needs a new service provider.","She expects to receive a status update soon."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"She understands that customers can be impatient.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"understand","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈstænd/","meaning":"hiểu, nắm bắt được"},{"word":"important","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪmˈpɔrtənt/","meaning":"có ý nghĩa; có ảnh hưởng; thiết yếu; chủ yếu; phê bình"},{"word":"supplier","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈplaɪ.ɚ/","meaning":"nhà cung cấp"},{"word":"customer","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkʌs.tə.mɚ/","meaning":"khách hàng"}]},{"questionNum":"153","passageTitle":"Attention! Some park visitors have been intentionally stacking piles of roc","passageText":"Attention! Some park visitors have been intentionally stacking piles of rocks as an art form or for amusement. Please refrain from doing this on park grounds, as these unofficial rock stacks can disrupt sensitive habitats and affect the area''s natural beauty. New rock piles can also end anger hikers who traditionally rely on stacked rock markers as navigational tools. Park officials are the only ones who should be stacking rocks, and they do so strategically on trails where the path may be unclear. If you see rocks that have been stacked, please leave them alone, and do not create confusion by making your own stack.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Attention! Some park visitors have been intentionally stacking piles of rocks as an art form or for amusement. Please refrain from doing this on park grounds, as these unofficial rock stacks can disrupt sensitive habitats and affect the area''s natural beauty. New rock piles can also end anger hikers who traditionally rely on stacked rock markers as navigational tools. Park officials are the only ones who should be stacking rocks, and they do so strategically on trails where the path may be unclear. If you see rocks that have been stacked, please leave them alone, and do not create confusion by making your own stack."}],"question":"What is the purpose of the sign?","bilingual":"Mục đích của biển hiệu là gì?","options":["To describe a historic monument","To warn hikers about dangerous trails","To change a behavior of visitors","To ask for help with a building project 212"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"To change a behavior of visitors\".","vocabList":[{"word":"attention","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈtɛnʃən/","meaning":"sự tập trung; xem xét; tập trung; chăm sóc;"},{"word":"sensitive","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɛnsɪtɪv/","meaning":"có khả năng cảm nhận; dễ bị"},{"word":"describe","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈskraɪb/","meaning":"minh họa; để giải thích; để mô tả; để làm sáng tỏ"},{"word":"monument","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mɔnjumənt/","meaning":"vật kỷ niệm, đài kỷ niệm, bia kỷ niệm"}],"optionMeanings":["Để mô tả một di tích lịch sử","Để cảnh báo những người đi bộ đường dài về những con đường nguy hiểm","Để thay đổi hành vi của khách truy cập","Để yêu cầu trợ giúp về một dự án xây dựng"]},{"questionNum":"154","passageTitle":"Attention! Some park visitors have been intentionally stacking piles of roc","passageText":"Attention! Some park visitors have been intentionally stacking piles of rocks as an art form or for amusement. Please refrain from doing this on park grounds, as these unofficial rock stacks can disrupt sensitive habitats and affect the area''s natural beauty. New rock piles can also end anger hikers who traditionally rely on stacked rock markers as navigational tools. Park officials are the only ones who should be stacking rocks, and they do so strategically on trails where the path may be unclear. If you see rocks that have been stacked, please leave them alone, and do not create confusion by making your own stack.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Attention! Some park visitors have been intentionally stacking piles of rocks as an art form or for amusement. Please refrain from doing this on park grounds, as these unofficial rock stacks can disrupt sensitive habitats and affect the area''s natural beauty. New rock piles can also end anger hikers who traditionally rely on stacked rock markers as navigational tools. Park officials are the only ones who should be stacking rocks, and they do so strategically on trails where the path may be unclear. If you see rocks that have been stacked, please leave them alone, and do not create confusion by making your own stack."}],"question":"According to the sign, what do park officials do?","bilingual":"","options":["They coordinate group activities.","Họ tạo ra những vật đánh dấu định hướng","Họcấp giấy phép (sửdụng) tài nguyên","They grant access to a scenic overlook."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Họ tạo ra những vật đánh dấu định hướng\".","vocabList":[{"word":"coordinate","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/koʊˈɔrdəˌneɪt/","meaning":"bình đẳng; tương đương; có cấp bậc hoặc quyền hạn ngang nhau"},{"word":"attention","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈtɛnʃən/","meaning":"sự tập trung; xem xé