e great work! Sincerely, Sita Kumar\n\n218"}],"question":"What is indicated about Ms. Kumar?","bilingual":"","options":["She is retiring from work.","She has started her own company.","She is relocating to be closer to her relatives.","She completed an internship at Aithal Research."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She is relocating to be closer to her relatives.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"internship","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.tɝːn.ʃɪp/","meaning":"kỳ thực tập"},{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"},{"word":"commitment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmɪtmənt/","meaning":"nghĩa vụ; hứa"},{"word":"appreciate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈpriː.ʃi.eɪt/","meaning":"đánh giá cao, cảm kích"}]},{"questionNum":"175","passageTitle":"From: | Sita J.Kumar","passageText":"From: | Sita J.Kumar\n\nTo: | Homestead Natural Pharmaceuticals Staff\n\nSubject: | News\n\nDate: | October 10\n\n[1] -, Thank you all for the wonderful fifteen years I have spent with Homestead Natural Pharmaceuticals. I am especially grateful for all the coworkers and mentors I have worked with over the years. Moreover, for those who worked on the projects that I directed, your commitment to developing safe, effective medicines has always been appreciated.—[2]. I will be returning to India to be near my extended family.—[3] —. However, I am not leaving the field. I will be taking a job with Aithal Research, where I will continue the work of making natural pharmaceuticals.[4]. I wish you all the best. Keep up the great work! Sincerely, Sita Kumar\n\n218","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"From: | Sita J.Kumar\n\nTo: | Homestead Natural Pharmaceuticals Staff\n\nSubject: | News\n\nDate: | October 10\n\n[1] -, Thank you all for the wonderful fifteen years I have spent with Homestead Natural Pharmaceuticals. I am especially grateful for all the coworkers and mentors I have worked with over the years. Moreover, for those who worked on the projects that I directed, your commitment to developing safe, effective medicines has always been appreciated.—[2]. I will be returning to India to be near my extended family.—[3] —. However, I am not leaving the field. I will be taking a job with Aithal Research, where I will continue the work of making natural pharmaceuticals.[4]. I wish you all the best. Keep up the great work! Sincerely, Sita Kumar\n\n218"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked[1],[2].[3] and[4] does the following sentence best belong? \"I am proud that, together, we have made positive advances in our industry.\"","bilingual":"Vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4] nào phù hợp nhất với câu sau đây? \"Tôi tự hào rằng, cùng nhau, chúng ta đã đạt được những tiến bộ tích cực trong ngành của mình.\"","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"[2]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"},{"word":"commitment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmɪtmənt/","meaning":"nghĩa vụ; hứa"},{"word":"appreciate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈpriː.ʃi.eɪt/","meaning":"đánh giá cao, cảm kích"},{"word":"effective","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈfek.tɪv/","meaning":"hiệu quả, có hiệu lực"}],"optionMeanings":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4] BÃN DỊCH: Đến: Sita J. KumarTừ: Nhân sựHomestead Natural PharmaceuticalsChủ đề: Bản tinNgày: Ngày 10 tháng 10 – [1] –. Cảm ơn bạn vì khoảng thời gian 15 năm tuyệt vời vừa đủ mà tôi đã dành cho Homestead Natural Pharmaceuticals. Tôi đặc biệt biết rõ về toàn bộ đồng nghiệp và hướng dẫn mà tôi đã làm việc cùng trong nhiều năm. Hơn nữa, với những người từng làm việc với dự án mà tôi chỉ đạo, bạn có thể kết thúc việc phát triển các loại thuốc an toàn và hiệu quảluôn quan trọng. – [2] –. Tôi sẽ quay lại Ấn Độ để được mở bên cạnh gia đình tôi. – [3] –. Tuy nhiên, tôi sẽ không rời bỏ điều này. Tôi sẽ nhận việc tại Aithal Research, nơi mà tôi sẽ tiếp tục công việc tạo ra sản phẩm từ thiên nhiên. – [4] –. Tôi chúc các bạn những điều tốt đẹp nhất. Hãy tiếp tục phát huy nhé! Trân trọng, Sita Kumar"]},{"questionNum":"176","passageTitle":"In the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaura","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nIn the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaurants work. Her new book, In the Kitchen: How to Thrive in the Restaurant Business, expertly advises restaurant managers on handling challenges in the industry, from creating reasonable schedules for chefs to appeasing picky diners. Throughout the book, Chien offers concise, practical suggestions with easy-to-understand concepts. Overall, the book offers a colorful snapshot of the various tasks involved in the day-to-day operations of a restaurant. Chien''s book is unique among other industry guides in that she interviewed restaurant owners, managers, and customers as part of her research. She even spoke to journalists who write restaurant reviews to get a good sense of what they most prize in a dining experience, My only criticism is that the book should have also included the perspective of chefs, especially since their role is crucial to a restaurant''s success. This caveat aside, In the Kitchen is an insightful and instructive read.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | editor@lakecountyherald.com From: | qichien@rapidonline.com Date: | August 5\n\nSubject: | In the Kitchen\n\nTo the Editor: I was delighted to read Peter Gottlieb''s review of my latest book, In the Kitchen, in your newspaper.I have appreciated his thoughtful comments about my works over the years, even if they are sometimes negative. In this case, I was especialiy glad that he liked the chapter about restaurant reviewers, since initially I had been reluctant to interview journalists for the book. It is true that I could have included a greater variety of in sights, but unfortunately the people whose views he most wanted to hear were just too busy to an updated edition of the book. speak with me before the publishing deadline. Perhaps this is something I can address in\n\nQi Chien\n\n220","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"In the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaurants work. Her new book, In the Kitchen: How to Thrive in the Restaurant Business, expertly advises restaurant managers on handling challenges in the industry, from creating reasonable schedules for chefs to appeasing picky diners. Throughout the book, Chien offers concise, practical suggestions with easy-to-understand concepts. Overall, the book offers a colorful snapshot of the various tasks involved in the day-to-day operations of a restaurant. Chien''s book is unique among other industry guides in that she interviewed restaurant owners, managers, and customers as part of her research. She even spoke to journalists who write restaurant reviews to get a good sense of what they most prize in a dining experience, My only criticism is that the book should have also included the perspective of chefs, especially since their role is crucial to a restaurant''s success. This caveat aside, In the Kitchen is an insightful and instructive read."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | editor@lakecountyherald.com From: | qichien@rapidonline.com Date: | August 5\n\nSubject: | In the Kitchen\n\nTo the Editor: I was delighted to read Peter Gottlieb''s review of my latest book, In the Kitchen, in your newspaper.I have appreciated his thoughtful comments about my works over the years, even if they are sometimes negative. In this case, I was especialiy glad that he liked the chapter about restaurant reviewers, since initially I had been reluctant to interview journalists for the book. It is true that I could have included a greater variety of in sights, but unfortunately the people whose views he most wanted to hear were just too busy to an updated edition of the book. speak with me before the publishing deadline. Perhaps this is something I can address in\n\nQi Chien\n\n220"}],"question":"What is the focus of Ms.Chien''s book?","bilingual":"Trọng tâm cuốn sách của cô Chiến là gì?","options":["How to properly train chefs","How to develop recipes","How to manage a restaurant","How to write an engaging story"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"How to manage a restaurant\".","vocabList":[{"word":"restaurants","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrɛˌstrɑnts/","meaning":"Nhà hàng"},{"word":"restaurant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrɛˌstrɑnt/","meaning":"Nhà hàng"},{"word":"understand","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈstænd/","meaning":"hiểu, nắm bắt được"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"}],"optionMeanings":["Cách đào tạo đầu bếp đúng cách","Cách phát triển công thức nấu ăn","Cách quản lý một nhà hàng","Cách viết một câu chuyện hấp dẫn177. Ông Gottlieb chỉ ra điều gì về bài viết của cô Chiến? (A) Nó mang tính thông tin. (B) Nó đã lỗi thời. (C) Nó giàu trí tưởng tượng. (D) Nó được tổ chức tốt.178. Trong phần đánh giá, từ “sense” ở đoạn 2, dòng 3, gần nghĩa nhất với(A) Intelligence(B) idea(C) Chance (D) hướng179. Điều gì được gợi ý về Mr. Gottlieb trong e - thư à? (A) Anh ấy đã làm việc ở cùng công ty với cô Chiến. (B) Anh ấy đã gặp cô Chiến tại một hội nghị ngành nhà hàng. (C) Anh ấy đã được cô Chiến phỏng vấn cho một trong những cuốn sách của cô ấy. (D) Anh ấy đã xem xét các cuốn sách khác do cô Chiến viết."]},{"questionNum":"177","passageTitle":"In the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaura","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nIn the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaurants work. Her new book, In the Kitchen: How to Thrive in the Restaurant Business, expertly advises restaurant managers on handling challenges in the industry, from creating reasonable schedules for chefs to appeasing picky diners. Throughout the book, Chien offers concise, practical suggestions with easy-to-understand concepts. Overall, the book offers a colorful snapshot of the various tasks involved in the day-to-day operations of a restaurant. Chien''s book is unique among other industry guides in that she interviewed restaurant owners, managers, and customers as part of her research. She even spoke to journalists who write restaurant reviews to get a good sense of what they most prize in a dining experience, My only criticism is that the book should have also included the perspective of chefs, especially since their role is crucial to a restaurant''s success. This caveat aside, In the Kitchen is an insightful and instructive read.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | editor@lakecountyherald.com From: | qichien@rapidonline.com Date: | August 5\n\nSubject: | In the Kitchen\n\nTo the Editor: I was delighted to read Peter Gottlieb''s review of my latest book, In the Kitchen, in your newspaper.I have appreciated his thoughtful comments about my works over the years, even if they are sometimes negative. In this case, I was especialiy glad that he liked the chapter about restaurant reviewers, since initially I had been reluctant to interview journalists for the book. It is true that I could have included a greater variety of in sights, but unfortunately the people whose views he most wanted to hear were just too busy to an updated edition of the book. speak with me before the publishing deadline. Perhaps this is something I can address in\n\nQi Chien\n\n220","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"In the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaurants work. Her new book, In the Kitchen: How to Thrive in the Restaurant Business, expertly advises restaurant managers on handling challenges in the industry, from creating reasonable schedules for chefs to appeasing picky diners. Throughout the book, Chien offers concise, practical suggestions with easy-to-understand concepts. Overall, the book offers a colorful snapshot of the various tasks involved in the day-to-day operations of a restaurant. Chien''s book is unique among other industry guides in that she interviewed restaurant owners, managers, and customers as part of her research. She even spoke to journalists who write restaurant reviews to get a good sense of what they most prize in a dining experience, My only criticism is that the book should have also included the perspective of chefs, especially since their role is crucial to a restaurant''s success. This caveat aside, In the Kitchen is an insightful and instructive read."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | editor@lakecountyherald.com From: | qichien@rapidonline.com Date: | August 5\n\nSubject: | In the Kitchen\n\nTo the Editor: I was delighted to read Peter Gottlieb''s review of my latest book, In the Kitchen, in your newspaper.I have appreciated his thoughtful comments about my works over the years, even if they are sometimes negative. In this case, I was especialiy glad that he liked the chapter about restaurant reviewers, since initially I had been reluctant to interview journalists for the book. It is true that I could have included a greater variety of in sights, but unfortunately the people whose views he most wanted to hear were just too busy to an updated edition of the book. speak with me before the publishing deadline. Perhaps this is something I can address in\n\nQi Chien\n\n220"}],"question":"What does Mr.Gottlieb indicate about Ms. Chien''s writing?","bilingual":"","options":["It is informative.","It is outdated.","It is imaginative.","It is well organized."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It is informative.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"restaurants","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrɛˌstrɑnts/","meaning":"Nhà hàng"},{"word":"understand","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈstænd/","meaning":"hiểu, nắm bắt được"},{"word":"restaurant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrɛˌstrɑnt/","meaning":"Nhà hàng"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"}]},{"questionNum":"178","passageTitle":"In the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaura","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nIn the Kitchen Reviewed by Peter Gottlieb Qi Chien understands how restaurants work. Her new book, In the Kitchen: How to Thrive in the Restaurant Business, expertly advises restaurant managers on handling challenges in the industry, from creating reasonable schedules for chefs to appeasing picky diners. Throughout the book, Chien offers concise, practical suggestions with easy-to-understand concepts. Overall, the book offers a colorful snapshot of the various tasks involved in the day-to-day operations of a restaurant. Chien''s book is unique among other industry guides in that she interviewed restaurant owners, managers, and customers as part of her research. She even spoke to journalists who write restaurant reviews to get a good sense of what they most prize in a dining experience, My only criticism is that the book should have also included the perspective of chefs, especially since their role is crucial to a restaurant''s success. This caveat aside, In the Kitchen is an insightful and instructive read.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | editor@lakecountyherald.com