Four square Housing offers corporate housing with apartment units in the gr","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nFour square Housing offers corporate housing with apartment units in the greater Miltonville area. The apartments are fully furnished and include wire less Internet service. Floor plans and photos of apartment interiors can be viewed online. Center Tower Located in downtown Miltonville, the ten-story building has shops on the ground level. Center Tower is on the south west corner of Beeman Square, features a rooftop garden, and is close to public transportation. Angora Plaza Located near downtown Miltonville, the building has a self-service laundromat and a large parking garage. It is also close to two subway stations. Regent Apartments Located approximately six miles outside of Miltonville, the building features an on-site business center and is within walking distance of public transportation. Cityview Gardens Cityview Gardens is a complex of four two-story buildings located in Dayton, about a twenty-minute drive from downtown Miltonville. The property boasts a fitness center and a swimming pool and is adjacent to a community park.A bus line operates a route through the neighborhood.\n\nFrom: | gsteuber@wardertechnology.com\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nTo: | info@foursquarehousing.com Date: | July 12\n\nSubject: | Inquiry\n\nFour square Housing, I work in the human resources office of Warder Technology''s Miltonville division. We are seeking an apartment that can be used by employees from outside the area who will work at our headquarters temporarily. We need an apartment for employees who will be in Miltonville for two months or more. The apartment should have amenities like a gym and a pool. Sincerely, Gina Steuber\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\n224\n\nFrom: | info@foursquarehousing.com To: | gsteuber@wardertechnology.com Date: | July 12\n\nSubject: | Information you requested\n\nAttachment: Pricing Leases.pdf\n\nDear Ms.Steuber, Thank you for your interest in Four square Housing. We have a two-bedroom apartment that wii be available on August 15 that should meet your requirements. I have attached a price list for this unit and our other apartments as well. If you agree that this meets your needs, I can send a contract. I should point out that your corporate headquarters in Beeman Square is next to apartments owned by Four square. One apartment here will also become available in August. This would be very convenient if you have short-term visitors. Sincerely, Sam Flannery Leasing Agent","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Four square Housing offers corporate housing with apartment units in the greater Miltonville area. The apartments are fully furnished and include wire less Internet service. Floor plans and photos of apartment interiors can be viewed online. Center Tower Located in downtown Miltonville, the ten-story building has shops on the ground level. Center Tower is on the south west corner of Beeman Square, features a rooftop garden, and is close to public transportation. Angora Plaza Located near downtown Miltonville, the building has a self-service laundromat and a large parking garage. It is also close to two subway stations. Regent Apartments Located approximately six miles outside of Miltonville, the building features an on-site business center and is within walking distance of public transportation. Cityview Gardens Cityview Gardens is a complex of four two-story buildings located in Dayton, about a twenty-minute drive from downtown Miltonville. The property boasts a fitness center and a swimming pool and is adjacent to a community park.A bus line operates a route through the neighborhood.\n\nFrom: | gsteuber@wardertechnology.com"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"To: | info@foursquarehousing.com Date: | July 12\n\nSubject: | Inquiry\n\nFour square Housing, I work in the human resources office of Warder Technology''s Miltonville division. We are seeking an apartment that can be used by employees from outside the area who will work at our headquarters temporarily. We need an apartment for employees who will be in Miltonville for two months or more. The apartment should have amenities like a gym and a pool. Sincerely, Gina Steuber"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"224\n\nFrom: | info@foursquarehousing.com To: | gsteuber@wardertechnology.com Date: | July 12\n\nSubject: | Information you requested\n\nAttachment: Pricing Leases.pdf\n\nDear Ms.Steuber, Thank you for your interest in Four square Housing. We have a two-bedroom apartment that wii be available on August 15 that should meet your requirements. I have attached a price list for this unit and our other apartments as well. If you agree that this meets your needs, I can send a contract. I should point out that your corporate headquarters in Beeman Square is next to apartments owned by Four square. One apartment here will also become available in August. This would be very convenient if you have short-term visitors. Sincerely, Sam Flannery Leasing Agent"}],"question":"190.What does Mr.Flannery suggest about Warder Technology''s corporate headquarters?","bilingual":"","options":["It is a twenty-minute drive from Miltonville.","It is next to the Center Tower building.","It is on the same road as the Regent Apartments.","It has a large parking garage."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"It is next to the Center Tower building.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"transportation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌtræn.spɚˈteɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự vận chuyển"},{"word":"approximately","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈprɑksəmətli/","meaning":"gần như; Về; xung quanh; khoảng"},{"word":"headquarters","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈhedˌkwɔːr.t̬ɚz/","meaning":"sở chỉ huy, bộ chỉ huy"},{"word":"neighborhood","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","meaning":"hàng xóm"}]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nhttps://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"}],"question":"What is the purpose of the first e-mail?","bilingual":"Mục đích của khóa học đầu tiên là gì - thư à?","options":["To describe an upcoming inspection","To invite nurses to give feedback","To announce an employment opportunity","To request suggestions for naming a robot"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To invite nurses to give feedback\".","vocabList":[{"word":"opportunity","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɒpərˈtyunɪti/","meaning":"cơ hội, thời cơ, dịp may"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"inspection","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈspɛkʃən/","meaning":"hành động xem xét cẩn thận và phê phán; chính thức"},{"word":"employment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɔɪ.mənt/","meaning":"việc làm, sự thuê người làm"}],"optionMeanings":["Để mô tả cuộc kiểm tra sắp tới","Mời y tá đưa ra phản hồi","Để thông báo cơ hội việc làm","Để yêu cầu gợi ý đặt tên cho robot192. Deonardo đã thực hiện nhiệm vụ gì vào ngày 28 tháng 1? (A) Tôi đã phân tích dữ liệu sức khỏe của bệnh nhân. (B) Nó sao chép hồ sơ bệnh nhân. (C) Nó mang thuốc đến cho bệnh nhân. (D) Nó chơi nhạc để giải trí cho bệnh nhân.193. Trong e thứ hai -mail, cô Robertson nói gì về Deonardo? (A) Nó có màn hình trông giống như một khuôn mặt. (B) Nó hợp tác chặt chẽ với các bác sĩ. (C) Nó sẽ bắt đầu phục vụ bữa ăn cho bệnh nhân. (D) Nó có một đế sạc đặc biệt.194. Đề xuất nào của cô Duy mà công ty chế tạo robot có nhiều khả năng áp dụng nhất? (A) Robot bây giờ sẽ chơi trò chơi với bệnh nhân. (B) Robot sẽ có bánh xe êm hơn. (C) Robot sẽ phản hồi các lệnh bằng giọng nói. (D) Robot bây giờ sẽ có sẵn để chụp ảnh với bệnh nhân.195. Bệnh viện có kế hoạch làm gì trong thời gian tới? (A) Thay thế robot (B) Mua thêm robot (C) Quảng cáo robot của mình(D) Sửa chữa robotB ẢN DỊCH: Đến: Nhân viên điều dưỡng Everlast Từ: Gretchen RobertsonNgày: 3 tháng 2 Chủ đề: Kiểm tra phần mềm của DeonardoCảm ơn các bạn đã đồng ý làm việc với độ cao của Cybernetic Robotics khi họ thửnghiệm rô -Tuyên bố mới của họ, Deonardo, trong bệnh viện của chúng ta. Như mọi người đã biết, Deonardo được phát triển để cho phép bạn, nhân viên điều dưỡng của chúng ta, có nhiều thời gian để tập trung vào bệnh nhân. Đây là công việc thú vị. Đã 1 tháng trôi qua và Cyberbetic Robotics muốn biết về trải nghiệm của các bạn vớiDeonardo. Vui lòng truy cập đường liên kết sau để hoàn thành 1 bài khảo sát trực tuyến. Đội của họ đặc biệt muốn biết về trải nghiệm trả lời của bạn với Deonardo trong cuộc kiểm tra những người tại bang vào ngày 28 tháng 1. Khi kết thúc bài khảo sát, bạn có thể trả lời bất kỳ ý kiến bổ sung nào mà bạn có về - bốt. https://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/Trân quan trọng, Gretchen Bệnh RobertsonGiám đốc, viện Everlasthttps://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282Deonardo rất dễđđ để làm việc tương tự. Tôi thích công việc không phải nói cụ thể ngừng việc mà Deonardo cần làm. Khi tôi cập nhật thông tin bệnh nhân trong hệ thống tối của chúng, công việc của Deonardo cũng được cập nhật theo. Tôi có thểtập trung tốt hơn vào bệnh nhân của mình vì tôi biết Deonardo sẽlo những công việc nhỏ mà trước đây sử dụng rất nhiều thời gian của tôi. Deonardo đặc biệt hữuích trong công cuộc giá cấp tiểu bangvì nó đãgiao thuốc của bệnh nhân thay cho các điều dưỡng để chúng tôi không cần phải làm như vậy, và chúng tôi có thểtập trung vào công việc chăm sóc bệnh nhân. Tôi tin rằng Deonardo đã giúp chúng tôi trong công việc nhận những phản hồi tích cực từ thanh tra. Tôi mong rằng Deonardo có thể phản hồi bằng giọng nói. Và đôi khi, bánh xe của nó kêu cótkét khi nó di chuyển xung quanh. Nhưng các bệnh nhân thích xem nó hoạt động, và ai cũng muốn chụp ảnh với nó. Tôi tự hỏi liệu bạn có thểkhiến Deonardo đứng yên để ch chụp ảnhkhông?Lan Duy, Cử nhân Khoa học Điều dưỡng (BSN = Cử nhân Điều dưỡng) Đến: Nhân viên điều dưỡng Everlast Từ: Gretchen RobertsonNgày: 13 tháng 2 Chủ đề: Nội bộ phần mềm Deonardo Cảm ơn mọi người đã giúp đỡDeonardo, robot điều dưỡng của chúng ta. Tôi rất vui vì nhânviên của chúng tôi đã có thể tham gia vào công trình mang tính đột phá như vậy. Những người làm việc trực tiếp với Deonardo có thể chờ việc nó sẽ hoạt động hơi khác 1 min trong tuần tới. Nó sẽ được cài đặt để thực hiện 1 số nhiệm vụ mới. Trước đây, nó có khả năng điều dưỡng giữa các việc làm. Bây giờ, nó sẽgiành ra một chút thời gian để tương tác với những bệnh nhân có thể tạo kiểu dáng với nó. Khi Deonardo mở chế độ tương tác, đôi mắt mở trên màn hình LED sẽ có hình trái tim thay vì hình tròn khi nó đang mở chế độ làm việc. Cuối cùng, Bệnh viện sẽ mua thêm 2 con robot trong vài tháng tới để làm việc tại các khu vực khác của bệnh viện. Tôi báo giá các sản phẩm sẵn có của bạn khi làm việc cùng hệ thống mới này. Chúng tôi mong muốn tìm hiểu các robot có thể cải thiện hơn nữa với các trải nghiệm của nhân viên và bệnh nhân. Trân trọng, Gretchen RobertsonGiám đốc, Everlast viện"]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nhttps://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"}],"question":"What task did Deonardoperformon January 28?","bilingual":"","options":["It analyzed patients'' health data.","It made copies of patients'' re cords.","It brought medications to patients.","It played music to entertain patients."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"It brought medications to patients.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"},{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"},{"word":"additional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈdɪʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"thêm vào, phụ thêm"}]},{"questionNum":"193","passageTitle":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nhttps://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"}],"question":"In the second e-mail, what does Ms.Robertson indicate about Deonardo?","bilingual":"","options":["It has a display that looks like a face.","It works closely with doctors.","It will begin serving patients their meals.","It has a special charging base."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It has a display that looks like a face.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"},{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"},{"word":"additional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈdɪʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"thêm vào, phụ thêm"}]},{"questionNum":"194","passageTitle":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nhttps://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"}],"question":"What suggestion from Ms.Duy did the robotics company most likely apply?","bilingual":"","options":["The robot will now play games with patients.","The robot will get quieter wheels.","The robot will respond to voice commands.","The robot will now be available for photographs with patients."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"The robot will now be available for photographs with patients.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"photographs","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfoʊtəˌgræfs/","meaning":"Ảnh"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"suggestion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈdʒes.tʃən/","meaning":"sự đề xuất"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"}]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nhttps://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 3\n\nSubject: | Deonardo pilot testing\n\nThank you for agreeing to work with the team at Cybernetic Robotics as they tested their new robot, Deonardo, in our hospital. As you know, Deonardo was developed to allow you, our nursing staff, more time to focus on patients. This is exciting work. It has been a month, and Cybernetic Robotics would like to hear about your experiences with Deonardo. Please use the following link to complete an online survey. The team especially wants to know about your experiences with Deonardo during the state reviewersinspection on January 28. At the end of the survey, you may leave any additional commentsyouhaveabouttherobot. www.cyberneticrobotics.com/surveyleverlast/ Best regards, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.cyberneticrobotics.com/survey/everlast/01282 Deonardo is easy to work with. I like that I don''t have to tell Deonardo directly what to do. When I update patient information in our system, Deonardo''s tasks are updated as well. Ihave been better able to concentrate on my patients because I know Deonardo takes care of little things that used to take up so much of my time. Deonardo was particularly helpful during a recent state review because it delivered patients'' medications for all the nurses so that we didn''t have to, and we were able to focus on patient care. I believe Deonardo helped us receive positive comments from the inspectors.\n\nI do wish Deonardo could respond to voice commands. And occasionally, its wheels squeak as it moves around. But patients like watching it work, and everyone wants to take pictures with it. I wonder if you could get Deonardo to stand still for pictures?\n\nLan Duy, BSN\n\n226"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | Ever last Hospital Nursing Staff\n\nFrom: | Gretchen Robertson\n\nDate: | February 13\n\nSubject: | Deonardo in-house pilot\n\nThank you all for your help with Deonardo, our nursing robot. I''m glad that our staff has been able to take part in such groundbreaking work. Those of you who work directly with Deonardo can expect it to behave a bit differently in the coming week. It will be programmed to perform some new tasks. Previously, it waited at the nurse''s station between tasks. Now, it will spend some of this time interacting with patients who may want to pose for pictures with it. When Deonardo is in this socializing mode, the eyes on its LED face will be heart-shaped instead of the round eyes that indicate that it is in work mode.\n\nFinally, the hospital will be purchasing two additional robots in the next few months to work in other areas of the hospital. I appreciate your willingness to work with this new patient experiences. technology. We look forward to learning how robots can further improve employee and\n\nSincerely, Gretchen Robertson Director, Ever last Hospital"}],"question":"What does the hospital plan to do in the near future?","bilingual":"","options":["Replace the robot","Buy more robots","Advertise its robot","Repair the robot"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Buy more robots\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"},{"word":"especially","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈspɛʃəli/","meaning":"cụ thể"},{"word":"additional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈdɪʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"thêm vào, phụ thêm"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"*E-mail*","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\n*E-mail*\n\nTo: | management_team@pfi.co.uk\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nFrom: | schakravarty@pfi.co.uk Subject: | R&D Director Search\n\nDate: | 24 July\n\nAttachment: U Files.txt\n\nDear Management Team Members,\n\nOn behalf of the hiring committee, I am pleased to report that the search for a new research and development director is nearing completion. Given the key selection criteria the suitable candidate must meet-a demonstrated ability to improve product offerings, a keen awareness of consumers'' tastes, and in-depth knowledge of nutritional science we have narrowed the applicant pool to Alex Mooring and Inez Fuentes. While either makes for an excellent choice, I believe that Ms.Fuentes is better suited to the role. Though somewhat less experienced than Mr.Mooring, she has innovative ideas that are in line with our company''s needs.\n\nAttached are the resumes and references of the two candidates. The dates, times, and location of their final interviews will be forthcoming in another e-mail when that information is finalized. We look forward to your participation in these meetings as well as your final hiring decision. Sincerely,\n\nSupriya Chakravarty, Chair, Hiring Committee Primidian Food Industries\n\nUpcoming Events at Primidian Food Industries On 7 October at 10 A.M., Ms, Inez Fuentes, director of research and development at Primidian Food Industries (PFI),will facilitate a workshop titled Food Innovation for the Future. Among other things, she will explain why PFI recently reformulated its pasta products and demonstrate how they can be prepared in novel, tasty ways. Ms. Fuentes is a certified nutritionist with a degree in food science from Mexico City''s Academy of Science and Technology. Upon graduation, she accepted a two-year internship at Italy''s prestigious Rome Institute of Culinary Arts. Before joining PFI''s executive team, she served for five years as lead product development manager at Zesty Meals, based in Montreal, Canada. Register for this free event at www.pfi.co.uk/events/register, specifying whether you will attend online or in person at our corporate headquarters in Birmingham.\n\n228\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nhttps://www.pfi.co.uk/contact-us Who We Are | Our Brands | News and Events | Contact Us\n\nPlease complete the form below so someone from our team can contact you.\n\nName: Chaim Auerbach\n\nE-mail: chaim_auerbach@equisend.net.uk Your Message: I thoroughly enjoyed the Food Innovation for the Future workshop led by Ms. Fuentes on 28 October.I almost missed it, though. Apparently, when details about the workshop were updated, including that it would be an online-only event, my registration--and, I learned, that of some other participants-was not transferred over. Luckily, a staffer charged with online registration was able to quickly reregister me.PFI may want to analyse its electronic registration system and make improvements where necessary so that this problem does not reoccur.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"*E-mail*\n\nTo: | management_team@pfi.co.uk"},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"From: | schakravarty@pfi.co.uk Subject: | R&D Director Search\n\nDate: | 24 July\n\nAttachment: U Files.txt\n\nDear Management Team Members,\n\nOn behalf of the hiring committee, I am pleased to report that the search for a new research and development director is nearing completion. Given the key selection criteria the suitable candidate must meet-a demonstrated ability to improve product offerings, a keen awareness of consumers'' tastes, and in-depth knowledge of nutritional science we have narrowed the applicant pool to Alex Mooring and Inez Fuentes. While either makes for an excellent choice, I believe that Ms.Fuentes is better suited to the role. Though somewhat less experienced than Mr.Mooring, she has innovative ideas that are in line with our company''s needs.\n\nAttached are the resumes and references of the two candidates. The dates, times, and location of their final interviews will be forthcoming in another e-mail when that information is finalized. We look forward to your participation in these meetings as well as your final hiring decision. Sincerely,\n\nSupriya Chakravarty, Chair, Hiring Committee Primidian Food Industries\n\nUpcoming Events at Primidian Food Industries On 7 October at 10 A.M., Ms, Inez Fuentes, director of research and development at Primidian Food Industries (PFI),will facilitate a workshop titled Food Innovation for the Future. Among other things, she will explain why PFI recently reformulated its pasta products and demonstrate how they can be prepared in novel, tasty ways. Ms. Fuentes is a certified nutritionist with a degree in food science from Mexico City''s Acade