as been doing since he retired from film making. The article also mentioned that Merrington Cinema would be showing his films. So I went to the cinema''s Web site and saw the two-for-one deal. I thought this would be an excellent way to spend a Saturday, so I wentl I saw two wonderful movies. One of the films I saw was new to me:it was about scientists ona mission in space.I loved it!\n\nFor a movie fan like me, Merrington Cinema''s promotion was perfect. I understand there will be a similar promotion for Meredeth Bui''s films in October. I''ll be sure to take advantage of great offers like this again.\n\n-Talia Pak"}],"question":"What movie did Ms.Pakseerecentlyfor the first time?","bilingual":"","options":["Put a Roof on It","Through a Diamond Rain","Weekends and Memories","The Strange Drive"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Through a Diamond Rain\".","vocabList":[{"word":"construction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"xây dựng; kết cấu; ngành xây dựng tòa nhà"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"throughout","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θruaʊt/","meaning":"ở mọi phần; tại mọi thời điểm hoặc thời điểm"},{"word":"understand","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈstænd/","meaning":"hiểu, nắm bắt được"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short f","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nSubmission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor"}],"question":"What does the policy indicate about Undeniable?","bilingual":"Chính sách này chỉ ra điều gì về Undeniable 2","options":["It does not accept poems.","It has no advertisements","It requires writers to submit drawings.","It publishes the work of famous authors."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It does not accept poems.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"advertisement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/æd.vɝːˈtaɪz.mənt/","meaning":"bản tin quảng cáo"},{"word":"illustration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪləˈstreɪʃən/","meaning":"hình ảnh trong một cuốn sách hoặc tác phẩm khác; giải thích;"},{"word":"publication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌpəblɪˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"quy trình sản xuất và phát hành ấn phẩm;"},{"word":"attachment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtætʃ.mənt/","meaning":"sự gắn thêm; phần kèm thêm"}],"optionMeanings":["Nó không chấp nhận thơ.","Nó không có quảng cáo.","Nó yêu cầu người viết phải gửi bản vẽ.","Nó xuất bản tác phẩm của các tác giả nổi tiếng."]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short f","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nSubmission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor"}],"question":"According to the first e-mail, where did Mr.Sutherland discover Undeniable?","bilingual":"Theo e đầu tiên -mail, ông Sutherland đã phát hiện ra Undeniable 2 ở đâu?","options":["In a public library","Ina school bookstore","In a writing class","Ina clothing shop"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"In a writing class\".","vocabList":[{"word":"illustration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪləˈstreɪʃən/","meaning":"hình ảnh trong một cuốn sách hoặc tác phẩm khác; giải thích;"},{"word":"publication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌpəblɪˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"quy trình sản xuất và phát hành ấn phẩm;"},{"word":"attachment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtætʃ.mənt/","meaning":"sự gắn thêm; phần kèm thêm"},{"word":"instructor","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəktər/","meaning":"nhà giáo dục; giáo viên; huấn luyện viên"}],"optionMeanings":["Trong thư viện công cộng","Trong hiệu sách của trường","Trong lớp viết văn","Trong cửa hàng quần áo198. Có thể kết luận gì về “Waygone Beach”?(A) Nó diễn ra ở Portland, Oregon. (B) Nó không được chấp nhận để xuất bản. (C) Đây là câu chuyện đầu tiên của ông Sutherland. (D) Nó không vượt quá 1.000 từ.199. Ông Sutherland đã nhận được bao nhiêu cho câu chuyện của mình trên tạp chí Không thể phủ nhận 2(A) $5(B) $50(C) $100(D) $250200 tháng 6. chữ e thứ hai có tác dụng gì -mail gợi ý về cô Jordan? (A) Cô ấy dự định gia hạn đăng ký của mình. (B) Cô ấy viết một chuyên mục cho Không thể phủ nhận. (C) Cô ấy dạy các lớp viết. (D) Cô ấy có một phương pháp viết khác thường. Chính sách gửiKhông thể phủ nhận là một tạp chí văn học được hỗ trợ quảng cáo vềtiểu thuyếtngắn và phi cấu hình của các nhà văn mới nổi. Chúng tôi miễn phí $5 cho những người gửi lần đầu. • Các câu chuyện phải từ250 đến 1.000 từ(không có thơ). • Không đính kèm hình ảnh minh họa. Tất cả các sản phẩm hình minh họa được sản xuất - house. • Đính kèm câu chuyện của bạn trong e - gửi thư tới: submit@undedenable.com. Vui lòng bao gồm một bản tóm tắt ngắn gọn về sản phẩm của bạn và cho chúng tôi biết bạn đã phát hiện raKhông thể phủ nhận như thếnào. • Chúng tôi trả lờithù tiền lao $50 sau khi nhận được bản xuất. • Nếu chúng tôi chấp nhận câu chuyện của bạn, chúng tôi sẽ đưa bạn đồng ý và biểu mẫu để thiết lập chuyển tiền điện tử. Tới: submits@undeniable.com Từ: len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Ngày: 15 tháng 3 Chủ đề: Thư xin việc và khen thưởng. Tập tin đính kèm: Hành trình của JiXin chào! Tài liệu đáng tin cậy của tôi, \"Hành trình của Ji.\" xoay quanh một nhà thiết kế trẻtuổi, Toby Ji, người đã vượt qua những trở lại để thực hiện ước mơ của mình trong ngành thời trang. Tôi đã được người hướng dẫn viết lách của mình tại Viện ArtmanởPortland, Oregon giới thiệu vềUndeniable vào nămngoái và kểtừ đó tôi đã trở thành người đăng ký. Tôi đặc biệt thíchGóc phi hư cấu của bạn; một trong những mục yêu thích của tôi là “Waygone Beach”, đã truyền cảm hứng cho tôi viết “Chuyến đi của Ji”. Tôi tin rằng nó sẽ là một sự hợp lý lý tưởng cho phần này. Như \"Waygone Beach\" \"Ji''sJourney\" là một câu chuyện có thật về hy vọng và sựkiên trì. Cảm ơn bạn đã quan tâm và tạo diễn đàn cho những người viết mới như tôi. Trân trọng, Len SutherlandĐ ẾN: len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Từ: jerrybuckman@undeniable.comNgày: 2 tháng 7 Chủ thể: Bài phụ thuộc của bạn Thưaông Sutherland, Câu chuyện của bạn, “Hành trình của Ji,” đã tạo ra rất nhiều phản hồi tích tích cựctrong tháng Sáu. Xin chúc mừng! Và bản năng của bạn đã đúng về câu chuyện của bạn. Chúng tôi hi vọng bạn sẽgửi nhiều câu chuyện hơn nữa cho Không thể phủ nhận. Như một động lực bổ sung, chúng tôi sẽ tăng số lượngtiềnthưởng của mình lên 100 đô la vào đầu tháng tới. Là người đăng ký, bạn có thể thuộc chuỗi câu hỏi và câu trả lờilời của Stacy Jordan giới thiệu một nhà văn khác mỗi tháng. Bạn có sẵn sàng trả lời một vài câu hỏi về việc làm sáng tạo văn học của bạn, phương pháp viết, và làm thếnào bạn tìm thấy những ý tưởng câu chuyện chuyện? Nếu vậy, tôi sẽ chuyển địa chỉ - thư của bạn cho cô Jordan, người sẽ liên lạc với bạn trong thời gian tới. Trân trọng, Jerry BuckmanPhó tổng biên tập"]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short f","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nSubmission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor"}],"question":"What can be concluded about\"Waygone Beach\"?","bilingual":"","options":["It takes place in Portland, Oregon.","It was not accepted for publication.","It is Mr.Sutherland''s first story.","It does not exceed 1,000 words. Stop! This is the end of the test. If you finish before time is called, you may go backtoParts5,6,and7andcheckyourwork."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"It does not exceed 1,000 words. Stop! This is the end of the test. If you finish before time is called, you may go backtoParts5,6,and7andcheckyourwork.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"illustration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪləˈstreɪʃən/","meaning":"hình ảnh trong một cuốn sách hoặc tác phẩm khác; giải thích;"},{"word":"publication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌpəblɪˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"quy trình sản xuất và phát hành ấn phẩm;"},{"word":"attachment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtætʃ.mənt/","meaning":"sự gắn thêm; phần kèm thêm"},{"word":"instructor","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəktər/","meaning":"nhà giáo dục; giáo viên; huấn luyện viên"}]},{"questionNum":"199","passageTitle":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short f","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nSubmission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\n*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland\n\n=== Văn bản 3 ===\nTo: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Submission Policy Undeniable is an ad-supported literary journal of short fiction and nonfiction by emerging writers. We waive our $5fee for first-time submitters. Stories must be between 250 and 1,000 words (no poetry, please). Do not include illustrations. All illustrations are produced in-house. Attach your story in an e-mail to: submissions@undeniable.com.Please include a brief synopsis of your piece, and tell us how you discovered Undeniable. We pay a$50honorarium upon acceptance for publication..If we accept your story, we will send you a contract and a form to set up an electronic money transfer."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"*E-mail* submissions@undeniable.com From: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com Date: | March 15\n\nSubject: | Cover letter and submission\n\nAttachment: Ji''s Journey\n\nGreetings! My submission,\"Ji''s Journey,\"centers on a young dress designer, Toby Ji, who overcomes obstacles to realize her dreams in the fashion industry. I was introduced to Undeniable last year by my writing instructor at the Artman Institute in Portland, Oregon, and have since become a subscriber.I particularly enjoy your Nonfiction Corner; one of my favorites was\"Waygone Beach,\"which inspired me to write“ji''s Journey.\"I believe it would be an ideal fit for this section. Like “Waygone Beach,\"“\"Ji''s Journey\"is a true story of hope and perseverance. Thank you for your consideration and for creating a forum for new writers like me. Sincerely, Len Sutherland"},{"label":"Văn bản 3","text":"To: | len.sutherland@onyxmail.com From: | jerrybuckman@undeniable.com Date: | July 2\n\nSubject: | Your submission\n\nDear Mr. Sutherland, Your story,“Ji''s Journey,\"generated a great deal of positive feedback about the June issue. Congratulations!And your instincts were correct regarding your story''s placement. All this has us hoping you will submit more stories to Undeniable. As an added incentive, we will be increasing ourhonorarium to $100 beginning next month. As a subscriber, you are likely familiar with Stacy Jordan''s question-and-answer column featuring a different writer each month. Would you be willing to answer a few questions about your literary training, writing method, and how you find story ideas? If so, I will forward your e-mail address to Ms. Jordan, who will reach out to you in the near future. Sincerely, Jerry Buckman Associate Editor"}],"questio