heir matching retirement funds in the form of cash. Instead, their retirement funds will be provided in the\n\nOur current retirement management firm, Proxave Futures, has been informed of this change in retirement benefits. The firm will manage the transition and will continue to provide customer support to Blanen Industries employees. Questions should be directed to Pierre Dehaeneat Proxave Futures rather than our human resources department. Please work with Yua Suzuki, head of human resources, to provide her with the information she should include in her all-staff communication about this important change in employee benefits. Our president notified me that he would like to receive all reports related to this transition. Aiso, please continue to send me daily financial reports. Best, Shamonica Walker, CFO Blanen Industries","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Bruce Holt\n\nFrom: | Shamonica Walker\n\nDate: | April 9\n\nSubject: | Immediate and confidential\n\nDear Bruce, Beginning with the new fiscal year, a change in retirement benefits will be applied for all full-time employees here at Blanen Industries. They will no longer be given their matching retirement funds in the form of cash. Instead, their retirement funds will be provided in the\n\nOur current retirement management firm, Proxave Futures, has been informed of this change in retirement benefits. The firm will manage the transition and will continue to provide customer support to Blanen Industries employees. Questions should be directed to Pierre Dehaeneat Proxave Futures rather than our human resources department. Please work with Yua Suzuki, head of human resources, to provide her with the information she should include in her all-staff communication about this important change in employee benefits. Our president notified me that he would like to receive all reports related to this transition. Aiso, please continue to send me daily financial reports. Best, Shamonica Walker, CFO Blanen Industries"}],"question":"Who is responsible for notifying all employees about the policy change?","bilingual":"","options":["Mr. Holt","Ms.Walker","Mr. Dehaene","Ms.Suzuki"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Ms.Suzuki\".","vocabList":[{"word":"communication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəmˌjunəˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"trao đổi thông tin hoặc ý tưởng; chuyển khoản; đi qua"},{"word":"responsible","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ri''spɔnsəbl/","meaning":"chịu trách nhiệm"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"retirement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈtaɪərmənt/","meaning":"sự ẩn dật, sự về hưu"}]},{"questionNum":"168","passageTitle":"Monica Zia(8:27A.M.)Hi, Yuji and Sung-ho.I wonder if one of you could help ","passageText":"Monica Zia(8:27A.M.)Hi, Yuji and Sung-ho.I wonder if one of you could help me later today. Dejani Jones was going to help, but she''s going to be out of the office today. Yuji Saito (8:28A.M.)That''s too bad. Did she say why? Monica Zia (8:28 A.M.) She said she had a slight cold but that she should be able to work fromhomeonthedataanalysesforherclients. Sung-ho Suh (8:29 A.M.) So, she won''t be coming in at all today? Monica Zia (8:31 A.M.) No. And Dejani and I were going to go to Willi''s Market to buy food and beverages for tomorrow''s office picnic. You remember, right? Saturday at noon at City Park. Anyhow, Dejani has a car and was going to drive us to the store and use her credit card to purchase the supplies. I know that both of you drive to work, so I thought one of you could help. Sung-ho Suh (8:32 A.M.) When were you thinking of going? Yuji Saito (8:32 A.M.) Sure. I can help, and we can use my credit card. Monica Zia (8:33A.M.)Around two. Yuji Saito (8:34 A.M.) No problem. Just stop by my cubicle, and we can take my car to go to the store. Sung-ho Suh (8:35 A.M.) That''s great, Yuji.I have several meetings this afternoon, so I wouldn''t be able to get away. Monica Zia (8:35 A.M.) Thanks, Yuji. I''ll see you this afternoon.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"Monica Zia(8:27A.M.)Hi, Yuji and Sung-ho.I wonder if one of you could help me later today. Dejani Jones was going to help, but she''s going to be out of the office today. Yuji Saito (8:28A.M.)That''s too bad. Did she say why? Monica Zia (8:28 A.M.) She said she had a slight cold but that she should be able to work fromhomeonthedataanalysesforherclients. Sung-ho Suh (8:29 A.M.) So, she won''t be coming in at all today? Monica Zia (8:31 A.M.) No. And Dejani and I were going to go to Willi''s Market to buy food and beverages for tomorrow''s office picnic. You remember, right? Saturday at noon at City Park. Anyhow, Dejani has a car and was going to drive us to the store and use her credit card to purchase the supplies. I know that both of you drive to work, so I thought one of you could help. Sung-ho Suh (8:32 A.M.) When were you thinking of going? Yuji Saito (8:32 A.M.) Sure. I can help, and we can use my credit card. Monica Zia (8:33A.M.)Around two. Yuji Saito (8:34 A.M.) No problem. Just stop by my cubicle, and we can take my car to go to the store. Sung-ho Suh (8:35 A.M.) That''s great, Yuji.I have several meetings this afternoon, so I wouldn''t be able to get away. Monica Zia (8:35 A.M.) Thanks, Yuji. I''ll see you this afternoon."}],"question":"Why is Ms. Jones going to be out of the office today?","bilingual":"Tại sao hôm nay cô Jones lại không có mặt ở văn phòng?","options":["She is feeling ill.","She works from home every Friday.","She is meeting with clients.","She is having car trouble."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"She is feeling ill.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"beverages","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"