ght for participants. In the event that attendance is high, we could also house participants in the nearby Hotel Milvio at 120 per night. - [2] -- I also looked into hotels in Genoa and Florence, but I could not find any that would be much cheaper in overall conference costs.—[3],More importantly, I am concerned that the greater cost of flights to those smaller cities could discourage some attendees. Rome, on the other hand, has affordable direct flights from most European cities.[4]- It will also be more affordable for our colleagues coming from Buenos Aires. If you would like to pursue the Hotel al Ponte option, I will provide a detailed write-up of the anticipated costs and of the amenities offered by the hotel. Best, Lucia no Moretti Secretary, International Technological Society"}],"question":"What is true about Hotel Milvio?","bilingual":"","options":["It is more expensive than Hotel al Ponte.","It is usually fully booked.","It has locations in Genoa and Florence.","It has more rooms than Hotel al Ponte."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It is more expensive than Hotel al Ponte.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"international","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.t̬ɚˈnæʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"quốc tế, đa quốc gia"},{"word":"participant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pa:´tisipənt/","meaning":"người tham gia, người tham dự"},{"word":"technology","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/tɛkˈnɑləʤi/","meaning":"khoa học nghệ thuật công nghiệp; khoa học ứng dụng"},{"word":"conference","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑnfərəns/","meaning":"cuộc họp; hội thảo; quy ước"}]},{"questionNum":"175","passageTitle":"To: | Dorota Kucharski <dkucharski@internationaltechnologicalsociety.org> F","passageText":"To: | Dorota Kucharski <dkucharski@internationaltechnologicalsociety.org> From: | Lucia no Moretti <lmoretti@internationaltechnologicalsociety.org> Date: | 8 August\n\nSubject: | Research results\n\nMs.Kucharski,\n\nThe following is a summary of what I have learned in my research about where to hold our next annual technology conference in June of next year. In Rome, the best option I have found is Hotel al Ponte. The total cost for conference eventstherewouldbeE31,500.[1]—.Individual hotel roomswouldcost80pernight for participants. In the event that attendance is high, we could also house participants in the nearby Hotel Milvio at 120 per night. - [2] -- I also looked into hotels in Genoa and Florence, but I could not find any that would be much cheaper in overall conference costs.—[3],More importantly, I am concerned that the greater cost of flights to those smaller cities could discourage some attendees. Rome, on the other hand, has affordable direct flights from most European cities.[4]- It will also be more affordable for our colleagues coming from Buenos Aires. If you would like to pursue the Hotel al Ponte option, I will provide a detailed write-up of the anticipated costs and of the amenities offered by the hotel. Best, Lucia no Moretti Secretary, International Technological Society","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"To: | Dorota Kucharski <dkucharski@internationaltechnologicalsociety.org> From: | Lucia no Moretti <lmoretti@internationaltechnologicalsociety.org> Date: | 8 August\n\nSubject: | Research results\n\nMs.Kucharski,\n\nThe following is a summary of what I have learned in my research about where to hold our next annual technology conference in June of next year. In Rome, the best option I have found is Hotel al Ponte. The total cost for conference eventstherewouldbeE31,500.[1]—.Individual hotel roomswouldcost80pernight for participants. In the event that attendance is high, we could also house participants in the nearby Hotel Milvio at 120 per night. - [2] -- I also looked into hotels in Genoa and Florence, but I could not find any that would be much cheaper in overall conference costs.—[3],More importantly, I am concerned that the greater cost of flights to those smaller cities could discourage some attendees. Rome, on the other hand, has affordable direct flights from most European cities.[4]- It will also be more affordable for our colleagues coming from Buenos Aires. If you would like to pursue the Hotel al Ponte option, I will provide a detailed write-up of the anticipated costs and of the amenities offered by the hotel. Best, Lucia no Moretti Secretary, International Technological Society"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2],[3], and [4] does the following sentence best belong? \"The savings to host the conference in one ofthosecitieswouldbeE500atmost.\"","bilingual":"","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"[3]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"international","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.t̬ɚˈnæʃ.ən.əl/","meaning":"quốc tế, đa quốc gia"},{"word":"participant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pa:´tisipənt/","meaning":"người tham gia, người tham dự"},{"word":"conference","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑnfərəns/","meaning":"cuộc họp; hội thảo; quy ước"},{"word":"technology","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/tɛkˈnɑləʤi/","meaning":"khoa học nghệ thuật công nghiệp; khoa học ứng dụng"}]},{"questionNum":"176","passageTitle":"https://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter Home | Customer Serv","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nhttps://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter Home | Customer Service | Subscribe | Account | Log In\n\nCentral University Health Newsletter-Your Guide to Nutrition and Well-Being\n\nTips on healthful eating are available almost everywhere from TV shows to online cooking forums. It''s often difficult to know whether the advice you encounter is based on scientific evidence. That''s why the Central University Health Newsletter is indispensable. Each month, it delivers informative, easy-to-understand articles that summarize findings by researchers at the Central University School of Nutrition. For example, last April''s issue evaluated nutritional supplements that are sold in supermarkets. The back page features our Ask an Expert column, in which the director of the School of Nutrition answers readers'' questions. A one-year subscription is$20andincludesonlineaccesstoall previous issues. We also offer a 10 percent discount on your first subscription renewal. What''s more, subscribers receive our free weekly\"Healthy Living\"e-mail update, which includes special reports plus links to videos and podcasts. To get started, simply go to our Subscribe page and follow the instructions.\n\n=== Văn bản 2 ===\nhttps://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter/reviews Publication:Central University Health Newsletter ★★★★★ Reviewed by:Ari Kipp Dateposted:August 4 This is my second year subscribing to the Central University Health Newsletter, which! read cover to cover.I''m particularly impressed with the Ask an Expert column, andl always learn something new. This month, for instance, Dr.Stella Boothgives a surprising answer to the question of which pasta is most nutritious.I didn''t know that be an-based pasta even existed, much less how much fiber it contains.I tried it and will never go","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1","text":"https://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter Home | Customer Service | Subscribe | Account | Log In\n\nCentral University Health Newsletter-Your Guide to Nutrition and Well-Being\n\nTips on healthful eating are available almost everywhere from TV shows to online cooking forums. It''s often difficult to know whether the advice you encounter is based on scientific evidence. That''s why the Central University Health Newsletter is indispensable. Each month, it delivers informative, easy-to-understand articles that summarize findings by researchers at the Central University School of Nutrition. For example, last April''s issue evaluated nutritional supplements that are sold in supermarkets. The back page features our Ask an Expert column, in which the director of the School of Nutrition answers readers'' questions. A one-year subscription is$20andincludesonlineaccesstoall previous issues. We also offer a 10 percent discount on your first subscription renewal. What''s more, subscribers receive our free weekly\"Healthy Living\"e-mail update, which includes special reports plus links to videos and podcasts. To get started, simply go to our Subscribe page and follow the instructions."},{"label":"Văn bản 2","text":"https://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter/reviews Publication:Central University Health Newsletter ★★★★★ Reviewed by:Ari Kipp Dateposted:August 4 This is my second year subscribing to the Central University Health Newsletter, which! read cover to cover.I''m particularly impressed with the Ask an Expert column, andl always learn something new. This month, for instance, Dr.Stella Boothgives a surprising answer to the question of which pasta is most nutritious.I didn''t know that be an-based pasta even existed, much less how much fiber it contains.I tried it and will never go"}],"question":"What is the purpose of the Web page?","bilingual":"Mục đích của trang Web là gì?","options":["To explain the reason for a price increase","To increase the size of the audience for a publication","To recruit volunteers for a research project","To sell nutritional supplements"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To increase the size of the audience for a publication\".","vocabList":[{"word":"subscription","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səbˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"sự đăng ký"},{"word":"publication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌpəblɪˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"quy trình sản xuất và phát hành ấn phẩm;"},{"word":"instruction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"giảng dạy; phương hướng; hướng dẫn; đào tạo; giáo dục;"},{"word":"volunteers","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪrz/","meaning":"Tình nguyện viên"}],"optionMeanings":["Để giải thích lý do tăng giá","Để tăng quy mô khán giả cho một ấn phẩm","Để tuyển tình nguyện viên cho một dự án nghiên cứu","Bán thực phẩm bổ sung dinh dưỡng177. Trong trang Web, từ “giao hàng” trong đoạn 1, dòng 4, gần nghĩa nhất với(A) trình bày(B) vận chuyển(C) hướng dẫn(D) khẳng định178. Điều gì đúng về ông Kipp?(A) Ông ấy là một người khỏe mạnh -chăm sóc chuyên nghiệp. (B) Anh ấy được giảm giá 20% khi đăng ký. (C) Anh ấy nhận được lời khuyên về dinh dưỡng từ một chương trình truyền hình. (D) Anh ấy nhận được email hàng tuần -mail từ Đại học Trung ương."]},{"questionNum":"177","passageTitle":"https://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter Home | Customer Serv","passageText":"=== Văn bản 1 ===\nhttps://www.centraluniversity.edu/nutrition/newsletter Home | Customer Service | Subscribe | Account | Log In\n\nCentral University Health Newsletter-Your Guide to Nutrition and Well-Being\n\nTips on healthful eating are available almost everywhere from TV shows to online cooking forums. It''s often difficult to know whether the advice you encounter is based on scientific evidence. That''s why the Central University Health Newsletter is indispensable. Each month, it delivers informative, easy-to-understand articles that summarize findings by researchers at the Central University School of Nutrition. For example, last April''s issue evaluated nutritional supplements that are sold in supermarkets. The back page features our Ask an Expert column, in which the director of the School of Nutrition answers readers'' questions. A one-year subscription is$20andincludesonl