ed within four years. ------- [4] -------.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Monorail Coming to Sudbury\n(4 Feb.) ------- Ottawa-based Saenger, Inc., has\nbeen selected by the city of Sudbury to build\na monorail system that will connect the city’s\ncommercial district to the airport. [I] -------.\nFunding for the system is drawn from a\ncombination of public agencies and private\ninvestors. [2] -------. Ticket sales for the\nmonorail will also provide a new source of\nrevenue for the city. ------- [3] -------. Construction is\nslated to begin in early June and is expected to\nbe completed within four years. ------- [4] -------."}],"question":"What kind of business most likely is Saenger, Inc.?","bilingual":"Saenger, Inc. có thể thuộc loại hình kinh doanh nào?","options":["A construction firm","A real estate agency","A cargo-handling company","A financial services provider"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"A construction firm\".","vocabList":[{"word":"kind","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/kaɪnd/","meaning":"kiểu; loại; lớp học; nhóm sự vật được phân loại"},{"word":"business","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈbɪznɪs/","meaning":"công ty; doanh nghiệp; buôn bán; thương mại; vấn đề"},{"word":"construction","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈstrəkʃən/","meaning":"xây dựng; kết cấu; ngành xây dựng tòa nhà"},{"word":"firm","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/fərm/","meaning":"công ty; kinh doanh thương mại; tập đoàn"}]},{"questionNum":"157","passageTitle":"Questions 156-158 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Monorail Coming to Sudbury\n(4 Feb.) ------- Ottawa-based Saenger, Inc., has\nbeen selected by the city of Sudbury to build\na monorail system that will connect the city’s\ncommercial district to the airport. [I] -------.\nFunding for the system is drawn from a\ncombination of public agencies and private\ninvestors. [2] -------. Ticket sales for the\nmonorail will also provide a new source of\nrevenue for the city. ------- [3] -------. Construction is\nslated to begin in early June and is expected to\nbe completed within four years. ------- [4] -------.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Monorail Coming to Sudbury\n(4 Feb.) ------- Ottawa-based Saenger, Inc., has\nbeen selected by the city of Sudbury to build\na monorail system that will connect the city’s\ncommercial district to the airport. [I] -------.\nFunding for the system is drawn from a\ncombination of public agencies and private\ninvestors. [2] -------. Ticket sales for the\nmonorail will also provide a new source of\nrevenue for the city. ------- [3] -------. Construction is\nslated to begin in early June and is expected to\nbe completed within four years. ------- [4] -------."}],"question":"What is indicated about the monorail?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về đường ray đơn?","options":["It needs more funding from investors.","It will take years to finish.","It was proposed by airport officials.","It offers discounted tickets to city residents."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"It will take years to finish.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"needs","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/nidz/","meaning":"cần"},{"word":"investor","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛstər/","meaning":"người bỏ tiền vào một dự án"},{"word":"finish","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈfɪnɪʃ/","meaning":"kết thúc; hoàn thành; Phần kết luận; đánh bóng; cái gì đó mà"},{"word":"airport","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɛrˌpɔrt/","meaning":"nơi máy bay cất cánh và hạ cánh"}]},{"questionNum":"158","passageTitle":"Questions 156-158 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Monorail Coming to Sudbury\n(4 Feb.) ------- Ottawa-based Saenger, Inc., has\nbeen selected by the city of Sudbury to build\na monorail system that will connect the city’s\ncommercial district to the airport. [I] -------.\nFunding for the system is drawn from a\ncombination of public agencies and private\ninvestors. [2] -------. Ticket sales for the\nmonorail will also provide a new source of\nrevenue for the city. ------- [3] -------. Construction is\nslated to begin in early June and is expected to\nbe completed within four years. ------- [4] -------.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Monorail Coming to Sudbury\n(4 Feb.) ------- Ottawa-based Saenger, Inc., has\nbeen selected by the city of Sudbury to build\na monorail system that will connect the city’s\ncommercial district to the airport. [I] -------.\nFunding for the system is drawn from a\ncombination of public agencies and private\ninvestors. [2] -------. Ticket sales for the\nmonorail will also provide a new source of\nrevenue for the city. ------- [3] -------. Construction is\nslated to begin in early June and is expected to\nbe completed within four years. ------- [4] -------."}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3] and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “Along the way, the line will stop at nine stations.”","bilingual":"Câu sau đây thuộc về vị trí nào trong số các vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4]? “Trên đường đi, tuyến sẽ dừng ở chín trạm.”","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"[1]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"along","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/əˈlɔŋ/","meaning":"Dọc theo"},{"word":"stop","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/stɑp/","meaning":"sự chấm dứt; kết thúc; thăm nom; trở ngại; sự cản trở"},{"word":"station","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsteɪʃən/","meaning":"chức vụ; nơi mà một người hoặc vật thường ở đó"}]},{"questionNum":"159","passageTitle":"Questions 159-160 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Dennis Beck (2:52 P.M.)\nHi, Corinne. I just want to be sure that you saw the document I\nsent you. It’s the combined market analysis and advertising\nproposal for the Keyes Elegant Home group. We’re preparing it\nfor tomorrow''s presentation to the client.\nCorinne McCall (2:53 P.M.)\nYes. I have just downloaded it. Is this about their new line\nof tableware?\nDennis Beck (2:54 P.M.)\nYes. I’d like you to read it over.\nCorinne McCall (3:01 P.M.)\nNo problem. Would you like me to revise anything, or do you\nwant me to just check that it is all clear?\nDennis Beck (3:02 P.M.)\nFeel free to add information to the section “Advertising\nStrategies,” since that is your area of expertise.\nCorinne McCall (3:03 P.M.)\nWill do. I’ll get it back to you before the end of the day.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Dennis Beck (2:52 P.M.)\nHi, Corinne. I just want to be sure that you saw the document I\nsent you. It’s the combined market analysis and advertising\nproposal for the Keyes Elegant Home group. We’re preparing it\nfor tomorrow''s presentation to the client.\nCorinne McCall (2:53 P.M.)\nYes. I have just downloaded it. Is this about their new line\nof tableware?\nDennis Beck (2:54 P.M.)\nYes. I’d like you to read it over.\nCorinne McCall (3:01 P.M.)\nNo problem. Would you like me to revise anything, or do you\nwant me to just check that it is all clear?\nDennis Beck (3:02 P.M.)\nFeel free to add information to the section “Advertising\nStrategies,” since that is your area of expertise.\nCorinne McCall (3:03 P.M.)\nWill do. I’ll get it back to you before the end of the day."}],"question":"At 3:01 P.M., what does Ms. McCall most likely mean when she writes, “No problem”?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 3:01 chiều, rất có thể cô McCall có ý gì khi viết, “Không vấn đề gì”?","options":["She did not have any issues logging on to her computer.","She does not think a document has errors.","She is willing to review a document.","She has time to meet representatives from Keyes Elegant Home."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She is willing to review a document.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"issue","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɪʃu/","meaning":"đề tài; chủ thể; vấn đề; câu hỏi; vấn đề; công bố"},{"word":"think","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/θɪŋk/","meaning":"nghĩ"}]},{"questionNum":"160","passageTitle":"Questions 159-160 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Dennis Beck (2:52 P.M.)\nHi, Corinne. I just want to be sure that you saw the document I\nsent you. It’s the combined market analysis and advertising\nproposal for the Keyes Elegant Home group. We’re preparing it\nfor tomorrow''s presentation to the client.\nCorinne McCall (2:53 P.M.)\nYes. I have just downloaded it. Is this about their new line\nof tableware?\nDennis Beck (2:54 P.M.)\nYes. I’d like you to read it over.\nCorinne McCall (3:01 P.M.)\nNo problem. Would you like me to revise anything, or do you\nwant me to just check that it is all clear?\nDennis Beck (3:02 P.M.)\nFeel free to add information to the section “Advertising\nStrategies,” since that is your area of expertise.\nCorinne McCall (3:03 P.M.)\nWill do. I’ll get it back to you before the end of the day.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Dennis Beck (2:52 P.M.)\nHi, Corinne. I just want to be sure that you saw the document I\nsent you. It’s the combined market analysis and advertising\nproposal for the Keyes Elegant Home group. We’re preparing it\nfor tomorrow''s presentation to the client.\nCorinne McCall (2:53 P.M.)\nYes. I have just downloaded it. Is this about their new line\nof tableware?\nDennis Beck (2:54 P.M.)\nYes. I’d like you to read it over.\nCorinne McCall (3:01 P.M.)\nNo problem. Would you like me to revise anything, or do you\nwant me to just check that it is all clear?\nDennis Beck (3:02 P.M.)\nFeel free to add information to the section “Advertising\nStrategies,” since that is your area of expertise.\nCorinne McCall (3:03 P.M.)\nWill do. I’ll get it back to you before the end of the day."}],"question":"What type of work does Ms. McCall most likely do?","bilingual":"Cô McCall thường làm loại công việc gì nhất?","options":["Marketing","Accounting","Legal consulting","Information technology services"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Marketing\".","vocabList":[{"word":"work","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/wərk/","meaning":"nhân công; nhiệm vụ; nghề nghiệp; nghề nghiệp; ơn gọi; cố gắng"},{"word":"marketing","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mɑ:kitiɳ/","meaning":"tiếp thị"},{"word":"accounting","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈkaʊn.t̬ɪŋ/","meaning":"sự tính toán, thanh toán"},{"word":"legal","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈligəl/","meaning":"của hoặc liên quan đến pháp luật; pháp luật cho phép"}]},{"questionNum":"161","passageTitle":"Questions 161-164 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang"}],"question":"What is suggested about the craft fair?","bilingual":"Hội chợ thủ công có gợi ý gì?","options":["It takes place in downtown Staffordsville.","It is being held for the first time.","It specializes in locally produced crafts.","It will be held outdoors."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"It will be held outdoors.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"craft","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kræft/","meaning":"tạo hình một cách khéo léo"},{"word":"fair","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/fer/","meaning":"hội chợ, phiên chợ; công bằng, không thiên vị"},{"word":"place","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pleɪs/","meaning":"vị trí; chức vụ; đứng; vai trò; chức năng"},{"word":"downtown","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈdaʊnˈtaʊn/","meaning":"trung tâm thương mại của thành phố; phân tâm kinh doanh"}]},{"questionNum":"162","passageTitle":"Questions 161-164 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang"}],"question":"What is NOT mentioned as a requirement for selling at the craft fair?","bilingual":"Điều gì KHÔNG được đề cập như một yêu cầu để bán hàng tại hội chợ thủ công?","options":["Sharing a space with another participant","Paying a fee to participate","Submitting images of the crafts","Providing one’s own tenting"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Sharing a space with another participant\".","vocabList":[{"word":"requirement","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈkwaɪr.mənt/","meaning":"yêu cầu, cần thiết"},{"word":"selling","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɛlɪŋ/","meaning":"bán"},{"word":"craft","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kræft/","meaning":"tạo hình một cách khéo léo"},{"word":"fair","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/fer/","meaning":"hội chợ, phiên chợ; công bằng, không thiên vị"}]},{"questionNum":"163","passageTitle":"Questions 161-164 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang"}],"question":"What does Ms. Renaldo most likely sell?","bilingual":"Cô Renaldo thường bán gì nhất?","options":["Sketches","Photographs","Pottery","Jewelry"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Jewelry\".","vocabList":[{"word":"sketches","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈskɛʧɪz/","meaning":"Bản phác thảo"},{"word":"photographs","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfoʊtəˌgræfs/","meaning":"Ảnh"},{"word":"pottery","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɑtəri/","meaning":"Đồ gốm"},{"word":"jewelry","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈʤuəlri/","meaning":"Trang sức"}]},{"questionNum":"164","passageTitle":"Questions 161-164 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: Mara Renaklo <mrenaldo@ viyamail.com>\nFrom: Lisa Yang <lyang@staftbrdsvillefair.org> Date: May 28\nSubject: RE: Staffordsville Craft Fair\nDear Ms. Renaklo,\nThank you for your interest in selling your handcrafted items at the annual Staffordsville\nCraft Fair. Please note that all applicants must submit a $25 application fee, whether or\nnot they want to share a space with another applicant. Moreover, all applicants must\nsubmit a minimum of four photographs of their work in order to be considered as a\nvendor. ------- [l] -------.\nIn addition to photographs, we ask that you submit a rough sketch showing how you\nwould display your work. Since you propose to share a space with a friend, local potter\nJulia Berens, it would be helpful if your sketch could indicate how you are planning to use\nthe space jointly. [2]\nAlso, because we hold the fair rain or shine, all vendors must supply their own tenting to\nprotect themselves and their wares from the possibility of rain. [3]-.\nFinally, please be aware that every year we receive far more applications from jewelry\nmakers than we can accept. We hope that you will not be too discouraged if your work is\nnot accepted this year, as you are applying for the first time. [4]-.\nThanks again, and best of luck with your application,\nLisa Yang"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3] and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “Make sure they clearly represent the items you wish to offer for purchase at the event.”","bilingual":"Câu sau đây thuộc về vị trí nào trong số các vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4]? “Hãy đảm bảo rằng chúng thể hiện rõ ràng những mặt hàng bạn muốn mua tại sự kiện.”","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"[1]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"clearly","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈklɪrli/","meaning":"rõ ràng; rõ ràng; không thể nhầm lẫn"},{"word":"represent","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌrep.rɪˈzent/","meaning":"miêu tả, hình dung"}]},{"questionNum":"165","passageTitle":"Questions 165-167 refer to the following information.","passageText":"SLEEP SOUNDLY SOLUTIONS\nThank you for choosing Sleep Soundly Solutions!\nThe updated control panel is linked to an integrated system that allows you to activate\nand disable all security systems in your home, including your Sleep Soundly motion\nsensor as well as your fire, smoke, and carbon monoxide detectors.\nAll Sleep Soundly residential alarm systems have been tested thoroughly to ensure the\nhighest quality and sensitivity, so you can sleep soundly in the knowledge that your\nhome is protected. We have also developed a new smartphone application that will\nnotify you of any disturbances wherever you are. The app is available for download now.\nSleep Soundly control equipment is carefully manufactured for use with Sleep Soundly\ndetectors and alarms. Using products manufactured by other companies may result in an\nalarm system that does not meet safety requirements for residential buildings or comply\nwith local laws.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"SLEEP SOUNDLY SOLUTIONS\nThank you for choosing Sleep Soundly Solutions!\nThe updated control panel is linked to an integrated system that allows you to activate\nand disable all security systems in your home, including your Sleep Soundly motion\nsensor as we