 (B) \"A smartphone application\".","vocabList":[{"word":"product","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɑdəkt/","meaning":"kết quả sản xuất; hàng hóa; hàng hóa"},{"word":"outdoor","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈaʊtˌdɔr/","meaning":"của thiên nhiên"},{"word":"application","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌæp.ləˈkeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"ứng dụng, sự áp dụng"},{"word":"installation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.stəˈleɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"sự cài đặt"}]},{"questionNum":"167","passageTitle":"Questions 165-167 refer to the following information.","passageText":"SLEEP SOUNDLY SOLUTIONS\nThank you for choosing Sleep Soundly Solutions!\nThe updated control panel is linked to an integrated system that allows you to activate\nand disable all security systems in your home, including your Sleep Soundly motion\nsensor as well as your fire, smoke, and carbon monoxide detectors.\nAll Sleep Soundly residential alarm systems have been tested thoroughly to ensure the\nhighest quality and sensitivity, so you can sleep soundly in the knowledge that your\nhome is protected. We have also developed a new smartphone application that will\nnotify you of any disturbances wherever you are. The app is available for download now.\nSleep Soundly control equipment is carefully manufactured for use with Sleep Soundly\ndetectors and alarms. Using products manufactured by other companies may result in an\nalarm system that does not meet safety requirements for residential buildings or comply\nwith local laws.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"SLEEP SOUNDLY SOLUTIONS\nThank you for choosing Sleep Soundly Solutions!\nThe updated control panel is linked to an integrated system that allows you to activate\nand disable all security systems in your home, including your Sleep Soundly motion\nsensor as well as your fire, smoke, and carbon monoxide detectors.\nAll Sleep Soundly residential alarm systems have been tested thoroughly to ensure the\nhighest quality and sensitivity, so you can sleep soundly in the knowledge that your\nhome is protected. We have also developed a new smartphone application that will\nnotify you of any disturbances wherever you are. The app is available for download now.\nSleep Soundly control equipment is carefully manufactured for use with Sleep Soundly\ndetectors and alarms. Using products manufactured by other companies may result in an\nalarm system that does not meet safety requirements for residential buildings or comply\nwith local laws."}],"question":"The word “meet” in paragraph 3, line 3, is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"Từ “gặp” ở đoạn 3, dòng 3, gần nghĩa nhất với","options":["greet","touch","satisfy","experience"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"satisfy\".","vocabList":[{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"greet","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/grit/","meaning":"chào"},{"word":"touch","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/təʧ/","meaning":"touch"},{"word":"satisfy","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''sætisfai/","meaning":"làm thoả mãn, làm hài lòng"}]},{"questionNum":"168","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy"}],"question":"What is one purpose of the letter?","bilingual":"Mục đích của bức thư là gì?","options":["To announce a name change","To honor distinguished alumni","To suggest revisions to a curriculum","To list an individual’s accomplishments"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"To announce a name change\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"letter","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlɛtər/","meaning":"ký tự là một phần của bảng chữ cái; bằng văn bản"},{"word":"name","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/neɪm/","meaning":"từ hoặc cụm từ mà ai đó hoặc một cái gì đó được dùng"},{"word":"change","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ʧeɪnʤ/","meaning":"thay thế; thay đổi; sự thay đổi; tiền xu; tiền nhận được"}]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy"}],"question":"The word “established” in paragraph 1, line 3, is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"Từ “thành lập” ở đoạn 1, dòng 3, gần nghĩa nhất với","options":["affected","founded","confirmed","settled"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"founded\".","vocabList":[{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"affected","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈfɛktɪd/","meaning":"bị ảnh hưởng"},{"word":"founded","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfaʊndɪd/","meaning":"đã thành lập"},{"word":"confirmed","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈfərmd/","meaning":"đã xác nhận"}]},{"questionNum":"170","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy"}],"question":"What is suggested about Dr. Geerlings?","bilingual":"Điều gì được gợi ý về Tiến sĩ Geerlings?","options":["She plans to attend JATA’s anniversary celebration.","She has taught courses in cybersecurity.","She can take part in JATA’s logo design contest.","She served on JATA’s Board of Trustees."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She can take part in JATA’s logo design contest.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"plans","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/plænz/","meaning":"kế hoạch"},{"word":"attend","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtend/","meaning":"tham dự"},{"word":"anniversary","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌænəˈvərsəri/","meaning":"ngày hàng năm kỷ niệm một sự kiện đặc biệt; sinh nhật"},{"word":"celebration","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌsel.əˈbreɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"lễ kỉ niệm"}]},{"questionNum":"171","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"March 29\nDr. Maritza Geerlings\nPoseidonstraat 392\nParamaribo\nSuriname\nDear Dr. Geerlings,\nI am writing to thank you for your years of service on the faculty of the Jamaican\nAgricultural Training Academy (JATA) and to let you know about some exciting\ndevelopments. As you know, JATA was originally established as a vocational school\nfor agriculture but now offers courses in a varied array of disciplines, including\ncybersecurity, electrical engineering, and health information management. Our\nstudent body, which for the first ten years consisted almost exclusively of locals, is\nnow culturally diverse, with students from across the Americas and Europe.\nToday’s students work with sophisticated equipment, much of which did not exist\nin our early days.\nTo reflect these and other significant changes that JATA has undergone over time,\nthe Board of Trustees has approved a proposal by the Faculty Senate to rename\nthe institution the Caribbean Academy of Science and Technology. As a result, a\nnew institutional logo will be adopted. All students and faculty members, both\ncurrent and former, are invited to participate in a logo design contest. Information\nabout the contest will be forthcoming.\nThe renaming ceremony and the introduction of the new logo will take place at\nII A.M. on 1 June, the twentieth anniversary of the institution. We hope you will be\nable to join us.\nSincerely,\nAudley Beu Hett\nAudley Bartlett\nVice President for Academic Affairs,\nJamaican Agricultural Training Academy"}],"question":"What is NOT indicated about JATA in the letter?","bilingual":"Điều gì KHÔNG được nêu về JATA trong thư?","options":["Its professors live on campus.","Its students have access to modern equipment.","It will be twenty years old on June 1.","It is attended by international students."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Its professors live on campus.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"letter","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlɛtər/","meaning":"ký tự là một phần của bảng chữ cái; bằng văn bản"},{"word":"students","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈstudənts/","meaning":"Sinh viên"},{"word":"access","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈæk.ses/","meaning":"quyền truy cập, sự tiếp cận; truy cập"},{"word":"equipment","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪkˈwɪpmənt/","meaning":"quân nhu; các mặt hàng cần thiết; công cụ, dụng cụ hoặc những thứ khác"}]},{"questionNum":"172","passageTitle":"Questions 172-175 refer to the following online chat discussion.","passageText":"Ashley Montaine 8:54 A.M.: How did the interview with Mr. Erickson go?\nDan Campbell 8:55 A.M.: I really enjoyed meeting him. I think he’d be a great reporter\nhere. He seems smart and organized, and his samples show that he’s a great writer.\nAshley Montaine 8:57 A.M.: Brooke, can you contact Mr. Erickson to set up the next\ninterview? Is that a problem?\nDan Campbell 8:58 A.M.: I’d really like to work with him. It is very important that he\nimpress Mr. Peters.\nBrooke Randolph 8:59 A.M.: Not at all.\nAshley Montaine 9:00 A.M.: Thanks. I also see that he has a varied work history. That\nwill make him a well-rounded reporter.\nBrooke Randolph 9:02 A.M.: When would you like to meet with him again?\nDan Campbell 9:03 A.M.: Ashley, I believe you will participate in the next interview.\nNote that Mr. Peters is probably going to ask why Mr. Erickson wants to transition from\nfreelance writing to in-house news reporting. Also, Mr. Peters will want assurances that\nhe’s committed and will stick around for several years.\nAshley Montaine 9:04 A.M.: Brooke, Mr. Peters and I are both free Friday morning.\nBrooke Randolph 9:06 A.M.: Great. I’ll write an e-mail shortly.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Ashley Montaine 8:54 A.M.: How did the interview with Mr. Erickson go?\nDan Campbell 8:55 A.M.: I really enjoyed meeting him. I think he’d be a great reporter\nhere. He seems smart and organized, and his samples show that he’s a great writer.\nAshley Montaine 8:57 A.M.: Brooke, can you contact Mr. Erickson to set up the next\ninterview? Is that a problem?\nDan Campbell 8:58 A.M.: I’d really like to work with him. It is very important that he\nimpress Mr. Peters.\nBrooke Randolph 8:59 A.M.: Not at all.\nAshley Montaine 9:00 A.M.: Thanks. I also see that he has a varied work history. That\nwill make him a well-rounded reporter.\nBrooke Randolph 9:02 A.M.: When would you like to meet with him again?\nDan Campbell 9:03 A.M.: Ashley, I believe you will participate in the next interview.\nNote that Mr. Peters is probably going to ask why Mr. Erickson wants to transition from\nfreelance writing to in-house news reporting. Also, Mr. Peters will want assurances that\nhe’s committed and will stick around for several years.\nAshley Montaine 9:04 A.M.: Brooke, Mr. Peters and I are both free Friday morning.\nBrooke Randolph 9:06 A.M.: Great. I’ll write an e-mail shortly."}],"question":"For what type of company do the writers work?","bilingual":"Người viết bài làm việc cho loại công ty nào?","options":["A book publisher","A newspaper","A film production company","A job-placement firm"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"A newspaper\".","vocabList":[{"word":"company","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkʌm.pə.ni/","meaning":"công ty, bạn bè, bằng hữu"},{"word":"work","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/wərk/","meaning":"nhân công; nhiệm vụ; nghề nghiệp; nghề nghiệp; ơn gọi; cố gắng"},{"word":"book","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/bʊk/","meaning":"cuốn sách; đặt phòng, đặt vé"},{"word":"publisher","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpəblɪʃər/","meaning":"người hoặc công ty sản xuất và phân phối"}]},{"questionNum":"173","passageTitle":"Questions 172-175 refer to the following online chat discussion.","passageText":"Ashley Montaine 8:54 A.M.: How did the interview with Mr. Erickson go?\nDan Campbell 8:55 A.M.: I really enjoyed meeting him. I think he’d be a great reporter\nhere. He seems smart and organized, and his samples sho