Rowell,\nI am the owner of Lenoiva, a health-care technology company. We plan to expand our\noperations and we need new office space. The An ton Building is one of the locations in\nClanton that we are considering. We have been informed that your restoration project of\nthis building will be finished sometime this spring, which is good timing for us. We are\nparticularly attracted by the easy access to public transportation services that your building\noffers. Do you still have spaces available for rent? We anticipate needing a space at least\n300 square metres in size. Would there be any reserved parking for our employees if we\nrented there? We would appreciate any information you can provide.\nThank you in advance,\nAna Bautista\n\nOne An ton Place-2nd Floor Plan (office space)\nUnit 2A\n350 m2\nT&M Accountancy\nUnit 2D\n250 m2\nAvailable\nUnit 2B Unit 2C\n150 m2 100 m2\nAvailable Available\nUnit 2E\n375 m2\nAvailable","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (article)","text":"An ton Building\nClanton (12 October) ------- The planned\nrenovation of the historic An ton Building by\nJantuni Property Developers (JPD) is facing\nnew delays. A JPD spokesperson says their\nnegotiations with the city regarding a package\nof subsidies and tax incentives are ongoing\nand are proving somewhat contentious.\nAccording to the renovation plan, JPD must\nprotect the historical integrity of the An ton\nBuilding while it creates a mixed-use interior,\noffering both office space and lower-level\nretail space. However, JPD’s city permit to do\nthe project is on hold pending the current\nnegotiations.\nThis is making city revitalization advocates\nincreasingly anxious. Aditi Yadav comments,\n“This plan to create useful space out of an\nempty decaying building will go a long way to\nrestoring vibrancy to that area of the city. I\nsincerely hope that JPD does not back out. In\ncreating their offer, the City Council should\nconsider JPD''s excellent record of beautifully\nrestoring and maintaining several other\nhistoric buildings in Clanton.”"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: ana bautista @lenoiva-health.com\nTo: t.rowell @jantunipropertydevelopers.com\nDate: 20 February\nSubject: Lease inquiry\nDear Mr. Rowell,\nI am the owner of Lenoiva, a health-care technology company. We plan to expand our\noperations and we need new office space. The An ton Building is one of the locations in\nClanton that we are considering. We have been informed that your restoration project of\nthis building will be finished sometime this spring, which is good timing for us. We are\nparticularly attracted by the easy access to public transportation services that your building\noffers. Do you still have spaces available for rent? We anticipate needing a space at least\n300 square metres in size. Would there be any reserved parking for our employees if we\nrented there? We would appreciate any information you can provide.\nThank you in advance,\nAna Bautista"},{"label":"Văn bản 3 (plan)","text":"One An ton Place-2nd Floor Plan (office space)\nUnit 2A\n350 m2\nT&M Accountancy\nUnit 2D\n250 m2\nAvailable\nUnit 2B Unit 2C\n150 m2 100 m2\nAvailable Available\nUnit 2E\n375 m2\nAvailable"}],"question":"What is suggested about JPD in Ms. Bautista’s e-mail?","bilingual":"Trong email của bà Bautista có đề cập gì về JPD?","options":["It received the approval it was seeking.","It has the only available office spaces for rent in Clanton.","It has moved its main office to the An ton Building.","It is a relatively new company."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It received the approval it was seeking.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"approval","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈpruvəl/","meaning":"xác nhận; chứng thực; ý kiến ​​tích cực"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"},{"word":"office","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔfəs/","meaning":"buồng; văn phòng; đương nhiệm; hãng; thẩm quyền"}]},{"questionNum":"194","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following article, e-mail, and plan.","passageText":"An ton Building\nClanton (12 October) ------- The planned\nrenovation of the historic An ton Building by\nJantuni Property Developers (JPD) is facing\nnew delays. A JPD spokesperson says their\nnegotiations with the city regarding a package\nof subsidies and tax incentives are ongoing\nand are proving somewhat contentious.\nAccording to the renovation plan, JPD must\nprotect the historical integrity of the An ton\nBuilding while it creates a mixed-use interior,\noffering both office space and lower-level\nretail space. However, JPD’s city permit to do\nthe project is on hold pending the current\nnegotiations.\nThis is making city revitalization advocates\nincreasingly anxious. Aditi Yadav comments,\n“This plan to create useful space out of an\nempty decaying building will go a long way to\nrestoring vibrancy to that area of the city. I\nsincerely hope that JPD does not back out. In\ncreating their offer, the City Council should\nconsider JPD''s excellent record of beautifully\nrestoring and maintaining several other\nhistoric buildings in Clanton.”\n\nFrom: ana bautista @lenoiva-health.com\nTo: t.rowell @jantunipropertydevelopers.com\nDate: 20 February\nSubject: Lease inquiry\nDear Mr. Rowell,\nI am the owner of Lenoiva, a health-care technology company. We plan to expand our\noperations and we need new office space. The An ton Building is one of the locations in\nClanton that we are considering. We have been informed that your restoration project of\nthis building will be finished sometime this spring, which is good timing for us. We are\nparticularly attracted by the easy access to public transportation services that your building\noffers. Do you still have spaces available for rent? We anticipate needing a space at least\n300 square metres in size. Would there be any reserved parking for our employees if we\nrented there? We would appreciate any information you can provide.\nThank you in advance,\nAna Bautista\n\nOne An ton Place-2nd Floor Plan (office space)\nUnit 2A\n350 m2\nT&M Accountancy\nUnit 2D\n250 m2\nAvailable\nUnit 2B Unit 2C\n150 m2 100 m2\nAvailable Available\nUnit 2E\n375 m2\nAvailable","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (article)","text":"An ton Building\nClanton (12 October) ------- The planned\nrenovation of the historic An ton Building by\nJantuni Property Developers (JPD) is facing\nnew delays. A JPD spokesperson says their\nnegotiations with the city regarding a package\nof subsidies and tax incentives are ongoing\nand are proving somewhat contentious.\nAccording to the renovation plan, JPD must\nprotect the historical integrity of the An ton\nBuilding while it creates a mixed-use interior,\noffering both office space and lower-level\nretail space. However, JPD’s city permit to do\nthe project is on hold pending the current\nnegotiations.\nThis is making city revitalization advocates\nincreasingly anxious. Aditi Yadav comments,\n“This plan to create useful space out of an\nempty decaying building will go a long way to\nrestoring vibrancy to that area of the city. I\nsincerely hope that JPD does not back out. In\ncreating their offer, the City Council should\nconsider JPD''s excellent record of beautifully\nrestoring and maintaining several other\nhistoric buildings in Clanton.”"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: ana bautista @lenoiva-health.com\nTo: t.rowell @jantunipropertydevelopers.com\nDate: 20 February\nSubject: Lease inquiry\nDear Mr. Rowell,\nI am the owner of Lenoiva, a health-care technology company. We plan to expand our\noperations and we need new office space. The An ton Building is one of the locations in\nClanton that we are considering. We have been informed that your restoration project of\nthis building will be finished sometime this spring, which is good timing for us. We are\nparticularly attracted by the easy access to public transportation services that your building\noffers. Do you still have spaces available for rent? We anticipate needing a space at least\n300 square metres in size. Would there be any reserved parking for our employees if we\nrented there? We would appreciate any information you can provide.\nThank you in advance,\nAna Bautista"},{"label":"Văn bản 3 (plan)","text":"One An ton Place-2nd Floor Plan (office space)\nUnit 2A\n350 m2\nT&M Accountancy\nUnit 2D\n250 m2\nAvailable\nUnit 2B Unit 2C\n150 m2 100 m2\nAvailable Available\nUnit 2E\n375 m2\nAvailable"}],"question":"What information about the building does Ms. Bautista request from Mr. Rowell?","bilingual":"Bà Bautista yêu cầu ông Rowell những thông tin gì về tòa nhà?","options":["The distance to the nearest train station","The other occupants’ types of business","The completion date of the renovation","The availability of employee parking"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"The availability of employee parking\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"building","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈbɪldɪŋ/","meaning":"căn nhà; nhà ở; kết cấu; cơ sở"},{"word":"request","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈkwest/","meaning":"yêu cầu"},{"word":"station","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsteɪʃən/","meaning":"chức vụ; nơi mà một người hoặc vật thường ở đó"}]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following article, e-mail, and plan.","passageText":"An ton Building\nClanton (12 October) ------- The planned\nrenovation of the historic An ton Building by\nJantuni Property Developers (JPD) is facing\nnew delays. A JPD spokesperson says their\nnegotiations with the city regarding a package\nof subsidies and tax incentives are ongoing\nand are proving somewhat contentious.\nAccording to the renovation plan, JPD must\nprotect the historical integrity of the An ton\nBuilding while it creates a mixed-use interior,\noffering both office space and lower-level\nretail space. However, JPD’s city permit to do\nthe project is on hold pending the current\nnegotiations.\nThis is making city revitalization advocates\nincreasingly anxious. Aditi Yadav comments,\n“This plan to create useful space out of an\nempty decaying building will go a long way to\nrestoring vibrancy to that area of the city. I\nsincerely hope that JPD does not back out. In\ncreating their offer, the City Council should\nconsider JPD''s excellent record of beautifully\nrestoring and maintaining several other\nhistoric buildings in Clanton.”\n\nFrom: ana bautista @lenoiva-health.com\nTo: t.rowell @jantunipropertydevelopers.com\nDate: 20 February\nSubject: Lease inquiry\nDear Mr. Rowell,\nI am the owner of Lenoiva, a health-care technology company. We plan to expand our\noperations and we need new office space. The An ton Building is one of the locations in\nClanton that we are considering. We have been informed that your restoration project of\nthis building will be finished sometime this spring, which is good timing for us. We are\nparticularly attracted by the easy access to public transportation services that your building\noffers. Do you still have spaces available for rent? We anticipate needing a space at least\n300 square metres in size. Would there be any reserved parking for our employees if we\nrented there? We would appreciate any information you can provide.\nThank you in advance,\nAna Bautista\n\nOne An ton Place-2nd Floor Plan (office space)\nUnit 2A\n350 m2\nT&M Accountancy\nUnit 2D\n250 m2\nAvailable\nUnit 2B Unit 2C\n150 m2 100 m2\nAvailable Available\nUnit 2E\n375 m2\nAvailable","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (article)","text":"An ton Building\nClanton (12 October) ------- The planned\nrenovation of the historic An ton Building by\nJantuni Property Developers (JPD) is facing\nnew delays. A JPD spokesperson says their\nnegotiations with the city regarding a package\nof subsidies and tax incentives are ongoing\nand are proving somewhat contentious.\nAccording to the renovation plan, JPD must\nprotect the historical integrity of the An ton\nBuilding while it creates a mixed-use interior,\noffering both office space and lower-level\nretail space. However, JPD’s city permit to do\nthe project is on hold pending the current\nnegotiations.\nThis is making city revitalization advocates\nincreasingly anxious. Aditi Yadav comments,\n“This plan to create useful space out of an\nempty decaying building will go a long way to\nrestoring vibrancy to that area of the city. I\nsincerely hope that JPD does not back out. In\ncreating their offer, the City Council should\nconsider JPD''s excellent record of beautifully\nrestoring and maintaining several other\nhistoric buildings in Clanton.”"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: ana bautista @lenoiva-health.com\nTo: t.rowell @jantunipropertydevelopers.com\nDate: 20 February\nSubject: Lease inquiry\nDear Mr. Rowell,\nI am the owner of Lenoiva, a health-care technology company. We plan to expand our\noperations and we need new office space. The An ton Building is one of the locations in\nClanton that we are considering. We have been informed that your restoration project of\nthis building will be finished sometime this spring, which is good timing for us. We are\nparticularly attracted by the easy access to public transportation services that your building\noffers. Do you still have spaces available for rent? We anticipate needing a space at least\n300 square metres in size. Would there be any reserved parking for our employees if we\nrented there? We would appreciate any information you can provide.\nThank you in advance,\nAna Bautista"},{"label":"Văn bản 3 (plan)","text":"One An ton Place-2nd Floor Plan (office space)\nUnit 2A\n350 m2\nT&M Accountancy\nUnit 2D\n250 m2\nAvailable\nUnit 2B Unit 2C\n150 m2 100 m2\nAvailable Available\nUnit 2E\n375 m2\nAvailable"}],"question":"What space would Lenoiva most likely choose to rent?","bilingual":"Lenoiva có khả năng sẽ chọn thuê không gian nào nhất?","options":["Unit 2B","Unit 2C","Unit 2D","Unit 2E"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Unit 2E\".","vocabList":[{"word":"space","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/speɪs/","meaning":"vũ trụ; khu vực trống; khoảng cách; khu vực; khoảng thời gian"},{"word":"choose","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ʧuz/","meaning":"lựa chọn; thích hơn; để chọn ; để thực hiện một sự lựa chọn"},{"word":"rent","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rent/","meaning":"sự thuê mướn"},{"word":"unit","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈjunɪt/","meaning":"số lượng cụ thể được coi là tiêu chuẩn; sự kết hợp"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and price list.","passageText":"From: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nTo: info@clanestongear.com Subject: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 29\nHello Daneston Gear Company (DGC),\nI am the president of an activities club. This month, our 30 members intend to take a day\ntrip to Daneston to go boating on the lake. Could you please send me information\nregarding your rates and offerings? We are most interested in renting boats that seat one\nperson. Some time ago, I rented a kayak for myself from DGC, but this will be my first\ntime renting from DGC for a group.\nThank you,\nTanya Jefferson\n\nFrom: info@danestongear.com To: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nSubject: RE: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 30\nAttachment: § Price list\nDear Ms. Jefferson,\nThank you for contacting us regarding your group''s anticipated visit to DGC. We look\nforward to equipping your club for its next adventure. A price list is attached to this\ne-mail. If you wish to discuss our rentals in more detail, please call me at (888) 555-1578.\nIncidentally, we recently added a row boat option that is an excellent choice for adults who\nwish to boat with their children.\nI will be pleased to help you when you are ready to make your reservation.\nBest,\nAdam Goldstein\n\nDGC Price list\nBoat type\nOption 1 2-person canoe\nOption 2 3-person canoe\nOption 3 1-person kayak\nOption 4 2-person kayak\nHourly rate Additional\n1/2 hour\n$13 $8\n$15 $8\n$11 $8\n$14 $8\nOption 5 3- or 4-person row boat $13 $9\n(3 adults or 2 adults\nand 2 small children)\n•We are open every day from April to October, 10:00 A.M. to 6:30 RM.\n•All boats must be returned by 6:15 EM. on the day they are rented.\n•Life jackets and paddles are included in the rental fee.\n•Groups of ten or more qualify for a discount if they book at least\none week in advance.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"From: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nTo: info@clanestongear.com Subject: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 29\nHello Daneston Gear Company (DGC),\nI am the president of an activities club. This month, our 30 members intend to take a day\ntrip to Daneston to go boating on the lake. Could you please send me information\nregarding your rates and offerings? We are most interested in renting boats that seat one\nperson. Some time ago, I rented a kayak for myself from DGC, but this will be my first\ntime renting from DGC for a group.\nThank you,\nTanya Jefferson"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (price list)","text":"From: info@danestongear.com To: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nSubject: RE: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 30\nAttachment: § Price list\nDear Ms. Jefferson,\nThank you for contacting us regarding your group''s anticipated visit to DGC. We look\nforward to equipping your club for its next adventure. A price list is attached to this\ne-mail. If you wish to discuss our rentals in more detail, please call me at (888) 555-1578.\nIncidentally, we recently added a row boat option that is an excellent choice for adults who\nwish to boat with their children.\nI will be pleased to help you when you are ready to make your reservation.\nBest,\nAdam Goldstein\n\nDGC Price list\nBoat type\nOption 1 2-person canoe\nOption 2 3-person canoe\nOption 3 1-person kayak\nOption 4 2-person kayak\nHourly rate Additional\n1/2 hour\n$13 $8\n$15 $8\n$11 $8\n$14 $8\nOption 5 3- or 4-person row boat $13 $9\n(3 adults or 2 adults\nand 2 small children)\n•We are open every day from April to October, 10:00 A.M. to 6:30 RM.\n•All boats must be returned by 6:15 EM. on the day they are rented.\n•Life jackets and paddles are included in the rental fee.\n•Groups of ten or more qualify for a discount if they book at least\none week in advance."}],"question":"What does Ms. Jefferson mention in the first e-mail?","bilingual":"Bà Jefferson đề cập đến điều gì trong e-mail đầu tiên?","options":["She has used DGC’s services before.","She teaches a course in boating safety.","She is a resident of Daneston.","She owns her own kayak."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"She has used DGC’s services before.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mention","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''menʃn/","meaning":"sự kể ra, sự nói đến, sự đề cập"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"service","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''sə:vis/","meaning":"sự phục vụ, sự hầu hạ"},{"word":"course","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kɔrs/","meaning":"đi săn; theo đuổi; chạy qua; đua"}]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and price list.","passageText":"From: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nTo: info@clanestongear.com Subject: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 29\nHello Daneston Gear Company (DGC),\nI am the president of an activities club. This month, our 30 members intend to take a day\ntrip to Daneston to go boating on the lake. Could you please send me information\nregarding your rates and offerings? We are most interested in renting boats that seat one\nperson. Some time ago, I rented a kayak for myself from DGC, but this will be my first\ntime renting from DGC for a group.\nThank you,\nTanya Jefferson\n\nFrom: info@danestongear.com To: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nSubject: RE: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 30\nAttachment: § Price list\nDear Ms. Jefferson,\nThank you for contacting us regarding your group''s anticipated visit to DGC. We look\nforward to equipping your club for its next adventure. A price list is attached to this\ne-mail. If you wish to discuss our rentals in more detail, please call me at (888) 555-1578.\nIncidentally, we recently added a row boat option that is an excellent choice for adults who\nwish to boat with their children.\nI will be pleased to help you when you are ready to make your reservation.\nBest,\nAdam Goldstein\n\nDGC Price list\nBoat type\nOption 1 2-person canoe\nOption 2 3-person canoe\nOption 3 1-person kayak\nOption 4 2-person kayak\nHourly rate Additional\n1/2 hour\n$13 $8\n$15 $8\n$11 $8\n$14 $8\nOption 5 3- or 4-person row boat $13 $9\n(3 adults or 2 adults\nand 2 small children)\n•We are open every day from April to October, 10:00 A.M. to 6:30 RM.\n•All boats must be returned by 6:15 EM. on the day they are rented.\n•Life jackets and paddles are included in the rental fee.\n•Groups of ten or more qualify for a discount if they book at least\none week in advance.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"From: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nTo: info@clanestongear.com Subject: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 29\nHello Daneston Gear Company (DGC),\nI am the president of an activities club. This month, our 30 members intend to take a day\ntrip to Daneston to go boating on the lake. Could you please send me information\nregarding your rates and offerings? We are most interested in renting boats that seat one\nperson. Some time ago, I rented a kayak for myself from DGC, but this will be my first\ntime renting from DGC for a group.\nThank you,\nTanya Jefferson"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (price list)","text":"From: info@danestongear.com To: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nSubject: RE: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 30\nAttachment: § Price list\nDear Ms. Jefferson,\nThank you for contacting us regarding your group''s anticipated visit to DGC. We look\nforward to equipping your club for its next adventure. A price list is attached to this\ne-mail. If you wish to discuss our rentals in more detail, please call me at (888) 555-1578.\nIncidentally, we recently added a row boat option that is an excellent choice for adults who\nwish to boat with their children.\nI will be pleased to help you when you are ready to make your reservation.\nBest,\nAdam Goldstein\n\nDGC Price list\nBoat type\nOption 1 2-person canoe\nOption 2 3-person canoe\nOption 3 1-person kayak\nOption 4 2-person kayak\nHourly rate Additional\n1/2 hour\n$13 $8\n$15 $8\n$11 $8\n$14 $8\nOption 5 3- or 4-person row boat $13 $9\n(3 adults or 2 adults\nand 2 small children)\n•We are open every day from April to October, 10:00 A.M. to 6:30 RM.\n•All boats must be returned by 6:15 EM. on the day they are rented.\n•Life jackets and paddles are included in the rental fee.\n•Groups of ten or more qualify for a discount if they book at least\none week in advance."}],"question":"What rental option best meets Ms. Jefferson’s needs?","bilingual":"Lựa chọn cho thuê nào đáp ứng tốt nhất nhu cầu của cô Jefferson?","options":["Option 1","Option 2","Option 3","Option 4"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Option 3\".","vocabList":[{"word":"rental","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈrɛntəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để cho thuê hoặc cho thuê"},{"word":"option","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔpʃən/","meaning":"sự lựa chọn; thay thế; khả năng; lựa chọn; cuộc bầu cử"},{"word":"needs","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/nidz/","meaning":"cần"},{"word":"supplier","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈplaɪ.ɚ/","meaning":"nhà cung cấp"}]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and price list.","passageText":"From: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nTo: info@clanestongear.com Subject: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 29\nHello Daneston Gear Company (DGC),\nI am the president of an activities club. This month, our 30 members intend to take a day\ntrip to Daneston to go boating on the lake. Could you please send me information\nregarding your rates and offerings? We are most interested in renting boats that seat one\nperson. Some time ago, I rented a kayak for myself from DGC, but this will be my first\ntime renting from DGC for a group.\nThank you,\nTanya Jefferson\n\nFrom: info@danestongear.com To: Tanya Jefferson <tjeff @key suppliers.com>\nSubject: RE: Request for group rental information\nDate: May 30\nAttachment: § Price list\nDear Ms. Jefferson,\nThank you for contacting us regarding your group''s anticipated visit to DGC. We look\nforward to equipping your 