rtunate. We need to follow up with that meeting to\nadvise our client about what is important to potential customers.\nMaria Andreou (9:10 A.M.) Exactly. So I would rather not have to reschedule. The client\nis expecting our report early next week. Would either of you be able to conduct the group\ninstead of me?\nSandra Liu (9:12 A.M.) Sorry, Maria. I’m traveling out of town tomorrow for the marketing\nconference, and won’t be back until Friday.\nJakob Wendt (9:15 A.M.) I’ve never led a focus group before, but I’m happy to do it.\nMaria Andreou (9:17 A.M.) Great. I’ll send you the participant consent form by e-mail.\nRemember that at the start of the group session, each participant will need to sign a copy.\nJakob Wendt (9:18 A.M.) OK. How many copies will be needed?\nSandra Liu (9:19 A.M.) Actually, there’s no need. I have copies left over from another group\nI ran last Tuesday. They’re still on my desk.\nJakob Wendt (9:20 A.M.) I’ll stop by and pick them up later today.\nMaria Andreou (9:21 A.M) Thank you both. This means we can meet and work on the\nadvertising report for the client next Monday.\nO","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Maria Andreou (9:06 A.M.) Good morning, Jakob and Sandra. I need help with the focus '' >\ngroup with the photographers that is taking place on Thursday morning. I’m no longer\navailable to lead it.\nJakob Wendt (9:09 A.M.) That’s unfortunate. We need to follow up with that meeting to\nadvise our client about what is important to potential customers.\nMaria Andreou (9:10 A.M.) Exactly. So I would rather not have to reschedule. The client\nis expecting our report early next week. Would either of you be able to conduct the group\ninstead of me?\nSandra Liu (9:12 A.M.) Sorry, Maria. I’m traveling out of town tomorrow for the marketing\nconference, and won’t be back until Friday.\nJakob Wendt (9:15 A.M.) I’ve never led a focus group before, but I’m happy to do it.\nMaria Andreou (9:17 A.M.) Great. I’ll send you the participant consent form by e-mail.\nRemember that at the start of the group session, each participant will need to sign a copy.\nJakob Wendt (9:18 A.M.) OK. How many copies will be needed?\nSandra Liu (9:19 A.M.) Actually, there’s no need. I have copies left over from another group\nI ran last Tuesday. They’re still on my desk.\nJakob Wendt (9:20 A.M.) I’ll stop by and pick them up later today.\nMaria Andreou (9:21 A.M) Thank you both. This means we can meet and work on the\nadvertising report for the client next Monday.\nO"}],"question":"At 9:19 A.M., what does Ms. Liu most likely mean when she writes, “there’s no need”?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 9:19 sáng, rất có thể cô Liu có ý gì khi viết, “không cần đâu”?","options":["She can cancel her business trip.","Focus group participants will not complete consent forms.","A focus group can be rescheduled.","Mr. Wendt should not print any consent forms."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Mr. Wendt should not print any consent forms.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"need","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/nid/","meaning":"yêu cầu; thiếu một mặt hàng không thể thiếu;"},{"word":"cancel","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkæn.səl/","meaning":"hủy bỏ, xóa"}]},{"questionNum":"176","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Our Company Our Products Our Partners Contact Us\nDrymotic is pleased to announce that our revolutionary vacuum-microwave\ndehydration process is now being used by more than 30 companies in the\nfood and pharmaceutical industries.\nHere''s how it works: Batches of raw organic materials, prepared in small pieces,\nare loaded into the machines rotatingdrum. As the drum turns, moisture is\nremoved from the pieces by microwave energy. The final moisture level can\nbe pre set by the operator. The dried pieces retain their color, taste, and\nnutrition, and are then ready for packaging. Drymotic machines produce better\nresults in less time (and at lower cost) than freeze-drying and air-drying.\nDrymotic machines are available in the following sizes:\nModel Number Power\nG4200 10 kw\nG4260 50 kw\nH4500 100 kw\nSuggested use\nTesting new products\nSmall-scale manufacturers\nLarge-scale, high-volume manufacturers\n\n*E-mail*\nTo: customerservice@drymotic.com From: ovolterra @yambrett.com.au\nDate: 6 May\nSubject: Malfunctioning unit\nDear Customer Service,\nWe purchased a Drymotic unit (product number: G4260, serial number: 01938207) last\nyear for use with our line of instant stew mixes. We had no issues with the unit until the\nbeginning of this month, when we began to notice an increase in processing time. We\nhave followed the recommended cleaning schedule, so this problem cannot be caused by\nexcess residue.\nPlease let me know if you have any suggestions for resolving this issue in a timely\nmanner. I always prefer to handle minor repairs on my own, but if this issue persists, we\nmay need to schedule a maintenance visit in the near future.\nBest regards,\nOlivia Vo1terra\nYambrett Corporation","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Our Company Our Products Our Partners Contact Us\nDrymotic is pleased to announce that our revolutionary vacuum-microwave\ndehydration process is now being used by more than 30 companies in the\nfood and pharmaceutical industries.\nHere''s how it works: Batches of raw organic materials, prepared in small pieces,\nare loaded into the machines rotatingdrum. As the drum turns, moisture is\nremoved from the pieces by microwave energy. The final moisture level can\nbe pre set by the operator. The dried pieces retain their color, taste, and\nnutrition, and are then ready for packaging. Drymotic machines produce better\nresults in less time (and at lower cost) than freeze-drying and air-drying.\nDrymotic machines are available in the following sizes:\nModel Number Power\nG4200 10 kw\nG4260 50 kw\nH4500 100 kw\nSuggested use\nTesting new products\nSmall-scale manufacturers\nLarge-scale, high-volume manufacturers"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nTo: customerservice@drymotic.com From: ovolterra @yambrett.com.au\nDate: 6 May\nSubject: Malfunctioning unit\nDear Customer Service,\nWe purchased a Drymotic unit (product number: G4260, serial number: 01938207) last\nyear for use with our line of instant stew mixes. We had no issues with the unit until the\nbeginning of this month, when we began to notice an increase in processing time. We\nhave followed the recommended cleaning schedule, so this problem cannot be caused by\nexcess residue.\nPlease let me know if you have any suggestions for resolving this issue in a timely\nmanner. I always prefer to handle minor repairs on my own, but if this issue persists, we\nmay need to schedule a maintenance visit in the near future.\nBest regards,\nOlivia Vo1terra\nYambrett Corporation"}],"question":"What are Drymotic processors designed to do?","bilingual":"Bộ xử lý Drymotic được thiết kế để","options":["Cut food into little pieces","Preserve food by drying it","Add moisture to organic material","Improve a product’s color and taste"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Preserve food by drying it\".","vocabList":[{"word":"food","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/fud/","meaning":"nuôi dưỡng; chất cung cấp cho cơ thể"},{"word":"piece","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pis/","meaning":"nối các bộ phận lại với nhau; để gắn các phân đoạn"},{"word":"preserve","pos":"Danh từ / Động 