":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''sə:vis/","meaning":"sự phục vụ, sự hầu hạ"},{"word":"department","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈpɑːrt.mənt/","meaning":"khoa, bộ"}]},{"questionNum":"180","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Our Company Our Products Our Partners Contact Us\nDrymotic is pleased to announce that our revolutionary vacuum-microwave\ndehydration process is now being used by more than 30 companies in the\nfood and pharmaceutical industries.\nHere''s how it works: Batches of raw organic materials, prepared in small pieces,\nare loaded into the machines rotatingdrum. As the drum turns, moisture is\nremoved from the pieces by microwave energy. The final moisture level can\nbe pre set by the operator. The dried pieces retain their color, taste, and\nnutrition, and are then ready for packaging. Drymotic machines produce better\nresults in less time (and at lower cost) than freeze-drying and air-drying.\nDrymotic machines are available in the following sizes:\nModel Number Power\nG4200 10 kw\nG4260 50 kw\nH4500 100 kw\nSuggested use\nTesting new products\nSmall-scale manufacturers\nLarge-scale, high-volume manufacturers\n\n*E-mail*\nTo: customerservice@drymotic.com From: ovolterra @yambrett.com.au\nDate: 6 May\nSubject: Malfunctioning unit\nDear Customer Service,\nWe purchased a Drymotic unit (product number: G4260, serial number: 01938207) last\nyear for use with our line of instant stew mixes. We had no issues with the unit until the\nbeginning of this month, when we began to notice an increase in processing time. We\nhave followed the recommended cleaning schedule, so this problem cannot be caused by\nexcess residue.\nPlease let me know if you have any suggestions for resolving this issue in a timely\nmanner. I always prefer to handle minor repairs on my own, but if this issue persists, we\nmay need to schedule a maintenance visit in the near future.\nBest regards,\nOlivia Vo1terra\nYambrett Corporation","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Our Company Our Products Our Partners Contact Us\nDrymotic is pleased to announce that our revolutionary vacuum-microwave\ndehydration process is now being used by more than 30 companies in the\nfood and pharmaceutical industries.\nHere''s how it works: Batches of raw organic materials, prepared in small pieces,\nare loaded into the machines rotatingdrum. As the drum turns, moisture is\nremoved from the pieces by microwave energy. The final moisture level can\nbe pre set by the operator. The dried pieces retain their color, taste, and\nnutrition, and are then ready for packaging. Drymotic machines produce better\nresults in less time (and at lower cost) than freeze-drying and air-drying.\nDrymotic machines are available in the following sizes:\nModel Number Power\nG4200 10 kw\nG4260 50 kw\nH4500 100 kw\nSuggested use\nTesting new products\nSmall-scale manufacturers\nLarge-scale, high-volume manufacturers"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nTo: customerservice@drymotic.com From: ovolterra @yambrett.com.au\nDate: 6 May\nSubject: Malfunctioning unit\nDear Customer Service,\nWe purchased a Drymotic unit (product number: G4260, serial number: 01938207) last\nyear for use with our line of instant stew mixes. We had no issues with the unit until the\nbeginning of this month, when we began to notice an increase in processing time. We\nhave followed the recommended cleaning schedule, so this problem cannot be caused by\nexcess residue.\nPlease let me know if you have any suggestions for resolving this issue in a timely\nmanner. I always prefer to handle minor repairs on my own, but if this issue persists, we\nmay need to schedule a maintenance visit in the near future.\nBest regards,\nOlivia Vo1terra\nYambrett Corporation"}],"question":"What problem has developed with the Yambrett Corporation’s process or?","bilingual":"Vấn đề gì đã xảy ra với bộ xử lý của Yambrett Corporation?","options":["It is operating more slowly.","It is making more noise.","It is using more power.","It requires cleaning more often."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It is operating more slowly.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"process","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''prouses/","meaning":"quá trình, sự tiến triển"},{"word":"making","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈmeɪkɪŋ/","meaning":"Thực hiện"},{"word":"noise","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/nɔɪz/","meaning":"Tiếng ồn"},{"word":"using","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈjuzɪŋ/","meaning":"sử dụng"}]},{"questionNum":"181","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following article and e-mail.","passageText":"Spotlight on Carl Ybor\nGORE, New Zealand (2 May) ------- Architect While Mr. Ybor is fully responsible for\nCarl Ybor has created a name for himself creating the design plans for the houses\nby helping clients turn their trash into he builds, he always involves\ntreasure. He has built dozens of houses in homeowners in the building process. With\nGore composed almost entirely of\nreclaimed, recovered, or found materials.\n“As much as possible, I like to use\nmaterials that are already available\nnearby,” says Mr. Ybor. “It just takes\nsome creativity, but that way nothing is\nwasted and houses can be built for a\nfraction of the price. Old fencing,\ndiscarded bottles, corks, mismatched\nbricks and tiles ------- nothing gets\noverlooked.”\n\nTo: contact@yborhabitats.co.nz From: c.holmes@hmail.net Date: 4 May\nSubject: Proposal\nDear Mr. Ybor,\na waiting list of at least a year, Mr. Ybor\nis able to carefully select his clients. He\nworks solely with homeowners who\nalready know how to operate power tools\nand are willing to do some of the hands-\non work themselves.\nSome of his houses have been featured in\nmagazines, travel shows, and online\ncar pen try demonstrations. Mr. Ybor’s Web\nsite, featuring photos of his projects, can\nbe found at yborhabitats.co.nz.\nI just read an article about you. I was excited to learn about your services and\nhow you work with the owners to create unique spaces. I have two projects I\nwant to work on:\n1.1 want to add an extension to my current house, incorporating leftover\nmaterials I have from the patio that I had built a few years ago.\n2. My roof needs to be replaced. I have researched ways to cut the cost, and\none suggestion was to leave the existing roof intact and just install new\nmetal sheeting on top. I like this idea!\nAre you available and interested in doing this work? I would like to start as early\nas next month. I can pay half the money up front by credit card to secure an\nappointment.\nCynthia Holmes!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (article)","text":"Spotlight on Carl Ybor\nGORE, New Zealand (2 May) ------- Architect While Mr. Ybor is fully responsible for\nCarl Ybor has created a name for himself creating the design plans for the houses\nby helping clients turn their trash into he builds, he always involves\ntreasure. He has built dozens of houses in homeowners in the building process. With\nGore composed almost entirely of\nreclaimed, recovered, or found materials.\n“As much as possible, I like to use\nmaterials that are already available\nnearby,” says Mr. Ybor. “It just takes\nsome creativity, but that way nothing is\nwasted and houses can be built for a\nfraction of the price. Old fencing,\ndiscarded bottles, corks, mismatched\nbricks and tiles ------- nothing gets\noverlooked.”"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: contact@yborhabitats.co.nz From: c.holmes@hmail.net Date: 4 May\nSubject: Proposal\nDear Mr. Ybor,\na waiting list of at least a year, Mr. Ybor\nis able to carefully select his clients. He\nworks solely with homeowners who\nalready know how to operate power tools\nand are willing to do some of the hands-\non work themselves.\nSome of his houses have been featured in\nmagazines, travel shows, and online\ncar pen try demonstrations. Mr. Ybor’s Web\nsite, featuring photos of his projects, can\nbe found at yborhabitats.co.nz.\nI just read an article about you. I was excited to learn about your services and\nhow you work with the owners to create unique spaces. I have two projects I\nwant to work on:\n1.1 want to add an extension to my current house, incorporating leftover\nmaterials I have from the patio that I had built a few years ago.\n2. My roof needs to be replaced. I have researched ways to cut the cost, and\none suggestion was to leave the existing roof intact and just install new\nmetal sheeting on top. I like this idea!\nAre you available and interested in doing this work? I would like to start as early\nas next month. I can pay half the money up front by credit card to secure an\nappointment.\nCynthia Holmes!"}],"question":"What does the article state about the houses Mr. Ybor builds?","bilingual":"Bài báo nói gì về những ngôi nhà mà ông Ybor xây dựng?","options":["They are large.","They are expensive.","They are located throughout New Zealand.","They are built with used materials."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"They are built with used materials.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"article","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɑrtɪkəl/","meaning":"mục; sự vật; đoạn văn bản; đoạn hợp đồng"},{"word":"state","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/steɪt/","meaning":"tình trạng; giai đoạn; tâm trạng; sự huy hoàng; Quốc gia"},{"word":"house","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/haʊs/","meaning":"liên quan đến chỗ ở; thuần hóa"},{"word":"build","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/bɪld/","meaning":"xây dựng; để tạo r