go.\n2. My roof needs to be replaced. I have researched ways to cut the cost, and\none suggestion was to leave the existing roof intact and just install new\nmetal sheeting on top. I like this idea!\nAre you available and interested in doing this work? I would like to start as early\nas next month. I can pay half the money up front by credit card to secure an\nappointment.\nCynthia Holmes!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (article)","text":"Spotlight on Carl Ybor\nGORE, New Zealand (2 May) ------- Architect While Mr. Ybor is fully responsible for\nCarl Ybor has created a name for himself creating the design plans for the houses\nby helping clients turn their trash into he builds, he always involves\ntreasure. He has built dozens of houses in homeowners in the building process. With\nGore composed almost entirely of\nreclaimed, recovered, or found materials.\n“As much as possible, I like to use\nmaterials that are already available\nnearby,” says Mr. Ybor. “It just takes\nsome creativity, but that way nothing is\nwasted and houses can be built for a\nfraction of the price. Old fencing,\ndiscarded bottles, corks, mismatched\nbricks and tiles ------- nothing gets\noverlooked.”"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: contact@yborhabitats.co.nz From: c.holmes@hmail.net Date: 4 May\nSubject: Proposal\nDear Mr. Ybor,\na waiting list of at least a year, Mr. Ybor\nis able to carefully select his clients. He\nworks solely with homeowners who\nalready know how to operate power tools\nand are willing to do some of the hands-\non work themselves.\nSome of his houses have been featured in\nmagazines, travel shows, and online\ncar pen try demonstrations. Mr. Ybor’s Web\nsite, featuring photos of his projects, can\nbe found at yborhabitats.co.nz.\nI just read an article about you. I was excited to learn about your services and\nhow you work with the owners to create unique spaces. I have two projects I\nwant to work on:\n1.1 want to add an extension to my current house, incorporating leftover\nmaterials I have from the patio that I had built a few years ago.\n2. My roof needs to be replaced. I have researched ways to cut the cost, and\none suggestion was to leave the existing roof intact and just install new\nmetal sheeting on top. I like this idea!\nAre you available and interested in doing this work? I would like to start as early\nas next month. I can pay half the money up front by credit card to secure an\nappointment.\nCynthia Holmes!"}],"question":"What does Ms. Holmes want to do?","bilingual":"Bà Holmes muốn làm gì?","options":["Remove her old roof","Replace the tiles in her patio","Increase the size of her house","Build a new house"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Increase the size of her house\".","vocabList":[{"word":"want","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/wɔnt/","meaning":"muốn"},{"word":"remove","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ri''mu:v/","meaning":"dời đi, di chuyển, dọn, cất dọn"},{"word":"replace","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪpleɪs/","meaning":"thay thế, thay chỗ ai/cái gì"},{"word":"patio","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈpætiəʊ/","meaning":"sân hiên ngoài trời"}]},{"questionNum":"185","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following article and e-mail.","passageText":"Spotlight on Carl Ybor\nGORE, New Zealand (2 May) ------- Architect While Mr. Ybor is fully responsible for\nCarl Ybor has created a name for himself creating the design plans for the houses\nby helping clients turn their trash into he builds, he always involves\ntreasure. He has built dozens of houses in homeowners in the building process. With\nGore composed almost entirely of\nreclaimed, recovered, or found materials.\n“As much as possible, I like to use\nmaterials that are already available\nnearby,” says Mr. Ybor. “It just takes\nsome creativity, but that way nothing is\nwasted and houses can be built for a\nfraction of the price. Old fencing,\ndiscarded bottles, corks, mismatched\nbricks and tiles ------- nothing gets\noverlooked.”\n\nTo: contact@yborhabitats.co.nz From: c.holmes@hmail.net Date: 4 May\nSubject: Proposal\nDear Mr. Ybor,\na waiting list of at least a year, Mr. Ybor\nis able to carefully select his clients. He\nworks solely with homeowners who\nalready know how to operate power tools\nand are willing to do some of the hands-\non work themselves.\nSome of his houses have been featured in\nmagazines, travel shows, and online\ncar pen try demonstrations. Mr. Ybor’s Web\nsite, featuring photos of his projects, can\nbe found at yborhabitats.co.nz.\nI just read an article about you. I was excited to learn about your services and\nhow you work with the owners to create unique spaces. I have two projects I\nwant to work on:\n1.1 want to add an extension to my current house, incorporating leftover\nmaterials I have from the patio that I had built a few years ago.\n2. My roof needs to be replaced. I have researched ways to cut the cost, and\none suggestion was to leave the existing roof intact and just install new\nmetal sheeting on top. I like this idea!\nAre you available and interested in doing this work? I would like to start as early\nas next month. I can pay half the money up front by credit card to secure an\nappointment.\nCynthia Holmes!","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (article)","text":"Spotlight on Carl Ybor\nGORE, New Zealand (2 May) ------- Architect While Mr. Ybor is fully responsible for\nCarl Ybor has created a name for himself creating the design plans for the houses\nby helping clients turn their trash into he builds, he always involves\ntreasure. He has built dozens of houses in homeowners in the building process. With\nGore composed almost entirely of\nreclaimed, recovered, or found materials.\n“As much as possible, I like to use\nmaterials that are already available\nnearby,” says Mr. Ybor. “It just takes\nsome creativity, but that way nothing is\nwasted and houses can be built for a\nfraction of the price. Old fencing,\ndiscarded bottles, corks, mismatched\nbricks and tiles ------- nothing gets\noverlooked.”"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: contact@yborhabitats.co.nz From: c.holmes@hmail.net Date: 4 May\nSubject: Proposal\nDear Mr. Ybor,\na waiting list of at least a year, Mr. Ybor\nis able to carefully select his clients. He\nworks solely with homeowners who\nalready know how to operate power tools\nand are willing to do some of the hands-\non work themselves.\nSome of his houses have been featured in\nmagazines, travel shows, and online\ncar pen try demonstrations. Mr. Ybor’s Web\nsite, featuring photos of his projects, can\nbe found at yborhabitats.co.nz.\nI just read an article about you. I was excited to learn about your services and\nhow you work with the owners to create unique spaces. I have two projects I\nwant to work on:\n1.1 want to add an extension to my current house, incorporating leftover\nmaterials I have from the patio that I had built a few years ago.\n2. My roof needs to be replaced. I have researched ways to cut the cost, and\none suggestion was to leave the existing roof intact and just install new\nmetal sheeting on top. I like this idea!\nAre you available and interested in doing this work? I would like to start as early\nas next month. I can pay half the money up front by credit card to secure an\nappointment.\nCynthia Holmes!"}],"question":"What part of Ms. Holmes'' s proposal will Mr. Ybor most likely refuse?","bilingual":"Ông Ybor có nhiều khả năng sẽ từ chối phần nào trong đề xuất của bà Holmes?","options":["The starting date","The suggested price","The method of payment","The choice of materials"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"The starting date\".","vocabList":[{"word":"proposal","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/prəˈpoʊzəl/","meaning":"gợi ý; mềm; kế hoạch; đề nghị kết hôn"},{"word":"refuse","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈfyuz/","meaning":"từ chối, khước từ, cự tuyệt"},{"word":"date","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/deɪt/","meaning":"ngày, tháng, năm theo dương lịch;"},{"word":"price","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/praɪs/","meaning":"trị giá; giá trị; đáng giá; tỷ lệ; đo lường"}]},{"questionNum":"186","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mails and agenda.","passageText":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA\n\nTo: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (agenda)","text":"To: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi"}],"question":"What is a purpose of the first e-mail?","bilingual":"Mục đích của email đầu tiên là gì?","options":["To notify staff of an upcoming visit","To advertise a job opening","To recommend an employee for promotion","To introduce a new colleague"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"To notify staff of an upcoming visit\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"notify","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/nəʊ.tɪ.faɪ/","meaning":"báo, khai báo; thông báo"},{"word":"staff","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/stæf/","meaning":"nhân viên"}]},{"questionNum":"187","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mails and agenda.","passageText":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA\n\nTo: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (agenda)","text":"To: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi"}],"question":"What meal were all employees asked to add to their calendars?","bilingual":"Tất cả nhân viên được yêu cầu thêm bữa ăn nào vào lịch của họ?","options":["Breakfast on October 23","Lunch on October 23","Dinner on October 23","Breakfast on October 24"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Breakfast on October 24\".","vocabList":[{"word":"employee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɔɪi/","meaning":"công nhân; người làm việc cho một công ty hoặc một"},{"word":"calendar","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkæləndər/","meaning":"viết ra thời gian biểu; đăng ký"},{"word":"breakfast","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈbrɛkfəst/","meaning":"Bữa sáng"},{"word":"staff","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/stæf/","meaning":"nhân viên"}]},{"questionNum":"188","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mails and agenda.","passageText":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA\n\nTo: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (agenda)","text":"To: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi"}],"question":"What is one reason Ms. Caspi writes to Mr. Chou?","bilingual":"Một lý do khiến cô Caspi viết thư cho ông Chou là gì?","options":["To apologize for a delay","To accept an offer","To discuss air travel plans","To ask for details about a job"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To accept an offer\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reason","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrizən/","meaning":"suy nghĩ ; để xem xét một cách hợp lý; tranh luận ; để yêu cầu"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"apologize","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈpɑː.lə.dʒaɪz/","meaning":"xin lỗi"},{"word":"delay","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈleɪ/","meaning":"sự chậm trễ, trì hoãn; làm chậm, hoãn lại"}]},{"questionNum":"189","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mails and agenda.","passageText":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA\n\nTo: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (agenda)","text":"To: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi"}],"question":"Who most likely is Mr. Georgopoulos?","bilingual":"Ông Georgopoulos có nhiều khả năng là ai nhất?","options":["A Medium Hills Bistro employee","A board member","A department head","A worker in the human resources department"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"A board member\".","vocabList":[{"word":"medium","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmidiəm/","meaning":"phương tiện biểu đạt; kênh liên lạc;"},{"word":"employee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɔɪi/","meaning":"công nhân; người làm việc cho một công ty hoặc một"},{"word":"board","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/bɔːrd/","meaning":"tấm ván, bảng, mạn thuyền"},{"word":"member","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmɛmbər/","meaning":"người thuộc một tổ chức, nhóm; phần;"}]},{"questionNum":"190","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mails and agenda.","passageText":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA\n\nTo: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: All CFA Staff\nFrom: Yung-Chien Chou\nDate: 16 October\nSubject: Plans\nAttachment:|Agenda\nDear Colleagues,\nHagit Caspi will be visiting for a couple of days next week to interview for the position of\nexecutive vice president here at Cliff Feiring Associates (CFA). She is highly qualified,\nand her background in international finance makes her particularly well suited for this role.\nPlease make every effort to welcome her.\nIt is important to the CFA leadership that everyone has the opportunity to get to know\nMs. Caspi. As such, I am asking all of you to attend certain events with her. Please see the\nattached agenda, and add the events marked CFA to your calendar. More details will\nfollow.\nBest,\nYung-Chien Chou\nCEO, Cliff Feiring Associates\nAgenda for Hagit Caspi''s Visit\nDate Time Event Invitees\n23 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast at La Brunch Board members\n23 October 12:30 P.M. Lunch in office Department heads\n23 October 3:00 P.M. Question-and-answer session CFA\n23 October 7:00 P.M. Dinner at Medium Hills Bistro Board members\n24 October 9:00 A.M. Breakfast in office CFA"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (agenda)","text":"To: Yung-Chien Chou <chou @clifffeiring.ca>\nFrom: Hagit Caspi <hagit.caspi @volumel.co.il>\nDate: 27 October\nSubject: Follow-up\nDear Mr. Chou,\nMany thanks for hosting me last week. I truly enjoyed meeting everyone. I particularly\nappreciated my conversation with Mr. Georgopoulos at Medium Hills Bistro. He told me\nsome amazing stories about CFA’s history.\nAgain, I am sorry for not attending the event on the 24th. The weather was worrying, and\nI did not want to miss my flight to Tel Aviv.\nLast but certainly not least, thank you for your offer, which I received this morning. I\nwould be honoured to take on the role of executive vice president of CFA starting in\nJanuary. The job description covers everything we discussed. The hours you noted for the\nposition seem appropriate, and I am very pleased with the benefits. I look forward to\nworking closely with you.\nMost sincerely,\nHagit Caspi"}],"question":"What does the second e-mail indicate about the job?","bilingual":"Email thứ hai nói gì về công việc?","options":["It will begin in January.","It will be based in Tel Aviv.","It involves working overtime.","It still needs a job description."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It will begin in January.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"second","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɛkənd/","meaning":"hỗ trợ một đề xuất hoặc tuyên bố; xác nhận; ĐẾN"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"indicate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.də.keɪt/","meaning":"chỉ ra, chứng tỏ, biểu thị"},{"word":"based","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/beɪst/","meaning":"dựa trên"}]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following article, chart, and e-mail.","passageText":"TRIVESS (l February) ------- Alacritum, Inc., has\nannounced plans to build charging stations for\nelectric vehicles along Highway 1. With over\n400 stations across Asia already, Alacritum\nbrings a wealth of experience to this large-\nscale undertaking. The Highway 1 stations,\nknown as PRO stations, will provide vehicles\nwith up to 200 kilowatts of power, achieving\nan 80 percent charge in 30 minutes. The\nsystem will periodically notify waiting drivers\nof the status of their battery charge by sending\ntexts to their cell phones or other mobile\ndevices. The company promises to provide\nmotorists with clean, comfortable, brightly lit\nwaiting facilities. A testing location will open\nat the beginning of next month in Logred..ii\n\\3\nPRO Stations: Proposed Distribution\nRegion Number of Stations Customers per Day\nElondell 26\nSouthern Borelvia 14\nWestern Borelvia 20\nNorth Shore 10\n9,220\n4,970\n6,390\n3,560\n\nTo: 1hsiao@a1acritum.com From: ctrigg@alacritum.com Date: 15 March\nSubject: Meeting\nDear Mr. Hsiao,\nFollowing the meeting with our community partners in Western Borelvia this week, I\nsuggest adding air-conditioning to the waiting areas in that region because of the desert\nconditions there. Although the addition entails higher costs, it will ensure the comfort and\nsafety of the customers. I have also learned first hand that poor cell service along\nHighway 1 will make the wire less networks at most PRO stations unreliable, so we will\nneed a technological solution for that as well. I will send a full report by the end of the\nweek.\nChuck Trigg","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"TRIVESS (l February) ------- Alacritum, Inc., has\nannounced plans to build charging stations for\nelectric vehicles along Highway 1. With over\n400 stations across Asia already, Alacritum\nbrings a wealth of experience to this large-\nscale undertaking. The Highway 1 stations,\nknown as PRO stations, will provide vehicles\nwith up to 200 kilowatts of power, achieving\nan 80 percent charge in 30 minutes. The\nsystem will periodically notify waiting drivers\nof the status of their battery charge by sending\ntexts to their cell phones or other mobile\ndevices. The company promises to provide\nmotorists with clean, comfortable, brightly lit\nwaiting facilities. A testing location will open\nat the beginning of next month in Logred..ii\n\\3\nPRO Stations: Proposed Distribution\nRegion Number of Stations Customers per Day\nElondell 26\nSouthern Borelvia 14\nWestern Borelvia 20\nNorth Shore 10\n9,220\n4,970\n6,390\n3,560\n\nTo: 1hsiao@a1acritum.com From: ctrigg@alacritum.com Date: 15 March\nSubject: Meeting\nDear Mr. Hsiao,\nFollowing the meeting with our community partners in Western Borelvia this week, I\nsuggest adding air-conditioning to the waiting areas in that region because of the desert\nconditions there. Although the addition entails higher costs, it will ensure the comfort and\nsafety of the customers. I have also learned first hand that poor cell service along\nHighway 1 will make the wire less networks at most PRO stations unreliable, so we will\nneed a technological solution for that as well. I will send a full report by the end of the\nweek.\nChuck Trigg"}],"question":"What does the article indicate about Alacritum, Inc.?","bilingual":"Bài viết nói gì về Alacritum, Inc.?","options":["It operates 80 percent of the charging stations in Asia.","It is moving its head office to Logred in February.","It built 400 PRO stations along Highway 1.","It will test a station site in March."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"It will test a station site in March.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"article","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɑrtɪkəl/","meaning":"mục; sự vật; đoạn văn bản; đoạn hợp đồng"},{"word":"indicate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.də.keɪt/","meaning":"chỉ ra, chứng tỏ, biểu thị"},{"word":"operate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''ɔpəreit/","meaning":"hoạt động; đang làm việc, thi hành (máy...)"},{"word":"percent","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pərˈsɛnt/","meaning":"một phần trăm"}]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following article, chart, and e-mail.","passageText":"TRIVESS (l February) ------- Alacritum, Inc., has\nannounced plans to build charging stations for\nelectric vehicles along Highway 1. With over\n400 stations across Asia already, Alacritum\nbrings a wealth of experience to this large-\nscale undertaking. The Highway 1 stations,\nknown as PRO stations, will provide vehicles\nwith up to 200 kilowatts of power, achieving\nan 80 percent charge in 30 minutes. The\nsystem will periodically notify waiting drivers\nof the status of their battery charge by sending\ntexts to their cell phones or other mobile\ndevices. The company promises to provide\nmotorists with clean, comfortable, brightly lit\nwaiting facilities. A testing location will open\nat the beginning of next month in Logred..ii\n\\3\nPRO Stations: Proposed Distribution\nRegion Number of Stations Customers per Day\nElondell 26\nSouthern Borelvia 14\nWestern Borelvia 20\nNorth Shore 10\n9,220\n4,970\n6,390\n3,560\n\nT