0 refer to the following press release.","passageText":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca."}],"question":"What is the topic of the press release?","bilingual":"Chủ đề của thông cáo báo chí là gì?","options":["The promotion of a company executive","The use of technology in stores","The launch of new product lines","The relocation of a company’s head office"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"The use of technology in stores\".","vocabList":[{"word":"topic","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈtɑpɪk/","meaning":"chủ đề; chủ đề của cuộc trò chuyện; vấn đề"},{"word":"press","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pres/","meaning":"sự ép, sự nén, sự bóp, sự ấn"},{"word":"release","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈliːs/","meaning":"thả ra, trả lại tự do"},{"word":"promotion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prə''mou∫n/","meaning":"sự thăng chức, sự đề bạt"}]},{"questionNum":"159","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following press release.","passageText":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca."}],"question":"What can Bailey do?","bilingual":"Bailey có thể làm gì?","options":["Clean a mess on the floor","Create labels for products","Find areas that have spills","Locate items for customers"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Find areas that have spills\".","vocabList":[{"word":"floor","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/flɔr/","meaning":"đánh ngã; làm kinh ngạc; gây sốc"},{"word":"create","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kriˈeɪt/","meaning":"sản xuất; để thiết kế; làm ; để sản xuất"},{"word":"label","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''leɪbl/","meaning":"nhãn, nhãn hiệu"},{"word":"products","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɑdəkts/","meaning":"sản phẩm"}]},{"questionNum":"160","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following press release.","passageText":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca."}],"question":"What is suggested in the press release?","bilingual":"","options":["A pilot program in Calgary was a success.","Tearson stores will be renovated in December.","A warehouse earned high marks for safety features.","Managers will be hired in several stores."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"A pilot program in Calgary was a success.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"press","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pres/","meaning":"sự ép, sự nén, sự bóp, sự ấn"},{"word":"release","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈliːs/","meaning":"thả ra, trả lại tự do"},{"word":"program","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈproʊˌgræm/","meaning":"lên lịch; lập kế hoạch; viết hệ điều hành"},{"word":"success","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/səkˈsɛs/","meaning":"đạt được điều gì đó mong muốn hoặc cố gắng;"}]},{"questionNum":"161","passageTitle":"Questions 161-163 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"From: Helen Dietrich <hdietrich @ morphospublishing.ca>\nTo: Alia Cervantes <alia.cervantes@gotomail.ca> Date: 3 March\nSubject: Practical Gardening\nDear Ms. Cervantes:\nI am sorry to report that next month’s issue of Practical Gardening will be our last. After\n62 years of monthly issues, we at Morphos Publishing have decided that Practical\nGardening will be among the periodicals that we must discontinue. We plan to redirect the\nresources gained through cost-cutting toward growing our book publishing and\ninstructional video production businesses.\nWe are grateful for your support as a long time subscriber to Practical Gardening. For the\nremainder of your subscription term, we hope you will allow us to instead send you Flora\nDiscovery, our popular publication about wild plants. However, if you would rather have\nthe balance of your subscription account refunded to you, please contact us at\n(822) 555-0127.\nSincerely,\nHelen Dietrich\nSubscription Manager, Morphos Publishing","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"From: Helen Dietrich <hdietrich @ morphospublishing.ca>\nTo: Alia Cervantes <alia.cervantes@gotomail.ca> Date: 3 March\nSubject: Practical Gardening\nDear Ms. Cervantes:\nI am sorry to report that next month’s issue of Practical Gardening will be our last. After\n62 years of monthly issues, we at Morphos Publishing have decided that Practical\nGardening will be among the periodicals that we must discontinue. We plan to redirect the\nresources gained through cost-cutting toward growing our book publishing and\ninstructional video production businesses.\nWe are grateful for your support as a long time subscriber to Practical Gardening. For the\nremainder of your subscription term, we hope you will allow us to instead send you Flora\nDiscovery, our popular publication about wild plants. However, if you would rather have\nthe balance of your subscription account refunded to you, please contact us at\n(822) 555-0127.\nSincerely,\nHelen Dietrich\nSubscription Manager, Morphos Publishing"}],"question":"What is the purpose of the e-mail?","bilingual":"","options":["To apologize for a delay","To promote a new product","To announce a cancellation","To address a billing error"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội du