\nCraig Kopalinski (2:24 P.M.) OK. Lindsay, in addition to those markers, could you please\norder a new chair for the second-floor conference room to replace the one that is broken?\nYou’ll need to look up the model number. Thanks.\n*"}],"question":"In what department does Ms. Daley most likely work?","bilingual":"Cô Daley có khả năng làm việc ở bộ phận nào nhất?","options":["Accounting","Human Resources","Purchasing","Shipping"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Human Resources\".","vocabList":[{"word":"department","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈpɑːrt.mənt/","meaning":"khoa, bộ"},{"word":"work","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/wərk/","meaning":"nhân công; nhiệm vụ; nghề nghiệp; nghề nghiệp; ơn gọi; cố gắng"},{"word":"accounting","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈkaʊn.t̬ɪŋ/","meaning":"sự tính toán, thanh toán"},{"word":"resource","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈrisɔrs/","meaning":"cung cấp; Cổ phần; phương tiện để hoàn thành mục tiêu;"}]},{"questionNum":"167","passageTitle":"Questions 164-167 refer to the following online chat discussion.","passageText":"0-0-0\nLindsay Pokora (2:15 P.M.) Hello, Mr. Kopalinski. I need to place the monthly office *\nsupplies order. In addition to the regular items, can you let me know if anything extra is\nneeded?\nCraig Kopalinski (2:17 P.M.) Let me check with the other managers. Kaitlyn and Jeffrey,\ndo you have any requests for office supplies in your departments?\nKaitlyn Daley (2:18 P.M.) Yes, we need more whiteboard markers.\nCraig Kopalinski (2:19 P.M.) And how about accounting?\nJeffrey Carden (2:20 P.M.) Nothing here.\nLindsay Pokora (2:22 P.M.) Markers? I just checked our inventory and we still have a box\nin the supply room. Do you need a special kind?\nKaitlyn Daley (2:23 P.M.) No, just regular black markers. Three boxes should be enough.\nI tried some markers from the box we have, but they seem to have dried up. A group of new\nemployees will be starting next week, and well need markers for the orientation and\ntraining sessions.\nCraig Kopalinski (2:24 P.M.) OK. Lindsay, in addition to those markers, could you please\norder a new chair for the second-floor conference room to replace the one that is broken?\nYou’ll need to look up the model number. Thanks.\n*","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"0-0-0\nLindsay Pokora (2:15 P.M.) Hello, Mr. Kopalinski. I need to place the monthly office *\nsupplies order. In addition to the regular items, can you let me know if anything extra is\nneeded?\nCraig Kopalinski (2:17 P.M.) Let me check with the other managers. Kaitlyn and Jeffrey,\ndo you have any requests for office supplies in your departments?\nKaitlyn Daley (2:18 P.M.) Yes, we need more whiteboard markers.\nCraig Kopalinski (2:19 P.M.) And how about accounting?\nJeffrey Carden (2:20 P.M.) Nothing here.\nLindsay Pokora (2:22 P.M.) Markers? I just checked our inventory and we still have a box\nin the supply room. Do you need a special kind?\nKaitlyn Daley (2:23 P.M.) No, just regular black markers. Three boxes should be enough.\nI tried some markers from the box we have, but they seem to have dried up. A group of new\nemployees will be starting next week, and well need markers for the orientation and\ntraining sessions.\nCraig Kopalinski (2:24 P.M.) OK. Lindsay, in addition to those markers, could you please\norder a new chair for the second-floor conference room to replace the one that is broken?\nYou’ll need to look up the model number. Thanks.\n*"}],"question":"What will Ms. Pokora most likely do next?","bilingual":"Cô Pokora sẽ làm gì tiếp theo?","options":["Locate some information","Review a training document","Conduct an orientation session","Contact department managers"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Locate some information\".","vocabList":[{"word":"locate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/loʊˈkeɪt/","meaning":"trụ sở ở, nằm ở"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"review","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˌrivˈju/","meaning":"sự khảo sát; nghiên cứu tổng quát; bài kiểm tra; điều tra"},{"word":"training","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈtreɪ.nɪŋ/","meaning":"sự huấn luyện, sự đào tạo"}]},{"questionNum":"168","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: All staff\nFrom: Jan Merchant\nDate: October 15\nSubject: Reginald Carmen\nDear Colleagues,\nIt is my pleasure to welcome Reginald Carmen to Edmonton Engineering Consultants,\nLLC.\nWith his expertise in engineering and education, Dr. Carmen will be a valuable addition to\nour distinguished staff. [2]. Upon graduating from university, he spent six years\ndesigning telecommunications systems for Astro Part, Inc. He comes to us directly from the\nGlasse School of Engineering, where he spent the past nineteen years. While there, he\nserved as a full-time professor for ten years, teaching advanced mathematics and various\nspecial courses in engineering. He was then appointed president of the school and served\nin that position for the remaining nine years of his tenure, [3]. During that time, he\nled the team that redesigned the school’s electrical engineering curriculum. [4] -------.\nDr. Carmen’s first day will be next Tuesday.\nJan Merchant, Director of Personnel","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: All staff\nFrom: Jan Merchant\nDate: October 15\nSubject: Reginald Carmen\nDear Colleagues,\nIt is my pleasure to welcome Reginald Carmen to Edmonton Engineering Consultants,\nLLC.\nWith his expertise in engineering and education, Dr. Carmen will be a valuable addition to\nour distinguished staff. [2]. Upon graduating from university, he spent six years\ndesigning telecommunications systems for Astro Part, Inc. He comes to us directly from the\nGlasse School of Engineering, where he spent the past nineteen years. While there, he\nserved as a full-time professor for ten years, teaching advanced mathematics and various\nspecial courses in engineering. He was then appointed president of the school and served\nin that position for the remaining nine years of his tenure, [3]. During that time, he\nled the team that redesigned the school’s electrical engineering curriculum. [4] -------.\nDr. Carmen’s first day will be next Tuesday.\nJan Merchant, Director of Personnel"}],"question":"Why did Ms. Merchant send the e-mail?","bilingual":"Tại sao bà Merchant gửi e-mail?","options":["To announce that she is retiring","To provide details about a new employee","To welcome a distinguished guest presenter","To publicize expansion into a new line of business"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To provide details about a new employee\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"provide","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/prəˈvaɪd/","meaning":"cung cấp; cấp ; để thiết lập; cung cấp"},{"word":"details","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈditeɪlz/","meaning":"chi tiết"},{"word":"employee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɔɪi/","meaning":"công nhân; người làm việc cho một công ty hoặc một"}]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: All staff\nFrom: Jan Merchant\nDate: October 15\nSubject: Reginald Carmen\nDear Colleagues,\nIt is my pleasure to welcome Reginald Carmen to Edmonton Engineering Consultants,\nLLC.\nWith his expertise in engineering and education, Dr. Carmen will be a valuable addition to\nour distinguished staff. [2]. Upon graduating from university, he spent six years\ndesigning telecommunications systems for Astro Part, Inc. He comes to us directly from the\nGlasse School of Engineering, where he spent the past nineteen years. While there, he\nserved as a full-time professor for ten years, teaching advanced mathematics and various\nspecial courses in engineering. He was then appointed president of the school and served\nin that position for the remaining nine years of his tenure, [3]. During that time, he\nled the team that redesigned the school’s electrical engineering curriculum. [4] -------.\nDr. Carmen’s first day will be next Tuesday.\nJan Merchant, Director of Personnel","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: All staff\nFrom: Jan Merchant\nDate: October 15\nSubject: Reginald Carmen\nDear Colleagues,\nIt is my pleasure to welcome Reginald Carmen to Edmonton Engineering Consultants,\nLLC.\nWith his expertise in engineering and education, Dr. Carmen will be a valuable addition to\nour distinguished staff. [2]. Upon graduating from university, he spent six years\ndesigning telecommunications systems for Astro Part, Inc. He comes to us directly from the\nGlasse School of Engineering, where he spent the past nineteen years. While there, he\nserved as a full-time professor for ten years, teaching advanced mathematics and various\nspecial courses in engineering. He was then appointed president of the school and served\nin that position for the remaining nine years of his tenure, [3]. During that time, he\nled the team that redesigned the school’s electrical engineering curriculum. [4] -------.\nDr. Carmen’s first day will be next Tuesday.\nJan Merchant, Director of Personnel"}],"question":"What is indicated about Dr. Carmen?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về Tiến sĩ Carmen?","options":["He has experience designing communications systems.","He worked as a consultant for Edmonton Engineering Consultants in the past.","He mentored Ms. Merchant at another company.","He graduated from the Glasse School of Engineering."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"He has experience designing communications systems.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"experience","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪr.i.əns/","meaning":"trải nghiệm, kinh nghiệm"},{"word":"communication","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəmˌjunəˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"trao đổi thông tin hoặc ý tưởng; chuyển khoản; đi qua"},{"word":"system","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪstəm/","meaning":"sự kết hợp của những thứ hoặc bộ phận liên quan tạo thành một"},{"word":"consultant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kənˈsʌl.tənt/","meaning":"tư vấn viên, cố vấn"}]},{"questionNum":"170","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: All staff\nFrom: Jan Merchant\nDate: October 15\nSubject: Reginald Carmen\nDear Colleagues,\nIt is my pleasure to welcome Reginald Carmen to Edmonton Engineering Consultants,\nLLC.\nWith his expertise in engineering and education, Dr. Carmen will be a valuable addition to\nour distinguished staff. [2]. Upon graduating from university, he spent six years\ndesigning telecommunications systems for Astro Part, Inc. He comes to us directly from the\nGlasse School of Engineering, where he spent the past nineteen years. While there, he\nserved as a full-time professor for ten years, teaching advanced mathematics and various\nspecial courses in engineering. He was then appointed president of the school and served\nin that position for the remaining nine years of his tenure, [3]. During that time, he\nled the team that redesigned the school’s electrical engineering curriculum. [4] -------.\nDr. Carmen’s first day will be next Tuesday.\nJan Merchant,