s Cards Custom Made by You\nLoretti Printing Co. is proud to announce loretticardprint.com, our new online platform for\ncreating customized business cards. While our customers can still place orders in person, as\nthey’ve done for nearly a decade, we now have a system that makes ordering business cards\nespecially quick and easy. Choose from hundreds of easy-to-use templates, include your own\ntext and images, and create professional-quality business cards within minutes.\nWe offer four different paper options:\nType Description Minimum Order\nMatte-Mi Standard card stock, reduces glare 50 cards\nGlossy-G4 Shiny, enhances colors and details 100 cards\nTextured-T3 Unique grid-like pattern, interesting to the touch 100 cards\nMetallic-M2 Extra shiny, unique, captures one’s attention 200 cards\nContact us before placing an online order if you’d like us to send you a sample\nof each type of paper."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail* n\nTo: hello@loretticardprint.com From: felix @thibaultautoworks.com\nDate: Tuesday, May 22\nSubject: Order 28 191 ------- Follow-up\nAttachment: l!Logo auto works\nThanks for pausing my order right away and explaining how to make the necessary\nchanges. I’m so glad I was able to get in touch before my business cards went off to\nprint. It would have been such a shame to have printed 50 cards I can’t use.\nAs I mentioned over the phone, I had accidentally uploaded an older version of my logo\nto the Web site. I''ve since replaced it with the current one in the same file size, and I’m\nhoping you can confirm that this change reflects the image I’ve included here. If so,\nplease go ahead and submit my order now.\nThank you.\nFelix Thibault\n128"}],"question":"In the e-mail, the word “reflects” in paragraph 2, line 3, is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"Trong e-mail, từ “phản ánh” ở đoạn 2, dòng 3, gần nghĩa nhất với","options":["returns","matches","considers","shines"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"matches\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"reflect","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈflɛkt/","meaning":"phản ánh; để gửi lại năng lượng từ một bề mặt; gây ra"},{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"returns","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈtərnz/","meaning":"trả về"}]},{"questionNum":"181","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted.\n\n*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130"}],"question":"According to the Web page, what is true regarding the series of screen writing classes?","bilingual":"Theo trang Web, điều gì đúng về chuỗi lớp học viết kịch bản?","options":["Morning classes are available.","The deadline to apply is January 10.","Class sizes are limited to ten students.","Classes are held every weekday night."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Class sizes are limited to ten students.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"page","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/peɪʤ/","meaning":"mảnh giấy; tiếp viên; người hầu"},{"word":"regarding","pos":"Giới từ (Preposition)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ri´ga:diη/","meaning":"về ( ai/cái gì), về việc, đối với (vấn đề...)"},{"word":"series","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪriz/","meaning":"sự liên tiếp; kế thừa; chương trình truyền hình phát sóng ở"},{"word":"screen","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/skrin/","meaning":"một phần của màn hình tivi hoặc máy tính nơi"}]},{"questionNum":"182","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted.\n\n*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130"}],"question":"What must be included with the application?","bilingual":"Những gì phải có trong đơn đăng ký?","options":["A deposit on the tuition fee","A brief personal history","A proof of residency form","Two published screen plays"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"A brief personal history\".","vocabList":[{"word":"application","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌæp.ləˈkeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"ứng dụng, sự áp dụng"},{"word":"deposit","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈpɑː.zɪt/","meaning":"tiền cọc; đặt cọc"},{"word":"brief","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/brif/","meaning":"trừu tượng; bản tóm tắt; báo cáo ngắn gọn; hướng dẫn"},{"word":"personal","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pə:snl/","meaning":"cá nhân, tư, riêng"}]},{"questionNum":"183","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted.\n\n*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130"}],"question":"What is the purpose of Mr. Hartzog’s e-mail?","bilingual":"","options":["To explain his numerous awards","To outline the first class assignment","To encourage a fellow writer to apply","To respond to a student’s application"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To respond to a student’s application\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"explain","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ɪkˈspleɪn/","meaning":"minh họa; làm sáng tỏ; để giải thích; để mô tả ; ĐẾN"},{"word":"award","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈwɔrd/","meaning":"phần thưởng; khoản trợ cấp; trọng tài"}]},{"questionNum":"184","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted.\n\n*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130"}],"question":"What is indicated about Mr. Hartzog?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về ông Hartzog?","options":["He heads the application committee.","He has taught at GCSW for 25 years.","Eight of his screen plays have won awards.","Three of his screen plays take place in Green City."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"He has taught at GCSW for 25 years.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"head","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/hɛd/","meaning":"trưởng; dẫn đầu; chủ yếu; hiệu trưởng"},{"word":"application","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌæp.ləˈkeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"ứng dụng, sự áp dụng"},{"word":"committee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kəˈmɪt̬.i/","meaning":"ủy ban"},{"word":"screen","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/skrin/","meaning":"một phần của màn hình tivi hoặc máy tính nơi"}]},{"questionNum":"185","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted.\n\n*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"[] (] http://www.greencityscreenwriters.org/workshopseries Green City Screen writers’ Workshop A\nGreen City Screen writers’ Workshop (GCSW) provides aspiring and practicing screen writers a\nplace for interaction and exchange of ideas. For the last 25 years, GCSW has helped writers\nfrom all over the country develop creative projects.\nAre you working on a movie script? Or do you have an idea for the next blockbuster film?\nConsider applying for the next series of classes at GCSW. We offer writing groups, staged\nreadings, and seminars with guest speakers.\n•The six class sessions begin on January 10 and are held every other Thursday.\n•Each class meets from 7 PM. to 9 PM. at Green City Foundation for the Arts.\n•Tuition is $500 in total and due by January 1.\n•A limited amount of financial aid is available to those who qualify.\n•Classes are capped at ten students.\nTO APPLY:\nPlease send a 20-page writing sample (this can be from any genre of writing) and a 200-word\nautobiographical statement to apply@greencityscreenwriters.org. An instructor will respond to\nyour inquiry if you are accepted."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Joshua Hartzog <jzog.2@greencityscreenwriters.org> To: Terry Hampton <hamptonlOO@webcentral.com> Date: December 10\nSubject: Upcoming screen writing class series\nAttachment: [0 NSI form\nDear Mr. Hampton:\nMy name is Joshua Hartzog, and 1 am one of the instructors at Green City\nScreen writers’ Workshop. I am pleased to inform you of your acceptance to our next\nseries of classes. Our committee was impressed with your writing sample.\nHere is a little about me: I have been a teacher at GCSW since it started. Additionally, I\nhave written eight film scripts, including An Incredible Summer and Toast of the Town,\nboth of which won National Writers’ Groups awards.\nPlease fill out the attached New Student Information form and return it to me either via\ne-mail or in person at the Green City Foundation for the Arts by January 1. I look\nforward to seeing you for our first class on January 10. Please pay attention to your\nin box for your first assignment, which will be due by our first class meeting.\nThank you,\nJoshua Hartzog\n130"}],"question":"What is Mr. Hampton asked to do?","bilingual":"Ông Hampton được yêu cầu làm gì?","options":["Complete an attached form","Send contact information","Apply for financial aid","Send a sample script"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Complete an attached form\".","vocabList":[{"word":"complete","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kəmˈpliːt/","meaning":"đầy đủ, hoàn thiện"},{"word":"form","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/fɔːrm/","meaning":"dáng hình; tạo hình"},{"word":"contact","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑnˌtækt/","meaning":"thiết lập giao tiếp; để tạo kết nối; ĐẾN"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"}]},{"questionNum":"186","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mail, review, and event schedule.","passageText":"*E-mail* i\nTo: Jane McNally <jmcnally @aap.org.ie>\nFrom: Yoko Nara <ynara @insleyhotel.com.ie>\nDate: 3 February\nSubject: Vouchers\nHi, Ms. McNally.\nThe water heater servicing the kitchen at the hotel is broken. We cannot serve meals\nbecause there is no hot water for washing pots and dishes. Technicians are diligently\nworking on this issue.\nI am offering vouchers to all guests that can be used for breakfast or lunch at Sarah’s\nCafe next door. If there is no resolution by tomorrow, the evening’s dinner will be\nmoved to Maury’s Restaurant. I have already discussed this with owner Maury\nRoebling, and he is preparing to welcome your professional group. Please accept my\napologies for any inconvenience.\nThank you,\nYoko Nara\n“The place was charming T\nA\nI enjoyed a soup and sandwich special at Sarah’s Cafe this afternoon because\nI received a voucher from my hotel. I arrived just at noon and had to wait almost\n25 minutes for a table. I would recommend visiting at a less busy time because\nthe cafe is relatively small. Other than that, even if my meal had not been free,\nI would still recommend the cafe. The atmosphere is warm and inviting and their\nhome made soup is delicious.\n-Stefan Nichols, 3 February\ni\n132\nv\n\n<1 > https://www.app.org.ie/annualmeeting/schedule Association of Accounting Professionals\nAnnual meeting-Scheduled events\nFriday, 4 February\nGuest speaker Mr. Ian Bagley, chief financial officer at Colford\n5:30 P.M., Room 213, Insley Hotel International, will discuss “Old Concerns and\nCurrent Trends in the Accounting Profession.”\nNetworking dinner Enjoy a gourmet dinner and relax with your\n7:00 P.M. Maury’s Restaurant colleagues at this popular eatery.\nSaturday, 5 February\nJob Fair Looking for a new opportunity? The job fair is for\n11:00 A.M. to 5:00 P.M. you. Meet with representatives from companies\naround the region. Bring copies of your resume.\nTour of Dublin Visit some interesting sites in our host city. Wear\n1:00 P.M. to 4:00 P.M. comfortable shoes, as tour participants will cover\napproximately two miles.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"*E-mail* i\nTo: Jane McNally <jmcnally @aap.org.ie>\nFrom: Yoko Nara <ynara @insleyhotel.com.ie>\nDate: 3 February\nSubject: Vouchers\nHi, Ms. McNally.\nThe water heater servicing the kitchen at the hotel is broken. We cannot serve meals\nbecause there is no hot water for washing pots and dishes. Technicians are diligently\nworking on this issue.\nI am offering vouchers to all guests that can be used for breakfast or lunch at Sarah’s\nCafe next door. If there is no resolution by tomorrow, the evening’s dinner will be\nmoved to Maury’s Restaurant. I have already discussed this with owner Maury\nRoebling, and he is preparing to welcome your professional group. Please accept my\napologies for any inconvenience.\nThank you,\nYoko Nara\n“The place was charming T\nA\nI enjoyed a soup and sandwich special at Sarah’s Cafe this afternoon because\nI received a voucher from my hotel. I arrived just at noon and had to wait almost\n25 minutes for a table. I would recommend visiting at a less busy time because\nthe cafe is relatively small. Other than that, even if my meal had not been free,\nI would still recommend the cafe. The atmosphere is warm and inviting and their\nhome made soup is delicious.\n-Stefan Nichols, 3 February\ni\n132\nv\n\n<1 > https://www.app.org.ie/annualmeeting/schedule Association of Accounting Professionals\nAnnual meeting-Scheduled events\nFriday, 4 February\nGuest speaker Mr. Ian Bagley, chief financial officer at Colford\n5:30 P.M., Room 213, Insley Hotel International, will discuss “Old Concerns and\nCurrent Trends in the Accounting Profession.”\nNetworking dinner Enjoy a gourmet dinner and relax with your\n7:00 P.M. Maury’s Restaurant colleagues at this popular eatery.\nSaturday, 5 February\nJob Fair Looking for a new opportunity? The job fair is for\n11:00 A.M. to 5:00 P.M. you. Meet with representatives from companies\naround the region. Bring copies of your resume.\nTour of Dublin Visit some interesting sites in our host city. Wear\n1:00 P.M. to 4:00 P.M. comfortable shoes, as tour participants will cover\napproximately two miles."}],"question":"Who most likely is Ms. McNally?","bilingual":"Cô McNally có nhiều khả năng là ai nhất?","options":["A receptionist","A banquet chef","An event organizer","A cafe owner"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"An event organizer\".","vocabList":[{"word":"receptionist","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈsɛpʃənɪst/","meaning":"người chào đón du khách hoặc khách hàng qua điện thoại"},{"word":"banquet","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈbæŋkwət/","meaning":"lễ ăn mừng; bữa tiệc; bữa tối; uống rượu"},{"word":"chef","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ʃef/","meaning":"đầu bếp"},{"word":"event","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪˈvent/","meaning":"sự kiện, sự việc"}]},{"questionNum":"187","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mail, review, and event schedule.","passageText":"*E-mail* i\nTo: Jane McNally <jmcnally @aap.org.ie>\nFrom: Yoko Nara <ynara @insleyhotel.com.ie>\nDate: 3 February\nSubject: Vouchers\nHi, Ms. McNall