we have been very successful in expanding our international reach. ------- [2] -------. In Brazil, sales increased 57%, which can be attributed to the Rio de Janeiro\nFashion Show where our evening wear was featured. A similar trend emerged in Russia,\nwhere sales were up by 32%. ------- [3] -------. There we anticipate sustained growth for the rest\nof the year, especially in our winter apparel line. We also saw sales growth in the United\nArab Emirates (UAE), but growth was a modest 10% due to fierce competition. That said,\nin this market, sign-ups for our credit card were strong. Finally, in Korea, where we have\nhad our most successful international market launch thus far, favorable news articles about\nour products drove very strong sales.\n[4]. Thus, overall, it ''s been an excellent year so far. I am confident that our new\nprogram, which offers discounts to customers who invite others to shop with us, will begin\nto boost sales growth at all locations.\nSincerely,\nTakeshi Ishiguro\nVice President of Sales"}],"question":"According to Mr. Ishiguro, what will likely bring increased business in the future?","bilingual":"Theo ông Ishiguro, điều gì có thể sẽ mang lại hoạt động kinh doanh tăng trưởng trong tương lai?","options":["Television commercials","An expanded credit card program","Company-sponsored contests","Referrals from customers"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Referrals from customers\".","vocabList":[{"word":"business","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈbɪznɪs/","meaning":"công ty; doanh nghiệp; buôn bán; thương mại; vấn đề"},{"word":"future","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/fˈjuʧər/","meaning":"tương lai"},{"word":"television","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈtɛləˌvɪʒən/","meaning":"Truyền hình"},{"word":"commercial","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kəˈmərʃəl/","meaning":"liên quan đến kinh doanh; liên quan đến việc mua và"}]},{"questionNum":"171","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"From: Takeshi Ishiguro\nTo: All Sevastya employees\nSubject: Update\nDate: December 13\nDear Sevastya employees,\nI am writing to give you an update on this year’s sales so far. ------- [l] -------. I am happy to\nreport that currently our sales volume is up 20% from last year. This is due in part to the\nfact that we have been very successful in expanding our international reach. ------- [2] -------. In Brazil, sales increased 57%, which can be attributed to the Rio de Janeiro\nFashion Show where our evening wear was featured. A similar trend emerged in Russia,\nwhere sales were up by 32%. ------- [3] -------. There we anticipate sustained growth for the rest\nof the year, especially in our winter apparel line. We also saw sales growth in the United\nArab Emirates (UAE), but growth was a modest 10% due to fierce competition. That said,\nin this market, sign-ups for our credit card were strong. Finally, in Korea, where we have\nhad our most successful international market launch thus far, favorable news articles about\nour products drove very strong sales.\n[4]. Thus, overall, it ''s been an excellent year so far. I am confident that our new\nprogram, which offers discounts to customers who invite others to shop with us, will begin\nto boost sales growth at all locations.\nSincerely,\nTakeshi Ishiguro\nVice President of Sales","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"From: Takeshi Ishiguro\nTo: All Sevastya employees\nSubject: Update\nDate: December 13\nDear Sevastya employees,\nI am writing to give you an update on this year’s sales so far. ------- [l] -------. I am happy to\nreport that currently our sales volume is up 20% from last year. This is due in part to the\nfact that we have been very successful in expanding our international reach. ------- [2] -------. In Brazil, sales increased 57%, which can be attributed to the Rio de Janeiro\nFashion Show where our evening wear was featured. A similar trend emerged in Russia,\nwhere sales were up by 32%. ------- [3] -------. There we anticipate sustained growth for the rest\nof the year, especially in our winter apparel line. We also saw sales growth in the United\nArab Emirates (UAE), but growth was a modest 10% due to fierce competition. That said,\nin this market, sign-ups for our credit card were strong. Finally, in Korea, where we have\nhad our most successful international market launch thus far, favorable news articles about\nour products drove very strong sales.\n[4]. Thus, overall, it ''s been an excellent year so far. I am confident that our new\nprogram, which offers discounts to customers who invite others to shop with us, will begin\nto boost sales growth at all locations.\nSincerely,\nTakeshi Ishiguro\nVice President of Sales"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3] and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “Here are some figures from around the world.”","bilingual":"Vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4] thuộc câu nào sau đây đúng nhất? “Đây là một số số liệu từ khắp nơi trên thế giới.”","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"[2]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"figure","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfɪɡ.jɚ/","meaning":"hình dáng, nhân vật; đánh giá, tính toán"},{"word":"world","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/wərld/","meaning":"thế giới"},{"word":"employee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɔɪi/","meaning":"công nhân; người làm việc cho một công ty hoặc một"}]},{"questionNum":"172","passageTitle":"Questions 172-175 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156"}],"question":"In what department do the writers most likely work?","bilingual":"","options":["Sales","Marketing","Billing","Research"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Marketing\".","vocabList":[{"word":"department","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈpɑːrt.mənt/","meaning":"khoa, bộ"},{"word":"work","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/wərk/","meaning":"nhân công; nhiệm vụ; nghề nghiệp; nghề nghiệp; ơn gọi; cố gắng"},{"word":"sales","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/seɪlz/","meaning":"tiếp thị; các hoạt động liên quan đến việc bán một sản phẩm"},{"word":"marketing","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mɑ:kitiɳ/","meaning":"tiếp thị"}]},{"questionNum":"173","passageTitle":"Questions 172-175 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156"}],"question":"To what project are the three writers assigned?","bilingual":"","options":["The O’Neil project","The McMillan project","The Greller project","The Allford project"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"The O’Neil project\".","vocabList":[{"word":"project","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈprɒdʒɛkt/","meaning":"đề án, dự án; kế hoạch"},{"word":"need","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/nid/","meaning":"yêu cầu; thiếu một mặt hàng không thể thiếu;"},{"word":"schedule","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''skedʒu:l/","meaning":"kế hoạch làm việc, tiến độ thi công"},{"word":"meeting","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mi:tiɳ/","meaning":"(chính trị) cuộc mít tinh, cuộc biểu tình"}]},{"questionNum":"174","passageTitle":"Questions 172-175 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156"}],"question":"At 1:18 P.M., what does Mr. Miller most likely mean when he writes, “Okay, I see”?","bilingual":"","options":["He understands that he was not moved to another team.","He recognizes that he did not come to a meeting on time.","He accepts that he is not going to meet with a client.","He acknowledges that he did not complete a task."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"He understands that he was not moved to another team.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"understand","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈstænd/","meaning":"hiểu, nắm bắt được"},{"word":"recognize","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''rekəgnaiz/","meaning":"công nhận, thừa nhận, chấp nhận"}]},{"questionNum":"175","passageTitle":"Questions 172-175 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Lynda McCann (1:08 P.M.) Hello, Bernadette and Harrison. We urgently need to schedule a\nteam meeting, so we can get working on our project.\nBernadette Ecco (1:10 P.M.) Sure. Are you wanting an all-marketing-staff meeting? Let me\nknow if I can assist.\nLynda McCann (1:12 P.M.) No, I was thinking of the O''Neil project, so only the three of us\nwho are on that team need to meet.\nBernadette Ecco (1:14 P.M.) Okay. I’m free either this Wednesday or Friday during the early\nafternoon.\nHarrison Miller (1:15 P.M.) I thought I had been reassigned to the McMillan project instead.\nBernadette Ecco (1:17 P.M.) No, the final slot on that team was filled by Jacob Aikens, since\nhe’s worked on similar projects in the past, like the Greller project and the Allford project.\nHarrison Miller (1:18 P.M.) Okay, I see.\nLynda McCann (1:19 P.M.) I''m available on Wednesday and Friday as well, but only before\n3 P.M.; I’ll be meeting with the sales team on Wednesday at 3 P.M. and the research team on\nFriday at 3:30 P.M.\nHarrison Miller (1:21 P.M.) Wednesday won’t work for me, but I could do Friday at 1 P.M.\nLynda McCann (1:23 P.M.) Sounds good! Bernadette?\nBernadette Ecco (1:23 P.M.) Perfect! I’ll reserve the small conference room for us.\n156"}],"question":"Why was the meeting scheduled for Friday rather than Wednesday?","bilingual":"Tại sao cuộc họp được lên lịch vào thứ Sáu thay vì thứ Tư?","options":["Ms. McCann has a commitment with another team on that day.","Ms. Ecco’s schedule is very busy this month.","Mr. Miller is unavailable on Wednesday.","A sales team will be using the conference room on Wednesday."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Mr. Miller is unavailable on Wednesday.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"meeting","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mi:tiɳ/","meaning":"(chính trị) cuộc mít tinh, cuộc biểu tình"},{"word":"scheduled","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈskɛʤʊld/","meaning":"đã lên lịch"},{"word":"friday","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfraɪˌdeɪ/","meaning":"Thứ sáu"},{"word":"rather","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrəðər/","meaning":"rất khá; ở một mức độ nào đó; phần nào; nhẹ nhàng; một chút;"}]},{"questionNum":"176","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following e-mail and Web page.","passageText":"To: Brody Dimmick <bdiminick @greerscoftee.com.au>\nFrom: Fawzia Gunnani <fgurmani@greerscoflfee.com.au> Subject: Following up on your recent call\nDate: l 7 September\nAttachment: [§ Proposal\nDear Mr. Dimmick,\nThank you for your recent call. We are always pleased to hear from one of our many local\nstore managers. I think your idea to reinstate the Greer’s Coffee Club is excellent, and I\nam also pleased to know your customers have been asking about the club punch cards. I\nagree that this is a good time to bring back the program, as we are working on rebranding\nthe company. I have drawn up your proposal and will forward it to Ms. So-Ra Oh, vice\npresident of marketing, tomorrow. Before I do that, can you please look it over and let me\nknow if I have missed any details? Please send me your feedback by the end of the day.\nThank you,\nFawzia Gurmani\nRegional Director http://www.greerscoffee.com.au/rewards Qree P$, the place for coffee, conversation, and snacks, is now even better!\nWe have brought back the Greers Coffee Club, but with an update: it is now even\neasier to use! Simply download our new mobile app and register. Use the app to scan\nyour receipt every time you visit any Greer’s Coffee location, and you will earn points.\nEach time you accrue 100 points, you can redeem the points for discounts on coffee,\nfood, and other items.\nv\n158","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: Brody Dimmick <bdiminick @greerscoftee.com.au>\nFrom: Fawzia Gunnani <fgurmani@greerscoflfee.com.au> Subject: Following up on your recent call\nDate: l 7 September\nAttachment: [§ Proposal\nDear Mr. Dimmick,\nThank you for your recent call. We are always pleased to hear from one of our many local\nstore managers. I think your idea to reinstate the Greer’s Coffee Club is excellent, and I\nam also pleased to know your customers have been asking about the club punch cards. I\nagree that this is a good time to bring back the program, as we are working on rebranding\nthe company. I have drawn up your proposal and will forward it to Ms. So-Ra Oh, vice\npresident of marketing, tomorrow. Before I do that, can you please look it over and let me\nknow if I have missed any details? Please send me your feedback by the end of the day.\nThank you,\nFawzia Gurmani\nRegional Director http://www.greerscoffee.com.au/rewards Qree P$, the place for coffee, conversation, and snacks, is now even better!\nWe have brought back the Greers Coffee Club, but with an update: it is now even\neasier to use! Simply download our new mobile app and register. Use the app to scan\nyour receipt every time you visit any Greer’s Coffee location, and you will earn points.\nEach time you accrue 100 points, you can redeem the points for discounts on coffee,\nfood, and other items.\nv\n158"}],"question":"Why did Ms. Gurmani send the e-mail?","bilingual":"Tại sao cô Gurmani lại gửi e-mail?","options":["To welcome a new employee","To describe how to join a club","To invite Mr. Dimmick to a meeting","To confirm the details of a proposal"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To confirm the details of a proposal\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"welcome","pos":"Danh từ