, fruit and nut trees, and other edibles\nV\nAttention Pink Begonia Farms Customers!\nWe are changing to new ownership on April 1. Several other changes\nwill follow, most notably renovation work that will cause the area\nwhere we service our bulk-order customers to be closed from April 1\nthrough May 5.\nAlso, we would kindly request that if you use our baskets or wagons\nto move your purchased items to your car, please do not leave them in\nthe middle of the parking area. Thanks!\n164\n\nhttp://www.retaileropinion.com/reviews/pinkbegoniafarms A\nI had a wonderful experience shopping at Pink Begonia Farms. Recently I was\npreparing a client’s property for sale, and I needed extensive landscaping work to\nbe done. The front entryway needed extra color and greenery before I could show\nthe house to potential buyers. Knowing nothing about plants, I asked the store staff\nto help me pick out an assortment of local favorites that would require very little\nmanual watering or care. When finished, the house looked so much more inviting.\nThanks Pink Begonia Farms for your excellent service! ------- Daphne Weigand\nApril 15"}],"question":"What area of Pink Begonia Farms will reopen in May?","bilingual":"Khu vực nào của Pink Begonia Farms sẽ mở cửa trở lại vào tháng 5?","options":["North Gate","South Gate","East Gate","West Gate"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"South Gate\".","vocabList":[{"word":"area","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈer.i.ə/","meaning":"khu vực, lĩnh vực, diện tích"},{"word":"gate","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/geɪt/","meaning":"phần tường hoặc hàng rào có thể đóng mở; bất kì"},{"word":"your","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/jʊr/","meaning":"của bạn"},{"word":"stop","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/stɑp/","meaning":"sự chấm dứt; kết thúc; thăm nom; trở ngại; sự cản trở"}]},{"questionNum":"194","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page, notice, and review.","passageText":"http://www.pinkbegoniafarms.com Pink Begonia Farms\nPink Begonia Farms is your one-stop shop for all your plant-related needs. Whether you\nare a landscape professional, a backyard gardener, or a houseplant enthusiast, we have\njust about everything you need! Some seeds, fertilizer, and equipment can be ordered\nonline, but please come visit our nursery in person for a much larger selection.\nOur sizable facility is divided into four distinct sections as follows:\n0 North Gate ------- indoor house plants, tropical plants, exotics\n° South Gate ------- plants and landscaping products sold in bulk quantities at wholesale prices\n•East Gate ------- local landscape plants that grow well in our area and require little maintenance\n* West Gate ------- herbs, vegetable plants, fruit and nut trees, and other edibles\nV\nAttention Pink Begonia Farms Customers!\nWe are changing to new ownership on April 1. Several other changes\nwill follow, most notably renovation work that will cause the area\nwhere we service our bulk-order customers to be closed from April 1\nthrough May 5.\nAlso, we would kindly request that if you use our baskets or wagons\nto move your purchased items to your car, please do not leave them in\nthe middle of the parking area. Thanks!\n164\n\nhttp://www.retaileropinion.com/reviews/pinkbegoniafarms A\nI had a wonderful experience shopping at Pink Begonia Farms. Recently I was\npreparing a client’s property for sale, and I needed extensive landscaping work to\nbe done. The front entryway needed extra color and greenery before I could show\nthe house to potential buyers. Knowing nothing about plants, I asked the store staff\nto help me pick out an assortment of local favorites that would require very little\nmanual watering or care. When finished, the house looked so much more inviting.\nThanks Pink Begonia Farms for your excellent service! ------- Daphne Weigand\nApril 15","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"http://www.pinkbegoniafarms.com Pink Begonia Farms\nPink Begonia Farms is your one-stop shop for all your plant-related needs. Whether you\nare a landscape professional, a backyard gardener, or a houseplant enthusiast, we have\njust about everything you need! Some seeds, fertilizer, and equipment can be ordered\nonline, but please come visit our nursery in person for a much larger selection.\nOur sizable facility is divided into four distinct sections as follows:\n0 North Gate ------- indoor house plants, tropical plants, exotics\n° South Gate ------- plants and landscaping products sold in bulk quantities at wholesale prices\n•East Gate ------- local landscape plants that grow well in our area and require little maintenance\n* West Gate ------- herbs, vegetable plants, fruit and nut trees, and other edibles\nV\nAttention Pink Begonia Farms Customers!\nWe are changing to new ownership on April 1. Several other changes\nwill follow, most notably renovation work that will cause the area\nwhere we service our bulk-order customers to be closed from April 1\nthrough May 5.\nAlso, we would kindly request that if you use our baskets or wagons\nto move your purchased items to your car, please do not leave them in\nthe middle of the parking area. Thanks!\n164\n\nhttp://www.retaileropinion.com/reviews/pinkbegoniafarms A\nI had a wonderful experience shopping at Pink Begonia Farms. Recently I was\npreparing a client’s property for sale, and I needed extensive landscaping work to\nbe done. The front entryway needed extra color and greenery before I could show\nthe house to potential buyers. Knowing nothing about plants, I asked the store staff\nto help me pick out an assortment of local favorites that would require very little\nmanual watering or care. When finished, the house looked so much more inviting.\nThanks Pink Begonia Farms for your excellent service! ------- Daphne Weigand\nApril 15"}],"question":"What most likely is Ms. Weigand’s job?","bilingual":"Rất có thể công việc của cô Weigand là gì?","options":["Landscaper","Event planner","Real estate agent","Nursery worker"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Real estate agent\".","vocabList":[{"word":"landscaper","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlændˌskeɪpər/","meaning":"người thiết kế khu vườn hoặc khu vực rộng lớn"},{"word":"event","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪˈvent/","meaning":"sự kiện, sự việc"},{"word":"estate","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɛˈsteɪt/","meaning":"mảnh đất rộng thường có một ngôi nhà lớn trên đó;"},{"word":"agent","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈeɪʤənt/","meaning":"tiêu biểu; trả lời; nhân tố; gây ra"}]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page, notice, and review.","passageText":"http://www.pinkbegoniafarms.com Pink Begonia Farms\nPink Begonia Farms is your one-stop shop for all your plant-related needs. Whether you\nare a landscape professional, a backyard gardener, or a houseplant enthusiast, we have\njust about everything you need! Some seeds, fertilizer, and equipment can be ordered\nonline, but please come visit our nursery in person for a much larger selection.\nOur sizable facility is divided into four distinct sections as follows:\n0 North Gate ------- indoor house plants, tropical plants, exotics\n° South Gate ------- plants and landscaping products sold in bulk quantities at wholesale prices\n•East Gate ------- local landscape plants that grow well in our area and require little maintenance\n* West Gate ------- herbs, vegetable plants, fruit and nut trees, and other edibles\nV\nAttention Pink Begonia Farms Customers!\nWe are changing to new ownership on April 1. Several other changes\nwill follow, most notably renovation work that will cause the area\nwhere we service our bulk-order customers to be closed from April 1\nthrough May 5.\nAlso, we would kindly request that if you use our baskets or wagons\nto move your purchased items to your car, please do not leave them in\nthe middle of the parking area. Thanks!\n164\n\nhttp://www.retaileropinion.com/reviews/pinkbegoniafarms A\nI had a wonderful experience shopping at Pink Begonia Farms. Recently I was\npreparing a client’s property for sale, and I needed extensive landscaping work to\nbe done. The front entryway needed extra color and greenery before I could show\nthe house to potential buyers. Knowing nothing about plants, I asked the store staff\nto help me pick out an assortment of local favorites that would require very little\nmanual watering or care. When finished, the house looked so much more inviting.\nThanks Pink Begonia Farms for your excellent service! ------- Daphne Weigand\nApril 15","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"http://www.pinkbegoniafarms.com Pink Begonia Farms\nPink Begonia Farms is your one-stop shop for all your plant-related needs. Whether you\nare a landscape professional, a backyard gardener, or a houseplant enthusiast, we have\njust about everything you need! Some seeds, fertilizer, and equipment can be ordered\nonline, but please come visit our nursery in person for a much larger selection.\nOur sizable facility is divided into four distinct sections as follows:\n0 North Gate ------- indoor house plants, tropical plants, exotics\n° South Gate ------- plants and landscaping products sold in bulk quantities at wholesale prices\n•East Gate ------- local landscape plants that grow well in our area and require little maintenance\n* West Gate ------- herbs, vegetable plants, fruit and nut trees, and other edibles\nV\nAttention Pink Begonia Farms Customers!\nWe are changing to new ownership on April 1. Several other changes\nwill follow, most notably renovation work that will cause the area\nwhere we service our bulk-order customers to be closed from April 1\nthrough May 5.\nAlso, we would kindly request that if you use our baskets or wagons\nto move your purchased items to your car, please do not leave them in\nthe middle of the parking area. Thanks!\n164\n\nhttp://www.retaileropinion.com/reviews/pinkbegoniafarms A\nI had a wonderful experience shopping at Pink Begonia Farms. Recently I was\npreparing a client’s property for sale, and I needed extensive landscaping work to\nbe done. The front entryway needed extra color and greenery before I could show\nthe house to potential buyers. Knowing nothing about plants, I asked the store staff\nto help me pick out an assortment of local favorites that would require very little\nmanual watering or care. When finished, the house looked so much more inviting.\nThanks Pink Begonia Farms for your excellent service! ------- Daphne Weigand\nApril 15"}],"question":"What is implied about Ms. Weigand?","bilingual":"Điều gì ngụ ý về cô Weigand?","options":["She has flowers delivered on a regular basis.","She learned of the store through one of her clients.","She plans to buy a house in the near future.","She shopped in the East Gate section of the nursery."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"She shopped in the East Gate section of the nursery.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"regular","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈreɡ.jə.lɚ/","meaning":"đều đặn, thường xuyên"},{"word":"basis","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈbeɪsɪs/","meaning":"sự thành lập; nối đất"},{"word":"store","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/stɔr/","meaning":"cửa hàng; nơi bán hàng hóa; cung cấp"},{"word":"through","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/θru/","meaning":"đến hết"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and receipt.","passageText":"To: Thanda Peterson <thandapeterson@thandapeterson.com> From: Milos Adamek <milosa@wistartravel.org> Subject: Travel arrangements\nDate: April 17\nHello Thanda,\nl hope you are well. I looked into available flights from Concord to Sumneyfeld\nfor your writers’ conference and discovered that discount carrier Alterr Airlines\noffers daily direct service on that route. The tentative itinerary would be:\nConcord depart: Friday, May 8, 8:50 A.M.\nSumneyfeld arrive: Friday, May 8, 11:05 A.M.\nSumneyfeld depart: Monday, May 11, 1:20 P.M\nConcord arrive: Monday, May 11, 3:35 P.M.\nI will book this as soon as you confirm. Keep in mind on your return trip that\nthe Sumneyfeld Airport is advising passengers to arrive a full two hours before\ndeparture because of extensive renovations being done there.\nBy the way, you might be interested in an excellent Peruvian lunch place near\nthe Sumneyfeld Airport. Just let me know and 1 will give you the name.\nBest,\nMilos\n\n*E-mail*\nTo: Milos Adamek <milosa @wistartravel.org>\nFrom: Thanda Peterson <thandapeterson @ thandapeterson.com>\nSubject: Re: Travel arrangements\nDate: April 18\nMilos,\nQuick update before you book. I will need a few days to consider whether I should\ndepart for Sumneyfeld on May 8 or leave one day earlier. There is an early conference\nworkshop the evening of May 7 that I might attend. Actually, a publisher representative\nwith whom I would like to talk regarding my latest manuscript may be in attendance! I\nwill let you know shortly.\nThanks so much for your help, as always.\nThanda\n166\n\nSumneyfeld Quick Taxi\n555-0194\nDate: May 7\nFrom: Sumneyfeld Airport\nIWM\nTo: Peru Dreaming Cafe, 98 Treetop Avenue\nPickup: 11:55 A.M.\nDrop off: 12:04 P.M.\nDistance: 1.2 miles\nTotal: $8.00\nPayment type: X credit card\ncash\nName on Credit Card: Thanda Peterson\nCredit Card Number: xxxx xxxx xxxx 5523","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: Thanda Peterson <thandapete