ng":"đi du lịch đến những vùng chưa biết; để điều tra; ĐẾN"},{"word":"your","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/jʊr/","meaning":"của bạn"},{"word":"option","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔpʃən/","meaning":"sự lựa chọn; thay thế; khả năng; lựa chọn; cuộc bầu cử"}]},{"questionNum":"158","passageTitle":"Questions 158-161 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Craverton Returns to Business as Usual ------- Bricuma Wible, Staff Reporter\nA power outage yesterday caused a number of businesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Craverton Returns to Business as Usual ------- Bricuma Wible, Staff Reporter\nA power outage yesterday caused a number of businesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual."}],"question":"What is the main topic of the article?","bilingual":"Chủ đề chính của bài viết là gì?","options":["Reasons to move to Craverton","An unexpected situation in Craverton","Reliable weather forecasting sources","Possible sites for a tourist attraction"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"An unexpected situation in Craverton\".","vocabList":[{"word":"main","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪn/","meaning":"đường ống hoặc ống dẫn chính trong hệ thống; phần chính của"},{"word":"topic","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈtɑpɪk/","meaning":"chủ đề; chủ đề của cuộc trò chuyện; vấn đề"},{"word":"article","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɑrtɪkəl/","meaning":"mục; sự vật; đoạn văn bản; đoạn hợp đồng"},{"word":"reason","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrizən/","meaning":"suy nghĩ ; để xem xét một cách hợp lý; tranh luận ; để yêu cầu"}]},{"questionNum":"159","passageTitle":"Questions 158-161 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Craverton Returns to Business as Usual ------- Bricuma Wible, Staff Reporter\nA power outage yesterday caused a number of businesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Craverton Returns to Business as Usual ------- Bricuma Wible, Staff Reporter\nA power outage yesterday caused a number of businesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual."}],"question":"Who most likely is Mr. Nam?","bilingual":"Rất có thể anh Nam là ai?","options":["A reporter","A professor","An art historian",