usinesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual."}],"question":"What does the article mention about the Craverton Art Museum?","bilingual":"Bài viết đề cập gì về Bảo tàng Nghệ thuật Craverton?","options":["It did not lose money yesterday.","It is located near downtown Craverton.","It is open to visitors on Tuesdays.","It will be starting a series of art classes. 182"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It did not lose money yesterday.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"article","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɑrtɪkəl/","meaning":"mục; sự vật; đoạn văn bản; đoạn hợp đồng"},{"word":"mention","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''menʃn/","meaning":"sự kể ra, sự nói đến, sự đề cập"},{"word":"museum","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/mˈjuziəm/","meaning":"viện bảo tàng"},{"word":"lose","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/luz/","meaning":"đặt nhầm chỗ; bị tước đoạt; bị đánh bại; thất bại;"}]},{"questionNum":"161","passageTitle":"Questions 158-161 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Craverton Returns to Business as Usual ------- Bricuma Wible, Staff Reporter\nA power outage yesterday caused a number of businesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Craverton Returns to Business as Usual ------- Bricuma Wible, Staff Reporter\nA power outage yesterday caused a number of businesses and area attractions in downtown\nCraverton to close. The cause of the outage is still unknown, but the early morning’s stormy\nweather most likely played a part. [1]-.\nSung Min Nam, who was leading a tour of some of the historic sites downtown, changed\nhis itinerary. “Fortunately, I know the area well,” Mr. Nam said. “1 led the group back to\nthe bus, and we headed to a different part of the city to discover alternative sites, such as\nGrantwood Park and Holtrop Tower.” ------- [2] -------.\nFor the Craverton Art Museum, the outage did not make a difference in earnings because\nits galleries are closed to the public on Tuesdays. ------- [3] -------. Craverton University canceled\nits classes, but generators powered residence halls and cafeterias. Power was restored to\nmost area businesses by late yesterday afternoon. ------- [4] -------. And today Craverton returned\nto business as usual."}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3] and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “However, staff members did get the day off.”","bilingual":"Câu sau đây thuộc về vị trí nào trong số các vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4]? “Tuy nhiên, các nhân viên đã được nghỉ ngày hôm đó.”","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"[3]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"staff","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/stæf/","meaning":"nhân viên"},{"word":"member","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmɛmbər/","meaning":"người thuộc một tổ chức, nhóm; phần;"},{"word":"returns","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈtərnz/","meaning":"trả về"}]},{"questionNum":"162","passageTitle":"Questions 162-165 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Isabelle Porter (8:15 A.M.): Hi. Our new intern, Mila Erben, arrives\ntomorrow. Do you have any tasks for Mila to start on?\nOmar Shirani (8:16 A.M.): I’m really sorry. I was out of the office last\nweek at the JNTD Convention. Can I get back to you later today?\nRico Alvarez (8:16 A.M.): I don’t have anything for Mila right now.\nIsabelle Porter (8:17 A.M.): I’m confused. Your department manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Isabelle Porter (8:15 A.M.): Hi. Our new intern, Mila Erben, arrives\ntomorrow. Do you have any tasks for Mila to start on?\nOmar Shirani (8:16 A.M.): I’m really sorry. I was out of the office last\nweek at the JNTD Convention. Can I get back to you later today?\nRico Alvarez (8:16 A.M.): I don’t have anything for Mila right now.\nIsabelle Porter (8:17 A.M.): I’m confused. Your department manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week."}],"question":"What is suggested about Ms. Erben?","bilingual":"Điều gì được gợi ý về cô Erben?","options":["She is an accountant.","She is a department manager.","She is a convention planner.","She is a student."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"She is a student.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"accountant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈkaʊntənt/","meaning":"người lưu giữ hồ sơ tài chính; một người"},{"word":"department","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Le