nt manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week."}],"question":"What did Mr. Shirani do last week?","bilingual":"Tuần trước ông Shirani đã làm gì?","options":["Attend a convention","Work at a branch office","Take a vacation","Start a new job"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Attend a convention\".","vocabList":[{"word":"last","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/læst/","meaning":"tiếp tục; đủ; chịu đựng; kiên trì"},{"word":"attend","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtend/","meaning":"tham dự"},{"word":"convention","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈvɛnʃən/","meaning":"hội nghị; lịch trình; phong tục; hiệp ước"},{"word":"work","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/wərk/","meaning":"nhân công; nhiệm vụ; nghề nghiệp; nghề nghiệp; ơn gọi; cố gắng"}]},{"questionNum":"164","passageTitle":"Questions 162-165 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Isabelle Porter (8:15 A.M.): Hi. Our new intern, Mila Erben, arrives\ntomorrow. Do you have any tasks for Mila to start on?\nOmar Shirani (8:16 A.M.): I’m really sorry. I was out of the office last\nweek at the JNTD Convention. Can I get back to you later today?\nRico Alvarez (8:16 A.M.): I don’t have anything for Mila right now.\nIsabelle Porter (8:17 A.M.): I’m confused. Your department manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Isabelle Porter (8:15 A.M.): Hi. Our new intern, Mila Erben, arrives\ntomorrow. Do you have any tasks for Mila to start on?\nOmar Shirani (8:16 A.M.): I’m really sorry. I was out of the office last\nweek at the JNTD Convention. Can I get back to you later today?\nRico Alvarez (8:16 A.M.): I don’t have anything for Mila right now.\nIsabelle Porter (8:17 A.M.): I’m confused. Your department manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week."}],"question":"At 8:20 A.M., what does Ms. Porter most likely mean when she writes, “That will do\"?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 8:20 sáng, rất có thể cô Porter có ý gì khi viết, “Điều đó sẽ làm được\"?","options":["She will complete a project by herself.","She thinks the work will take two weeks to do.","She agrees with the idea Mr. Alvarez proposed.","She will give Mr. Shirani more information later."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She agrees with the idea Mr. Alvarez proposed.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"complete","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kəmˈpliːt/","meaning":"đầy đủ, hoàn thiện"},{"word":"project","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈprɒdʒɛkt/","meaning":"đề án, dự án; kế hoạch"}]},{"questionNum":"165","passageTitle":"Questions 162-165 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Isabelle Porter (8:15 A.M.): Hi. Our new intern, Mila Erben, arrives\ntomorrow. Do you have any tasks for Mila to start on?\nOmar Shirani (8:16 A.M.): I’m really sorry. I was out of the office last\nweek at the JNTD Convention. Can I get back to you later today?\nRico Alvarez (8:16 A.M.): I don’t have anything for Mila right now.\nIsabelle Porter (8:17 A.M.): I’m confused. Your department manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Isabelle Porter (8:15 A.M.): Hi. Our new intern, Mila Erben, arrives\ntomorrow. Do you have any tasks for Mila to start on?\nOmar Shirani (8:16 A.M.): I’m really sorry. I was out of the office last\nweek at the JNTD Convention. Can I get back to you later today?\nRico Alvarez (8:16 A.M.): I don’t have anything for Mila right now.\nIsabelle Porter (8:17 A.M.): I’m confused. Your department manager\nmentioned that your team would greatly benefit from having an\nintern. Can you work together to find something for her to do?\nOmar Shirani (8:17 A.M.): Can you remind us what she’s studying\nat the university?\nIsabelle Porter (8:18 A.M.): Accounting. Her resume says she’d like\nto become an auditor.\nRico Alvarez (8:19 A.M.): Well, I might have a few tasks, although\nthey may be a bit dull.\nIsabelle Porter (8:20 A.M.): That will do. And I might have some\ndocuments for her to copy. That ought to be enough for Mila’s first\nweek. But I’d appreciate it if you could meet with your team by\nThursday and organize additional tasks for Mila for next week."}],"question":"What does Ms. Porter ask the writers to do before Thursday?","bilingual":"Cô Porter yêu cầu người viết bài làm gì trước thứ Năm?","options":["Hire an intern","Copy documents","Send her an e-mail","Plan a set of tasks"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Plan a set of tasks\".","vocabList":[{"word":"thursday","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈθərzˌdeɪ/","meaning":"Thứ năm"},{"word":"hire","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/haɪr/","meaning":"sự thuê; thuê, mướn"},{"word":"intern","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɝːn/","meaning":"thực tập sinh"},{"word":"copy","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑpi/","meaning":"nhân đôi; bắt chước"}]},{"questionNum":"166","passageTitle":"Questions 166-168 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Vera Fernandez\nTo: Carla Rosa\nSent: June 07, 12:47 P.M.\nSubject: Initiatives for distance learning\nDear Ms. Rosa,\nI am contacting you on behalf of the Dolina Foundation. Our mission is to promote the\nuse of distance-learning platforms in rural areas and communities that are isolated\ngeographically. We do so through a network of partners in the technology industry. We\nwould be honored to have your company join our network.\nAt 2:00 P.M. on June 25, Dolina is sponsoring a presentation entitled “Distance Learning\nin Rural Libraries.” The presentation will be given online as a webinar, using some of\nthe technologies our partners have developed. Jay Ralston, the foundation’s director of\nsystems integration, will describe technologies being used to support academic and\nvocational education programs. In addition, five librarians will discuss how they offer a\nvariety of education programs in their regions using technologies developed and\ndelivered by our business partners. To register for the webinar, and to learn more about\nour foundation’s projects, visit our Web site at www.dolinafoundation.org. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. We hope that you will consider our\ninvitation.\nWith kind regards,\nVera Fernandez, Outreach Coordinator","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Vera Fernandez\nTo: Carla Rosa\nSent: June 07, 12:47 P.M.\nSubject: Initiatives for distance learning\nDear Ms. Rosa,\nI am contacting you on behalf of the Dolina Foundation. Our mission is to promote the\nuse of distance-learning platforms in rural areas and communities that are isolated\ngeographically. We do so through a network of partners in the technology industry. We\nwould be honored to have your company join our network.\nAt 2:00 P.M. on June 25, Dolina is sponsoring a presentation entitled “Distance Learning\nin Rural Libraries.” The presentation will be given online as a webinar, using some of\nthe technologies our partners have developed. Jay Ralston, the foundation’s director of\nsystems integration, will describe technologies being used to support academic and\nvocational education programs. In addition, five librarians will discuss how they offer a\nvariety of education programs in their regions using technologies developed and\ndelivered by our business partners. To register for the webinar, and to learn more about\nour foundation’s projects, visit our Web site at www.dolinafoundation.org. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. We hope that you will consider our\ninvitation.\nWith kind regards,\nVera Fernandez, Outreach Coordinator"}],"question":"What does the Dolina Foundation do?","bilingual":"Quỹ Dolina làm gì?","options":["Sell software to schools","Print textbooks used in schools","Use technology to support learning","Build libraries in large cities"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Use technology to support learning\".","vocabList":[{"word":"foundation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃən/","meaning":"căn cứ; nền tảng; công trình phụ; thành lập; tổ chức"},{"word":"software","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɑːft.wer/","meaning":"phần mềm"},{"word":"school","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/skul/","meaning":"trường học"},{"word":"textbooks","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈtɛkstˌbʊks/","meaning":"Sách giáo khoa"}]},{"questionNum":"167","passageTitle":"Questions 166-168 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Vera Fernandez\nTo: Carla Rosa\nSent: June 07, 12:47 P.M.\nSubject: Initiatives for distance learning\nDear Ms. Rosa,\nI am contacting you on behalf of the Dolina Foundation. Our mission is to promote the\nuse of distance-learning platforms in rural areas and communities that are isolated\ngeographically. We do so through a network of partners in the technology industry. We\nwould be honored to have your company join our network.\nAt 2:00 P.M. on June 25, Dolina is sponsoring a presentation entitled “Distance Learning\nin Rural Libraries.” The presentation will be given online as a webinar, using some of\nthe technologies our partners have developed. Jay Ralston, the foundation’s director of\nsystems integration, will describe technologies being used to support academic and\nvocational education programs. In addition, five librarians will discuss how they offer a\nvariety of education programs in their regions using technologies developed and\ndelivered by our business partners. To register for the webinar, and to learn more about\nour foundation’s projects, visit our Web site at www.dolinafoundation.org. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. We hope that you will consider our\ninvitation.\nWith kind regards,\nVera Fernandez, Outreach Coordinator","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Vera Fernandez\nTo: Carla Rosa\nSent: June 07, 12:47 P.M.\nSubject: Initiatives for distance learning\nDear Ms. Rosa,\nI am contacting you on behalf of the Dolina Foundation. Our mission is to promote the\nuse of distance-learning platforms in rural areas and communities that are isolated\ngeographically. We do so through a network of partners in the technology industry. We\nwould be honored to have your company join our network.\nAt 2:00 P.M. on June 25, Dolina is sponsoring a presentation entitled “Distance Learning\nin Rural Libraries.” The presentation will be given online as a webinar, using some of\nthe technologies our partners have developed. Jay Ralston, the foundation’s director of\nsystems integration, will describe technologies being used to support academic and\nvocational education programs. In addition, five librarians will discuss how they offer a\nvariety of education programs in their regions using technologies developed and\ndelivered by our business partners. To register for the webinar, and to learn more about\nour foundation’s projects, visit our Web site at www.dolinafoundation.org. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. We hope that you will consider our\ninvitation.\nWith kind regards,\nVera Fernandez, Outreach Coordinator"}],"question":"What is Ms. Rosa asked to do?","bilingual":"Cô Rosa được yêu cầu làm gì?","options":["Approve a grant","Participate in a webinar","Apply for a job opening","Visit some libraries 184"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Participate in a webinar\".","vocabList":[{"word":"approve","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈpruːv/","meaning":"tán thành, phê chuẩn"},{"word":"grant","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/grænt/","meaning":"đồng ý; cho ; ban cho ; trả lời ; quyên góp"},{"word":"participate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/pɑrˈtɪsəˌpeɪt/","meaning":"được tham gia; tham gia vào"},{"word":"apply","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈplaɪ/","meaning":"áp dụng, ứng tuyển"}]},{"questionNum":"168","passageTitle":"Questions 166-168 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Vera Fernandez\nTo: Carla Rosa\nSent: June 07, 12:47 P.M.\nSubject: Initiatives for distance learning\nDear Ms. Rosa,\nI am contacting you on behalf of the Dolina Foundation. Our mission is to promote the\nuse of distance-learning platforms in rural areas and communities that are isolated\ngeographically. We do so through a network of partners in the technology industry. We\nwould be honored to have your company join our network.\nAt 2:00 P.M. on June 25, Dolina is sponsoring a presentation entitled “Distance Learning\nin Rural Libraries.” The presentation will be given online as a webinar, using some of\nthe technologies our partners have developed. Jay Ralston, the foundation’s director of\nsystems integration, will describe technologies being used to support academic and\nvocational education programs. In addition, five librarians will discuss how they offer a\nvariety of education programs in their regions using technologies developed and\ndelivered by our business partners. To register for the webinar, and to learn more about\nour foundation’s projects, visit our Web site at www.dolinafoundation.org. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. We hope that you will consider our\ninvitation.\nWith kind regards,\nVera Fernandez, Outreach Coordinator","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Vera Fernandez\nTo: Carla Rosa\nSent: June 07, 12:47 P.M.\nSubject: Initiatives for distance learning\nDear Ms. Rosa,\nI am contacting you on behalf of the Dolina Foundation. Our mission is to promote the\nuse of distance-learning platforms in rural areas and communities that are isolated\ngeographically. We do so through a network of partners in the technology industry. We\nwould be honored to have your company join our network.\nAt 2:00 P.M. on June 25, Dolina is sponsoring a presentation entitled “Distance Learning\nin Rural Libraries.” The presentation will be given online as a webinar, using some of\nthe technologies our partners have developed. Jay Ralston, the foundation’s director of\nsystems integration, will describe technologies being used to support academic and\nvocational education programs. In addition, five librarians will discuss how they offer a\nvariety of education programs in their regions using technologies developed and\ndelivered by our business partners. To register for the webinar, and to learn more about\nour foundation’s projects, visit our Web site at www.dolinafoundation.org. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. We hope that you will consider our\ninvitation.\nWith kind regards,\nVera Fernandez, Outreach Coordinator"}],"question":"Who most likely is Ms. Fernandez?","bilingual":"Cô Fernandez có nhiều khả năng là ai nhất?","options":["A student in a foundation program","An executive at a technology firm","A researcher at a rural library","An employee of the foundation"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"An employee of the foundation\".","vocabList":[{"word":"student","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈstudənt/","meaning":"Sinh viên"},{"word":"foundation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃən/","meaning":"căn cứ; nền tảng; công trình phụ; thành lập; tổ chức"},{"word":"program","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈproʊˌgræm/","meaning":"lên lịch; lập kế hoạch; viết hệ điều hành"},{"word":"executive","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪɡˈzek.jə.t̬ɪv/","meaning":"(thuộc) chấp hành, sự thi hành; tổ chức hành"}]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"Questions 169-171 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"29 July\nShari Mac Cauley\n103 East on Lane\nTomintoul, Ballindalloch AB37 9EX\nDear Ms. Mac Cauley,\nIt was a privilege to stay in your home during the week of 22 July as part of the\nScottish Connections home exchange program.\nThe location was the perfect setting for our family gathering. My daughter and\nson-in-law relished the peace and quiet of the village, while their children enjoyed\nplaying in the wide-open space behind your home. And my husband was quite\npleased with the large-screen television set in the living room.\nIt was very thoughtful of you to provide so many extra blankets. We did not expect\nit to be so cold at night in July.\nAs I said in the note I left on your dining room table on 25 July, the day of my\nwedding anniversary party, the lid of your food process or cracked as we were\npreparing our meal. We ordered a replacement lid that same day, which should be\ndelivered to your home soon, assuming it hasn’t been already I sincerely apologize\nfor the mishap.\nI hope that you and your friends enjoyed our apartment here in Aberdeen just as\nmuch as we enjoyed your mountain home. If so, we hope you will be willing to\nexchange homes with us again in the future.\nSincerely,\nClara/3rLvuvaU/\nClara Brinwall","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"29 July\nShari Mac Cauley\n103 East on Lane\nTomintoul, Ballindalloch AB37 9EX\nDear Ms. Mac Cauley,\nIt was a privilege to stay in your home during the week of 22 July as part of the\nScottish Connections home exchange program.\nThe location was the perfect setting for our family gathering. My daughter and\nson-in-law relished the peace and quiet of the village, while their children enjoyed\nplaying in the wide-open space behind your home. And my husband was quite\npleased with the large-screen television set in the living room.\nIt was very thoughtful of you to provide so many extra blankets. We did not expect\nit to be so cold at night in July.\nAs I said in the note I left on your dining room table on 25 July, the day of my\nwedding anniversary party, the lid of your food process or cracked as we were\npreparing our meal. We ordered a replacement lid that same day, which should be\ndelivered to your home soon, assuming it hasn’t been already I sincerely apologize\nfor the mishap.\nI hope that you and your friends enjoyed our apartment here in Aberdeen just as\nmuch as we enjoyed your mountain home. If so, we hope you will be willing to\nexchange homes with us again in the future.\nSincerely,\nClara/3rLvuvaU/\nClara Brinwall"}],"question":"What is a purpose of the letter?","bilingual":"Mục đích của bức thư là gì?","options":["To explain a family tradition","To confirm that a package was received","To express appreciation for a house","To outline the benefits of taking vacation"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"To express appreciation for a house\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"letter","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlɛtər/","meaning":"ký tự là một phần của bảng chữ cái; bằng văn bản"},{"word":"explain","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ɪkˈspleɪn/","meaning":"minh họa; làm sáng tỏ; để giải thích; để mô tả ; ĐẾN"},{"word":"family","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfæməli/","meaning":"gia đình"}]},{"questionNum":"170","passageTitle":"Questions 169-171 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"29 July\nShari Mac Cauley\n103 East on Lane\nTomintoul, Ballindalloch AB37 9EX\nDear Ms. Mac Cauley,\nIt was a privilege to stay in your home during the week of 22 July as part of the\nScottish Connections home exchange program.\nThe location was the perfect setting for our family gathering. My daughter and\nson-in-law relished the peace and quiet of the village, while their children enjoyed\nplaying in the wide-open space behind your home. And my husband was quite\npleased with the large-screen television set in the living room.\nIt was very thoughtful of you to provide so many extra blankets. We did not expect\nit to be so cold at night in July.\nAs I said in the note I left on your dining room table on 25 July, the day of my\nwedding anniversary party, the lid of your food process or cracked as we were\npreparing our meal. We ordered a replacement lid that same day, which should be\ndelivered to your home soon, assuming it hasn’t been already I sincerely apologize\nfor the mishap.\nI hope that you and your friends enjoyed our apartment here in Aberdeen just as\nmuch as we enjoyed your mountain home. If so, we hope you will be willing to\nexchange homes with us again in the future.\nSincerely,\nClara/3rLvuvaU/\nClara Brinwall","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"29 July\nShari Mac Cauley\n103 East on Lane\nTomintoul, Ballindalloch AB37 9EX\nDear Ms. Mac Cauley,\nIt was a privilege to stay in your home during the week of 22 July as part of the\nScottish Connections home exchange program.\nThe location was the perfect setting for our family gathering. My daughter and\nson-in-law relished the peace and quiet of the village, while their children enjoyed\nplaying in the wide-open space behind your home. And my husband was quite\npleased with the large-screen television set in the living room.\nIt was very thoughtful of you to provide so many extra blankets. We did not expect\nit to be so cold at night in July.\nAs I said in the note I left on your dining room table on 25 July, the day of my\nwedding anniversary party, the lid of your food process or cracked as we were\npreparing our meal. We ordered a replacement lid that same day, which should be\ndelivered to your home soon, assuming it hasn’t been already I sincerely apologize\nfor the mishap.\nI hope that you and your friends enjoyed our apartment here in Aberdeen just as\nmuch as we enjoyed your mountain home. If so, we hope you will be willing to\nexchange homes with us again in the future.\nSincerely,\nClara/3rLvuvaU/\nClara Brinwall"}],"question":"What happened on July 25?","bilingual":"Chuyện gì đã xảy ra vào ngày 25 tháng 7?","options":["An item was damaged.","An order was delivered.","An event was catered.","A wedding was held."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"An item was damaged.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"item","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈaɪ.t̬əm/","meaning":"món đồ"},{"word":"order","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''ɔ:də/","meaning":"thứ, bậc, ngô