ses managers to give\nfacts and reactions, rather than advice and\ncriticism.\nMs. Bishara will be speaking at Stonecliff\nBookstore on Monday, 6 April at 2:00 P.M. For\nmore details, visit www.stoneclifif.co.uk. To: Oscar Burton <oburton @harstonindustries.com.hk>\nFrom: Mi-Sook Pan <mpan @harstonindustries.kr>\nSubject: Suggestion\nDate: 10 April\nHello Oscar,\nI understand that we have not yet booked all of the workshop leaders for our upcoming\nprofessional development program at the Onyx Hotel. I was in London a few days ago\nworking on the Phillips account. While there, on 6 April, I had a chance to meet Sarnia\nBishara and hear her speak on the topic of her new book, Facts on Feedback. I believe she\nwould be an excellent choice to lead one of our workshops. I will gather further details\nabout Ms. Bishara’s background and availability and send that to you shortly. I look\nforward to joining you during Thursday''s teleconference planning meeting.\nSincerely,\nMi-Sook Pan\n190","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Business Happenings\nBy Harriet Mellors\nLONDON (l April) ------- It is often hard for\nmanagers or team leaders to learn the best way\nto give feedback to employees and colleagues.\nSarnia Bishara’s new book, Facts on\nFeedback (Fox Mill Press), offers advice on\nthis subject. Ms. Bishara is an expert\nconsultant on company management problems\nand solutions. She advises managers to give\nfacts and reactions, rather than advice and\ncriticism.\nMs. Bishara will be speaking at Stonecliff\nBookstore on Monday, 6 April at 2:00 P.M. For\nmore details, visit www.stoneclifif.co.uk. To: Oscar Burton <oburton @harstonindustries.com.hk>\nFrom: Mi-Sook Pan <mpan @harstonindustries.kr>\nSubject: Suggestion\nDate: 10 April\nHello Oscar,\nI understand that we have not yet booked all of the workshop leaders for our upcoming\nprofessional development program at the Onyx Hotel. I was in London a few days ago\nworking on the Phillips account. While there, on 6 April, I had a chance to meet Sarnia\nBishara and hear her speak on the topic of her new book, Facts on Feedback. I believe she\nwould be an excellent choice to lead one of our workshops. I will gather further details\nabout Ms. Bishara’s background and availability and send that to you shortly. I look\nforward to joining you during Thursday''s teleconference planning meeting.\nSincerely,\nMi-Sook Pan\n190"}],"question":"In the article, the word “hard” in paragraph 1, line 1, is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"","options":["durable","difficult","solid","true"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"difficult\".","vocabList":[{"word":"article","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɑrtɪkəl/","meaning":"mục; sự vật; đoạn văn bản; đoạn hợp đồng"},{"word":"hard","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/hɑrd/","meaning":"khó; phức tap; cứng nhắc; cứng nhắc"},{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"durable","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈdʊrəbəl/","meaning":"vững chắc; lâu dài"}]},{"questionNum":"182","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following article and e-mail.","passageText":"Business Happenings\nBy Harriet Mellors\nLONDON (l April) ------- It is often hard for\nmanagers or team leaders to learn the best way\nto give feedback to employees and colleagues.\nSarnia Bishara’s new book, Facts on\nFeedback (Fox Mill Press), offers advice on\nthis subject. Ms. Bishara is an expert\nconsultant on company management problems\nand solutions. She advises managers to give\nfacts and reactions, rather than advice and\ncriticism.\nMs. Bishara will be speaking at Stonecliff\nBookstore on Monday, 6 April at 2:00 P.M. For\nmore details, visit www.stonec