onths, many of the chairs were broken and unusable.\nWe were initially happy with the replacement chairs that you delivered free of charge, but\nsome of those have now broken as well.\nI am here by requesting that you replace all 22 with chairs from your new Executive line\n(Item #10612) at no extra charge ------- assuming that they are better quality. These are\ncomparable in price to the original model we purchased. If you are unable to do this, we\nwill be forced to look elsewhere for our furnishing needs.\nAlexandra Martin, Office Administrator\nNetforce Events\n(http://www.hansons-office.com/ergonomic-task-chair A\nHANSON S: YOUR ONE-STOP SHOP FOR OFFICE SUPPLIES\nHome Products I f Customer f About Us\nHelp^\nErgonomic Task Chair\nThe Ergonomic Task Chair is our best-selling swivel • Black, Item Code 429BL\nmodel. It is specially designed to promote good posture • Blue, Item Code 469BB\nand avoid discomfort, and therefore it is perfect for those •Green, Item Code 490GN\nlong workdays at the office. Best of all, it is built to last •Red, Item Code 459RD\nand comes with a lifetime warranty. The model is available\nin four attractive colors.\n$159 per unit\n194\n\nHANSON S: YOUR ONE-STOP SHOP FOR OFFICE SUPPLIES\nINVOICE\nClient: Netforce Events\nAddress: 342 Collat''d Boulevard, Hampton, ME\nDate: September 10\nItem Quantity Unit Price Total\nErgonomic Task Chair, 22 $159.00 $3,498.00\nItem 490GN\nSubtotal $3,498.00\nDiscount for first-time customers -$159.00\nTotal $3,339.00\nPlease contact customerhelp@hansons-office.com if you have any questions."}],"question":"What color are the chairs Netforce Events ordered from Hanson’s?","bilingual":"Ghế Netforce Events đặt hàng từ Hanson''s có màu gì?","options":["Black","Blue","Green","Red"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Green\".","vocabList":[{"word":"chair","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/tʃer/","meaning":"ghế ngồi"},{"word":"events","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪˈvɛnts/","meaning":"sự kiện"},{"word":"black","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/blæk/","meaning":"Đen"},{"word":"blue","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/blu/","meaning":"Xanh lam"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following notice, chart, and e-mail.","passageText":"KLOOF PHOTOGRAPHY EVENT\nOn 21 November, all Kloof employees are invited to a celebration to commemorate\nour first five years in business. Please attend our company picnic featuring a\ntraditional braai as well as live music and competitive games. The company will\nprovide meats fresh off the grill prepared in the traditional braai style. Beverages will\nalso be provided. In exchange, we ask that attendees either plan to bring a side dish\nto share or volunteer to join the setup crew. To make the event run smoothly, we will\nneed at least two people to help with setup.\nOur gathering will convene from 1 to 8 P.M. on the patio of our headquarters\nbuilding. If you plan to attend, please open the sign-up sheet saved on the company\ndrive and indicate there how you will contribute. Employees are welcome to bring a\nguest, so long as they indicate their intention to do so. Any questions may be\ndirected to our events coordinator, Noxolo Nwosu, at nnwosu@kloofphoto.sa. ------- n x\nKloof Photography Sign-Up Sheet\nName Side dish Bringing a guest?\nMason Kivundu sweet corn No\nClara Singh potato salad Yes\nKarl Williams garlic bread Yes\nSaid Diallo jollof rice Yes\nSekou Lombard Yes\nPatricia Williams on drinks Yes\n196\n\nFrom: Dawyd Johnson\nTo: Noxolo Nwosu\nSubject: Kloof summer event\nDate: 3 November\nDear Ms. Nwosu,\nA\nThank you for organizing the upcoming event. Several of my Kloof colleagues have been\ndiscussing the dishes they intend to bring. However, since I have just arrived in South\nAfrica, the culture surrounding a braai picnic is quite new to me. Also, I am not much of a\ncook, but I do want to contribute to the success of the picnic. Please let me know what\nwould be most helpful.\nSincerely,\nDawyd Johnson","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"KLOOF PHOTOGRAPHY EVENT\nOn 21 November, all Kloof employees are invited to a celebration to commemorate\nour first five years in business. Please attend our company picnic featuring a\ntraditional braai as well as live music and competitive games. The company will\nprovide meats fresh off the grill prepared in the traditional braai style. Beverages will\nalso be provided. In exchange, we ask that attendees either plan to bring a side dish\nto share or volunteer to join the setup crew. To make the event run smoothly, we will\nneed at least two people to help with setup.\nOur gathering will convene from 1 to 8 P.M. on the patio of our headquarters\nbuilding. If you plan to attend, please open the sign-up sheet saved on the company\ndrive and indicate there how you will contribute. Employees are welcome to bring a\nguest, so long as they indicate their intention to do so. Any questions may be\ndirected to our events coordinator, Noxolo Nwosu, at nnwosu@kloofphoto.sa. ------- n x\nKloof Photography Sign-Up Sheet\nName Side dish Bringing a guest?\nMason Kivundu sweet corn No\nClara Singh potato salad Yes\nKarl Williams garlic bread Yes\nSaid Diallo jollof rice Yes\nSekou Lombard Yes\nPatricia Williams on drinks Yes\n196\n\nFrom: Dawyd Johnson\nTo: Noxolo Nwosu\nSubject: Kloof summer event\nDate: 3 November\nDear Ms. Nwosu,\nA\nThank you for organizing the upcoming event. Several of my Kloof colleagues have been\ndiscussing the dishes they intend to bring. However, since I have just arrived in South\nAfrica, the culture surrounding a braai picnic is quite new to me. Also, I am not much of a\ncook, but I do want to contribute to the success of the picnic. Please let me know what\nwould be most helpful.\nSincerely,\nDawyd Johnson"}],"question":"What is the reason for the event?","bilingual":"Lý do của sự kiện là gì?","options":["To promote a product","To celebrate a store opening","To welcome a new company president","To mark a company anniversary"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To mark a company anniversary\".","vocabList":[{"word":"reason","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrizən/","meaning":"suy nghĩ ; để xem xét một cách hợp lý; tranh luận ; để yêu cầu"},{"word":"event","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪˈvent/","meaning":"sự kiện, sự việc"},{"word":"promote","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/prəˈmoʊt/","meaning":"thăng chức, thăng cấp; đề bạt"},{"word":"product","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈprɑdəkt/","meaning":"kết quả sản xuất; hàng hóa; hàng hóa"}]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following notice, chart, and e-mail.","passageText":"KLOOF PHOTOGRAPHY EVENT\nOn 21 November, all Kloof employees are invited to a celebration to commemorate\nour first five years in business. Please attend our company picnic featuring a\ntraditional braai as well as live music and competitive games. The company will\nprovide meats fresh off the grill prepared in the traditional braai style. Beverages will\nalso be provided. In exchange, we ask that attendees either plan to bring a side dish\nto share or volunteer to join the setup crew. To make the event run smoothly, we will\nneed at least two people to help with setup.\nOur gathering will convene from 1 to 8 P.M. on the patio of our headquarters\nbuilding. If you plan to attend, please open the sign-up sheet saved on the company\ndrive and indicate there how you will contribute. Employees are welcome to bring a\nguest, so long as they indicate their intention to do so. Any questions may be\ndirected to our events coordinator, Noxolo Nwosu, at nnwosu@kloofphoto.sa. ------- n x\nKloof Photography Sign-Up Sheet\nName Side dish Bringing a guest?\nMason Kivundu sweet corn No\nClara Singh potato salad Yes\nKarl Williams garlic bread Yes\nSaid Diallo jollof rice Yes\nSekou Lombard Yes\nPatricia Williams on drinks Yes\n196\n\nFrom: Dawyd Johnson\nTo: Noxolo Nwosu\nSubject: Kloof summer event\nDate: 3 November\nDear Ms. Nwosu,\nA\nThank you for organizing the upcoming event. Several of my Kloof colleagues have been\ndiscussing the dishes they intend to bring. However, since I have just arrived in South\nAfrica, the culture surrounding a braai picnic is quite new to me. Also, I am not much of a\ncook, but I do want to contribute to the success of the picnic. Please let me know what\nwould be most helpful.\nSincerely,\nDawyd Johnson","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"KLOOF PHOTOGRAPHY EVENT\nOn 21 November, all Kloof employees are invited to a celebration to commemorate\nour first five years in business. Please attend our company picnic featuring a\ntraditional braai as well as live music and competitive games. The company will\nprovide meats fresh off the grill prepared in the traditional braai style. Beverages will\nalso be provided. In exchange, we ask that attendees either plan to bring a side dish\nto share or volunteer to join the setup crew. To make the event run smoothly, we will\nneed at least two people to help with setup.\nOur gathering will convene from 1 to 8 P.M. on the patio of our headquarters\nbuilding. If you plan to attend, please open the sign-up sheet saved on the company\ndrive and indicate there how you will contribute. Employees are welcome to bring a\nguest, so long as they indicate their intention to do so. Any questions may be\ndirected to our events coordinator, Noxolo Nwosu, at nnwosu@kloofphoto.sa. ------- n x\nKloof Photography Sign-Up Sheet\nName Side dish Bringing a guest?\nMason Kivundu sweet corn No\nClara Singh potato salad Yes\nKarl Williams garlic bread Yes\nSaid Diallo jollof rice Yes\nSekou Lombard Yes\nPatricia Williams on drinks Yes\n196\n\nFrom: Dawyd Johnson\nTo: Noxolo Nwosu\nSubject: Kloof summer event\nDate: 3 November\nDear Ms. Nwosu,\nA\nThank you for organizing the upcoming event. Several of my Kloof colleagues have been\ndiscussing the dishes they intend to bring. However, since I have just arrived in South\nAfrica, the culture surrounding a braai picnic is quite new to me. Also, I am not much of a\ncook, but I do want to contribute to the success of the picnic. Please let me know what\nwould be most helpful.\nSincerely,\nDawyd Johnson"}],"question":"According to the notice, where will the event be held?","bilingual":"Theo thông báo thì sự kiện sẽ được tổ chức ở đâu?","options":["At a park","Near an office building","At a retail store","On a sports field"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Near an office building\".","vocabList":[{"word":"notice","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''nəƱtis/","meaning":"thông tri, yết thị, thông báo"},{"word":"event","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪˈvent/","meaning":"sự kiện, sự việc"},{"word":"near","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/nɪr/","meaning":"gần"},{"word":"office","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔfəs/","meaning":"buồng; văn phòng; đương nhiệm; hãng; thẩm quyền"}]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following notice, chart, and e-mail.","passageText":"KLOOF PHOTOGRAPHY EVENT\nOn 21 November, all Kloof employees are invited to a celebration to commemorate\nour first five years in business. Please attend our company picnic featuring a\ntraditional braai as well as live music and competitive games. The company will\nprovide meats fresh off the grill prepared in the traditional braai style. Beverages will\nalso be provided. In exc