nh trị) cuộc mít tinh, cuộc biểu tình"},{"word":"interview","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.t̬ɚ.vjuː/","meaning":"phỏng vấn"},{"word":"candidate","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkæn.dɪ.dət/","meaning":"/ˈkæn.dɪ.deɪt/"}]},{"questionNum":"154","passageTitle":"Questions 153-154 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Leann Oliver (9:20 A.M.)\nHi, Rafael. Will you be coming to the hiring committee\nmeeting this afternoon?\nRafael Sauceda (9:21 A.M.)\n1 wasn’t planning to. Do you need me there?\nLeann Oliver (9:22 A.M.)\nWe had more candidates apply for the job than we anticipated.\nWe need to decide who to interview, and your expertise would\nbe very helpful.\nRafael Sauceda (9:23 A.M.)\nI’ll be happy to help. It’s at 4, right?\nLeann Oliver (9:24 A.M.)\nExactly. In conference room B. I’ll see you there. Thanks.\n•9 •m","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Leann Oliver (9:20 A.M.)\nHi, Rafael. Will you be coming to the hiring committee\nmeeting this afternoon?\nRafael Sauceda (9:21 A.M.)\n1 wasn’t planning to. Do you need me there?\nLeann Oliver (9:22 A.M.)\nWe had more candidates apply for the job than we anticipated.\nWe need to decide who to interview, and your expertise would\nbe very helpful.\nRafael Sauceda (9:23 A.M.)\nI’ll be happy to help. It’s at 4, right?\nLeann Oliver (9:24 A.M.)\nExactly. In conference room B. I’ll see you there. Thanks.\n•9 •m"}],"question":"At 9:24 A.M., what does Ms. Oliver most likely mean when she writes, “Exactly”?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 9:24 sáng, rất có thể cô Oliver có ý gì khi viết “Chính xác”?","options":["The meeting room is on the fourth floor.","The meeting is scheduled for 4:00 P.M.","Four people will attend the meeting.","The committee will meet four times."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"The meeting is scheduled for 4:00 P.M.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"exactly","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ɪgˈzæktli/","meaning":"chính xác"},{"word":"meeting","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mi:tiɳ/","meaning":"(chính trị) cuộc mít tinh, cuộc biểu tình"}]},{"questionNum":"155","passageTitle":"Questions 155-157 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Manufacturer Celebrates IV Illestone\nMINNEAPOLIS (August 13) ------- Lindgren was purchased by James Wall in. Today,\nMachinery, a manufacturer of precision the firm continues as a family-owned and\nmachine parts, recently celebrated the one family-directed operation. In recent years,\nhundredth anniversary of its founding.\nThe company was started by Jona\nLindgren, who began his career as an\napprentice at a metal parts firm in\nSweden. He eventually immigrated to the\nUnited States and settled in the outskirts\nof the city of Minneapolis. Mr. Lindgren\nestablished a modest enterprise that grew,\ngenerating most of its revenue from the\nproduction of custom machine parts.\nThirty years ago, Lindgren Machinery\ncurrent president and CEO Mary Wall in\nhas gradually assumed the leadership role\nfrom her father.\nLindgren Machinery makes parts for\nair planes, exercise equipment, and health-\ncare devices. According to Ms. Wall in, the\ncompany is planning to expand its facility\nand add capacity as its product list grows\nand diversifies.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Manufacturer Celebrates IV Illestone\nMINNEAPOLIS (August 13) ------- Lindgren was purchased by James Wall in. Today,\nMachinery, a manufacturer of precision the firm continues as a family-owned and\nmachine parts, recently celebrated the one family-directed operation. In recent years,\nhundredth anniversary of its founding.\nThe company was started by Jona\nLindgren, who began his career as an\napprentice at a metal parts firm in\nSweden. He eventually immigrated to the\nUnited States and settled in the outskirts\nof the city of Minneapolis. Mr. Lindgren\nestablished a modest enterprise that grew,\ngenerating most of its revenue from the\nproduction of custom machine parts.\nThirty years ago, Lindgren Machinery\ncurrent president and CEO Mary Wall in\nhas gradually assumed the leadership role\nfrom her father.\nLindgren Machinery makes parts for\nair planes, exercise equipment, and health-\ncare devices. According to Ms. Wall in, the\ncompany is planning to expand its facility\nand add capacity as its product list grows\nand diversifies."}],"question":"What is the main purpose of the article?","bilingual":"Mục đích chính của bài viết là gì?","options":["To announce job openings at a company","To tell about the relocation of a company","To summarize the history of a company","To describe successful manufacturing strategies"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"To summarize the history of a company\".","vocabList":[{"word":"main","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪn/","meaning":"đường ống hoặc ống dẫn chính trong hệ thống; phần chính của"},{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"article","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈɑrtɪkəl/","meaning":"mục; sự vật; đoạn văn bản; đoạn hợp đồng"},{"word":"opening","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈoʊpənɪŋ/","meaning":"khai trương"}]},{"questionNum":"156","passageTitle":"Questions 155-157 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Manufacturer Celebrates IV Illestone\nMINNEAPOLIS (August 13) ------- Lindgren was purchased by James Wall in. Today,\nMachinery, a manufacturer of precision the firm continues as a family-owned and\nmachine parts, recently celebrated the one family-directed operation. In recent years,\nhundredth anniversary of its founding.\nThe company was started by Jona\nLindgren, who began his career as an\napprentice at a metal parts firm in\nSweden. He eventually immigrated to the\nUnited States and settled in the outskirts\nof the city of Minneapolis. Mr. Lindgren\nestablished a modest enterprise that grew,\ngenerating most of its revenue from the\nproduction of custom machine parts.\nThirty years ago, Lindgren Machinery\ncurrent president and CEO Mary Wall in\nhas gradually assumed the leadership role\nfrom her father.\nLindgren Machinery makes parts for\nair planes, exercise equipment, and health-\ncare devices. According to Ms. Wall in, the\ncompany is planning to expand its facility\nand add capacity as its product list grows\nand diversifies.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Manufacturer Celebrates IV Illestone\nMINNEAPOLIS (August 13) ------- Lindgren was purchased by James Wall in. Today,\nMachinery, a manufacturer of precision the firm continues as a family-owned and\nmachine parts, recently celebrated the one family-directed operation. In recent years,\nhundredth anniversary of its founding.\nThe company was started by Jona\nLindgren, who began his career as an\napprentice at a metal parts firm in\nSweden. He eventually immigrated to the\nUnited States and settled in the outskirts\nof the city of Minneapolis. Mr. Lindgren\nestablished a modest enterprise that grew,\ngenerating most of its revenue from the\nproduction of custom machine parts.\nThirty years ago, Lindgren Machinery\ncurrent president and CEO Mary Wall in\nhas gradually assumed the leadership role\nfrom her father.\nLindgren Machinery makes parts for\nair planes, exercise equipment, and health-\ncare devices. According to Ms. Wall in, the\ncompany is planning to expand its facility\nand add capacity as its product list grows\nand diversifies."}],"question":"The word “assumed” in paragraph 2, line 6 is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"Từ “assumed” ở đoạn 2, dòng 6 gần nghĩa nhất với","options":["undertaken","pretended","thought","attempted"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"undertaken\".","vocabList":[{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"undertaken","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈəndərˌteɪkən/","meaning":"đảm nhận"},{"word":"pretended","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/priˈtɛndɪd/","meaning":"giả vờ"},{"word":"thought","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/θɔt/","meaning":"ý tưởng; ý tưởng; sản phẩm của tâm trí"}]},{"questionNum":"157","passageTitle":"Questions 155-157 refer to the following article.","passageText":"Manufacturer Celebrates IV Illestone\nMINNEAPOLIS (August 13) ------- Lindgren was purchased by James Wall in. Today,\nMachinery, a manufacturer of precision the firm continues as a family-owned and\nmachine parts, recently celebrated the one family-directed operation. In recent years,\nhundredth anniversary of its founding.\nThe company was started by Jona\nLindgren, who began his career as an\napprentice at a metal parts firm in\nSweden. He eventually immigrated to the\nUnited States and settled in the outskirts\nof the city of Minneapolis. Mr. Lindgren\nestablished a modest enterprise that grew,\ngenerating most of its revenue from the\nproduction of custom machine parts.\nThirty years ago, Lindgren Machinery\ncurrent president and CEO Mary Wall in\nhas gradually assumed the leadership role\nfrom her father.\nLindgren Machinery makes parts for\nair planes, exercise equipment, and health-\ncare devices. According to Ms. Wall in, the\ncompany is planning to expand its facility\nand add capacity as its product list grows\nand diversifies.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Manufacturer Celebrates IV Illestone\nMINNEAPOLIS (August 13) ------- Lindgren was purchased by James Wall in. Today,\nMachinery, a manufacturer of precision the firm continues as a family-owned and\nmachine parts, recently celebrated the one family-directed operation. In recent years,\nhundredth anniversary of its founding.\nThe company was started by Jona\nLindgren, who began his career as an\napprentice at a metal parts firm in\nSweden. He eventually immigrated to the\nUnited States and settled in the outskirts\nof the city of Minneapolis. Mr. Lindgren\nestablished a modest enterprise that grew,\ngenerating most of its revenue from the\nproduction of custom machine parts.\nThirty years ago, Lindgren Machinery\ncurrent president and CEO Mary Wall in\nhas gradually assumed the leadership role\nfrom her father.\nLindgren Machinery makes parts for\nair planes, exercise equipment, and health-\ncare devices. According to Ms. Wall in, the\ncompany is planning to expand its facility\nand add capacity as its product list grows\nand diversifies."}],"question":"What is currently true about Lindgren Machinery?","bilingual":"Điều gì hiện tại đúng về Lindgren Machinery?","options":["It is training new management.","It has recently moved its headquarters.","It is the largest employer in the city.","It is a family-operated business."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"It is a family-operated business.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"currently","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkərəntli/","meaning":"hiện tại"},{"word":"training","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈtreɪ.nɪŋ/","meaning":"sự huấn luyện, sự đào tạo"},{"word":"management","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmænɪʤmənt/","meaning":"người của nhóm người điều hành và quản lý một"},{"word":"recently","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrisəntli/","meaning":"gần đây"}]},{"questionNum":"158","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Reservations reservations@panticohotels.com >\nTo: Roger Underhill <runderhill @month press.com>\nDate: 10 February\nSubject: Pantico Lisbon\nDear Mr. Underhill:\nThank you for booking your reservation with the Pantico Hotel Group. We are looking\nforward to your upcoming stay with us in Lisbon from 8 March through 12 March.\nWe are proud to offer a range of services, including a 24-hour coffee shop, a fitness\ncenter, and a business lounge. There is also a parking area for guests who wish to travel\nby car. However, the Pantico Lisbon is well situated and is within walking distance to\nmany fine shopping, entertainment, and dining options. We also have convenient access\nto public transportation, and airport transfers can be booked for a fee.\nTo learn more about us, please visit our Web site, www.panticohotels.com/lisbon. A\ncalendar with details about upcoming events, both at our hotel and in the surrounding\narea, can be found there.\nIf you have any questions or concerns, please feel free to respond directly to this e-mail.\nAll the best,\nBranca Lopes\nPantico Lisbon Hotel","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"*E-mail*\nFrom: Reservations reservations@panticohotels.com >\nTo: Roger Underhill <runderhill @month press.com>\nDate: 10 February\nSubject: Pantico Lisbon\nDear Mr. Underhill:\nThank you for booking your reservation with the Pantico Hotel Group. We are looking\nforward to your upcoming stay with us in Lisbon from 8 March through 12 March.\nWe are proud to offer a range of services, including a 24-hour coffee shop, a fitness\ncenter, and a business lounge. There is also a parking area for 