5 A.M.] The Hong Kong office is sending Sara Wang\nand Neha Agarwal. Others can call in if needed.\nDavid Tham [8:07 A.M.] Where will Sara and Neha be working when\nthey arrive?\nKelly Cromwell [8:09 A.M. l They''ll be set up in conference room B.\nOtherwise, they can use the empty desks located near Michael Klein in\nHuman Resources.\nJonathan Li [8:11 A.M. l Hold on. Actually, there are going to be three.\nLillian Zhang is coming, too.\nDavid Tham [8:12 A.M. l We will need another work space then. I''d like\nto keep them together. Maybe there''s a spare office in Accounting?\nKelly Cromwell [8:13 A.M. l Why is Ms. Zhang coming? I thought it was\njust the marketing team.\nJonathan Li [8:14 A.M. l The packaging designers have been working\nclosely with Marketing on this project.\nKelly Cromwell [8:17 A.M.] Got it. I''ll take care of it. I''ll send a final\nschedule to you before lunch. Jonathan, please update the list of call-in\nparticipants'' names and numbers and send it to all of us.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"David Tham [8:04 A.M.] Hello, Kelly and Jonathan. Have we confirmed &\nwho will be arriving from Hong Kong next week?\nKelly Cromwell [8:05 A.M.] The Hong Kong office is sending Sara Wang\nand Neha Agarwal. Others can call in if needed.\nDavid Tham [8:07 A.M.] Where will Sara and Neha be working when\nthey arrive?\nKelly Cromwell [8:09 A.M. l They''ll be set up in conference room B.\nOtherwise, they can use the empty desks located near Michael Klein in\nHuman Resources.\nJonathan Li [8:11 A.M. l Hold on. Actually, there are going to be three.\nLillian Zhang is coming, too.\nDavid Tham [8:12 A.M. l We will need another work space then. I''d like\nto keep them together. Maybe there''s a spare office in Accounting?\nKelly Cromwell [8:13 A.M. l Why is Ms. Zhang coming? I thought it was\njust the marketing team.\nJonathan Li [8:14 A.M. l The packaging designers have been working\nclosely with Marketing on this project.\nKelly Cromwell [8:17 A.M.] Got it. I''ll take care of it. I''ll send a final\nschedule to you before lunch. Jonathan, please update the list of call-in\nparticipants'' names and numbers and send it to all of us."}],"question":"What does Ms. Cromwell ask Mr. Li to do?","bilingual":"Cô Cromwell yêu cầu ông Li làm gì?","options":["Print a meeting schedule","Prepare a list of contacts","Distribute a lunch menu","Assign visitors to offices"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Prepare a list of contacts\".","vocabList":[{"word":"meeting","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''mi:tiɳ/","meaning":"(chính trị) cuộc mít tinh, cuộc biểu tình"},{"word":"schedule","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''skedʒu:l/","meaning":"kế hoạch làm việc, tiến độ thi công"},{"word":"prepare","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/priˈpɛr/","meaning":"chuẩn bị sẵn sàng; chuẩn bị sẵn sàng; để đưa vào"},{"word":"list","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/list/","meaning":"danh sách, sổ, bản kê khai"}]},{"questionNum":"168","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following information.","passageText":"Request for Proposal\nPurpose\nI ’he City of New Langston is seeking proposals for the manufacture and installation of electronic\nsignage at bus stops throughout the city. New Langston plans to deploy new electronic signs that\ndisplay real-time arrival information to bus riders.\nBackground\nCurrently, New Langston’s bus stops are marked by simple metal signs displaying only the\nlocation of the stop and the lines that stop at the location. Cities around the world have begun to\nincorporate real-time arrival information into bus stop signage. Electronic signs are proving to be\nvery popular with riders, and studies show that the introduction of such signage has contributed\nto increased ridership in numerous cities.\nProject Description\nThe successful bidder will provide New Langston with up to 350 electronic signs. The signs\nmust be powered by solar energy and have a battery backup allowing them to operate at night,\non cloudy days, and in all weather conditions. The signs must have a reliability factor of at least\n99 percent. The signs must display at least three and no more than five lines of text, and be\nconnected to the Internet in order to provide real-time information to bus riders.\nPlease submit detailed bids outlining costs by 11:59 p.m. on May 31 to the City of\nNew Langston Regional Council at regionalcoimcil@cityofnewlangston.gov.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Request for Proposal\nPurpose\nI ’he City of New Langston is seeking proposals for the manufacture and installation of electronic\nsignage at bus stops throughout the city. New Langston plans to deploy new electronic signs that\ndisplay real-time arrival information to bus riders.\nBackground\nCurrently, New Langston’s bus stops are marked by simple metal signs displaying only the\nlocation of the stop and the lines that stop at the location. Cities around the world have begun to\nincorporate real-time arrival information into bus stop signage. Electronic signs are proving to be\nvery popular with riders, and studies show that the introduction of such signage has contributed\nto increased ridership in numerous cities.\nProject Description\nThe successful bidder will provide New Langston with up to 350 electronic signs. The signs\nmust be powered by solar energy and have a battery backup allowing them to operate at night,\non cloudy days, and in all weather conditions. The signs must have a reliability factor of at least\n99 percent. The signs must display at least three and no more than five lines of text, and be\nconnected to the Internet in order to provide real-time information to bus riders.\nPlease submit detailed bids outlining costs by 11:59 p.m. on May 31 to the City of\nNew Langston Regional Council at regionalcoimcil@cityofnewlangston.gov."}],"question":"What is the purpose of the information?","bilingual":"Mục đích của thông tin là gì?","options":["To detail a city’s public transportation issues","To solicit bids for a city project","To outline the history of bus ridership","To encourage environmental responsibility"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To solicit bids for a city project\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"detail","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈdiː.teɪl/","meaning":"chi tiết, tiểu tiết; trình bày chi tiết, làm rõ"},{"word":"city","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪti/","meaning":"thị trấn; khu đô thị lớn"}]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following information.","passageText":"Request for Proposal\nPurpose\nI ’he City of New Langston is seeking proposals for the manufacture and installation of electronic\nsignage at bus stops throughout the city. New Langston plans to deploy new electronic signs that\ndisplay real-time arrival information to bus riders.\nBackground\nCurrently, New Langston’s bus stops are marked by simple metal signs displaying only the\nlocation of the stop and the lines that stop at the location. Cities around the world have begun to\nincorporate real-time arrival information into bus stop signage. Electronic signs are proving to be\nvery popular with riders, and studies show that the introduction of such signage has contributed\nto increased ridership in numerous cities.\nProject Description\nThe successful bidder will provide New Langston with up to 350 electronic signs. The signs\nmust be powered by solar energy and have a battery backup allowing them to operate at night,\non cloudy days, and in all weather conditions. The signs must have a reliability factor of at least\n99 percent. The signs must display at least three and no more than five lines of text, and be\nconnected to the Internet in order to provide real-time information to bus riders.\nPlease submit detailed bids outlining costs by 11:59 p.m. on May 31 to the City of\nNew Langston Regional Council at regionalcoimcil@cityofnewlangston.gov.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Request for Proposal\nPurpose\nI ’he City of New Langston is seeking proposals for the manufacture and installation of electronic\nsignage at bus stops throughout the city. New Langston plans to deploy new electronic signs that\ndisplay real-time arrival information to bus riders.\nBackground\nCurrently, New Langston’s bus stops are marked by simple metal signs displaying only the\nlocation of the stop and the lines that stop at the location. Cities around the world have begun to\nincorporate real-time arrival information into bus stop signage. Electronic signs are proving to be\nvery popular with riders, and studies show that the introduction of such signage has contributed\nto increased ridership in numerous cities.\nProject Description\nThe successful bidder will provide New Langston with up to 350 electronic signs. The signs\nmust be powered by solar energy and have a battery backup allowing them to operate at night,\non cloudy days, and in all weather conditions. The signs must have a reliability factor of at least\n99 percent. The signs must display at least three and no more than five lines of text, and be\nconnected to the Internet in order to provide real-time information to bus riders.\nPlease submit detailed bids outlining costs by 11:59 p.m. on May 31 to the City of\nNew Langston Regional Council at regionalcoimcil@cityofnewlangston.gov."}],"question":"What is indicated about the proposed signs?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về các biển báo được đề xuất?","options":["They would look exactly like the current bus stop signs in New Langston.","They would be manufactured by a company in New Langston.","They would inform riders about the arrival of the next bus.","They would need to be programmed only once a month."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"They would inform riders about the arrival of the next bus.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"sign","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/saɪn/","meaning":"đánh dấu; biểu tượng; chỉ định; gợi ý; dấu vết; để ý;"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"exactly","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ɪgˈzæktli/","meaning":"chính xác"},{"word":"current","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkɝː.ənt/","meaning":"dòng, luồng; hiện tại, hiện thời"}]},{"questionNum":"170","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following information.","passageText":"Request for Proposal\nPurpose\nI ’he City of New Langston is seeking proposals for the manufacture and installation of electronic\nsignage at bus stops throughout the city. New Langston plans to deploy new electronic signs that\ndisplay real-time arrival information to bus riders.\nBackground\nCurrently, New Langston’s bus stops are marked by simple metal signs displaying only the\nlocation of the stop and the lines that stop at the location. Cities around the world have begun to\nincorporate real-time arrival information into bus stop signage. Electronic signs are proving to be\nvery popular with riders, and studies show that the introduction of such signage has contributed\nto increased ridership in numerous cities.\nProject Description\nThe successful bidder will provide New Langston with up to 350 electronic signs. The signs\nmust be 