ry on May 8 will need to\nbe rescheduled, as 1 will be away for business that week. I have already prepared some\nexciting materials that I think library patrons will really enjoy, so I am still interested in\ngiving the lecture. It is currently scheduled to take place in the Stokes Room, which is\nthe perfect size for the crowd I hope to draw. It also has all the necessary technology\nfor my lecture, so I would still like to use that room.\nI apologize for the inconvenience of needing to reschedule, but I appreciate your help in\ngetting this event rebooked, as I am excited to present my topic.\nBest,\nJax Morrison"}],"question":"What event will need to be rescheduled?","bilingual":"Sự kiện nào sẽ cần được lên lịch lại?","options":["Idaho Literature","History of the Dictionary","Philosophical Nonfiction","Programming as a Skill"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"History of the Dictionary\".","vocabList":[{"word":"event","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪˈvent/","meaning":"sự kiện, sự việc"},{"word":"need","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/nid/","meaning":"yêu cầu; thiếu một mặt hàng không thể thiếu;"},{"word":"skill","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/skɪl/","meaning":"khả năng; năng khiếu; trình độ; chuyên môn; thủ công hoặc buôn bán"},{"word":"library","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlaɪbrɛˌri/","meaning":"nơi mà người ta có thể mượn sách"}]},{"questionNum":"190","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following e-mails and schedule.","passageText":"To: All Library Members\nFrom: Ada County Library\nDate: March 20\nSubject: Upcoming lectures\nAttachment: li Spring schedule\nDear Ada County Library members:\nOur long-a waited spring lecture schedule has been finalized. We expect an excellent\nturnout for these lectures. A highlight is a presentation on Arabic poetry translation,\npresented by a lecturer who will make her first visit to Ada County Library.\nAccess to library events is always free and is on a first-come, first-served basis, so please\nplan accordingly, especially for events in our two smallest venues, the Helms Room, which\nseats 35, and the A very Room, which has only 20 computer stations.\nAda County Library\nSpring Lecture Schedule\nFeatured Topic Guest Lecturer Date and Time Location\nIdaho Literature Yvonne Briggs April 10, 4-6 P.M. Helms Room\nArabic Poetry Translation Carole Elgin April 17, 3-5 P.M. Stokes Room\nEffective Resume Design Marc D''Angelo April 24,3-5 P.M. A very Room\nHistory of the Dictionary Jax Morrison May 8, 4-6 P.M. Stokes Room\nPhilosophical Nonfiction Darla Weiss May 15,3-5 P.M. Fredricks Room\nProgramming as a Skill Alissa Reynolds May 22, 4-6 P.M. A very Room\n222\n\n*E-mail*\nTo: Mary Carlton <mcarlton @aclacountylibrary.org>\nFrom:.fax Morrison <jmorrison @ book press.com>\nDate: April 3\nSubject: Scheduled library event\nDear Ms. Carlton,\nI am writing to let you know that my planned event at the library on May 8 will need to\nbe rescheduled, as 1 will be away for business that week. I have already prepared some\nexciting materials that I think library patrons will really enjoy, so I am still interested in\ngiving the lecture. It is currently scheduled to take place in the Stokes Room, which is\nthe perfect size for the crowd I hope to draw. It also has all the necessary technology\nfor my lecture, so I would still like to use that room.\nI apologize for the inconvenience of needing to reschedule, but I appreciate your help in\ngetting this event rebooked, as I am excited to present my topic.\nBest,\nJax Morrison","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: All Library Members\nFrom: Ada County Library\nDate: March 20\nSubject: Upcoming lectures\nAttachment: li Spring schedule\nDear Ada County Library members:\nOur long-a waited spring lecture schedule has been finalized. We expect an excellent\nturnout for these lectures. A highlight is a presentation on Arabic poetry translation,\npresented by a lecturer who will make her first visit to Ada County Library.\nAccess to library events is always free and is on a first-come, first-served basis, so please\nplan accordingly, especially for events in our two smallest venues, the Helms Room, which\nseats 35, and the A very Room, which has only 20 computer stations.\nAda County Library\nSpring Lecture Schedule\nFeatured Topic Guest Lecturer Date and Time Location\nIdaho Literature Yvonne Briggs April 10, 4-6 P.M. Helms Room\nArabic Poetry Translation Carole Elgin April 17, 3-5 P.M. Stokes Room\nEffective Resume Design Marc D''Angelo April 24,3-5 P.M. A very Room\nHistory of the Dictionary Jax Morrison May 8, 4-6 P.M. Stokes Room\nPhilosophical Nonfiction Darla Weiss May 15,3-5 P.M. Fredricks Room\nProgramming as a Skill Alissa Reynolds May 22, 4-6 P.M. A very Room\n222"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (schedule)","text":"*E-mail*\nTo: Mary Carlton <mcarlton @aclacountylibrary.org>\nFrom:.fax Morrison <jmorrison @ book press.com>\nDate: April 3\nSubject: Scheduled library event\nDear Ms. Carlton,\nI am writing to let you know that my planned event at the library on May 8 will need to\nbe rescheduled, as 1 will be away for business that week. I have already prepared some\nexciting materials that I think library patrons will really enjoy, so I am still interested in\ngiving the lecture. It is currently scheduled to take place in the Stokes Room, which is\nthe perfect size for the crowd I hope to draw. It also has all the necessary technology\nfor my lecture, so I would still like to use that room.\nI apologize for the inconvenience of needing to reschedule, but I appreciate your help in\ngetting this event rebooked, as I am excited to present my topic.\nBest,\nJax Morrison"}],"question":"What is indicated about Mr. Morrison?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về ông Morrison?","options":["He has not yet begun to prepare for his lecture.","He will visit the library on May 8.","He is not required to travel for his job.","He plans to utilize technology in his presentation."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"He plans to utilize technology in his presentation.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"prepare","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/priˈpɛr/","meaning":"chuẩn bị sẵn sàng; chuẩn bị sẵn sàng; để đưa vào"},{"word":"lecture","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlɛkʧər/","meaning":"đưa ra một bài diễn thuyết trước khán giả; khiển trách"},{"word":"visit","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈvɪzɪt/","meaning":"tạm trú ở đâu đó; ví dụ về việc dành thời gian"},{"word":"library","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlaɪbrɛˌri/","meaning":"nơi mà người ta có thể mượn sách"}]},{"questionNum":"191","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page and e-mails.","passageText":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality\n\nTo: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mails)","text":"To: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary"}],"question":"What are the volunteer river advocates responsible for?","bilingual":"Những người ủng hộ dòng sông tình nguyện chịu trách nhiệm gì?","options":["Monitoring changes in water quality","Promoting water conservation practices","Keeping the river banks clean","Leading educational tours of rivers and creeks"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Monitoring changes in water quality\".","vocabList":[{"word":"volunteer","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪr/","meaning":"một người cung cấp dịch vụ của mình theo ý chí tự do của riêng mình hoặc"},{"word":"responsible","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ri''spɔnsəbl/","meaning":"chịu trách nhiệm"},{"word":"change","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ʧeɪnʤ/","meaning":"thay thế; thay đổi; sự thay đổi; tiền xu; tiền nhận được"},{"word":"water","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈwɔtər/","meaning":"Nước"}]},{"questionNum":"192","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page and e-mails.","passageText":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality\n\nTo: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mails)","text":"To: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary"}],"question":"What is implied about the recipients of the first e-mail?","bilingual":"Điều gì ngụ ý về những người nhận e-mail đầu tiên?","options":["They will be sharing a vehicle.","They have helped to recruit volunteers.","They have committed to being available once a month.","They will enter records into a computer system."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"They have committed to being available once a month.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"recipient","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/rɪˈsɪpiənt/","meaning":"người chấp nhận; người lấy hoặc nhận"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"vehicle","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈviɪkəl/","meaning":"phương tiện vận tải (ô tô, xe buýt, v.v.); dụng cụ; có nghĩa;"}]},{"questionNum":"193","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page and e-mails.","passageText":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality\n\nTo: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mails)","text":"To: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary"}],"question":"What does the first e-mail indicate about the training?","bilingual":"Email đầu tiên cho biết gì về khóa đào tạo?","options":["It will be held at the Central River Foundation building.","It will take place in the morning.","It will last for one hour.","It will take place at multiple sites."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"It will take place in the morning.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"indicate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.də.keɪt/","meaning":"chỉ ra, chứng tỏ, biểu thị"},{"word":"training","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈtreɪ.nɪŋ/","meaning":"sự huấn luyện, sự đào tạo"},{"word":"central","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɛntrəl/","meaning":"chủ yếu; hiệu trưởng; lớn lao"}]},{"questionNum":"194","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page and e-mails.","passageText":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality\n\nTo: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mails)","text":"To: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary"}],"question":"Where will Ms. Lim most likely meet Ms. Connors?","bilingual":"Cô Lim sẽ gặp cô Connors ở đâu nhiều nhất?","options":["At Sutton Bridge","At Bradford Bend","At Alderwick Cove","At Tanner Park"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"At Alderwick Cove\".","vocabList":[{"word":"volunteer","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪr/","meaning":"một người cung cấp dịch vụ của mình theo ý chí tự do của riêng mình hoặc"},{"word":"ship","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ʃɪp/","meaning":"tàu lớn dùng để đi biển; phi cơ;"},{"word":"central","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɛntrəl/","meaning":"chủ yếu; hiệu trưởng; lớn lao"},{"word":"foundation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃən/","meaning":"căn cứ; nền tảng; công trình phụ; thành lập; tổ chức"}]},{"questionNum":"195","passageTitle":"Questions 191-195 refer to the following Web page and e-mails.","passageText":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality\n\nTo: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"http://www.crfoundation.org/volunteer Advocate ship\nRiver\nThe Central River Foundation coordinates water-monitoring operations at various\nsites along the Central River and its tributaries. The foundation would like to train\nindividuals in area communities to conduct periodic water-quality tests.\nIf interested in becoming a river advocate, contact us at www.crfoundation.org. Requirements:\nReliable transportation is essential; we work in relatively remote areas.\nAttention to detail and the ability to take precise measurements\nAvailability to conduct testing at least once every four weeks to detect any\nchanges in water quality"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mails)","text":"To: Janis Gutierrez, Mitch Gregory, Mary Connors, Ross Howard\nFrom: Clare Schroeder <cschroeder@crfoundation.org> Subject: Training\nDate: May 5\nA\nThank you for your interest in participating as a river advocate for the Central River\nFoundation.\nA training session has been scheduled at Clifford Park on Saturday, May 8, from\n9:00 A.M. to 12 noon. During the training you will practice using the sample kits and be\nintroduced to your mentors. You will leave with your first assignments and a certificate\nof completion. Then your mentor will accompany you on your first one-hour assignment.\nThis will prepare you to work independently afterwards.\nAlthough we will be training at Clifford Park, you will usually be working at other sites.\nPlease see your individual testing sites below.\nWater Testing Site Volunteer\nSutton Bridge Janis Gutierrez\nBradford Bend Mitch Gregory\nAlderwick Cove Mary Connors\nTanner Park Ross Howard\nI look forward to seeing you all on Saturday!\nClare Schroeder\n224\nv\n\nTo: Susan Lim\nFrom: Mary Connors\nDate: May 13\nSubject: Site visit\nHi Susan,\nI’m supposed to complete my first water testing on May 20. Are you available to meet me\nthere to help me do it correctly? I’m available any time between 3:00 P.M. and 6:00 P.M.\nI looked up the site online, and it looks like we will have to park about half a kilometer\naway from the river and then walk to the site. Ms. Schroeder mentioned that it will add\nabout 30 minutes to our trip.\nAlso, do you have an extra water-testing kit? It looks like mine is missing a few pieces.\nCan we use one of yours until I can get my supplies replaced?\nThanks,\nMary"}],"question":"In the second e-mail, what does Ms. Connors ask Ms. Lim to do?","bilingual":"Trong e-mail thứ hai, cô Connors yêu cầu cô Lim làm gì?","options":["Give her a ride","Contact Ms. Schroeder","Arrive 30 minutes early","Bring a water-testing kit"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Bring a water-testing kit\".","vocabList":[{"word":"second","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɛkənd/","meaning":"hỗ trợ một đề xuất hoặc tuyên bố; xác nhận; ĐẾN"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"contact","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑnˌtækt/","meaning":"thiết lập giao tiếp; để tạo kết nối; ĐẾN"},{"word":"arrive","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əraɪv/","meaning":"đến đích; quay trở lại ; quay trở lại; ĐẾN"}]},{"questionNum":"196","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and Web page.","passageText":"To: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@budaceramics.com> From: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nSubject: Solar power options\nDate: January 25\nDear Mr. Szasz:\nThank you for your recent e-mail requesting recommendations for solar power options for\nyour ceramics company. Before I make a recommendation for which company would best\nserve your needs, could you answer these questions?\n1. How flexible is your budget for solar panel purchase and installation?\n2. What is your time frame? The government plans to provide financial incentives toward\nthe cost of installing solar power that will take effect in about two years.\n3. What is the configuration of your property? If you have the space, you could choose to\ninstall solar panels in a parking area or on the ground. The first choice consists of\ncanopies over your parking lot, while the second choice is great for large, unused areas.\n4. What kind of roof do you have? A flat roof is not ideal. Neither is a roof that has a lot\nof equipment on it, as there is not enough room for large solar panels.\n5. Are you planning on expanding your business in the future?\n1 look forward to hearing back from you soon.\nAnouk Ayala\n\nTo: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nFrom: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@ budaceramics.com>\nSubject: RE: Solar power options\nDate: January 27\nDear Ms. Ayala:\nOur company headquarters is located outside of the capital city. The ceramics factory\noccupies approximately one-half of our property. To ensure sufficient cooling, much of the\nroof space is taken up by industrial-sized air-conditioning units and venting silos for our\novens. The rest of our property contains a size able parking lot, because there is no public\ntransportation in the area, and our 150 employees must drive to work.\nThe solar power business we choose should be well established. We have an inflexible\ndeadline for our current project, so 1 am willing to sacrifice money to get the panels\ninstalled as soon as possible. I hope these answers help you with your recommendation.\nKristof Szasz\n226\n\nhttp://www.solarinsider.com Based on a recent customer survey, these four solar power companies in the\ncapital city area are rated the most successful.\nCompany Specialty\nAKX Solar Rooftop\nSun365 All types\nBeranek Systems Parking areas\nComments\nVery low cost; a very stable company\nSuperior quality; very thorough; but\na bit slow\nFast turn around; but quite expensive\nPlutosolar Ground installation Cannot begin until March","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@budaceramics.com> From: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nSubject: Solar power options\nDate: January 25\nDear Mr. Szasz:\nThank you for your recent e-mail requesting recommendations for solar power options for\nyour ceramics company. Before I make a recommendation for which company would best\nserve your needs, could you answer these questions?\n1. How flexible is your budget for solar panel purchase and installation?\n2. What is your time frame? The government plans to provide financial incentives toward\nthe cost of installing solar power that will take effect in about two years.\n3. What is the configuration of your property? If you have the space, you could choose to\ninstall solar panels in a parking area or on the ground. The first choice consists of\ncanopies over your parking lot, while the second choice is great for large, unused areas.\n4. What kind of roof do you have? A flat roof is not ideal. Neither is a roof that has a lot\nof equipment on it, as there is not enough room for large solar panels.\n5. Are you planning on expanding your business in the future?\n1 look forward to hearing back from you soon.\nAnouk Ayala"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (Web page)","text":"To: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nFrom: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@ budaceramics.com>\nSubject: RE: Solar power options\nDate: January 27\nDear Ms. Ayala:\nOur company headquarters is located outside of the capital city. The ceramics factory\noccupies approximately one-half of our property. To ensure sufficient cooling, much of the\nroof space is taken up by industrial-sized air-conditioning units and venting silos for our\novens. The rest of our property contains a size able parking lot, because there is no public\ntransportation in the area, and our 150 employees must drive to work.\nThe solar power business we choose should be well established. We have an inflexible\ndeadline for our current project, so 1 am willing to sacrifice money to get the panels\ninstalled as soon as possible. I hope these answers help you with your recommendation.\nKristof Szasz\n226\n\nhttp://www.solarinsider.com Based on a recent customer survey, these four solar power companies in the\ncapital city area are rated the most successful.\nCompany Specialty\nAKX Solar Rooftop\nSun365 All types\nBeranek Systems Parking areas\nComments\nVery low cost; a very stable company\nSuperior quality; very thorough; but\na bit slow\nFast turn around; but quite expensive\nPlutosolar Ground installation Cannot begin until March"}],"question":"What most likely is Ms. Ayala’s job?","bilingual":"Công việc của cô Ayala rất có thể là gì?","options":["Technical consultant","Factory supervisor","Magazine writer","Maintenance worker"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Technical consultant\".","vocabList":[{"word":"technical","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈtek.nɪ.kəl/","meaning":"có tính kỹ thuật"},{"word":"consultant","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kənˈsʌl.tənt/","meaning":"tư vấn viên, cố vấn"},{"word":"factory","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfæk.tɚ.i/","meaning":"nhà máy, xí nghiệp"},{"word":"supervisor","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsupərˌvaɪzər/","meaning":"người giám sát; giám đốc; giám đốc"}]},{"questionNum":"197","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and Web page.","passageText":"To: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@budaceramics.com> From: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nSubject: Solar power options\nDate: January 25\nDear Mr. Szasz:\nThank you for your recent e-mail requesting recommendations for solar power options for\nyour ceramics company. Before I make a recommendation for which company would best\nserve your needs, could you answer these questions?\n1. How flexible is your budget for solar panel purchase and installation?\n2. What is your time frame? The government plans to provide financial incentives toward\nthe cost of installing solar power that will take effect in about two years.\n3. What is the configuration of your property? If you have the space, you could choose to\ninstall solar panels in a parking area or on the ground. The first choice consists of\ncanopies over your parking lot, while the second choice is great for large, unused areas.\n4. What kind of roof do you have? A flat roof is not ideal. Neither is a roof that has a lot\nof equipment on it, as there is not enough room for large solar panels.\n5. Are you planning on expanding your business in the future?\n1 look forward to hearing back from you soon.\nAnouk Ayala\n\nTo: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nFrom: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@ budaceramics.com>\nSubject: RE: Solar power options\nDate: January 27\nDear Ms. Ayala:\nOur company headquarters is located outside of the capital city. The ceramics factory\noccupies approximately one-half of our property. To ensure sufficient cooling, much of the\nroof space is taken up by industrial-sized air-conditioning units and venting silos for our\novens. The rest of our property contains a size able parking lot, because there is no public\ntransportation in the area, and our 150 employees must drive to work.\nThe solar power business we choose should be well established. We have an inflexible\ndeadline for our current project, so 1 am willing to sacrifice money to get the panels\ninstalled as soon as possible. I hope these answers help you with your recommendation.\nKristof Szasz\n226\n\nhttp://www.solarinsider.com Based on a recent customer survey, these four solar power companies in the\ncapital city area are rated the most successful.\nCompany Specialty\nAKX Solar Rooftop\nSun365 All types\nBeranek Systems Parking areas\nComments\nVery low cost; a very stable company\nSuperior quality; very thorough; but\na bit slow\nFast turn around; but quite expensive\nPlutosolar Ground installation Cannot begin until March","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@budaceramics.com> From: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nSubject: Solar power options\nDate: January 25\nDear Mr. Szasz:\nThank you for your recent e-mail requesting recommendations for solar power options for\nyour ceramics company. Before I make a recommendation for which company would best\nserve your needs, could you answer these questions?\n1. How flexible is your budget for solar panel purchase and installation?\n2. What is your time frame? The government plans to provide financial incentives toward\nthe cost of installing solar power that will take effect in about two years.\n3. What is the configuration of your property? If you have the space, you could choose to\ninstall solar panels in a parking area or on the ground. The first choice consists of\ncanopies over your parking lot, while the second choice is great for large, unused areas.\n4. What kind of roof do you have? A flat roof is not ideal. Neither is a roof that has a lot\nof equipment on it, as there is not enough room for large solar panels.\n5. Are you planning on expanding your business in the future?\n1 look forward to hearing back from you soon.\nAnouk Ayala"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (Web page)","text":"To: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nFrom: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@ budaceramics.com>\nSubject: RE: Solar power options\nDate: January 27\nDear Ms. Ayala:\nOur company headquarters is located outside of the capital city. The ceramics factory\noccupies approximately one-half of our property. To ensure sufficient cooling, much of the\nroof space is taken up by industrial-sized air-conditioning units and venting silos for our\novens. The rest of our property contains a size able parking lot, because there is no public\ntransportation in the area, and our 150 employees must drive to work.\nThe solar power business we choose should be well established. We have an inflexible\ndeadline for our current project, so 1 am willing to sacrifice money to get the panels\ninstalled as soon as possible. I hope these answers help you with your recommendation.\nKristof Szasz\n226\n\nhttp://www.solarinsider.com Based on a recent customer survey, these four solar power companies in the\ncapital city area are rated the most successful.\nCompany Specialty\nAKX Solar Rooftop\nSun365 All types\nBeranek Systems Parking areas\nComments\nVery low cost; a very stable company\nSuperior quality; very thorough; but\na bit slow\nFast turn around; but quite expensive\nPlutosolar Ground installation Cannot begin until March"}],"question":"What does Ms. Ayala indicate about solar power?","bilingual":"Cô Ayala nói gì về năng lượng mặt trời?","options":["Many government buildings are equipped with solar panels.","Solar businesses overseas are growing extremely fast.","Rooftop panels provide the most energy efficiency.","Delaying installation of solar panels for two years would lower costs."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Delaying installation of solar panels for two years would lower costs.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"indicate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈɪn.də.keɪt/","meaning":"chỉ ra, chứng tỏ, biểu thị"},{"word":"solar","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsoʊ.lɚ/","meaning":"hệ mặt trời"},{"word":"power","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈpauə(r)/","meaning":"khả năng; tài năng, năng lực"},{"word":"government","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈgəvərnmənt/","meaning":"cai trị một quốc gia hoặc khu vực; kiểm soát chính trị; thẩm quyền"}]},{"questionNum":"198","passageTitle":"Questions 196-200 refer to the following e-mails and Web page.","passageText":"To: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@budaceramics.com> From: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nSubject: Solar power options\nDate: January 25\nDear Mr. Szasz:\nThank you for your recent e-mail requesting recommendations for solar power options for\nyour ceramics company. Before I make a recommendation for which company would best\nserve your needs, could you answer these questions?\n1. How flexible is your budget for solar panel purchase and installation?\n2. What is your time frame? The government plans to provide financial incentives toward\nthe cost of installing solar power that will take effect in about two years.\n3. What is the configuration of your property? If you have the space, you could choose to\ninstall solar panels in a parking area or on the ground. The first choice consists of\ncanopies over your parking lot, while the second choice is great for large, unused areas.\n4. What kind of roof do you have? A flat roof is not ideal. Neither is a roof that has a lot\nof equipment on it, as there is not enough room for large solar panels.\n5. Are you planning on expanding your business in the future?\n1 look forward to hearing back from you soon.\nAnouk Ayala\n\nTo: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nFrom: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@ budaceramics.com>\nSubject: RE: Solar power options\nDate: January 27\nDear Ms. Ayala:\nOur company headquarters is located outside of the capital city. The ceramics factory\noccupies approximately one-half of our property. To ensure sufficient cooling, much of the\nroof space is taken up by industrial-sized air-conditioning units and venting silos for our\novens. The rest of our property contains a size able parking lot, because there is no public\ntransportation in the area, and our 150 employees must drive to work.\nThe solar power business we choose should be well established. We have an inflexible\ndeadline for our current project, so 1 am willing to sacrifice money to get the panels\ninstalled as soon as possible. I hope these answers help you with your recommendation.\nKristof Szasz\n226\n\nhttp://www.solarinsider.com Based on a recent customer survey, these four solar power companies in the\ncapital city area are rated the most successful.\nCompany Specialty\nAKX Solar Rooftop\nSun365 All types\nBeranek Systems Parking areas\nComments\nVery low cost; a very stable company\nSuperior quality; very thorough; but\na bit slow\nFast turn around; but quite expensive\nPlutosolar Ground installation Cannot begin until March","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (e-mails)","text":"To: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@budaceramics.com> From: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nSubject: Solar power options\nDate: January 25\nDear Mr. Szasz:\nThank you for your recent e-mail requesting recommendations for solar power options for\nyour ceramics company. Before I make a recommendation for which company would best\nserve your needs, could you answer these questions?\n1. How flexible is your budget for solar panel purchase and installation?\n2. What is your time frame? The government plans to provide financial incentives toward\nthe cost of installing solar power that will take effect in about two years.\n3. What is the configuration of your property? If you have the space, you could choose to\ninstall solar panels in a parking area or on the ground. The first choice consists of\ncanopies over your parking lot, while the second choice is great for large, unused areas.\n4. What kind of roof do you have? A flat roof is not ideal. Neither is a roof that has a lot\nof equipment on it, as there is not enough room for large solar panels.\n5. Are you planning on expanding your business in the future?\n1 look forward to hearing back from you soon.\nAnouk Ayala"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (Web page)","text":"To: Anouk Ayala <a ayala @ayala.net>\nFrom: Kristof Szasz <kszasz@ budaceramics.com>\nSubject: RE: Solar power options\nDate: January 27\nDear Ms. Ayala:\nOur company headquarters is located outside of the capital city. The ceramics factory\noccupies approximately one-half of our property. To ensure sufficient cooling, much of the\nroof space is taken up by industrial-sized air-conditioning units and venting silos for our\novens. The rest of our property contains a size able parking lot, because there is no public\ntransportation in the area, and our 150 employees must drive to work.\nThe solar power business we choose should be well established. We have an inflexible\ndeadline for our current project, so 1 am willing to sacrifice money to get the panels\ninstalled as soon as possible. I hope these answers help you with your recommendation.\nKristof Szasz\n226\n\nhttp://www.solarinsider.com Based on a recent customer survey, these four solar power companies in the\ncapital city area are rated the most successful.\nCompany Specialty\nAKX Solar Rooftop\nSun365 All types\nBeranek Systems Parking areas\nComments\nVery low cost; a very stable company\nSuperior quality; very thorough; but\na bit slow\nFast turn around; but quite expensive\nPlutosolar Ground installation Cannot begin until March"}],"question":"Which of Ms. Ayala’s questions does Mr. Szasz fail to answer?","bilingual":"Ông Szasz không trả lời được câu hỏi nào của cô Ayala?","options":["Number 1","Number 3","Number 4","Number 5 Stop! This is 