 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtætʃ/","meaning":"gán thêm, kèm thêm"},{"word":"description","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈskrɪp.ʃən/","meaning":"bản mô tả, sự mô tả"},{"word":"financial","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/faɪˈnæn.ʃəl/","meaning":"/fəˈnæn.ʃəl/"},{"word":"report","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ri''pɔ:t/","meaning":"bản báo cáo, bản tường thuật; biên bản"}]},{"questionNum":"155","passageTitle":"Questions 153-155 refer to the following e-mail.","passageText":"To: Mary Lim <mlim4 l 2@ mailhouz.com>\nFrom: George Siskos <gsiskos@crehcorp.com> Date: September 24\nSubject: Referral from Joe Argento\nAttachment: l|Information\nHello Ms. Lim,\nI am George Siskos, Recruiting Manager at Crehcorp Ltd. We are currently looking to hire\nan accounting clerk, and Joe Argento recommended you. From what Joe told me, your\nbackground makes you a good fit for the role (posting attached). If you are interested in\nlearning more about Crehcorp and the position, I will be happy to provide further\ninformation. Let me know when you are available to talk, and I will give you a call.\nI look forward to hearing back from you!\nGeorge Siskos","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"To: Mary Lim <mlim4 l 2@ mailhouz.com>\nFrom: George Siskos <gsiskos@crehcorp.com> Date: September 24\nSubject: Referral from Joe Argento\nAttachment: l|Information\nHello Ms. Lim,\nI am George Siskos, Recruiting Manager at Crehcorp Ltd. We are currently looking to hire\nan accounting clerk, and Joe Argento recommended you. From what Joe told me, your\nbackground makes you a good fit for the role (posting attached). If you are interested in\nlearning more about Crehcorp and the position, I will be happy to provide further\ninformation. Let me know when you are available to talk, and I will give you a call.\nI look forward to hearing back from you!\nGeorge Siskos"}],"question":"What is Ms. Lim asked to do?","bilingual":"Cô Lim được yêu cầu làm gì?","options":["Visit Crehcorp’s Web site","Contact Mr. Argento","Mail a resume","Respond to the e-mail"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Respond to the e-mail\".","vocabList":[{"word":"visit","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈvɪzɪt/","meaning":"tạm trú ở đâu đó; ví dụ về việc dành thời gian"},{"word":"site","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/saɪt/","meaning":"địa điểm; vị trí; khu vực"},{"word":"contact","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑnˌtækt/","meaning":"thiết lập giao tiếp; để tạo kết nối; ĐẾN"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"}]},{"questionNum":"156","passageTitle":"Questions 156-157 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Francis Chang [4:32 PM.]\nHi, Connie. I''m putting together the schedule for the summer. Will you still be able\nto teach the Friday afternoon workshops twice a month? We could take turns, and\nI would take the other two Fridays.\nConnie Kehoe [4:39 P.M.]\nThanks for getting in touch, Francis. I’d still like to be involved, but I’ll be busier\nthis summer. I’m coordinating a volleyball league.\nFrancis Chang [4:40 P.M.]\nWell, OK. I guess I could cover the workshops three Fridays a month.\nConnie Kehoe [4:42 P.M.]\nThat would be perfect. That will give me enough time for my other obligation.\nFrancis Chang [4:43 P.M.]\nThe other thing is, this summer we want to focus on painting with water colors\nrather than basic drawing.\nConnie Kehoe [4:44 P.M.]\nI''ll look over some old lesson plans, but that should be fine. Also, let’s get together\nsoon to work on a budget for the class materials.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Francis Chang [4:32 PM.]\nHi, Connie. I''m putting together the schedule for the summer. Will you still be able\nto teach the Friday afternoon workshops twice a month? We could take turns, and\nI would take the other two Fridays.\nConnie Kehoe [4:39 P.M.]\nThanks for getting in touch, Francis. I’d still like to be involved, but I’ll be busier\nthis summer. I’m coordinating a volleyball league.\nFrancis Chang [4:40 P.M.]\nWell, OK. I guess I could cover the workshops three Fridays a month.\nConnie Kehoe [4:42 P.M.]\nThat would be perfect. That will give me enough time for my other obligation.\nFrancis Chang [4:43 P.M.]\nThe other thing is, this summer we want to focus on painting with water colors\nrather than basic drawing.\nConnie Kehoe [4:44 P.M.]\nI''ll look over some old lesson plans, but that should be fine. Also, let’s get together\nsoon to work on a budget for the class materials."}],"question":"At 4:42 P.M., what does Ms. Kehoe mean when she writes, “That would be perfect”?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 4:42 chiều, cô Kehoe có ý gì khi viết “Điều đó sẽ hoàn hảo”?","options":["She is looking forward to summer.","She thinks a workshop will be popular.","She is happy with a proposed schedule.","She is glad that Mr. Chang will be hired."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She is happy with a proposed schedule.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"perfect","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpərˌfɪkt/","meaning":"tinh chỉnh; để cải thiện; để hoàn thành; làm cho không có lỗi"},{"word":"forward","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfɔːr.wɚd/","meaning":"về phía trước, tiến lên"}]},{"questionNum":"157","passageTitle":"Questions 156-157 refer to the following text-message chain.","passageText":"Francis Chang [4:32 PM.]\nHi, Connie. I''m putting together the schedule for the summer. Will you still be able\nto teach the Friday afternoon workshops twice a month? We could take turns, and\nI would take the other two Fridays.\nConnie Kehoe [4:39 P.M.]\nThanks for getting in touch, Francis. I’d still like to be involved, but I’ll be busier\nthis summer. I’m coordinating a volleyball league.\nFrancis Chang [4:40 P.M.]\nWell, OK. I guess I could cover the workshops three Fridays a month.\nConnie Kehoe [4:42 P.M.]\nThat would be perfect. That will give me enough time for my other obligation.\nFrancis Chang [4:43 P.M.]\nThe other thing is, this summer we want to focus on painting with water colors\nrather than basic drawing.\nConnie Kehoe [4:44 P.M.]\nI''ll look over some old lesson plans, but that should be fine. Also, let’s get together\nsoon to work on a budget for the class materials.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Francis Chang [4:32 PM.]\nHi, Connie. I''m putting together the schedule for the summer. Will you still be able\nto teach the Friday afternoon workshops twice a month? We could take turns, and\nI would take the other two Fridays.\nConnie Kehoe [4:39 P.M.]\nThanks for getting in touch, Francis. I’d still like to be involved, but I’ll be busier\nthis summer. I’m coordinating a volleyball league.\nFrancis Chang [4:40 P.M.]\nWell, OK. I guess I could cover the workshops three Fridays a month.\nConnie Kehoe [4:42 P.M.]\nThat would be perfect. That will give me enough time for my other obligation.\nFrancis Chang [4:43 P.M.]\nThe other thing is, this summer we want to focus on painting with water colors\nrather than basic drawing.\nConnie Kehoe [4:44 P.M.]\nI''ll look over some old lesson plans, but that should be fine. Also, let’s get together\nsoon to work on a budget for the class materials."}],"question":"What type of workshop is being planned?","bilingual":"Loại hội thảo nào đang được lên kế hoạch?","options":["Art","Personal finance","Travel","Customer service"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Art\".","vocabList":[{"word":"workshop","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈwɝːk.ʃɑːp/","meaning":"hội thảo"},{"word":"personal","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pə:snl/","meaning":"cá nhân, tư, riêng"},{"word":"finance","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfaɪ.næns/","meaning":"tài chính; hỗ trợ tài chính"},{"word":"travel","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈtrævəl/","meaning":"sự chuyển động; hành trình"}]},{"questionNum":"158","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"May 15\nMr. Roger Lang, Executive Director\nParker Solutions Foundation\n40 Northside Drive, Suite 500\nPortland, OR 97215\nDear Mr. Lang:\nThe purpose of this letter is to invite you, on behalf of the board of directors, to be\nthe keynote speaker at the International Green Solutions Research Institute\n(IGSRI) Conference. ------- [1] -------. It will be held at the Fairview Conference Center in\nSaint Louis, Missouri, from December 3 to 5. You were recommended by a number\nof my colleagues. ------- [2] -------.\nProfessor Suzanne Benedetto will deliver the opening speech on the morning of\nDecember 3. A draft program will be sent to you in two weeks to give you an idea\nof the topics that will be highlighted at the conference.\nWe expect attendance this year to be the highest ever, around 2,500 delegates and\n40 speakers. ------- [3] -------. This includes a large contingent from our newest chapter in\nGeneva. [4]-.\nI hope to contact you in a week to follow up and answer any questions you may\nhave.\nYours sincerely,\nBr Ccm/ Morgcvn/\nBrian Morgan","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"May 15\nMr. Roger Lang, Executive Director\nParker Solutions Foundation\n40 Northside Drive, Suite 500\nPortland, OR 97215\nDear Mr. Lang:\nThe purpose of this letter is to invite you, on behalf of the board of directors, to be\nthe keynote speaker at the International Green Solutions Research Institute\n(IGSRI) Conference. ------- [1] -------. It will be held at the Fairview Conference Center in\nSaint Louis, Missouri, from December 3 to 5. You were recommended by a number\nof my colleagues. ------- [2] -------.\nProfessor Suzanne Benedetto will deliver the opening speech on the morning of\nDecember 3. A draft program will be sent to you in two weeks to give you an idea\nof the topics that will be highlighted at the conference.\nWe expect attendance this year to be the highest ever, around 2,500 delegates and\n40 speakers. ------- [3] -------. This includes a large contingent from our newest chapter in\nGeneva. [4]-.\nI hope to contact you in a week to follow up and answer any questions you may\nhave.\nYours sincerely,\nBr Ccm/ Morgcvn/\nBrian Morgan"}],"question":"Why was the letter to Mr. Lang written?","bilingual":"Tại sao lại viết thư cho ông Lang?","options":["To request a recommendation letter from him","To ask him to evaluate some conference topics","To congratulate him for receiving an award","To ask him to participate in a conference"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To ask him to participate in a conference\".","vocabList":[{"word":"letter","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlɛtər/","meaning":"ký tự là một phần của bảng chữ cái; bằng văn bản"},{"word":"request","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈkwest/","meaning":"yêu cầu"},{"word":"recommendation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/¸rekəmen´deiʃən/","meaning":"sự giới thiệu, sự tiến cử"},{"word":"evaluate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪˈvæl.ju.eɪt/","meaning":"ước lượng, đánh giá"}]},{"questionNum":"159","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"May 15\nMr. Roger Lang, Executive Director\nParker Solutions Foundation\n40 Northside Drive, Suite 500\nPortland, OR 97215\nDear Mr. Lang:\nThe purpose of this letter is to invite you, on behalf of the board of directors, to be\nthe keynote speaker at the International Green Solutions Research Institute\n(IGSRI) Conference. ------- [1] -------. It will be held at the Fairview Conference Center in\nSaint Louis, Missouri, from December 3 to 5. You were recommended by a number\nof my colleagues. ------- [2] -------.\nProfessor Suzanne Benedetto will deliver the opening speech on the morning of\nDecember 3. A draft program will be sent to you in two weeks to give you an idea\nof the topics that will be highlighted at the conference.\nWe expect attendance this year to be the highest ever, around 2,500 delegates and\n40 speakers. ------- [3] -------. This includes a large contingent from our newest chapter in\nGeneva. [4]-.\nI hope to contact you in a week to follow up and answer any questions you may\nhave.\nYours sincerely,\nBr Ccm/ Morgcvn/\nBrian Morgan","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"May 15\nMr. Roger Lang, Executive Director\nParker Solutions Foundation\n40 Northside Drive, Suite 500\nPortland, OR 97215\nDear Mr. Lang:\nThe purpose of this letter is to invite you, on behalf of the board of directors, to be\nthe keynote speaker at the International Green Solutions Research Institute\n(IGSRI) Conference. ------- [1] -------. It will be held at the Fairview Conference Center in\nSaint Louis, Missouri, from December 3 to 5. You were recommended by a number\nof my colleagues. ------- [2] -------.\nProfessor Suzanne Benedetto will deliver the opening speech on the morning of\nDecember 3. A draft program will be sent to you in two weeks to give you an idea\nof the topics that will be highlighted at the conference.\nWe expect attendance this year to be the highest ever, around 2,500 delegates and\n40 speakers. ------- [3] -------. This includes a large contingent from our newest chapter in\nGeneva. [4]-.\nI hope to contact you in a week to follow up and answer any questions you may\nhave.\nYours sincerely,\nBr Ccm/ Morgcvn/\nBrian Morgan"}],"question":"In what city will the IGSRI Conference be held?","bilingual":"Hội nghị IGSRI sẽ được tổ chức ở thành phố nào?","options":["Portland","Fairview","Saint Louis","Geneva 242"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Saint Louis\".","vocabList":[{"word":"city","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪti/","meaning":"thị trấn; khu đô thị lớn"},{"word":"conference","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkɑnfərəns/","meaning":"cuộc họp; hội thảo; quy ước"},{"word":"portland","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɔrtlənd/","meaning":"Portland"},{"word":"fairview","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfɛrvˌju/","meaning":"Fairview"}]},{"questionNum":"160","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"May 15\nMr. Roger Lang, Executive Director\nParker Solutions Foundation\n40 Northside Drive, Suite 500\nPortland, OR 97215\nDear Mr. Lang:\nThe purpose of this letter is to invite you, on behalf of the board of directors, to be\nthe keynote speaker at the International Green Solutions Research Institute\n(IGSRI) Conference. ------- [1] -------. It will be held at the Fairview Conference Center in\nSaint Louis, Missouri, from December 3 to 5. You were recommended by a number\nof my colleagues. ------- [2] -------.\nProfessor Suzanne Benedetto will deliver the opening speech on the morning of\nDecember 3. A draft program will be sent to you in two weeks to give you an idea\nof the topics that will be highlighted at the conference.\nWe expect attendance this year to be the highest ever, around 2,500 delegates and\n40 speakers. ------- [3] -------. This includes a large contingent from our newest chapter in\nGeneva. [4]-.\nI hope to contact you in a week to follow up and answer any questions you may\nhave.\nYours sincerely,\nBr Ccm/ Morgcvn/\nBrian Morgan","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"May 15\nMr. Roger Lang, Executive Director\nParker Solutions Foundation\n40 Northside Drive, Suite 500\nPortland, OR 97215\nDear Mr. Lang:\nThe purpose of this letter is to invite you, on behalf of the board of directors, to be\nthe keynote speaker at the International Green Solutions Research Institute\n(IGSRI) Conference. ------- [1] -------. It will be held at the Fairview Conference Center in\nSaint Louis, Missouri, from December 3 to 5. You were recommended by a number\nof my colleagues. ------- [2] -------.\nProfessor Suzanne Benedetto will deliver the opening speech on the morning of\nDecember 3. A draft program will be sent to you in two weeks to give you an idea\nof the topics that will be highlighted at the conference.\nWe expect attendance this year to be the highest ever, around 2,500 delegates and\n40 speakers. ------- [3] -------. This includes a large contingent from our newest chapter in\nGeneva. [4]-.\nI hope to contact you in a week to follow up and answer any questions you may\nhave.\nYours sincerely,\nBr Ccm/ Morgcvn/\nBrian Morgan"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3] and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “They spoke highly of your expertise.”","bilingual":"Câu sau đây thuộc về vị trí nào trong số các vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4]? “Họ đánh giá cao chuyên môn của bạn.”","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"[2]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"highly","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈhaɪ.li/","meaning":"rất, lắm, tốt"},{"word":"your","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/jʊr/","meaning":"của bạn"}]},{"questionNum":"161","passageTitle":"Questions 161-163 refer to the following Web page.","passageText":"www.sergeyparksandrec.gov/survey Welcome! A.\nYou have been directed to this survey through a page on the Sergey Parks and\nRecreation Department’s Web site, from one of Ecology Alive’s most recent online\nnewsletters, or from a friend’s social media page. Regardless of how you got here,\nwe appreciate your taking the time to complete it.\nThis survey aims to help local wildlife organizations find practical approaches to\nattracting a dedicated and reliable volunteer base. The survey takes about 15 minutes\nto complete, and your participation is completely optional. If you do not wish to\nanswer a particular question, you can move on to the next one.\nIf you have any questions regarding how this survey will be used, please contact\nStefan McHann at stefan_mchann@sergeyparksandrec.gov.\nSurvey #4123\nName: Kenshawn Odeyemi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"www.sergeyparksandrec.gov/survey Welcome! A.\nYou have been directed to this survey through a page on the Sergey Parks and\nRecreation Department’s Web site, from one of Ecology Alive’s most recent online\nnewsletters, or from a friend’s social media page. Regardless of how you got here,\nwe appreciate your taking the time to complete it.\nThis survey aims to help local wildlife organizations find practical approaches to\nattracting a dedicated and reliable volunteer base. The survey takes about 15 minutes\nto complete, and your participation is completely optional. If you do not wish to\nanswer a particular question, you can move on to the next one.\nIf you have any questions regarding how this survey will be used, please contact\nStefan McHann at stefan_mchann@sergeyparksandrec.gov.\nSurvey #4123\nName: Kenshawn Odeyemi"}],"question":"What is indicated about the survey?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra trong cuộc khảo sát?","options":["It was recently modified.","It can be accessed from multiple online sources.","It requires an hour to complete.","It is being sent only to university students."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"It can be accessed from multiple online sources.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"survey","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsərˌveɪ/","meaning":"ôn tập; Tổng quan; nghiên cứu thống kê"},{"word":"recently","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈrisəntli/","meaning":"gần đây"},{"word":"source","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/sɔrs/","meaning":"nguồn gốc; điểm bắt đầu"},{"word":"require","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ri''kwaiə(r)/","meaning":"đòi hỏi, yêu cầu; quy định"}]},{"questionNum":"162","passageTitle":"Questions 161-163 refer to the following Web page.","passageText":"www.sergeyparksandrec.gov/survey Welcome! A.\nYou have been directed to this survey through a page on the Sergey Parks and\nRecreation Department’s Web site, from one of Ecology Alive’s most recent online\nnewsletters, or from a friend’s social media page. Regardless of how you got here,\nwe appreciate your taking the time to complete it.\nThis survey aims to help local wildlife organizations find practical approaches to\nattracting a dedicated and reliable volunteer base. The survey takes about 15 minutes\nto complete, and your participation is completely optional. If you do not wish to\nanswer a particular question, you can move on to the next one.\nIf you have any questions regarding how this survey will be used, please contact\nStefan McHann at stefan_mchann@sergeyparksandrec.gov.\nSurvey #4123\nName: Kenshawn Odeyemi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"www.sergeyparksandrec.gov/survey Welcome! A.\nYou have been directed to this survey through a page on the Sergey Parks and\nRecreation Department’s Web site, from one of Ecology Alive’s most recent online\nnewsletters, or from a friend’s social media page. Regardless of how you got here,\nwe appreciate your taking the time to complete it.\nThis survey aims to help local wildlife organizations find practical approaches to\nattracting a dedicated and reliable volunteer base. The survey takes about 15 minutes\nto complete, and your participation is completely optional. If you do not wish to\nanswer a particular question, you can move on to the next one.\nIf you have any questions regarding how this survey will be used, please contact\nStefan McHann at stefan_mchann@sergeyparksandrec.gov.\nSurvey #4123\nName: Kenshawn Odeyemi"}],"question":"What is the purpose of the survey?","bilingual":"Mục đích của cuộc khảo sát là gì?","options":["To find ways to recruit volunteers","To evaluate an organization''s strengths","To assess an area’s wildlife populations","To determine important leadership tra its"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"To find ways to recruit volunteers\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"survey","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsərˌveɪ/","meaning":"ôn tập; Tổng quan; nghiên cứu thống kê"},{"word":"recruit","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ri''kru:t/","meaning":"tuyển, chiêu mộ (lính mới); tìm thêm"},{"word":"volunteers","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪrz/","meaning":"Tình nguyện viên"}]},{"questionNum":"163","passageTitle":"Questions 161-163 refer to the following Web page.","passageText":"www.sergeyparksandrec.gov/survey Welcome! A.\nYou have been directed to this survey through a page on the Sergey Parks and\nRecreation Department’s Web site, from one of Ecology Alive’s most recent online\nnewsletters, or from a friend’s social media page. Regardless of how you got here,\nwe appreciate your taking the time to complete it.\nThis survey aims to help local wildlife organizations find practical approaches to\nattracting a dedicated and reliable volunteer base. The survey takes about 15 minutes\nto complete, and your participation is completely optional. If you do not wish to\nanswer a particular question, you can move on to the next one.\nIf you have any questions regarding how this survey will be used, please contact\nStefan McHann at stefan_mchann@sergeyparksandrec.gov.\nSurvey #4123\nName: Kenshawn Odeyemi","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"www.sergeyparksandrec.gov/survey Welcome! A.\nYou have been directed to this survey through a page on the Sergey Parks and\nRecreation Department’s Web site, from one of Ecology Alive’s most recent online\nnewsletters, or from a friend’s social media page. Regardless of how you got here,\nwe appreciate your taking the time to complete it.\nThis survey aims to help local wildlife organizations find practical approaches to\nattracting a dedicated and reliable volunteer base. The survey takes about 15 minutes\nto complete, and your participation is completely optional. If you do not wish to\nanswer a particular question, you can move on to the next one.\nIf you have any questions regarding how this survey will be used, please contact\nStefan McHann at stefan_mchann@sergeyparksandrec.gov.\nSurvey #4123\nName: Kenshawn Odeyemi"}],"question":"What is suggested about the survey respondents?","bilingual":"Người trả lời khảo sát được đề xuất gì?","options":["They can skip some of the questions.","They must subscribe to Ecology Alive.","They will be paid for their participation.","They will receive an additional survey from Mr. McHann."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"They can skip some of the questions.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"survey","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsərˌveɪ/","meaning":"ôn tập; Tổng quan; nghiên cứu thống kê"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"subscribe","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səbˈskraɪb/","meaning":"đăng ký"},{"word":"alive","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈlaɪv/","meaning":"tích cực; chú ý"}]},{"questionNum":"164","passageTitle":"Questions 164-167 refer to the following notice.","passageText":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing."}],"question":"What is the purpose of the notice?","bilingual":"Mục đích của thông báo là gì?","options":["To ask employees to submit information","To encourage greater use of the facilities","To discuss renovations to a building","To announce security system changes"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"To announce security system changes\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"notice","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''nəƱtis/","meaning":"thông tri, yết thị, thông báo"},{"word":"employee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɔɪi/","meaning":"công nhân; người làm việc cho một công ty hoặc một"},{"word":"submit","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səbˈmɪt/","meaning":"xác nhận, gửi đi"}]},{"questionNum":"165","passageTitle":"Questions 164-167 refer to the following notice.","passageText":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing."}],"question":"The word “points” in paragraph 1, line 6, is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"Từ “điểm” trong đoạn 1, dòng 6, gần nghĩa nhất với","options":["purposes","details","places","moments"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"places\".","vocabList":[{"word":"point","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pɔint/","meaning":"điểm"},{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"purposes","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈpərpəsɪz/","meaning":"mục đích"},{"word":"details","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈditeɪlz/","meaning":"chi tiết"}]},{"questionNum":"166","passageTitle":"Questions 164-167 refer to the following notice.","passageText":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing."}],"question":"What is a stated advantage of the new ID badges?","bilingual":"Ưu điểm đã nêu của huy hiệu ID mới là gì?","options":["They fit conveniently into a pocket.","They allow access to additional areas of a building.","They are more durable than the older ID cards.","They can track an employee’s location on-site. 244"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"They can track an employee’s location on-site. 244\".","vocabList":[{"word":"advantage","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ədˈvæn.t̬ɪdʒ/","meaning":"lợi thế"},{"word":"badge","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/bæʤ/","meaning":"nhãn; dấu hiệu; thẻ nhận dạng"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"conveniently","pos":"Trạng từ (Adverb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kənˈviː.ni.ənt.li/","meaning":"thuận tiện, tiện lợi"}]},{"questionNum":"167","passageTitle":"Questions 164-167 refer to the following notice.","passageText":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"r''/ ’\nDecember 1\nAttention, All Employees:\nBeginning on January 1, Barkley-Stephens Corporation (BSC) will transition to\na security system that uses integrated ID badges. Until now, BSC employees have\nused traditional identification cards that security personnel checked at entrances\nto the building. They simply compared the badge photograph with the employee’s\nappearance. The new system will be more technologically advanced, integrating\nID badge information with various access points around our facility.\nIntegrated ID badges allow employees entry only to areas of the building that are\npermitted to them. Moreover, the badges create an electronic record of who has\nentered which areas of the building and when. In the case of temporary employees,\nbadges will be disabled when their tenure ends.\nNew photographs of all staff will be taken in mid-December, when everyone will be\nasked to fill out a brief form to complete badge processing."}],"question":"According to the notice, what feature of the current IDs will be updated?","bilingual":"Theo thông báo, tính năng nào của ID hiện tại sẽ được cập nhật?","options":["The photo","The company logo","The shape","The employee’s job title"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"The photo\".","vocabList":[{"word":"notice","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''nəƱtis/","meaning":"thông tri, yết thị, thông báo"},{"word":"feature","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfiː.tʃɚ/","meaning":"nét, đặc điểm"},{"word":"current","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkɝː.ənt/","meaning":"dòng, luồng; hiện tại, hiện thời"},{"word":"photo","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈfoʊˌtoʊ/","meaning":"hình ảnh; ảnh chụp nhanh"}]},{"questionNum":"168","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following online chat discussion.","passageText":"Franklin Smith (7:51 A.M.)\nGood morning, Josephine and Carl. Is either one of you at the office yet? My train is\nrunning late and I want to make sure everything is set up for our 8:30 A.M. workshop.\nJosephine Mallian (7:56 A.M.)\nI''m walking in now. What can I do to help, Franklin?\nCarl Domingo (7:57 A.M.)\nI''ll be there in about ten minutes. Are you talking about the workshop in the Aster\nRoom? Because there is another workshop taking place in Obeli Hall too.\nFranklin Smith (7:59 A.M.)\nYes, the one in the Aster Room ------- the Savvy Steel sales workshop. I would appreciate it\nif you would rearrange the seats into a circle, turn on the projector, and run through\nthe presentation slides I sent last night, just to make sure that everything, including\nthe audio, is working.\nCarl Domingo (8:02 A.M.)\nGot it. I actually set the chairs up last night.\nJosephine Mallian (8:04 A.M.)\nThanks, Carl. Would you mind printing out fifteen copies of the agenda while I take\ncare of the rest?\nCarl Domingo (8:05 A.M.)\nSure.I''ll get it done as soon as possible.\nFranklin Smith (8:07 A.M.)\nThank you both. My train is arriving now. I think I''ll make it in time.\nJosephine Mallian (8:08 A.M.)\nNo problem, Franklin. We will also make sure there is plenty of coffee for you!\n4 4","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Franklin Smith (7:51 A.M.)\nGood morning, Josephine and Carl. Is either one of you at the office yet? My train is\nrunning late and I want to make sure everything is set up for our 8:30 A.M. workshop.\nJosephine Mallian (7:56 A.M.)\nI''m walking in now. What can I do to help, Franklin?\nCarl Domingo (7:57 A.M.)\nI''ll be there in about ten minutes. Are you talking about the workshop in the Aster\nRoom? Because there is another workshop taking place in Obeli Hall too.\nFranklin Smith (7:59 A.M.)\nYes, the one in the Aster Room ------- the Savvy Steel sales workshop. I would appreciate it\nif you would rearrange the seats into a circle, turn on the projector, and run through\nthe presentation slides I sent last night, just to make sure that everything, including\nthe audio, is working.\nCarl Domingo (8:02 A.M.)\nGot it. I actually set the chairs up last night.\nJosephine Mallian (8:04 A.M.)\nThanks, Carl. Would you mind printing out fifteen copies of the agenda while I take\ncare of the rest?\nCarl Domingo (8:05 A.M.)\nSure.I''ll get it done as soon as possible.\nFranklin Smith (8:07 A.M.)\nThank you both. My train is arriving now. I think I''ll make it in time.\nJosephine Mallian (8:08 A.M.)\nNo problem, Franklin. We will also make sure there is plenty of coffee for you!\n4 4"}],"question":"Why did Mr. Smith send the first message?","bilingual":"Tại sao ông Smith lại gửi tin nhắn đầu tiên?","options":["To extend an invitation","To request some help","To apologize for a mistake","To confirm a travel reservation"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To request some help\".","vocabList":[{"word":"message","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmɛsɪʤ/","meaning":"giao tiếp; thông tin; thông báo; ghi chú;"},{"word":"extend","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈstend/","meaning":"duỗi thẳng, nới rộng, gia hạn"},{"word":"invitation","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪnvɪˈteɪʃən/","meaning":"yêu cầu sự hiện diện của một người; triệu tập; gọi"},{"word":"request","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/rɪˈkwest/","meaning":"yêu cầu"}]},{"questionNum":"169","passageTitle":"Questions 168-171 refer to the following online chat discussion.","passageText":"Franklin Smith (7:51 A.M.)\nGood morning, Josephine and Carl. Is either one of you at the office yet? My train is\nrunning late and I want to make sure everything is set up for our 8:30 A.M. workshop.\nJosephine Mallian (7:56 A.M.)\nI''m walking in now. What can I do to help, Franklin?\nCarl Domingo (7:57 A.M.)\nI''ll be there in about ten minutes. Are you talking about the workshop in the Aster\nRoom? Because there is another workshop taking place in Obeli Hall too.\nFranklin Smith (7:59 A.M.)\nYes, the one in the Aster Room ------- the Savvy Steel sales workshop. I would appreciate it\nif you would rearrange the seats into a circle, turn on the projector, and run through\nthe presentation slides I sent last night, just to make sure that everything, including\nthe audio, is working.\nCarl Domingo (8:02 A.M.)\nGot it. I actually set the chairs up last night.\nJosephine Mallian (8:04 A.M.)\nThanks, Carl. Would you mind printing out fifteen copies of the agenda while I take\ncare of the rest?\nCarl Domingo (8:05 A.M.)\nSure.I''ll get it done as soon as possible.\nFranklin Smith (8:07 A.M.)\nThank you both. My train is arriving now. I think I''ll make it in time.\nJosephine Mallian (8:08 A.M.)\nNo problem, Franklin. We will also make sure there is plenty of coffee for you!\n4 4","passageTextVi":"","pa