---- [3] -------. We would\nlike to develop a similar partnership with Obsidian Villa.\nTo give you an idea of the advertising possibilities we offer, our graphic design team\nhas created four potential advertisements. They are enclosed with this letter. ------- [4] ------- • I hope these samples demonstrate how enthusiastic we are about promoting\nObsidian Villa to the over three million passengers who fly with us every year. If you\nare interested in exploring this idea further, please contact me by phone at\n546-555-0182 or by e-mail at i.r.bolton@foxtailairlines.com. I hope to have the\nopportunity to work with you.\nSincerely,\nI^uuo Bolton/\nIsaac Bolton, Director of Marketing\nFoxtail Airlines\nEnclosures\n246","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Foxtail\nAirlines4\nJuly 30\nMs. Gina Carracia\nGeneral Manager\nObsidian Villa\n1121 Marine Boulevard\nSeattle, WA 98101\nDear Ms. Carracia:\nMy name is Isaac Bolton, and I am Director of Marketing at Foxtail Airlines. ------- [1] -------. I am writing to share a marketing idea with you that would be beneficial\nfor both our companies. Our crew members who fly into Seattle have stayed at\nObsidian Villa several times in the past. They report that the rooms are consistently\ncomfortable and clean and that the staff is friendly and efficient. ------- [2] -------. However,\nthere is often no vacancy at your excellent establishment, and so our crews must stay\nelsewhere. We have arrangements with hotels in several cities around the world in\nwhich rooms are reserved for our crews in advance. Foxtail Airlines advertises for\nthese hotels in our in-flight magazine at a significant discount. ------- [3] -------. We would\nlike to develop a similar partnership with Obsidian Villa.\nTo give you an idea of the advertising possibilities we offer, our graphic design team\nhas created four potential advertisements. They are enclosed with this letter. ------- [4] ------- • I hope these samples demonstrate how enthusiastic we are about promoting\nObsidian Villa to the over three million passengers who fly with us every year. If you\nare interested in exploring this idea further, please contact me by phone at\n546-555-0182 or by e-mail at i.r.bolton@foxtailairlines.com. I hope to have the\nopportunity to work with you.\nSincerely,\nI^uuo Bolton/\nIsaac Bolton, Director of Marketing\nFoxtail Airlines\nEnclosures\n246"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3], and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “I have read numerous positive reviews that say the same.”","bilingual":"Câu sau đây thuộc về vị trí nào trong số các vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4]?","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"[2]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"review","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˌrivˈju/","meaning":"sự khảo sát; nghiên cứu tổng quát; bài kiểm tra; điều tra"},{"word":"general","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈʤɛnərəl/","meaning":"sĩ quan quân đội cấp cao"},{"word":"manager","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmænɪʤər/","meaning":"người điều hành một công ty; giám đốc; quản trị viên;"}]},{"questionNum":"176","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following schedule and e-mail.","passageText":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers.\n\nFrom: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (schedule)","text":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248"}],"question":"What is stated about the reading series?","bilingual":"Điều gì được nêu về loạt bài đọc?","options":["It is held once a month.","It features both new and well-known writers.","It requires a ticket to attend.","It highlights recently published books."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"It features both new and well-known writers.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"series","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪriz/","meaning":"sự liên tiếp; kế thừa; chương trình truyền hình phát sóng ở"},{"word":"feature","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfiː.tʃɚ/","meaning":"nét, đặc điểm"},{"word":"require","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ri''kwaiə(r)/","meaning":"đòi hỏi, yêu cầu; quy định"},{"word":"ticket","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈtɪkɪt/","meaning":"giấy chứng nhận; thẻ nhập cảnh; nhãn"}]},{"questionNum":"177","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following schedule and e-mail.","passageText":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers.\n\nFrom: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (schedule)","text":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248"}],"question":"What should writers send to the bookstore?","bilingual":"Người viết nên gửi gì đến hiệu sách?","options":["Information about their background","A book they would like to read to customers","The location at which they prefer to lecture","A signed contract"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Information about their background\".","vocabList":[{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"background","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈbæk.ɡraʊnd/","meaning":"phông nền, gia cảnh, quá trình học tập"},{"word":"book","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/bʊk/","meaning":"cuốn sách; đặt phòng, đặt vé"},{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"}]},{"questionNum":"178","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following schedule and e-mail.","passageText":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers.\n\nFrom: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (schedule)","text":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248"}],"question":"Why did Ms. Rodcliff write the e-mail?","bilingual":"Tại sao cô Rodcliff lại viết e-mail?","options":["To introduce herself to a new client","To describe her experience to a potential employer","To arrange an interview as part of her work","To schedule a visit to a university"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"To arrange an interview as part of her work\".","vocabList":[{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"introduce","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪntrəˈdus/","meaning":"trình bày lần đầu tiên; bắt đầu; thành lập; ĐẾN"},{"word":"herself","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/hərˈsɛlf/","meaning":"bản thân"}]},{"questionNum":"179","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following schedule and e-mail.","passageText":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers.\n\nFrom: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (schedule)","text":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248"}],"question":"On what date does Ms. Rodcliff hope to hear Professor Sandene read?","bilingual":"Cô Rodcliff hy vọng được nghe giáo sư Sandene đọc vào ngày nào?","options":["June 2","June 3","June 11","June 13"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"June 13\".","vocabList":[{"word":"date","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/deɪt/","meaning":"ngày, tháng, năm theo dương lịch;"},{"word":"monthly","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈmənθli/","meaning":"hàng tháng"},{"word":"series","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪriz/","meaning":"sự liên tiếp; kế thừa; chương trình truyền hình phát sóng ở"},{"word":"schedule","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''skedʒu:l/","meaning":"kế hoạch làm việc, tiến độ thi công"}]},{"questionNum":"180","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following schedule and e-mail.","passageText":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers.\n\nFrom: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (schedule)","text":"r\nMonthly Reading Series at the Spotted Cat Bookstore\nJune Schedule\nli\nSaturday, June 2 Brian Stenick, author of Into the Sea: Collected Poems\nSunday, June 3 David Callander, author of The Mastery of Comfort\nii Monday, June 11 Nina Brown, author of Family Threads\nWednesday, June 13 Bernice Sandene, author of Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear\nReadings begin at 7:00 P.M., and there is a reception with light refreshments afterward. II\nIf you are a published writer interested in reading for our series this July, please submit a\nfive-page example of your work as an attachment to readings@spottedcatbooks.com. With\nyour writing sample, send a one-paragraph biography. Your bio should mention your\nli education and artist residencies, publications, readings, and lectures, if applicable. The II\nseries welcomes both well-established and emerging writers."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"From: Jo Ann Rodcliff <jrodcliff @weekly courier.com>\nTo: David Callander <dcallander@elwyn.edu> Date: May 16\nSubject: Reading\nDear Professor Callander,\nI heard that you and Professor Sandene are reading at the Spotted Cat in a few weeks.\nHow exciting! I am hoping to attend both readings and am looking forward to seeing you\nboth again.\nSince graduating from Elwyn University last year, I’ve been working for the\nWeekly Courier as an arts and culture columnist. Mostly, I write reviews on art shows,\nconcerts, and other cultural events around the city. I also write profiles and book reviews.\nI would like to ask whether I may feature you and your book in my next column. The\ncolumn will be published the day before your reading.\nI was fascinated by your book, and it would be my pleasure to review it in the\nWeekly Courier. Are you available for a phone call tomorrow? Of course, I would prefer to\ninterview you in person, but I’m out of town on assignment until next week. Please let me\nknow if you are interested.\nSincerely,\nJo Ann Rodcliff\n248"}],"question":"What book does Ms. Rodcliff want to review in her column?","bilingual":"Cô Rodcliff muốn đánh giá cuốn sách nào trong chuyên mục của mình?","options":["Into the Sea: Collected Poems","The Mastery of Comfort","Family Threads","Retroactive: A History of Athletic Wear"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"The Mastery of Comfort\".","vocabList":[{"word":"book","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/bʊk/","meaning":"cuốn sách; đặt phòng, đặt vé"},{"word":"want","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/wɔnt/","meaning":"muốn"},{"word":"review","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ˌrivˈju/","meaning":"sự khảo sát; nghiên cứu tổng quát; bài kiểm tra; điều tra"},{"word":"comfort","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈkəmfərt/","meaning":"mang lại sự nhẹ nhõm; khuyến khích; để an ủi"}]},{"questionNum":"181","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V\n\nTo: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250"}],"question":"What is indicated about Kerilyn Fashions?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về Thời trang Kerilyn?","options":["It is a family-run company.","It offers overnight shipping.","Its prices are competitive.","Its product selection is updated regularly."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Its product selection is updated regularly.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"fashion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfæʃən/","meaning":"Thời trang"},{"word":"family","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfæməli/","meaning":"gia đình"},{"word":"company","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkʌm.pə.ni/","meaning":"công ty, bạn bè, bằng hữu"},{"word":"offer","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔfər/","meaning":"gợi ý; đề xuất giá; mềm; giá thầu"}]},{"questionNum":"182","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V\n\nTo: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250"}],"question":"What is NOT a stated advantage of Kerilyn Fashions’ service?","bilingual":"Ưu điểm đã nêu của dịch vụ của Kerilyn Fashions là gì?","options":["It can provide sample products to examine in advance of ordering.","Shipping charges are waived on large orders.","Merchandise arrives at a client’s business pre labeled.","It assigns special managers to assist new clients."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"Shipping charges are waived on large orders.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"advantage","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ədˈvæn.t̬ɪdʒ/","meaning":"lợi thế"},{"word":"fashion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfæʃən/","meaning":"Thời trang"},{"word":"service","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''sə:vis/","meaning":"sự phục vụ, sự hầu hạ"},{"word":"provide","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/prəˈvaɪd/","meaning":"cung cấp; cấp ; để thiết lập; cung cấp"}]},{"questionNum":"183","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V\n\nTo: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250"}],"question":"Who most likely is Mr. Anderson?","bilingual":"Ai có nhiều khả năng là ông Anderson nhất?","options":["A fashion model","A fashion designer","An account manager","An office supervisor"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"An account manager\".","vocabList":[{"word":"fashion","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈfæʃən/","meaning":"Thời trang"},{"word":"account","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/əˈkaʊnt/","meaning":"giải thích; để báo cáo; gây ra ; liên quan đến"},{"word":"manager","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈmænɪʤər/","meaning":"người điều hành một công ty; giám đốc; quản trị viên;"},{"word":"office","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔfəs/","meaning":"buồng; văn phòng; đương nhiệm; hãng; thẩm quyền"}]},{"questionNum":"184","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V\n\nTo: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250"}],"question":"In the e-mail, the word “anticipate” in paragraph 1, line 4, is closest in meaning to","bilingual":"Trong e-mail, từ “dự đoán” ở đoạn 1, dòng 4, có nghĩa gần nhất với","options":["expect","prevent","look forward to","depend on"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"expect\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mail","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/meɪl/","meaning":"dịch vụ bưu chính; thư và các vật phẩm khác được gửi qua"},{"word":"anticipate","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ænˈtɪs.ə.peɪt/","meaning":"phỏng đoán, dự đoán"},{"word":"paragraph","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈpɛrəˌgræf/","meaning":"đoạn văn; phần văn bản riêng biệt (thường bắt đầu bằng một"},{"word":"expect","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ɪkˈspekt/","meaning":"chờ đợi, trông chờ"}]},{"questionNum":"185","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following Web page and e-mail.","passageText":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V\n\nTo: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (Web page)","text":"Kerilyn Fashions ------- Exceptional Apparel for Your Company’s Brand\nAre you an apparel retailer seeking products that you can rebrand as your own?\nWe offer shirts, pants, shoes, and fashion accessories as a business-to-business\nwholesaler. Shop our extensive catalog and choose products for your customer\nbase. We will badge the products in your order with sewn-in labels carrying\nyour company’s branded logo. Your order will arrive in three to four weeks.\nKerilyn Fashions saves you time in product production so that your\nmerchandise gets to market quickly. And we offer fresh, new designs every\nseason; sample items can be sent to you upon request.\nWe extend discounts on large orders. We ship anywhere in the world, with\ncharges that are based on the weight of the order.\nMerchandise is nonrefundable, and a credit will be issued for any items that\narrive damaged. To get started with your first order, you are invited to set up an\nonline account. You will be assigned an account manager who will contact you\nwithin 24 hours and facilitate your first and future orders.! V"},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Terrence Anderson ctanderson @kerilynfashions.com>\nFrom: Sandeep Baliga <sbaliga @baligadesigns.in>\nDate: 15 August\nSubject: Enquiry for new order\nDear Mr. Anderson\nThank you very kindly for so effectively facilitating our very first order last month from\nKerilyn Fashions ------- the cotton blend T-shirts. They were well made, and our customers\nliked them so much that we sold out in two weeks. We would like to request the same\nitems, but we anticipate needing a larger quantity. What order amount is required for us to\nreceive discount pricing? Thank you in advance for a speedy response.\nKind regards,\nMr. Sandeep Baliga\n250"}],"question":"What is mentioned by Mr. Baliga?","bilingual":"Ông Baliga đã đề cập đến điều gì?","options":["His firm is planning to open branch locations.","His stock of T-shirts was too large.","He ordered T-shirts in several colors.","He believes Kerilyn Fashions’ goods are of high quality. GO ON TO THE NEXI PAGE"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"He believes Kerilyn Fashions’ goods are of high quality. GO ON TO THE NEXI PAGE\".","vocabList":[{"word":"firm","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/fərm/","meaning":"công ty; kinh doanh thương mại; tập đoàn"},{"word":"branch","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/bræntʃ/","meaning":"cành cây, chi nhánh"},{"word":"locations","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/loʊˈkeɪʃənz/","meaning":"địa điểm"},{"word":"stock","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/stɑːk/","meaning":"kho hàng, kho dự trữ"}]},{"questionNum":"186","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following sign, receipt, and e-mail.","passageText":"BETH S SECONDHAND FURNITURE\nHold Rules\n1. Purchased merchandise can be held for 7 days.\n2. Merchandise unclaimed after 7 days will be returned to inventory\nand resold.\n3. We are not responsible for damage to items that are a waiting\ncollection.\n4. We will provide delivery services for large furniture on request.\nLarge furniture is considered 25 kg or heavier.\n5. All sales are final.\nRECEIPT\nBETH S SECONDHAND FURNITURE\nItem Number: 39235\nReceipt Number: 477I2\nWeight:18 k0\nDate of Purchase: 8 August\nCustomer Name:Edward awa\nHase^\n135.00\nTotal:^\nPayment Method: Credit Card\nNote: Please hold -Por pickup\n252\n\nTo: Customer Service <customerservice@bethssecondhand.ca> From: Edward Hasegawa <e.hasegawa@abodemail.com> Subject: Furniture pickup\nDate: 10 August\nMy name is Edward Hasegawa. On Tuesday, 8 August, I bought a desk from your store. I\nplanned to borrow my coworker’s truck to pick up the desk, but today I learned that his\ntruck will be in the repair shop for the next two weeks. I’d like to ask whether the hold\ntime can be extended because of these unforeseen circumstances. I have been a long-time\ncustomer of your store and have purchased sofas, shelving, a kitchen table, and other\nitems.\nSincerely,\nEdward","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"BETH S SECONDHAND FURNITURE\nHold Rules\n1. Purchased merchandise can be held for 7 days.\n2. Merchandise unclaimed after 7 days will be returned to inventory\nand resold.\n3. We are not responsible for damage to items that are a waiting\ncollection.\n4. We will provide delivery services for large furniture on request.\nLarge furniture is considered 25 kg or heavier.\n5. All sales are final.\nRECEIPT\nBETH S SECONDHAND FURNITURE\nItem Number: 39235\nReceipt Number: 477I2\nWeight:18 k0\nDate of Purchase: 8 August\nCustomer Name:Edward awa\nHase^\n135.00\nTotal:^\nPayment Method: Credit Card\nNote: Please hold -Por pickup\n252\n\nTo: Customer Service <customerservice@bethssecondhand.ca> From: Edward Hasegawa <e.hasegawa@abodemail.com> Subject: Furniture pickup\nDate: 10 August\nMy name is Edward Hasegawa. On Tuesday, 8 August, I bought a desk from your store. I\nplanned to borrow my coworker’s truck to pick up the desk, but today I learned that his\ntruck will be in the repair shop for the next two weeks. I’d like to ask whether the hold\ntime can be extended because of these unforeseen circumstances. I have been a long-time\ncustomer of your store and have purchased sofas, shelving, a kitchen table, and other\nitems.\nSincerely,\nEdward"}],"question":"According to the sign, what happens to unclaimed furniture?","bilingual":"Theo biển báo, điều gì sẽ xảy ra với đồ nội thất không có người nhận?","options":["It is made available for sale again.","It is donated to a local charity.","It is promptly disposed of.","It is moved to long-term storage."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It is made available for sale again.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"sign","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/saɪn/","meaning":"đánh dấu; biểu tượng; chỉ định; gợi ý; dấu vết; để ý;"},{"word":"furniture","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈfɝː.nɪ.tʃɚ/","meaning":"đồ đạc"},{"word":"available","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈveɪ.lə.bəl/","meaning":"có sẵn để dùng"},{"word":"sale","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/seil/","meaning":"sự bán, việc bán"}]},{"questionNum":"187","passageTitle":"Questions 186-190 refer to the following sign, receipt, and e-mail.","passageTex