 back\ngarden. We’re expecting the delivery of some new patio furniture later this afternoon,\nand that will be set up as soon as it arrives.\n•i HU i •"}],"question":"At 10:25 A.M., what does Ms. Truesdell most likely mean when she writes, “That’s right”?","bilingual":"Vào lúc 10:25 sáng, rất có thể cô Truesdell có ý gì khi viết “Đúng vậy”?","options":["She requested that some trees be trimmed.","She confirmed the guest reservations.","She remembered why a job was not done.","She understood why some furniture had not been delivered."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"She remembered why a job was not done.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"mean","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/min/","meaning":"điểm giữa; ở giữa; cách xa hai thái cực như nhau;"},{"word":"write","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raɪt/","meaning":"viết, sáng tác"},{"word":"right","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/rait/","meaning":"điều tốt, điều phải, điều đứng đắn"},{"word":"confirmed","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kənˈfərmd/","meaning":"đã xác nhận"}]},{"questionNum":"153","passageTitle":"Questions 153-154 refer to the following advertisement.","passageText":"SAFT’S BOOKSHOP\nMoving Sale\nFrom 23 September through 30 September, Saft’s Bookshop at\n312 High Street will be selling all its store fixtures, furniture, and\nequipment. This includes the beautiful antique bookshelves from\nour main storefront window. Don’t miss this great opportunity to\npurchase gently used items to furnish your own store. We are\noffering items at amazing prices and are even willing to negotiate.\nSaft’s Bookshop will reopen its doors at 4900 Bundar Street in\nFebruary. It will be significantly more spacious and feature a\ndistinct interior design. Please be sure to visit us at our new\nlocation.\n0%","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"SAFT’S BOOKSHOP\nMoving Sale\nFrom 23 September through 30 September, Saft’s Bookshop at\n312 High Street will be selling all its store fixtures, furniture, and\nequipment. This includes the beautiful antique bookshelves from\nour main storefront window. Don’t miss this great opportunity to\npurchase gently used items to furnish your own store. We are\noffering items at amazing prices and are even willing to negotiate.\nSaft’s Bookshop will reopen its doors at 4900 Bundar Street in\nFebruary. It will be significantly more spacious and feature a\ndistinct interior design. Please be sure to visit us at our new\nlocation.\n0%"}],"question":"What is indicated about antique bookshelves?","bilingual":"Giá sách cổ nói lên điều gì?","options":["They will be moved to a location on Bundar Street.","They have been on display in a shop window.","They are in poor condition.","They were built by a famous designer. 270"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"They have been on display in a shop window.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"they","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðeɪ/","meaning":"họ"},{"word":"location","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/loʊˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"địa điểm; chức vụ; tình huống; địa điểm; điểm"},{"word":"display","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dɪˈspleɪ/","meaning":"sự bày biện; trưng bày, phô diễn"},{"word":"shop","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ʃɑp/","meaning":"cửa hàng bán lẻ nhỏ; phòng thu; việc kinh doanh; văn phòng; chỗ thoát"}]},{"questionNum":"154","passageTitle":"Questions 153-154 refer to the following advertisement.","passageText":"SAFT’S BOOKSHOP\nMoving Sale\nFrom 23 September through 30 September, Saft’s Bookshop at\n312 High Street will be selling all its store fixtures, furniture, and\nequipment. This includes the beautiful antique bookshelves from\nour main storefront window. Don’t miss this great opportunity to\npurchase gently used items to furnish your own store. We are\noffering items at amazing prices and are even willing to negotiate.\nSaft’s Bookshop will reopen its doors at 4900 Bundar Street in\nFebruary. It will be significantly more spacious and feature a\ndistinct interior design. Please be sure to visit us at our new\nlocation.\n0%","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"SAFT’S BOOKSHOP\nMoving Sale\nFrom 23 September through 30 September, Saft’s Bookshop at\n312 High Street will be selling all its store fixtures, furniture, and\nequipment. This includes the beautiful antique bookshelves from\nour main storefront window. Don’t miss this great opportunity to\npurchase gently used items to furnish your own store. We are\noffering items at amazing prices and are even willing to negotiate.\nSaft’s Bookshop will reopen its doors at 4900 Bundar Street in\nFebruary. It will be significantly more spacious and feature a\ndistinct interior design. Please be sure to visit us at our new\nlocation.\n0%"}],"question":"What is suggested about the new Saft’s Bookshop?","bilingual":"Có gợi ý gì về Hiệu sách của Saft mới?","options":["It will be on the same street as the current location.","It will be open seven days a week.","It will be larger than the old shop.","It will retain most of its staff."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"It will be larger than the old shop.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"current","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkɝː.ənt/","meaning":"dòng, luồng; hiện tại, hiện thời"},{"word":"location","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/loʊˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"địa điểm; chức vụ; tình huống; địa điểm; điểm"},{"word":"than","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ðən/","meaning":"hơn"},{"word":"shop","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/ʃɑp/","meaning":"cửa hàng bán lẻ nhỏ; phòng thu; việc kinh doanh; văn phòng; chỗ thoát"}]},{"questionNum":"155","passageTitle":"Questions 155-157 refer to the following newsletter.","passageText":"Birch Hill Center for the Arts Committee\nSupporters'' Newsletter\nThe committee has been hard at work this year! We are close to reaching our goal of\nbuilding a community arts center that will serve all the people of our lovely town of\nBirch Hill. Here is what we have accomplished so far.\n•In January, we completed a community survey about what activities to offer in\nthe new Birch Hill Center for the Arts.\n•In February, we completed a feasibility report and narrowed the potential\nbuilding sites to three possibilities.\n• In April, we submitted our project budget proposal to the city council for approval.\n• In May, we interviewed several candidates for the managing director position.\nDuring the next two months, we will:\n•Select our new managing director\n•Choose the location for the center\n•Complete the construction blueprints\n•Finalize the construction budget and timeline\n•Draft our events calendar\nAnd this fall, we should begin construction on the Birch Hill Center for the Arts!\nAs always, we welcome your input on the process. Please send questions or comments\nto our committee at project@bhca.org. If you are interested in serving on the\ncommittee, please call 952-555-0128.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Birch Hill Center for the Arts Committee\nSupporters'' Newsletter\nThe committee has been hard at work this year! We are close to reaching our goal of\nbuilding a community arts center that will serve all the people of our lovely town of\nBirch Hill. Here is what we have accomplished so far.\n•In January, we completed a community survey about what activities to offer in\nthe new Birch Hill Center for the Arts.\n•In February, we completed a feasibility report and narrowed the potential\nbuilding sites to three possibilities.\n• In April, we submitted our project budget proposal to the city council for approval.\n• In May, we interviewed several candidates for the managing director position.\nDuring the next two months, we will:\n•Select our new managing director\n•Choose the location for the center\n•Complete the construction blueprints\n•Finalize the construction budget and timeline\n•Draft our events calendar\nAnd this fall, we should begin construction on the Birch Hill Center for the Arts!\nAs always, we welcome your input on the process. Please send questions or comments\nto our committee at project@bhca.org. If you are interested in serving on the\ncommittee, please call 952-555-0128."}],"question":"When did the committee send a proposed budget to the city?","bilingual":"Ủy ban đã gửi ngân sách đề xuất cho thành phố khi nào?","options":["In January","In February","In April","In May"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"In April\".","vocabList":[{"word":"committee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kəˈmɪt̬.i/","meaning":"ủy ban"},{"word":"budget","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈbʌdʒ.ɪt/","meaning":"ngân sách; dự thảo ngân sách"},{"word":"city","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/ˈsɪti/","meaning":"thị trấn; khu đô thị lớn"},{"word":"supporter","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈpɔːr.t̬ɚ/","meaning":"người trợ giúp"}]},{"questionNum":"156","passageTitle":"Questions 155-157 refer to the following newsletter.","passageText":"Birch Hill Center for the Arts Committee\nSupporters'' Newsletter\nThe committee has been hard at work this year! We are close to reaching our goal of\nbuilding a community arts center that will serve all the people of our lovely town of\nBirch Hill. Here is what we have accomplished so far.\n•In January, we completed a community survey about what activities to offer in\nthe new Birch Hill Center for the Arts.\n•In February, we completed a feasibility report and narrowed the potential\nbuilding sites to three possibilities.\n• In April, we submitted our project budget proposal to the city council for approval.\n• In May, we interviewed several candidates for the managing director position.\nDuring the next two months, we will:\n•Select our new managing director\n•Choose the location for the center\n•Complete the construction blueprints\n•Finalize the construction budget and timeline\n•Draft our events calendar\nAnd this fall, we should begin construction on the Birch Hill Center for the Arts!\nAs always, we welcome your input on the process. Please send questions or comments\nto our committee at project@bhca.org. If you are interested in serving on the\ncommittee, please call 952-555-0128.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Birch Hill Center for the Arts Committee\nSupporters'' Newsletter\nThe committee has been hard at work this year! We are close to reaching our goal of\nbuilding a community arts center that will serve all the people of our lovely town of\nBirch Hill. Here is what we have accomplished so far.\n•In January, we completed a community survey about what activities to offer in\nthe new Birch Hill Center for the Arts.\n•In February, we completed a feasibility report and narrowed the potential\nbuilding sites to three possibilities.\n• In April, we submitted our project budget proposal to the city council for approval.\n• In May, we interviewed several candidates for the managing director position.\nDuring the next two months, we will:\n•Select our new managing director\n•Choose the location for the center\n•Complete the construction blueprints\n•Finalize the construction budget and timeline\n•Draft our events calendar\nAnd this fall, we should begin construction on the Birch Hill Center for the Arts!\nAs always, we welcome your input on the process. Please send questions or comments\nto our committee at project@bhca.org. If you are interested in serving on the\ncommittee, please call 952-555-0128."}],"question":"Where did the committee gather information about what activities to offer?","bilingual":"Ủy ban thu thập thông tin về những hoạt động nào sẽ được cung cấp ở đâu?","options":["From a survey","From a report","From a proposal","From personal interviews"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"From a survey\".","vocabList":[{"word":"committee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kəˈmɪt̬.i/","meaning":"ủy ban"},{"word":"gather","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈgæðər/","meaning":"vẽ cùng nhau; nếp gấp; vết nhăn"},{"word":"information","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɚˈmeɪ.ʃən/","meaning":"thông tin"},{"word":"offer","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈɔfər/","meaning":"gợi ý; đề xuất giá; mềm; giá thầu"}]},{"questionNum":"157","passageTitle":"Questions 155-157 refer to the following newsletter.","passageText":"Birch Hill Center for the Arts Committee\nSupporters'' Newsletter\nThe committee has been hard at work this year! We are close to reaching our goal of\nbuilding a community arts center that will serve all the people of our lovely town of\nBirch Hill. Here is what we have accomplished so far.\n•In January, we completed a community survey about what activities to offer in\nthe new Birch Hill Center for the Arts.\n•In February, we completed a feasibility report and narrowed the potential\nbuilding sites to three possibilities.\n• In April, we submitted our project budget proposal to the city council for approval.\n• In May, we interviewed several candidates for the managing director position.\nDuring the next two months, we will:\n•Select our new managing director\n•Choose the location for the center\n•Complete the construction blueprints\n•Finalize the construction budget and timeline\n•Draft our events calendar\nAnd this fall, we should begin construction on the Birch Hill Center for the Arts!\nAs always, we welcome your input on the process. Please send questions or comments\nto our committee at project@bhca.org. If you are interested in serving on the\ncommittee, please call 952-555-0128.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Birch Hill Center for the Arts Committee\nSupporters'' Newsletter\nThe committee has been hard at work this year! We are close to reaching our goal of\nbuilding a community arts center that will serve all the people of our lovely town of\nBirch Hill. Here is what we have accomplished so far.\n•In January, we completed a community survey about what activities to offer in\nthe new Birch Hill Center for the Arts.\n•In February, we completed a feasibility report and narrowed the potential\nbuilding sites to three possibilities.\n• In April, we submitted our project budget proposal to the city council for approval.\n• In May, we interviewed several candidates for the managing director position.\nDuring the next two months, we will:\n•Select our new managing director\n•Choose the location for the center\n•Complete the construction blueprints\n•Finalize the construction budget and timeline\n•Draft our events calendar\nAnd this fall, we should begin construction on the Birch Hill Center for the Arts!\nAs always, we welcome your input on the process. Please send questions or comments\nto our committee at project@bhca.org. If you are interested in serving on the\ncommittee, please call 952-555-0128."}],"question":"What is someone who wants to join the committee directed to do?","bilingual":"Người muốn tham gia ủy ban được hướng dẫn phải làm gì?","options":["Complete a questionnaire","Send an e-mail","Visit a Web site","Make a phone call"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Make a phone call\".","vocabList":[{"word":"someone","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈsəmˌwən/","meaning":"ai đó"},{"word":"wants","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/wɔnts/","meaning":"muốn"},{"word":"join","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/dʒɔɪn/","meaning":"nối, ghép"},{"word":"committee","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/kəˈmɪt̬.i/","meaning":"ủy ban"}]},{"questionNum":"158","passageTitle":"Questions 158-160 refer to the following job advertisement.","passageText":"Patton Advertising Is Hiring Wow!\nWe are seeking motivated, enthusiastic individuals to join us in our design, finance, and IT\ndepartments. Previous experience in the advertising sector is useful but not required.\nOur Work\nHere at Patton, we’ve designed advertisements and created marketing strategies for a wide\nrange of clients. This work has included designing logos and Web sites, as well as creating\nads for local radio and a national billboard. Under the leadership of CEO Amie Adesina,\nwe’re looking to expand in new directions and tackle even more exciting projects.\nSome Employee Comments\n•“In my first six months as a designer at Patton, I’ve already had the chance to work\nwith several clients and even lead my own team. The work isn’t always easy, but if you\nenjoy a fast-paced, challenging environment, you’ll really thrive here.” Thomas Kuti\n•“I’ve been working as a legal consultant at Patton for just under a year now, and I’ve\nenjoyed every moment. There’s a fantastic working culture, with generous employee\nbenefits including a gym membership and paid time off for volunteering. It’s the best\ncompany I''ve ever worked for.” Sabina Hussain\nVisit our Web site www.pattonads.com/careers to see vacancies and apply for jobs.","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Patton Advertising Is Hiring Wow!\nWe are seeking motivated, enthusiastic individuals to join us in our design, finance, and 