 as an assistant to our two on-site registered nurses\nat Summer Camp West, four days a week for the past two summers. The young\ncampers here have grown quite fond of Mr. Silva. They appreciate his kind but\ndedicated approach to wellness. ------- [2] -------. He is patient and nurturing, and I am\nconfident that he will succeed in a nursing program me such as yours.\nAs a nurse myself for more than three decades, I have worked with young\nprofessionals in various settings, including large hospitals, small clinics, schools,\nand, for the past several years, exclusively at Summer Camp West. ------- [3] -------.\nI therefore strongly believe that Mr. Silva will be an active and successful\nprogram me participant. ------- [4] -------. If you have any questions about Mr. Silva, please feel free to call me at\n(876) 555-0140.\nYours sincerely,\n3evu£iw (9ltve6ro/\nBenita Oliveira"}],"question":"What is indicated about Ms. Oliveira?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về cô Oliveira?","options":["Her child attends Summer Camp West.","She has been employed in health care for over 30 years.","She works at Summer Camp West four days a week.","She supervises nursing staff at a hospital."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"She has been employed in health care for over 30 years.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"attend","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈtend/","meaning":"tham dự"},{"word":"summer","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈsəmər/","meaning":"mùa hè"},{"word":"health","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/hɛlθ/","meaning":"sức khỏe thể chất hoặc tinh thần; thoát khỏi bệnh tật"},{"word":"care","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kɛr/","meaning":"được quan tâm đến; để ý tới; để trông chừng; ĐẾN"}]},{"questionNum":"163","passageTitle":"Questions 161-163 refer to the following letter.","passageText":"31 July\nDr. Shamalie Mowatt\nCornwall University Hospital\n22-28 Victoria Avenue\nKingston 6\nDear Dr. Mowatt,\nIt is a pleasure to recommend Mr. Renaldo Silva for your nursing program me. ------- [1] -------. Mr. Silva has served as an assistant to our two on-site registered nurses\nat Summer Camp West, four days a week for the past two summers. The young\ncampers here have grown quite fond of Mr. Silva. They appreciate his kind but\ndedicated approach to wellness. ------- [2] -------. He is patient and nurturing, and I am\nconfident that he will succeed in a nursing program me such as yours.\nAs a nurse myself for more than three decades, I have worked with young\nprofessionals in various settings, including large hospitals, small clinics, schools,\nand, for the past several years, exclusively at Summer Camp West. ------- [3] -------.\nI therefore strongly believe that Mr. Silva will be an active and successful\nprogram me participant. ------- [4] -------. If you have any questions about Mr. Silva, please feel free to call me at\n(876) 555-0140.\nYours sincerely,\n3evu£iw (9ltve6ro/\nBenita Oliveira","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"31 July\nDr. Shamalie Mowatt\nCornwall University Hospital\n22-28 Victoria Avenue\nKingston 6\nDear Dr. Mowatt,\nIt is a pleasure to recommend Mr. Renaldo Silva for your nursing program me. ------- [1] -------. Mr. Silva has served as an assistant to our two on-site registered nurses\nat Summer Camp West, four days a week for the past two summers. The young\ncampers here have grown quite fond of Mr. Silva. They appreciate his kind but\ndedicated approach to wellness. ------- [2] -------. He is patient and nurturing, and I am\nconfident that he will succeed in a nursing program me such as yours.\nAs a nurse myself for more than three decades, I have worked with young\nprofessionals in various settings, including large hospitals, small clinics, schools,\nand, for the past several years, exclusively at Summer Camp West. ------- [3] -------.\nI therefore strongly believe that Mr. Silva will be an active and successful\nprogram me participant. ------- [4] -------. If you have any questions about Mr. Silva, please feel free to call me at\n(876) 555-0140.\nYours sincerely,\n3evu£iw (9ltve6ro/\nBenita Oliveira"}],"question":"In which of the positions marked [1], [2], [3] and [4] does the following sentence best belong? “As such, I can at test to Mr. Silva’s professionalism and his compassion for those in his care.”","bilingual":"Câu nào sau đây được đánh dấu là đúng nhất trong các vị trí được đánh dấu [1], [2], [3] và [4]? “Như vậy, tôi có thể chứng thực tính chuyên nghiệp của ông Silva và lòng trắc ẩn của ông đối với những người được ông chăm sóc.”","options":["[1]","[2]","[3]","[4]"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"[3]\".","vocabList":[{"word":"position","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃən/","meaning":"vị trí, chỗ (của một vật gì)"},{"word":"care","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/kɛr/","meaning":"được quan tâm đến; để ý tới; để trông chừng; ĐẾN"},{"word":"hospital","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈhɑˌspɪtəl/","meaning":"địa điểm nơi người bệnh và người bị thương được chăm sóc y tế"},{"word":"pleasure","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈplɛʒər/","meaning":"hưởng thụ; vui chơi giải trí; sự giải trí; vui thích; vui sướng"}]},{"questionNum":"164","passageTitle":"Questions 164-167 refer to the following document.","passageText":"Sky-High Roofing\nWorkers doing construction or repair work on roofs face multiple potential\nhazards. Ladders, sky lights, and physical exposure to the natural elements\ninvolve risks. Stay safe by using common sense practices. Follow these\nguidelines.\nDress for safety.\n•Wear long-sleeved shirts, even in warm weather, and keep your\nwrist cuffs buttoned\n•Wear long pants without cuffs, as they can snag on roofing material\nand catch debris\n•Wear work boots that cover the ankles, and replace boots when the\nsoles show excessive wear\nUse personal protective equipment.\n•Wear gloves that cover the wrists, making sure there is no gap\nbetween the top of the gloves and the bottom of the sleeve cuffs\n•Use protective eyewear\nBegin the day right.\n•Review the work plan with all members of the team\n•Check the condition of ladders and all safety equipment\nI confirm that I have reviewed and understood these guidelines.\nSignature: Date:","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Bài đọc","text":"Sky-High Roofing\nWorkers doing construction or repair work on roofs face multiple potential\nhazards. Ladders, sky lights, and physical exposure to the natural elements\ninvolve risks. Stay safe by using common sense practices. Follow these\nguidelines.\nDress for safety.\n•Wear long-sleeved shirts, even in warm weather, and keep your\nwrist cuffs buttoned\n•Wear long pants without cuffs, as they can snag on roofing material\nand catch debris\n•Wear work boots that cover the ankles, and replace boots when the\nsoles show excessive wear\nUse personal protective equipment.\n•Wear gloves that cover the wrists, making sure there is no gap\nbetween the top of the gloves and the bottom of the sleeve cuffs\n•Use protective eyewear\nBegin the day right.\n•Review the work plan with all members of the team\n•Check the condition of ladders and all safety equipment\nI confirm that I have reviewed and understood these guidelines.\nSignature: Date:"}],"question":"For whom is the document most likely intended?","bilingual":"","options":["Ladder manufacturers","Clothing designers","Home inspectors","Roof installers"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (D) \"Roof installers\".","vocabList":[{"word":"document","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈdɑː.kjə.mən