charmail.net.uk From: martin.sampsell @haplers.co.uk\nDate: 22 February\nSubject: Proposal\nAttachment: |j) haplers-draftl.org\nDear Ms. Grotenhuis,\nI have attached an initial draft of a landscape design for you to consider. In our property\nwalk-through, you indicated where you want to have a walkway from the parking area to\nyour office. However, we are proposing something slightly different for you to consider.\nExperience has taught us to make pathways in commercial settings as direct as possible.\nOtherwise, people often walk through the grass anyway. You also mentioned wanting\nyear-round flowers, so we have incorporated a variety of native plants with different\nblooming seasons into the design.\nPlease give me a call once you '' ve had a chance to look at this design and I'' ll walk you\nthrough the details.\nMartin Sampsell\n308","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (brochure)","text":"Here at Hapler’s Landscape Company, we believe that landscape design does not\nhave to be challenging. Our goal is to design unique, beautiful gardens that meet our\nclients’ specifications and require minimal care once they have been planted. We\nalso care deeply about reducing air, soil, and water pollution. For more information\nabout how we achieve this, visit haplers.co.uk.\nOur process is implemented in four phases. This is how it works:\nPhase 1 ------- One of our consultants will call you and discuss your goals and vision for\nyour property.\nPhase 2 ------- We will conduct a thorough survey of your land to collect information on\nwater level, elevation, soil type, and sun patterns. Note that we work on many\nprojects at once and may not complete the survey until up to a month after your\ninitial consultation call.\nPhase 3 ------- Our design specialists will present you with a proposed design to suit your\nexisting landscape. We will discuss adjustments until you are satisfied with every\naspect of the plan.\nPhase 4 ------- We will implement the design per approved project specifications.\nAre you ready to get this process started and watch your land change before your\neyes? Contact Hapler’s at 01632 960255."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: me linda grotenhuis@charmail.net.uk From: martin.sampsell @haplers.co.uk\nDate: 22 February\nSubject: Proposal\nAttachment: |j) haplers-draftl.org\nDear Ms. Grotenhuis,\nI have attached an initial draft of a landscape design for you to consider. In our property\nwalk-through, you indicated where you want to have a walkway from the parking area to\nyour office. However, we are proposing something slightly different for you to consider.\nExperience has taught us to make pathways in commercial settings as direct as possible.\nOtherwise, people often walk through the grass anyway. You also mentioned wanting\nyear-round flowers, so we have incorporated a variety of native plants with different\nblooming seasons into the design.\nPlease give me a call once you '' ve had a chance to look at this design and I'' ll walk you\nthrough the details.\nMartin Sampsell\n308"}],"question":"What is indicated about Hapler’s?","bilingual":"Điều gì được chỉ ra về Hapler?","options":["It provides services to multiple clients at the same time.","It bills all of its clients on an hourly basis.","It works with residential clients only.","It is recommended by most of its clients."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"It provides services to multiple clients at the same time.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"provide","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/prəˈvaɪd/","meaning":"cung cấp; cấp ; để thiết lập; cung cấp"},{"word":"service","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/''sə:vis/","meaning":"sự phục vụ, sự hầu hạ"},{"word":"clients","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/klaɪənts/","meaning":"Khách hàng"},{"word":"bill","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/bɪl/","meaning":"hóa đơn"}]},{"questionNum":"179","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following brochure and e-mail.","passageText":"Here at Hapler’s Landscape Company, we believe that landscape design does not\nhave to be challenging. Our goal is to design unique, beautiful gardens that meet our\nclients’ specifications and require minimal care once they have been planted. We\nalso care deeply about reducing air, soil, and water pollution. For more information\nabout how we achieve this, visit haplers.co.uk.\nOur process is implemented in four phases. This is how it works:\nPhase 1 ------- One of our consultants will call you and discuss your goals and vision for\nyour property.\nPhase 2 ------- We will conduct a thorough survey of your land to collect information on\nwater level, elevation, soil type, and sun patterns. Note that we work on many\nprojects at once and may not complete the survey until up to a month after your\ninitial consultation call.\nPhase 3 ------- Our design specialists will present you with a proposed design to suit your\nexisting landscape. We will discuss adjustments until you are satisfied with every\naspect of the plan.\nPhase 4 ------- We will implement the design per approved project specifications.\nAre you ready to get this process started and watch your land change before your\neyes? Contact Hapler’s at 01632 960255.\n\nTo: me linda grotenhuis@charmail.net.uk From: martin.sampsell @haplers.co.uk\nDate: 22 February\nSubject: Proposal\nAttachment: |j) haplers-draftl.org\nDear Ms. Grotenhuis,\nI have attached an initial draft of a landscape design for you to consider. In our property\nwalk-through, you indicated where you want to have a walkway from the parking area to\nyour office. However, we are proposing something slightly different for you to consider.\nExperience has taught us to make pathways in commercial settings as direct as possible.\nOtherwise, people often walk through the grass anyway. You also mentioned wanting\nyear-round flowers, so we have incorporated a variety of native plants with different\nblooming seasons into the design.\nPlease give me a call once you '' ve had a chance to look at this design and I'' ll walk you\nthrough the details.\nMartin Sampsell\n308","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (brochure)","text":"Here at Hapler’s Landscape Company, we believe that landscape design does not\nhave to be challenging. Our goal is to design unique, beautiful gardens that meet our\nclients’ specifications and require minimal care once they have been planted. We\nalso care deeply about reducing air, soil, and water pollution. For more information\nabout how we achieve this, visit haplers.co.uk.\nOur process is implemented in four phases. This is how it works:\nPhase 1 ------- One of our consultants will call you and discuss your goals and vision for\nyour property.\nPhase 2 ------- We will conduct a thorough survey of your land to collect information on\nwater level, elevation, soil type, and sun patterns. Note that we work on many\nprojects at once and may not complete the survey until up to a month after your\ninitial consultation call.\nPhase 3 ------- Our design specialists will present you with a proposed design to suit your\nexisting landscape. We will discuss adjustments until you are satisfied with every\naspect of the plan.\nPhase 4 ------- We will implement the design per approved project specifications.\nAre you ready to get this process started and watch your land change before your\neyes? Contact Hapler’s at 01632 960255."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: me linda grotenhuis@charmail.net.uk From: martin.sampsell @haplers.co.uk\nDate: 22 February\nSubject: Proposal\nAttachment: |j) haplers-draftl.org\nDear Ms. Grotenhuis,\nI have attached an initial draft of a landscape design for you to consider. In our property\nwalk-through, you indicated where you want to have a walkway from the parking area to\nyour office. However, we are proposing something slightly different for you to consider.\nExperience has taught us to make pathways in commercial settings as direct as possible.\nOtherwise, people often walk through the grass anyway. You also mentioned wanting\nyear-round flowers, so we have incorporated a variety of native plants with different\nblooming seasons into the design.\nPlease give me a call once you '' ve had a chance to look at this design and I'' ll walk you\nthrough the details.\nMartin Sampsell\n308"}],"question":"At which phase of the process is Ms. Grotenhuis’ project?","bilingual":"Dự án của bà Grotenhuis ở giai đoạn nào của quy trình?","options":["Phase 1","Phase 2","Phase 3","Phase 4"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"Phase 3\".","vocabList":[{"word":"process","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''prouses/","meaning":"quá trình, sự tiến triển"},{"word":"project","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈprɒdʒɛkt/","meaning":"đề án, dự án; kế hoạch"},{"word":"landscape","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˈlænˌskeɪp/","meaning":"xem; phong cảnh; hướng trang ngang"},{"word":"company","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈkʌm.pə.ni/","meaning":"công ty, bạn bè, bằng hữu"}]},{"questionNum":"180","passageTitle":"Questions 176-180 refer to the following brochure and e-mail.","passageText":"Here at Hapler’s Landscape Company, we believe that landscape design does not\nhave to be challenging. Our goal is to design unique, beautiful gardens that meet our\nclients’ specifications and require minimal care once they have been planted. We\nalso care deeply about reducing air, soil, and water pollution. For more information\nabout how we achieve this, visit haplers.co.uk.\nOur process is implemented in four phases. This is how it works:\nPhase 1 ------- One of our consultants will call you and discuss your goals and vision for\nyour property.\nPhase 2 ------- We will conduct a thorough survey of your land to collect information on\nwater level, elevation, soil type, and sun patterns. Note that we work on many\nprojects at once and may not complete the survey until up to a month after your\ninitial consultation call.\nPhase 3 ------- Our design specialists will present you with a proposed design to suit your\nexisting landscape. We will discuss adjustments until you are satisfied with every\naspect of the plan.\nPhase 4 ------- We will implement the design per approved project specifications.\nAre you ready to get this process started and watch your land change before your\neyes? Contact Hapler’s at 01632 960255.\n\nTo: me linda grotenhuis@charmail.net.uk From: martin.sampsell @haplers.co.uk\nDate: 22 February\nSubject: Proposal\nAttachment: |j) haplers-draftl.org\nDear Ms. Grotenhuis,\nI have attached an initial draft of a landscape design for you to consider. In our property\nwalk-through, you indicated where you want to have a walkway from the parking area to\nyour office. However, we are proposing something slightly different for you to consider.\nExperience has taught us to make pathways in commercial settings as direct as possible.\nOtherwise, people often walk through the grass anyway. You also mentioned wanting\nyear-round flowers, so we have incorporated a variety of native plants with different\nblooming seasons into the design.\nPlease give me a call once you '' ve had a chance to look at this design and I'' ll walk you\nthrough the details.\nMartin Sampsell\n308","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (brochure)","text":"Here at Hapler’s Landscape Company, we believe that landscape design does not\nhave to be challenging. Our goal is to design unique, beautiful gardens that meet our\nclients’ specifications and require minimal care once they have been planted. We\nalso care deeply about reducing air, soil, and water pollution. For more information\nabout how we achieve this, visit haplers.co.uk.\nOur process is implemented in four phases. This is how it works:\nPhase 1 ------- One of our consultants will call you and discuss your goals and vision for\nyour property.\nPhase 2 ------- We will conduct a thorough survey of your land to collect information on\nwater level, elevation, soil type, and sun patterns. Note that we work on many\nprojects at once and may not complete the survey until up to a month after your\ninitial consultation call.\nPhase 3 ------- Our design specialists will present you with a proposed design to suit your\nexisting landscape. We will discuss adjustments until you are satisfied with every\naspect of the plan.\nPhase 4 ------- We will implement the design per approved project specifications.\nAre you ready to get this process started and watch your land change before your\neyes? Contact Hapler’s at 01632 960255."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: me linda grotenhuis@charmail.net.uk From: martin.sampsell @haplers.co.uk\nDate: 22 February\nSubject: Proposal\nAttachment: |j) haplers-draftl.org\nDear Ms. Grotenhuis,\nI have attached an initial draft of a landscape design for you to consider. In our property\nwalk-through, you indicated where you want to have a walkway from the parking area to\nyour office. However, we are proposing something slightly different for you to consider.\nExperience has taught us to make pathways in commercial settings as direct as possible.\nOtherwise, people often walk through the grass anyway. You also mentioned wanting\nyear-round flowers, so we have incorporated a variety of native plants with different\nblooming seasons into the design.\nPlease give me a call once you '' ve had a chance to look at this design and I'' ll walk you\nthrough the details.\nMartin Sampsell\n308"}],"question":"Why does Mr. Sampsell suggest changing the location of a pathway?","bilingual":"Tại sao ông Sampsell lại đề xuất thay đổi vị trí của một lối đi?","options":["To avoid a potential hazard","To provide the most efficient option","To take advantage of the shade available","To show the most attractive side of a building"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (B) \"To provide the most efficient option\".","vocabList":[{"word":"suggest","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/səˈdʒest/","meaning":"đề xuất"},{"word":"location","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/loʊˈkeɪʃən/","meaning":"địa điểm; chức vụ; tình huống; địa điểm; điểm"},{"word":"avoid","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈvɔɪd/","meaning":"tránh xa, ngăn ngừa"},{"word":"potential","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/pəˈtenʃl/","meaning":"tiềm năng; tiềm tàng"}]},{"questionNum":"181","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following notice and e-mail.","passageText":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged.\n\nTo: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over your late-night bus driving shift on Saturday, May\n22. I realize that I ''ll have to be alert, so I'' ll make sure to get plenty of rest.\nIn return, could you possibly take over my day shift on Tuesday, May 25? A friend of\nmine, who works for the same Chicago-based company that I used to work for, will be\nvisiting me that day.\nThanks in advance for your assistance.\nClaire Brunkhorst, MRBA Associate\n310","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (notice)","text":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over your late-night bus driving shift on Saturday, May\n22. I realize that I ''ll have to be alert, so I'' ll make sure to get plenty of rest.\nIn return, could you possibly take over my day shift on Tuesday, May 25? A friend of\nmine, who works for the same Chicago-based company that I used to work for, will be\nvisiting me that day.\nThanks in advance for your assistance.\nClaire Brunkhorst, MRBA Associate\n310"}],"question":"What is the purpose of the notice?","bilingual":"Mục đích của thông báo là gì?","options":["To introduce a new bus route","To report on the closing of a bus station","To announce transportation-service improvements","To invite comments about proposed schedule changes"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"To announce transportation-service improvements\".","vocabList":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''pɜ:pəs/","meaning":"mục đích, ý định"},{"word":"notice","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''nəƱtis/","meaning":"thông tri, yết thị, thông báo"},{"word":"introduce","pos":"Động từ (Verb)","level":"Level 3: 300 - 400 đ","ipa":"/ˌɪntrəˈdus/","meaning":"trình bày lần đầu tiên; bắt đầu; thành lập; ĐẾN"},{"word":"route","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raʊt/","meaning":"tuyến đường; lộ trình; đường đi"}]},{"questionNum":"182","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following notice and e-mail.","passageText":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged.\n\nTo: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over your late-night bus driving shift on Saturday, May\n22. I realize that I ''ll have to be alert, so I'' ll make sure to get plenty of rest.\nIn return, could you possibly take over my day shift on Tuesday, May 25? A friend of\nmine, who works for the same Chicago-based company that I used to work for, will be\nvisiting me that day.\nThanks in advance for your assistance.\nClaire Brunkhorst, MRBA Associate\n310","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (notice)","text":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over your late-night bus driving shift on Saturday, May\n22. I realize that I ''ll have to be alert, so I'' ll make sure to get plenty of rest.\nIn return, could you possibly take over my day shift on Tuesday, May 25? A friend of\nmine, who works for the same Chicago-based company that I used to work for, will be\nvisiting me that day.\nThanks in advance for your assistance.\nClaire Brunkhorst, MRBA Associate\n310"}],"question":"What is suggested in the notice about Bus 47?","bilingual":"Thông báo về Xe buýt 47 có nội dung gì?","options":["It has new stops on its route.","It has the earliest departure time.","It used to depart only in the afternoon.","It is in service on only one day of the week."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (C) \"It used to depart only in the afternoon.\".","vocabList":[{"word":"notice","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''nəƱtis/","meaning":"thông tri, yết thị, thông báo"},{"word":"stop","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 4: 400 - 495 đ","ipa":"/stɑp/","meaning":"sự chấm dứt; kết thúc; thăm nom; trở ngại; sự cản trở"},{"word":"route","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/raʊt/","meaning":"tuyến đường; lộ trình; đường đi"},{"word":"departure","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 2: 200 - 300 đ","ipa":"/dɪˈpɑrʧər/","meaning":"rời đi; đi xa; ngược lại với sự xuất hiện"}]},{"questionNum":"183","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following notice and e-mail.","passageText":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged.\n\nTo: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over your late-night bus driving shift on Saturday, May\n22. I realize that I ''ll have to be alert, so I'' ll make sure to get plenty of rest.\nIn return, could you possibly take over my day shift on Tuesday, May 25? A friend of\nmine, who works for the same Chicago-based company that I used to work for, will be\nvisiting me that day.\nThanks in advance for your assistance.\nClaire Brunkhorst, MRBA Associate\n310","passageTextVi":"","passages":[{"label":"Văn bản 1 (notice)","text":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged."},{"label":"Văn bản 2 (e-mail)","text":"To: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over your late-night bus driving shift on Saturday, May\n22. I realize that I ''ll have to be alert, so I'' ll make sure to get plenty of rest.\nIn return, could you possibly take over my day shift on Tuesday, May 25? A friend of\nmine, who works for the same Chicago-based company that I used to work for, will be\nvisiting me that day.\nThanks in advance for your assistance.\nClaire Brunkhorst, MRBA Associate\n310"}],"question":"What bus will Ms. Brunkhorst most likely drive on May 22?","bilingual":"Cô Brunkhorst sẽ đi xe buýt nào nhiều nhất vào ngày 22 tháng 5?","options":["Bus 36","Bus 47","Bus 51","Bus 65"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Căn cứ vào nội dung bài đọc, đáp án chính xác là (A) \"Bus 36\".","vocabList":[{"word":"drive","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/draɪv/","meaning":"cuộc đua; lái xe"},{"word":"regional","pos":"Tính từ (Adjective)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/ˈridʒənl/","meaning":"(thuộc) vùng; địa phương"},{"word":"authority","pos":"Danh từ (Noun)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/əˈθɔːr.ə.t̬i/","meaning":"quyền thế, nhà chức trách, chính quyền"},{"word":"notice","pos":"Danh từ / Động từ (Noun / Verb)","level":"Level 1: Dưới 200 đi","ipa":"/''nəƱtis/","meaning":"thông tri, yết thị, thông báo"}]},{"questionNum":"184","passageTitle":"Questions 181-185 refer to the following notice and e-mail.","passageText":"Merenville Regional Bus Authority c\nNotice to the Public\nIn response to its recently conducted passenger survey, the Merenville Regional\nBus Authority (MRBA) will be adjusting its Saturday and Sunday service\nbetween Merenville Central Station (MCS) and Louberg. The following schedule\nchanges will be in effect as of May 1.\n•Bus 36, in service on Saturdays only, will be departing MCS every hour on\nthe hour, with the first departure scheduled for 6:00 A.M. and the last to take\nplace at midnight. This adjustment is intended to provide passengers with\nmore departure options.\n•Bus 47, which runs on both days, will now be departing MCS at 7:00 A.M. in\naddition to its regularly scheduled departure times of 12:15 P.M. and 6:15 P.M.\n® Bus 51, which runs on both days, will continue to have three departures from\nMCS. However, they are now scheduled to take place at 7:30 A.M., 1:30 P.M.,\nand 4:30 P.M.\n•Bus 65, in service on Sundays only, will now be departing MCS at 10:00 A.M.\ninstead of 8:00 A.M. Departures scheduled for 1:00 P.M., 3:00 P.M., and\n5:00 P.M. remain unchanged.\n\nTo: Adriano Martinez <amartinez@mrba.com> From: Claire Brunkhorst <cbrunkhorst@mrba.com> Date: May 14\nRe: Switch shift request\nHi Adriano,\nRegarding your request, I can take over 